Develop the performance of the less known Padovan sequence, limiting the total of numerical results to a prescribed checkpoint 'n'.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
In the following Python code, the Padovan sequence is generated up to 'n'. In this sequence, each term is the sum of the two preceding ones, but with a shift. If counting from 0, the nth padovan number can be given by formula p(n) = p(n-2) + p(n-3).

```python
def padovan(n):
    sequence = [0, 1, 1]
    if n <= 2:
        return sequence[:n+1]
    for i in range(3, n+1):
        sequence.append(sequence[i-2] + sequence[i-3])
    return sequence

n = 10
print(padovan(n))
```

This script will print the first ten elements of the Padovan sequence.
