Craft a sophisticated C++ software application designed to produce an elaborately designed ornamental pattern based on the Fibonacci number sequence.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
To design an ornamental pattern based on the Fibonacci sequence, we'll create a simple rectangular pattern where the width and height of the rectangles follow the Fibonacci sequence. In console mode, we can represent rectangles by printing out a certain number of 'X' characters.

```C++
#include <iostream>
#include <vector>

std::vector<int> fib_sequence(int seq_size) {
    std::vector<int> sequence(seq_size);
    sequence[0] = 1;
    if(seq_size > 1) {
        sequence[1] = 1;
        for(int i=2; i<seq_size; i++) {
            sequence[i] = sequence[i-1] + sequence[i-2];
        }
    }
    return sequence;
}

void print_rectangle(int width, int height) {
    for(int i=0; i<height; i++) {
        for(int j=0; j<width; j++) {
            std::cout << "X";
        }
        std::cout << "\n";
    }
}

int main() {
    int seq_size;
    std::cout << "Enter the size of the Fibonacci sequence: ";
    std::cin >> seq_size;

    std::vector<int> sequence = fib_sequence(seq_size);

    for(int i=0; i<seq_size; i++) {
        std::cout << "Fibonacci number " << (i+1) << " rectangle:\n";
        print_rectangle(sequence[i], sequence[i]); //Creates a square
        std::cout << "\n";
    }

    return 0;
}
```

To execute, enter a number to determine how many Fibonacci numbers will be generated. The output is a series of "X" pattern squares where the side length of the square is the corresponding Fibonacci number.

Remember, this is just a basic implementation. The "ornamental pattern" can be designed in many different ways and this is just one example.

Also, note that the program does not handle incorrect input. It's always a good practice to check whether the input is valid, so you might want to add error checking if you plan to use this code for anything serious. 

Lastly, the console application may not be able to properly display large patterns due to the size limitation of the console window. If you want to create large patterns, it might be better to output the pattern into a file or create a graphical application.
