Develop a responsive CSS mixin for a navigation menu designed for a mobile device.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here is an example of a CSS mixin using SCSS that you can use as a starting point for a responsive navigation menu:

```scss
@mixin responsive-nav($breakpoint) {
  @media (max-width: $breakpoint) {
    .mobile-nav {
      display: block;
    }

    .desktop-nav {
      display: none;
    }

    .nav-item {
      display: block;
      width: 100%;
      text-align: left;
    }
  }
}

@include responsive-nav(480px);
```

In the CSS mixin (`responsive-nav`), we use a `@media` directive to conditionally apply styles if the viewport width is less than or equal to the specified `$breakpoint` (480px in this case). 

In mobile mode (viewport width <= 480px), the `mobile-nav` will be displayed, and `desktop-nav` will be hidden. Each `nav-item` (individual navigation links) will be displayed as a block that takes up the full width of the container and the text will be left-aligned.

Please adapt and extend this mixin according to your exact needs and specifications.
<|end|>


