Here is the required solution in Java that not only finds the smallest element but also its index in the array.

```java
public class Main
{
  public static void main(String[] args)
  {
    double[] myList = {1.9, 2.9, 3.4, 3.5};
    
    System.out.println(findSmallestIndex(myList));
  }

  public static int findSmallestIndex(double[] myList)
  {
    double smallest = myList[0];
    int smallestIndex = 0;
    for (int i = 1; i < myList.length; i++)
    {
      if(myList[i] < smallest){
        smallest = myList[i];
        smallestIndex = i;
      }
    }
    return smallestIndex;
  }
}
```
