How can I create a simple trading strategy using Pine Script?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Pine Script is a language created by TradingView for developing your own indicators and strategies. Here is an example of a basic strategy script using EMA (Exponential Moving Average):

```pinescript
//@version=4
strategy("EMA Long Only", overlay = true)
length = input(50, minval=1) // Increment for the EMA, default is 50
price = close // Define what price to apply the EMA to; close is the close price of each candle
val = ema(price, length) // Calculate the EMA

plot(val, title="EMA") // Plot the EMA on the chart

// Define long condition as when the close price crosses over the EMA
if crossover(close, val)
    strategy.entry("Long", strategy.long) // Send a long order

// Plot arrows on the chart where the strategy would enter a trade
plotshape(series=strategy.position_size>0, style=shape.labelup, location=location.belowbar, color=color.green, style=shape.triangleup)
```

This script applies an EMA to the closing price of each candlestick. When the closing price crosses over the EMA, the script enters a long trade.

Note: Before using any strategy in real-time trading, make sure to backtest it thoroughly, as past performance is not necessarily indicative of future results.
<|end|>


