To load a JSON file from a URL using pandas and then return the last 5 rows, we must first import the pandas and requests libraries. Here is how you do it:

Sample code:
```python
import pandas as pd
import requests
import json

# Make a GET request to the API
url = "https://api.myjson.com/bins/g8wsy"  #replace with your URL 
res = requests.get(url)

# Parse the JSON data from the response
data = json.loads(res.text)

# Convert the 'data' list into a DataFrame
df = pd.DataFrame(data)

# Return the last 5 rows
df.tail(5)
```
Please replace "https://api.myjson.com/bins/g8wsy" with your desired URL. The JSON file at the given URL will be loaded into a pandas DataFrame. The last five rows of this DataFrame will be returned by the "df.tail(5)" function. 

This process assumes that the JSON data is in a format directly translatable to a pandas DataFrame and that the requested URL does not require any specific headers or authentication. In case of needing headers or authentication you must include these in the GET request.

Keep in mind pandas can directly read a json file from a url if it is presented like a file (i.e., having a proper structure of a JSON format). For endpoints giving json response, the above method works well.
