Write a JavaScript program to change the color of a paragraph when it is clicked.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here is a simple JavaScript program to change the color of a paragraph when it is clicked:

HTML:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
    <body>
        <p id="myPara">This is a demo paragraph.</p>
    </body>
</html>
```

JavaScript:

```javascript
document.getElementById("myPara").addEventListener("click", function() {
    this.style.color = "red";
});
```

In this program, we're first getting the paragraph by its id "myPara" with the `getElementById()` function. Then, we're attaching a "click" event listener to it with the `addEventListener()` function. When the paragraph is clicked, the function we passed to the `addEventListener()` function will get called. This function changes the color of the paragraph to red with the line `this.style.color = "red";`.

Note: You have to add JavaScript code inside `<script>` tags in the HTML document.
