Design a programming function that, when supplied with a textual string as input, carries out the process of discerning and enumerating the instances of distinct palindromic sequences. This must involve multiple-step reasoning including isolating words, identifying palindrome patterns and counting distinct ones.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here is a Python based solution for the problem described:

```python
def find_palindromes(text):
    words = text.split(" ")
    palindromes = set()  # use set to automatically handle duplicates

    for word in words:
        word = word.lower()
        if word == word[::-1]:   # check if the word is the same when reversed
            palindromes.add(word)
    
    return len(palindromes), palindromes

text = "madam Arora teaches malayalam Madam runs a race car level wow"
print(find_palindromes(text))
```
This script first splits the text into words. It then iterates over each word, and checks if it is the same word when reversed, which is the property of a palindrome. If so, it adds the word to a set. Sets in Python automatically ignore duplicates so using a set ensures we only count distinct palindromes. Finally, it returns the number of distinct palindromes and the palindromes found. Please note that this code considers palindromes as case-insensitive.

Ensure to include exception handling and robustness in your implementation as per your requirements. Make sure to strip punctuation (etc. commas, dots, exclamation marks) if not consider as part of palindromes in your requirement.
<|end|>


