Develop a user interface to present a pie chart showcasing the distribution of people based on their job sector and education level.
Sample JSON data to be used:

[
  {
    "name": "Nick",
    "education": "Bachelor's",
    "job": "Engineering"
  },
  {
    "name": "Susan",
    "education": "Master's",
    "job": "Finance"
  },
  {
    "name": "Greg",
    "education": "PhD",
    "job": "Science"
  },
  {
    "name": "Lindsay",
    "education": "Bachelor's",
    "job": "Healthcare"
  }
]
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here is a solution written in Python using the pandas, matplotlib, and tkinter libraries. It loads the JSON data, processes it into a format suitable for creating pie charts, and then displays two pie charts; one for job sector distribution and one for education level distribution.

```python
import pandas as pd
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt

from matplotlib.figure import Figure
from matplotlib.backends.backend_tkagg import FigureCanvasTkAgg
from tkinter import Tk

# Load data from JSON
data = [
  {
    "name": "Nick",
    "education": "Bachelor's",
    "job": "Engineering"
  },
  {
    "name": "Susan",
    "education": "Master's",
    "job": "Finance"
  },
  {
    "name": "Greg",
    "education": "PhD",
    "job": "Science"
  },
  {
    "name": "Lindsay",
    "education": "Bachelor's",
    "job": "Healthcare"
  }
]

# Convert data into pandas dataframe
df = pd.DataFrame(data)

# Create a figure to hold the plots
fig = Figure(figsize=(10, 5))

# Create the job sector distribution pie chart
job_axis = fig.add_subplot(121)
job_counts = df['job'].value_counts()
job_axis.pie(job_counts, labels=job_counts.index)

# Create the education level distribution pie chart
education_axis = fig.add_subplot(122)
education_counts = df['education'].value_counts()
education_axis.pie(education_counts, labels=education_counts.index)

# Create tkinter window
window = Tk()
canvas = FigureCanvasTkAgg(fig, master=window)
canvas.draw()
canvas.get_tk_widget().pack()

window.mainloop()
```
This solution assumes the JSON data is embedded right in the script. If the data comes from a file, replace the embedded JSON data with a statement that loads and parses the JSON from that file.

This solution also uses very simple pie charts; it includes no legend or title and does minimal formatting on the charts. Additional configuration of the pie chart can be done as per requirement.
<|end|>


