Here's one possible binary search tree structure:

```
     5
    / \
   4  11
     /  \
    6   10
       /
      8
```

Explanation:

- The first number, 5, starts as the root.
- 4 is less than 5, so it goes to the left of 5.
- 11 is greater than 5, so it goes to the right of 5.
- 6 is less than 11 but greater than 5, so it goes to the left of 11.
- 10 is less than 11 but greater than 5 and 6, so it goes to the left of 11 but to the right of 6.
- Finally, 8 is less than 10 and 11 but greater than 5 and 6, so it goes to the left of 10.
