Develop a sentiment analysis algorithm using natural language processing (NLP) techniques that classifies a given set of statements and accurately assigns sentiment classifications. The sentiments should include but not be limited to positive, negative, and neutral. The algorithm should not only be able to classify obvious sentiments but also understand context and interpret more complex sentiments. For testing the accuracy of your algorithm, use the following statement: "This was the worst experience ever.", however, extend your solution to accept and evaluate a variety of different types of input text. Consider incorporating machine learning models to enhance the complexity and accuracy of the sentiment analysis.
