Given an array of academic scores achieved by learners, write a JavaScript program to generate HTML markup to display these records in a structured tabular format. Additionally, the table should include a fifth column that calculates and displays the deviation of each score from the mean score. Also, ensure that this new column is updated whenever a new score is added or an existing score is modified.
let grades = [85, 90, 77, 95];
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here's a simple solution in Javascript that uses tables in HTML and no external libraries. I've assumed an "academic score" is an integer:

```javascript
let grades = [85, 90, 77, 95];

function average(arr) {
    var total = 0;
    for (var i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {
        total += arr[i];
    }
    return total / arr.length;
}

function deviation(value, average) {
    return value - average;
}

function generateTable(grades) {
    let table = '<table><tr><th>Index</th><th>Score</th><th>Deviation</th></tr>';
    const avg = average(grades);
    for(let i = 0; i < grades.length; i++) {
        table += '<tr><td>' + i + '</td><td>' + grades[i] + '</td><td>' + deviation(grades[i], avg) + '</td></tr>';
    }
    table += '</table>';
    return table
}

function appendGrade(grade, elementId) {
    grades.push(grade);
    document.getElementById(elementId).innerHTML = generateTable(grades);
}

function modifyGrade(index, newGrade, elementId) {
    grades[index] = newGrade;
    document.getElementById(elementId).innerHTML = generateTable(grades);
}

document.getElementById('scores_table').innerHTML = generateTable(grades);

appendGrade(80, 'scores_table');
modifyGrade(0, 90, 'scores_table');
```

In the above example, you start by defining your array of scores. The average function calculates the average of the scores. The deviation function calculates the deviation from the mean.
Next, you have the generateTable() function that generates an HTML string that represents a table, then appendGrade() and modifyGrade() modify the global grades variable and regenerate the HTML table.
Finally, the HTML is added to the scores_table div by accessing the innerHTML property. 

This code doesn't handle invalid input and is very simplified - it's meant to be a starting point for a more robust solution. 

Also, make sure to trigger appendGrade and modifyGrade function based on user actions.

Note: You need to run appendGrade function and modifyGrade function base on user actions, they are added here just for demonstration. Replace `scores_table` with the id of your HTML element where you want to show this table.
<|end|>


