Here, `class Avatar` defines the class. `def __init__(self, alias):` is the constructor method which is called when an object is created from the class and it allows the class to initialize the attributes of the class. `self.alias = alias` sets the attribute for the object. The `self` parameter is a reference to the current instance of the class and is used to access variables and methods associated with that instance.
