Modify this precise bit of Java function code, instigating it to relentlessly produce only lexemes that particularly comply as anagrams of each other. The function must cognitively scrutinize each lexeme, meticulously sort their respective characters in a systematic sequence, and then concisely compare the structured output across them to promote an efficient and unambiguous solution.

public static String[] findAnagrams(String[] lexemes) {
    ArrayList<String> resultantArray = new ArrayList<>();
    for (String lexeme : lexemes) {
        if (lexeme.length() >= 2) {
            resultantArray.add(lexeme);
