Please construct a sample query, utilizing SQL, that aims to extract a list of users who had registered within the previous 24-month period and simultaneously have a record of exceeding five file uploads.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here's a sample SQL query to achieve the mentioned requirements.

Note: I will be assuming the existence of two tables, 'users' and 'uploads'. 'users' table contains user information including the registration date (registered_at) and 'uploads' table tracks file uploads by users containing a foreign key 'user_id' linked to the 'users' table.

```SQL
SELECT u.id, u.name
FROM users u
JOIN (
  SELECT user_id 
  FROM uploads 
  GROUP BY user_id 
  HAVING COUNT(*) > 5
) up ON u.id = up.user_id
WHERE u.registered_at >= NOW() - INTERVAL 24 MONTH;
```

This SQL query works as follows:

The subquery from the uploads table groups the data by 'user_id' and retains only the groups (users) who have uploaded more than 5 files (HAVING COUNT(*) > 5).

The main query then joins this result with the users table on 'id' (users.id = uploads.user_id), and filters out users who have registered within the previous 24 months based on 'registered_at' (registered_at >= NOW() - INTERVAL 24 MONTH).

The result will be a list of users (their id and names in this case) who registered within the previous 24-month period and have uploaded more than five files.
<|end|>


