Sure, here is a simple C++ function that can be used to print a given string in reverse order.

```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <string>

void printReverse(std::string str) {
    int length = str.length();
    
    for (int i = length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
        std::cout << str[i];
    }
}

int main() {
    std::string str = "Programming";
    printReverse(str);
    return 0;
}
```

In this function, we are simply iterating the characters of the string in reverse order by starting from the last character. Each character is printed out in an individual manner. After compiling and running this program, "gnimmargorP" will be printed to the console.
