To achieve this, you can use an UPDATE query in the SQL, which will identify the rows with NULL values in the column_y and then replace them with their respective column_x values. Note that 'B' assumed to be the table's name.

Here is the SQL command:

```sql
UPDATE B 
SET column_y = column_x 
WHERE column_y IS NULL;
```

This command will update the 'column_y' with the value of 'column_x' wherever 'column_y' is NULL. Be sure to use this carefully as UPDATE command will change the existing data in your table.
