Write a Javascript program to check if a number is even or odd.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here is a simple Javascript program that checks if a number is even or odd:

```javascript
function evenOrOdd(num) {
    if (num % 2 == 0) {
        console.log(num + ' is even');
    } else {
        console.log(num + ' is odd');
    }
}

evenOrOdd(10);  // call the function with number 10
evenOrOdd(15);  // call the function with number 15
```

In this code, the function `evenOrOdd` accepts a number as a parameter. Inside the function, the input number is divided by 2 using the modulus operator. If this operation results in a remainder of 0, then the number is even and "num is even" is printed to the console. If there is a remainder, then the number is odd and "num is odd" is printed to the console.

When you run this code, it will print out:

```
10 is even
15 is odd
```
<|end|>


