My application is targeted for Compact .Net 1.0 framework. The application has to check and download any updates available from a web-site. I am thinking of providing the updates as CAB files. Since the CAB files are processor type specific, I want to download the CAB file based on the Processor Type. What is the API for getting the Processor type (ARM/SH/MIPS/etc)?

Thanks,
Kishore A
<|end|>
<|asst|>
You can use the System.Environment.GetEnvironmentVariable method to extract the "PROCESSOR_ARCHITECTURE" environment variable which should provide information about the current machine's processor instruction set:

```csharp
string arch = System.Environment.GetEnvironmentVariable("PROCESSOR_ARCHITECTURE");
```

If you want to get more specific information, you could use P/Invoke to call the GetSystemInfo API, but keep in mind the GetSystemInfo API is not accessible directly in the .NET Compact Framework. Thus, you would need to make a call to this native API as it is available only from the Windows API.

This is a simple example of using GetSystemInfo from C#:

```csharp
[StructLayout(LayoutKind.Sequential)]
public struct SYSTEM_INFO
{
    public ushort processorArchitecture;
    //... (other members of SYSTEM_INFO struct)
};

[DllImport("kernel32.dll")]
public static extern void GetSystemInfo(ref SYSTEM_INFO lpSystemInfo);

public SYSTEM_INFO GetProcessorArchitecture
{
    SYSTEM_INFO sysInfo = new SYSTEM_INFO();
    GetSystemInfo(ref sysInfo);

    return sysInfo.processorArchitecture;
}
```

The returned value in the processorArchitecture field will help determine the processor type. Here are some of the possible values and their corresponding types:

- PROCESSOR_ARCHITECTURE_INTEL x86
- PROCESSOR_ARCHITECTURE_MIPS
- PROCESSOR_ARCHITECTURE_ALPHA
- PROCESSOR_ARCHITECTURE_PPC
- PROCESSOR_ARCHITECTURE_SHX
- PROCESSOR_ARCHITECTURE_ARM
- PROCESSOR_ARCHITECTURE_IA64
- PROCESSOR_ARCHITECTURE_ALPHA64
- PROCESSOR_ARCHITECTURE_MSIL
- PROCESSOR_ARCHITECTURE_AMD64
- PROCESSOR_ARCHITECTURE_IA32_ON_WIN64
- PROCESSOR_ARCHITECTURE_UNKNOWN

For a real application you would need to handle the other members of the SYSTEM_INFO struct and marshal it correctly, but hopefully above given basic example will give you a good place to start from.
<|end|>


