I use apollo clinet and react with graphql. When I try to mutate, it says types are not the same.
But they are the same.
Error:

Field "xMutation" argument "type" requires type X_value, found X_value.



mutation Product (
        $id: String
        $type: milk
        $productId: String
    ) {
        productMutation (
            id: $id
            type: milk
            productId: $productId
        ) {
            ...productDetails
        }
    }
<|end|>
<|asst|>
It seems that you're not passing variables correctly. You should pass the variable name instead of the value to the mutation parameters. Try the following: 

```graphql
mutation Product (
        $id: String
        $type: X_value!
        $productId: String
    ) {
        productMutation (
            id: $id
            type: $type
            productId: $productId
        ) {
            ...productDetails
        }
    }
```

You should also make sure you're passing the correct value when you call the mutation in your react component.

Remember, arguments (variables) must begin with " $ ", and you can't replace the variable definition in the mutation with direct values.

Lastly, Double check your GraphQL schema to make sure type `X_value` exists and it is indeed the type for the argument `type` in mutation `productMutation`. 

Keep in mind that GraphQL is strongly-typed. If you're passing a string value to a variable expected to be a different type, you'll receive a type mismatch error.
<|end|>


