<|end|>
<|asst|>
Since the original code is not provided, I'll provide a simple SVG sunburst code and then follow the given requirements. 

Below is the initial SVG sunburst representation:

```html
<svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
    <circle cx="50" cy="50" r="40" style="fill: orange;"/>
    <path d="M50,10 a40,40 0 0 1 0,80 a40,40 0 0 1 0,-80" style="fill: yellow;"/> 
</svg>
```

This code creates a sunburst with a large orange circle (the sun) and a yellow semi-circle (sun ray). But, we want a full circle for our rays and let the user decide how many rays there should be.

Here is the corrected code with added feature:

```html
<svg id="sunburst" viewBox="0 0 100 100" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
    <circle id="sun" cx="50" cy="50" r="40" style="fill: orange;"/>
</svg>

<script>
function createSunburst(numberOfRays) {
    var sunburst = document.getElementById('sunburst');
    var angle = 360 / numberOfRays;
    var rotation = 0;

    // Remove any existing rays
    while (sunburst.firstChild.id !== 'sun') {
        sunburst.firstChild.remove();
    }

    // Add new rays
    for (var i = 0; i < numberOfRays; i++) {
        var ray = document.createElementNS('http://www.w3.org/2000/svg', 'path');
        ray.setAttribute('d', 'M50,10 a40,40 0 0 1 0,80 a40,40 0 0 1 0,-80');
        ray.setAttribute('style', 'fill: yellow;');
        ray.setAttribute('transform', 'rotate(' + rotation + ' 50 50)');
        sunburst.insertBefore(ray, sunburst.firstChild);

        rotation += angle;
    }
}

createSunburst(8);  // Call this function with desired number of rays
</script>
```

This code initializes an SVG container for the sunburst and add a sun in the center. It then uses JavaScript to generate rays. The `createSunburst()` function accepts a parameter for the desired number of rays. It first removes any existing rays, than adds the desired number of rays using a loop. Each ray is rotated accordingly so that they're evenly dispersed around the circle. The function `createSunburst(8)` is then called to create a sunburst with 8 rays.
<|end|>


