Create a C++ program to calculate Fibonacci numbers. The program should take an integer as an input and print out the first n Fibonacci numbers of the given integer.
7
<|end|>
<|asst|>
```cpp
#include <iostream>
using namespace std;

void printFibonacci(int n){    
    int t1 = 0, t2 = 1, nextTerm = 0;

    for (int i = 1; i <= n; ++i)
    {
        // Prints the first two terms.
        if(i == 1)
        {
            cout << " " << t1;
            continue;
        }
        if(i == 2)
        {
            cout << t2 << " ";
            continue;
        }
        nextTerm = t1 + t2;
        t1 = t2;
        t2 = nextTerm;
        
        cout << nextTerm << " ";
    }
}

int main(){
    int n;
    cout << "Enter the number of terms: ";
    cin >> n;
    
    printFibonacci(n);
    return 0;
}
```
This program will calculate the required Fibonacci numbers. Here `t1` and `t2` are used to store the last two terms of the series. `nextTerm` stores the next term in the series. For a number `n`, we loop from 1 to `n` and print `nextTerm` for the Fibonacci series in each iteration.
<|end|>


