Here is a simple Java code to find the maximum value in an array.

```java
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[] arr = { 8, 9, 5, 3, 17, 4 };
        
        int max = arr[0]; // assuming the first number in array is the largest initially

        for(int i=1;i<arr.length;i++)
        {
            // if any number in array is greater than max, replace max with that number
            if(arr[i] > max)
            {
               max = arr[i];
            }
        }
        // print out the maximum value
        System.out.println("Maximum value in the array is: " + max);
    }
}
```

This Java program starts by assuming the first element of the array is the maximum. Then, iterate through the array, each time finding a higher number than current maximum, it replaces the current max with that higher number. After the iteration finishes, we end up with max having the maximum value in the array.
