I have a gridview that is within an updatepanel for a modal popup I have on a page.
The issue is that the entire page refreshes every time I click an imagebutton that is within my gridview. This causes my entire page to load and since I have grayed out the rest of the page so that the user cannot click on it this is very annoying.

Does any one know what I am missing.  

 I entered a better solution at the bottom
<|end|>
<|asst|>
It seems like your ImageButton is causing a full postback, which you ideally want to avoid. You should make sure that your ImageButton is performing an asynchronous postback instead. This can be achieved in the .NET framework using `UpdatePanels`.

Here is an example of how you can setup your UpdatePanel and your ImageButton to update asynchronously:

```ASP.NET
<asp:ScriptManager ID="ScriptManager1" runat="server" />
<asp:UpdatePanel ID="UpdatePanel1" runat="server" UpdateMode="Conditional">
  <ContentTemplate>
    <asp:GridView ID="GridView1" runat="server">
      <!-- Your GridView definition here -->
    </asp:GridView>
  </ContentTemplate>
  <Triggers>
    <asp:AsyncPostBackTrigger ControlID="YourImageButtonID" EventName="Click" />
  </Triggers>
</asp:UpdatePanel>
```

In this example, replace `YourImageButtonID` with the actual ID of your ImageButton. With this setup, when you click the ImageButton, only the GridView inside the UpdatePanel will update and the rest of the page will remain as it is. 

Please note that the `ScriptManager` control should be added only once per page, preferably at the top.

Note: AsyncPostBackTrigger only works with a server control that is inside or outside an UpdatePanel control. For other controls you can use PostBackTrigger.

If your ImageButton is inside a templated control like a GridView or a Repeater, you might need to register the ImageButton to trigger asynchronous postbacks manually from code-behind:

```C#
ScriptManager scriptManager = ScriptManager.GetCurrent(this.Page);
scriptManager.RegisterAsyncPostBackControl(yourImageButton);
```
<|end|>


