What is the best way to make a delphi application (delphi 2007 for win32 here) go completely full screen, removing the application border and covering windows task bar ?

I am looking for something similar to what IE does when you hit F11.

I wish this to be a run time option for the user not a design time decision by my good self.

As Mentioned in the accepted answer 


BorderStyle := bsNone;



was part of the way to do it.  Strangely I kept getting a `E2010 Incompatible types: 'TFormBorderStyle' and 'TBackGroundSymbol'` error when using that line (another type had `bsNone` defined).

To overcome this I had to use : 


BorderStyle := Forms.bsNone;
<|end|>
<|asst|>
You can set `BorderStyle := bsNone;` and `WindowState := wsMaximized;` to make your form go full screen.

`bsNone` will remove the borders of the form and `wsMaximized` will maximize your form. This combination will give you full screen mode.

To cover up the task bar, you can get the screen dimensions using `Screen.Width` and `Screen.Height` and set your form’s height and width accordingly.

You can then use the form's `OnKeyDown` event to catch when the user presses F11 and toggle between full screen and normal mode like this:

```pascal
procedure TForm1.FormKeyDown(Sender: TObject; var Key: Word;
  Shift: TShiftState);
begin
  if Key = VK_F11 then
  begin
    if BorderStyle = bsNone then
    begin
      BorderStyle := bsSizeable;
      WindowState := wsNormal;
    end
    else
    begin
      BorderStyle := bsNone;
      WindowState := wsMaximized;
    end;
  end;
end;
```
Remember to include `Windows` in your unit's uses clause to get the definition of `VK_F11`.

Also, you might want to store away the form's previous size, position, and window state before going full screen so you can restore them when the user wants to exit full screen.
<|end|>


