<|asst|>
Yes, it is possible. Python has built-in methods to convert a string to different cases. Here is a very basic example:

```python
def convert_case(original_string, target_case):
    if target_case == 'upper':
        return original_string.upper()
    elif target_case == 'lower':
        return original_string.lower()
    elif target_case == 'title':
        return original_string.title()
    else:
        return "Invalid target case"
    
# Test the function
print(convert_case("Hello, World!", 'lower'))  # Output: hello, world!
print(convert_case("Hello, World!", 'upper'))  # Output: HELLO, WORLD!
print(convert_case("Hello, World!", 'title'))  # Output: Hello, World!
```

In this example, the `upper()` method converts all characters in a string to upper case, the `lower()` method converts them to lower case, and the `title()` method converts the first character of each word to upper case and the rest to lower case.
