When using craco, I wonder if the existing configuration file is overwritten or added to the existing options?

//craco.config.ts

module.exports = {
    babel: {
      presets: ["@emotion/babel-preset-css-prop"]
    },
};
<|end|>
<|asst|>
When using craco, the existing configuration isn't completely overwritten. Instead, craco extends the base Webpack, Babel, ESLint, etc. configurations provided by 'create-react-app' and allows you to customize them. 

In your example, you are extending the Babel configuration to include a new preset "@emotion/babel-preset-css-prop". This doesn't overwrite the existing Babel configuration, but adds on to it. Hence, the preset will work in conjunction with the existing Babel presets set by 'create-react-app', rather than replacing them.
<|end|>


