The SVG, as a vector graphic format, can directly apply a radial blur effect like a raster image format like jpg or png can. However, SVG does have filters you can use to create similar visual effects.

You can use SVG blur filter in conjunction with other effects to create an illusion of radial blur. Here is an example of an approach using `feGaussianBlur` and `feOffset` to create an impression of radial blur:

