Develop an HTML structurally ordered list (use unordered list if not specified) from the given JSON object containing data on color types.
info = {
    "listItems": ["Red", "Green", "Blue"], 
    "listTitle": "Colors"
}
<|end|>
<|asst|>
We can create an HTML structurally ordered list using JavaScript to parse the JSON object and dynamically create the HTML. For this, we need an HTML container where we can insert our created elements.

HTML:
```html
<!doctype html>
<html>
<head>
    
</head>
<body>
    <div id="content"></div>

    <script src="json_to_list.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
```

json_to_list.js (JavaScript file):
```javascript
// Your given JSON object
var info = {
    "listItems": ["Red", "Green", "Blue"], 
    "listTitle": "Colors"
}

// Get the HTML container where we will place our list
var content = document.getElementById('content');

// Create the list title
var h1 = document.createElement('h1');
h1.innerText = info.listTitle;
content.appendChild(h1);

// Create the ordered list
var ol = document.createElement('ol');

// For each item in the JSON array, create a new list item and add it to the ordered list
info.listItems.forEach(function(item) {
    var li = document.createElement('li');
    li.innerText = item;
    ol.appendChild(li);
});

content.appendChild(ol);
```
This code first accesses the div with the id 'content'. We will then create dynamic HTML elements, add the relevant information to these elements and then add these to our content div. 

The 'h1' element is created to hold the listTitle from our JSON object. The ordered list (ol) is then created and for each listItem, we create a new list item (li), add the text from the listItem and append it to our ordered list. Finally, the ordered list is added to our content div.

This program will output an HTML document containing a header with the text 'Colors' and an ordered list with the items 'Red', 'Green', and 'Blue'.
