result = list(filter(find_odd, number_list))

print(result)
```
When you run this code, it inspects each number in the number_list. If a number is odd (number % 2 is not equal to 0), it includes it in the resulting list. The result list will contain all the odd numbers from the input list, which are [3, 7] in this case.
