```cpp
#include<iostream>
#include<string>
using namespace std;

string change_base(int x,int base){
    string result = "";
    int	divisor, remainder;
    while(x > 0){
        divisor = x / base;
        remainder = x - base * divisor;
        result = to_string(remainder) + result; // Add the remainder to the beginning of the result
        x = divisor;
    }
    return result;
}

int main() {
    cout << "Change 8 to base 3: "  << change_base(8, 3) << endl;
    cout << "Change 8 to base 2: "  << change_base(8, 2) << endl;
    cout << "Change 7 to base 2: "  << change_base(7, 2) << endl;
    return 0;
}
```

This code functions by dividing the input number "x" by the desired "base", retaining the remainder and adding it to the output string "result". It then updates "x" as the new quotient and repeats the process until "x" is less than or equal to 0. The result string represents the input number expressed in the chosen base.

Note: Don't forget to import the `iostream` library, which is necessary for input/output operations in C++.
