```python
def check_string(string):
    # Check if string only contains digits
    if string.isdigit():
        # Check if string has minimum length of 3
        if len(string) >= 3:
            print("The string is valid.")
        else:
            print("The string is not valid. It is less than 3 characters long.")
    else:
        print("The string is not valid. It contains non-digit characters.")

# Test the function
check_string("12345")
```

When this function runs, it first checks if the input string contains only digits using the `isdigit()` method. If this is true, it then checks if the length of the string is at least 3 using the `len()` function. If both conditions are met, the function prints "The string is valid." If either condition is not met, the function prints an appropriate error message.
