Python code can be used to generate a Fibonacci sequence and plot the generated sequence using matplotlib. 

```python
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt

# Fibonacci sequence generation
def generate_fibonacci(n_terms):
    fibonacci_seq = [0, 1]
    while len(fibonacci_seq) < n_terms:
        fibonacci_seq.append(fibonacci_seq[-1] + fibonacci_seq[-2])
    return fibonacci_seq

# Plotting function
def plot_fibonacci(fibonacci_seq):
    plt.figure()
    plt.plot(fibonacci_seq, 'o-')
    plt.title('Fibonacci Sequence')
    plt.xlabel('Index')
    plt.ylabel('Value')
    plt.grid(True)
    plt.show()

# Generate and plot the Fibonacci sequence
fibonacci_seq = generate_fibonacci(10)
plot_fibonacci(fibonacci_seq)
```

To run the script you must have Python installed on your machine with matplotlib and NumPy.

This script first creates a function `generate_fibonacci` that takes an integer argument `n_terms` (the number of terms in the sequence) and generates the number of terms in the Fibonacci sequence. 

Then, the function `plot_fibonacci` is defined to create a line plot of the Fibonacci sequence using matplotlib. 

The script then calls these two functions to first generate first 10 terms of the Fibonacci sequence and then plot them. The resulting plot has the index of the Fibonacci sequence on the x-axis and the value of the Fibonacci term on the y-axis.
