<|asst|>
Designing a fully-fledged text-based dungeon crawler game as described in the problem within this space would not fit since it should be reasonably complex and large. However, we will give a simplified example to illustrate how one can start building a game like this in Python. This example only introduces the basic structure without the implementation of save/load, AI-controlled enemies. You can then build upon this structure to create a more complex and complete game.

```python
class Character:
    def __init__(self, name, health):
        self.name = name
        self.health = health
    
    def take_damage(self, damage):
        self.health -= damage
        if self.health <= 0:
            self.die()

    def die(self):
        print(f"{self.name} has died..")


class Player(Character):
    def __init__(self, name, health, damage):
        super().__init__(name, health)
        self.damage = damage

    def attack(self, enemy):
        print(f"{self.name} attacks {enemy.name} for {self.damage} damage!")
        enemy.take_damage(self.damage)


class Enemy(Character):
    def __init__(self, name, health, damage):
        super().__init__(name, health)
        self.damage = damage

    def attack(self, player):
        print(f"{self.name} attacks {player.name} for {self.damage} damage!")
        player.take_damage(self.damage)


class Game:
    def __init__(self, player, enemy):
        self.player = player
        self.enemy = enemy
        
    def combat(self):
        while self.player.health > 0 and self.enemy.health > 0:
            self.player.attack(self.enemy)
            if (self.enemy.health > 0):
                self.enemy.attack(self.player)


player = Player("Hero", 100, 20)
enemy = Enemy("Ogre", 50, 10)
game = Game(player, enemy)
game.combat()
```

Please run this on your local machine as it may not function in this environment.

To create enemies with AI, you can make different subclasses of the Enemy class and override their attack method with different tactics. For save/load functionality, you can convert the character object into a string, save it to a file, and later fetch it and convert it back into an object. Tests need to be done to ensure unexpected inputs and conditions are managed.
<|end|>


