The code you have appears to be correct and should output 'Greetings, Earth' assuming the Document Object Model (DOM) is available (i.e., running in a browser environment). However, using 'document.write' is generally considered to be a bad practice because it directly writes to the HTML document and can overwrite existing data.

Here's a more modern JavaScript version using 'console.log' instead:

```javascript
function greetPlanet() {
   console.log('Greetings, Earth');
}
