```javascript
function greetPlanet() {
  let greeting = document.getElementById('greeting');
  greeting.innerText = 'Greetings, Earth';
}
```
This requires an HTML element with the id 'greeting' to exist in your HTML.

JavaScript does not typically have syntax issues unless it is not well-formed, or if you're attempting to use ES6+ functionality in an environment that only supports ES5 or lower.
