I'm using a Visual Studio web setup project to install an application that extends the functionality of Project Server. I want to call a method from the PSI ( Project Server Interface ) from one of the custom actions of my setup project, but every time a get a "401 Unauthorized access" error. What should I do to be able to access the PSI? The same code, when used from a Console Application, works without any issues.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Accessing the PSI from a setup project is different from accessing it from a console application because the setup project runs under the SYSTEM account rather than a user account. This is a security feature and attempting to access the PSI from such an elevated account is likely the cause of your "401 Unauthorized access" error.

There are a few things you can try to resolve this issue:

1. Execute code as another user: You can change the identity under which your code is running to a user who has the necessary permissions to access the service.

2. Use Impersonation: Impersonation allows your code to run under a different identity temporarily. This is a common way to deal with such an issue, but might not be suitable for all scenarios.

3. Network Service Account: You could try to change the application pool for your Project Server web application in IIS to run as Network Service account.

Remember to keep in mind the security implications of each method. It is not recommended to store sensitive information like usernames and passwords in your code. If you decide to store such information, make sure it is encrypted and stored securely.
 
Finally, be sure the account you are using has the necessary permissions to access the PSI.
<|end|>


