You are required to construct an interactive HTML interface that also utilizes JavaScript and CSS, and is capable of error handling. It should comprise three data entry fields, specifically: Personal Identifier (Name), Chronological Age demarcation (Age), and Electronic Mailing Address (Email). 

In addition, you must implement JavaScript functions: 
1) To validate that the Name only contains alphabets and space (no special characters or numbers), 
2) Age is a positive number and within the range of valid human age (0-120), and 
3) Email is in a correct format. 

Upon submission, if any validation fails, display an error message next to the respective field mentioning the issue and do not allow the form to be submitted.

Moreover, using CSS, ensure that the interface is responsive and has an intuitive UI/UX design.

Below is an erroneous code for reference:

```
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<body>

<form action="/submit.php">
  Name: <input type="text" name="Name"><br>
  Age: <input type="text" name="Age"><br>
  E-mail: <input type="text" name="Email"><br>
</form> 

</body>
</html>
```
Explain why this code is flawed and cannot fulfill the criteria mentioned above. Then, provide a corrected version of the code along with the JavaScript validation functions and CSS for responsiveness.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
The given code is erroneous because of the following reasons:
1. There's no validation on the entries of the form. It won't check if the entries match the requirements specified by the problem.
2. It lacks the error messages that are supposed to be displayed upon invalid form submission.
3. It doesn't prevent submission of the form if entries are invalid.
4. It's not styled for responsiveness.
5. It doesn't have JavaScript implemented to handle the form's error checking or submission.
6. It's not user friendly and lacks basic UI/UX design principles. 

Here's a correct version of the code with JavaScript validation functions and the respective CSS:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <style>
    input[type=text] {
        width: 100%;
        padding: 12px 20px;
        margin: 8px 0;
        box-sizing: border-box;
        border-radius: 4px;
    }
    .error {
        color: red;
        margin-left: 5px;
    }
    @media only screen and (max-width: 600px) {
        input[type=text] {
            width: 100%;
        }
    }
  </style>
  <script>
    function validateForm() {
        var valid = true;
        var name = document.forms["myForm"]["Name"].value;
        var age = document.forms["myForm"]["Age"].value;
        var email = document.forms["myForm"]["Email"].value;

        const nameReg = /^[a-z ,.'-]+$/i;
        const emailReg = /^([\w-\.]+@([\w-]+\.)+[\w-]{2,4})?$/;

        document.getElementById("errorName").innerHTML = "";
        document.getElementById("errorAge").innerHTML = "";
        document.getElementById("errorEmail").innerHTML = "";

        if (!nameReg.test(name)) {
            document.getElementById("errorName").innerHTML = "Error: Name can only contains alphabets and spaces.";
            valid = false;
        }
        if (age < 0 || age > 120) {
            document.getElementById("errorAge").innerHTML = "Error: Invalid age input.";
            valid = false;
        }

        if (!emailReg.test(email)) {
            document.getElementById("errorEmail").innerHTML = "Error: Invalid email input.";
            valid = false;
        }

        return valid;
    }
  </script>
</head>
<body>
  <form name="myForm" action="/submit.php" onsubmit="return validateForm()">
    Name: <input type="text" name="Name"> <span id="errorName" class="error"></span><br>
    Age: <input type="text" name="Age"> <span id="errorAge" class="error"></span><br>
    E-mail: <input type="text" name="Email"> <span id="errorEmail" class="error"></span><br>
    <input type="submit" value="Submit">
  </form> 
</body>
</html>
```

In the above code: 

The CSS ensures that the interface is responsive. It applies styles to input elements and creates a responsive design for smaller screens. 

The JavaScript part is the validation functions with the help of RegEx patterns. The `validateForm()` function is called whenever the form is submitted. If any of the input fields fails its validation, an error message is displayed, the form submission is prevented by returning `valid = false` and the user is required to fix the error to successfully submit the form.
<|end|>


