<|asst|>
Windows Communication Foundation (WCF) is a framework developed by Microsoft for building service-oriented applications. It allows developers to create methods that can be remotely called over any network and any device. This means, you can send data as asynchronous from one service point to another, which can be locally on the same system or over the Internet. The services can then be consumed by clients or applications which need those data. It essentially helps in exchanging data between different services in a secure and reliable way.
