1. Image Preprocessing:
    The first step is data preprocessing. All images should be resized to the same dimension, grayscale applied to remove color and reduce computational intensity, noise removal if necessary, and applying other image processing techniques for better results.

2. Feature Extraction:
    This step involves extracting the most important details from each image that will help in distinguishing between different types of clothing. You can use techniques like Histogram of Oriented Gradients (HOG), Gray-level Co-occurrence matrix (GLCM), etc.

3. Define a Classification Model:
    This is the step where we use a machine learning model to train on our data. Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs) are popular for image classification tasks. Split the preprocessed dataset into a training set (about 70-80%) and a testing set (about 20-30%).

4. Training the Model:
    Feed the training data (images and their labels) to the model and let it learn the features of different types of clothes. You can use transfer learning with pre-trained models like VGG16, ResNet, etc. to make the learning process efficient.

5. Model Evaluation:
    Once the model is trained, evaluate its performance on the testing set. Calculate metrics like accuracy, precision, recall, F1-score, etc. to determine how accurately the model can classify images into different types of clothes.

6. Optimization:
    Depending on the performance on the testing set, you might need to debug and optimize the model by adjusting its hyperparameters, trying other models, or adding more data to the training set.

7. Prediction:
    After achieving satisfactory accuracy, use this model to classify new clothes images. The model will output the type of clothing by analyzing the features of the input image.

The overall idea is to use machine learning and especially deep learning techniques to perform image classification on clothing items. Note that the machine learning model would require lots of images of different types of clothes for training to be able to classify correctly.

