in latex how to make a figure with a caption fill exactly the page height without rescaling the caption? can I insert the boxO instead of repeating the content of the caption?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
You can make a figure fill exactly the page height using the adjustbox package. For the caption, you can box it separately. By using the "measuredfigure" environment, you can measure the size of the caption box and exclude it from the height of the figure. 

First, include in your preamble:

```latex
\usepackage{adjustbox}
\usepackage{calc}
\usepackage{caption}

\newsavebox{\captionbox} % to save the boxed caption
\newenvironment{measuredfigure}[1][t]
  {\begin{figure}[#1]}
  {\end{figure}\par\addvspace{.5\baselineskip}} % standard spacing below the figure
```

Then, in your document:
```latex
\begin{measuredfigure}
\savebox{\captionbox}{%
  \parbox{\textwidth}{\caption{Caption text goes here.}}%
}
\usebox{\captionbox} % prints the caption
\vskip\abovecaptionskip % standard spacing above the figure
\begin{adjustbox}{valign=t,raise=\ht\captionbox+\abovecaptionskip,minipage=[t][\textheight-\ht\captionbox-2\abovecaptionskip]{\linewidth}}
\includegraphics[width=\linewidth,height=\textheight-\ht\captionbox-2\abovecaptionskip,keepaspectratio]{filename}% image file
\end{adjustbox}
\end{measuredfigure}
```

You can replace `\abovecaptionskip` with your desired spacing, measured in points (a point is 1/72 inch). If you want the spacing in millimeters, you can use the calculation symbol "\valign", for example, `raise=\ht\captionbox+\valign{5mm}`.

This snippet creates a new savebox `\captionbox` and an environment `measuredfigure` that measures the size of the caption box and adjust the size of the image correspondingly. You input the caption text in the `\parbox` command, and the filename in the `\includegraphics`. You can also adjust the width of the image by replacing `\linewidth` with a specific width in `\includegraphics`. The height of the image is automatically adjusted to fill the remaining space, preserving the aspect ratio of the image.
<|end|>


