Below is the translation of the Python code to C#, using `AmazonLambdaClient` from `Amazon.Lambda` namespace from the AWS SDK for .NET. Please note that the `IsFunctionIdle` method is pseudo code because it will depend on your criteria for an idle function.

Please ensure that the AWS SDK for .NET is installed. The easiest way to do this is via the NuGet package manager in Visual Studio.

In C#, error handling is done using `try-catch` blocks similar to Python. AWS Service exceptions are caught accordingly.

```csharp
using Amazon;
using Amazon.Lambda;
using Amazon.Lambda.Model;
using System;
using System.Threading.Tasks;

class Program {

    static async Task Main(string[] args) {
        
        // Creating the Amazon Lambda client using AWS region
        var lambdaClient = new AmazonLambdaClient(RegionEndpoint.USWest2);

        try {
            // Fetching the list of all functions in the specified region
            var listResponse = await lambdaClient.ListFunctionsAsync(new ListFunctionsRequest());

            // Looping through each function
            foreach (var function in listResponse.Functions) {
                var functionName = function.FunctionName;

                // Here, we need to determine if the function is idle
                // If the function is idle, we delete it
                // Please replace `IsFunctionIdle` with your actual check
                if (IsFunctionIdle(function)) {
                    await lambdaClient.DeleteFunctionAsync(new DeleteFunctionRequest {
                        FunctionName = functionName
                    });
                    Console.WriteLine($"Deleted function: {functionName}");
                }
            }

        } catch (AmazonLambdaException ex) {
            // Catching specific AWS Service Exceptions
            if (ex.ErrorCode == "ResourceNotFoundException") {
                Console.WriteLine("The specified lambda function does not exist.");
            } else if (ex.ErrorCode == "NoCredentialsError") {
                Console.WriteLine("No AWS credentials were found.");
            } else {
                throw;
            }
        }
    }

    // Pseudo code for determining idle function. Replace with your logic.
    private static bool IsFunctionIdle(FunctionConfiguration function) {
        // Replace with your actual logic to check if the function is idle
        return false;
    }
}
```
Remember that evaluating whether a Lambda function is idle or not will depend on your specific need/criteria.
