<|asst|>
Here's the corrected code snippet:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
  <head>
    <title>Contact Information</title>
    <style>
      .contact {
        font-family: Arial;
      }
      .title {
        font-weight: bold;
        margin-bottom: 10px;
      }
      .info p {
        margin: 0;
      }
    </style>
    <script>
      function validate() {
        var age = document.getElementById('age');
        var phone = document.getElementById('phone');
        var email = document.getElementById('email');

        if (age.value < 0 || age.value > 120) {
          age.style.border = '1px solid red';
          return false;
        } else {
          age.style.border = '1px solid green';
        }

        var phonePattern = /^(\+\d{1,2}\s)?(\(\d{3}\))[-. ]?(\d{3})[-. ]?(\d{4})$/;
        if (!phone.value.match(phonePattern)) {
          phone.style.border = '1px solid red';
          return false;
        } else {
          phone.style.border = '1px solid green';
        }

        var emailPattern = /^\S+@\w+(\.\w+)+$/;
        if (!email.value.match(emailPattern)) {
          email.style.border = '1px solid red';
          return false;
        } else {
          email.style.border = '1px solid green';
        }

        return true;
      }
    </script>
  </head>
  <body>
    <div class="contact">
      <div class="title">Contact Information</div>
      <div class="info">
        <p>Name: <input type="text" id="name" value="John Doe;" /></p>
        <p>Age: <input type="number" id="age" value="46" /></p>
        <p>Phone: <input type="text" id="phone" value="+1 (312) 555-4879" /></p>
        <p>Email: <input type="text" id="email" value="john.doe@example.com" /></p>
        <button onclick="return validate()">Validate</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
```
Changes Made:

1) Corrected `document.getElementYId` to `document.getElementById`.

2) Corrected phone regular expression to make "+1 " part optional.

3) Corrected email regular expression to match emails containing multiple periods.

4) Inputs for Name, Age, Phone and Email are reorganized to visually impose data prescriptiveness.

5) `validate` function now returns `true` if all fields are valid to indicate successful validation.

6) `return` statement added before onclick event in validate button to prevent form submission when validation fails.
