- We know that division by zero is undefined in mathematics, so it will throw an `ArithmeticException`.
- We catch this exception in the catch block and print a user-friendly message to notify that there's an error.
- The `finally` block is optional and it generally contains the code that must run whether an exception is thrown or not.
