def printPascal(n): 

    arr = [[0 for x in range(n+1)] 
              for y in range(n+1)]  
  
    for line in range (0, n+1): 
  
        for i in range (0, line + 1): 
  
            if(i is 0 or i is line): 
                arr[line][i] = 1
            else: 
                arr[line][i] = (arr[line-1][i-1] + arr[line-1][i]) 
            print(arr[line][i], end = " ")            
        print("\n", end = "") 

n = 5
printPascal(n)
```

In this program, the function `printPascal(n)` is defined which prints the nth line of Pascal's Triangle. The 2D array `arr` is initialized with all elements as 0. The outer for loop runs `n+1` times which is the number of lines upto which we want to print. The inner for loop runs `line+1` times where `line` is the current line number. The elements at first and last position in a line are always 1. Other than these positions, the current element is the sum of the elements just above and left of the above element from the previous line. In the end of every line, newline is printed to move to next line. Last 5th line is `1 4 6 4 1` according to the implementation of Pascal Triangle.
