Implementing a serverless application using AWS Lambda and API Gateway can be accomplished by performing the following steps:

Step 1: First, create a Python function for AWS Lambda.

```python
def lambda_handler(event, context):
    # Run your function code here
    return {
        'statusCode': 200,
        'body': 'Hello, world!'
    }
```

Step 2: Configure AWS Lambda service
Go to AWS Management Console > Select Lambda from services > Click on "Create function" > Author from scratch > Give the function a name and a role, then Create function > On next page, insert your Python function code into the Function code section.

Step 3: Prepare API Gateway
Go back to AWS Management Console > Select API Gateway > Create API > REST API (Build) > Build > Settings (Create New API) > API name and description > Create API > Actions > Create Method > GET > Tick Lambda Function, Use Lambda Proxy Integration > write Lambda Function name > Save.

Step 4: Allow API Gateway to access the Lambda function
Go back to Lambda API > Configuration > Add trigger > API Gateway > Type API name, Deployment stage, Security > Add.

Step 5: Deploy your API
Go back to API Gateway Management > Select API name > Actions > Deploy API > Selector Deployment stage > Deploy.

Step 6: Test API
After deploying, you will get an Invoke URL. If you open this URL in your browser, you will see the response body.

