Below is the XML schema (XSD) based on your requirements:

```xml
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<xs:schema xmlns:xs="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
    <xs:element name="Person">
        <xs:complexType>
            <xs:sequence>
                <xs:element name="Name" type="xs:string"/>
                <xs:element name="Age" type="xs:integer"/>
                <xs:element name="City" type="xs:string"/>
            </xs:sequence>
        </xs:complexType>
    </xs:element>
</xs:schema>
```

The above schema defines three elements: Name (of type string), Age (of type integer), and City (of type string). All these elements are encapsulated within the "Person" tag in the sequence order.

And then, the XML instance document that would comply with the above schema may look something like this:

```xml
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Person xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="person.xsd">
    <Name>Maria</Name>
    <Age>46</Age>
    <City>San Francisco</City>
</Person>
