Develop a coding solution that takes a provided message as input and outputs the text in the reverse order. Utilize "Hello World!" as the test string.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here is a simple Python solution:

```python
def reverse_text(text):
    return text[::-1]

print(reverse_text("Hello World!"))
```

This will output: "!dlroW olleH"

The key part of this program is the slicing operation "text[::-1]". The slicing syntax in Python is [start:stop:step], so by leaving start and stop blank and making step -1, it steps through the string from end to start, effectively reversing it.
<|end|>


