I need a translation of this code in Java:
import (
    "sort"
    "strconv"
)

func hasEvenDigit(num int) bool {
    str := strconv.Itoa(num)
    for i := 0; i < len(str); i++ {
        digit, _ := strconv.Atoi(string(str[i]))
        if digit%2 == 0 {
            return true
        }
    }
    return false
}

func UniqueDigits(x []int) []int {
    nums := make([]int, 0, len(x))
    for _, num := range x {
        if !hasEvenDigit(num) {
            nums = append(nums, num)
        }
    }
    sort.Ints(nums)
    return nums
}
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here's how you can translate the code to Java:

```java
import java.util.*;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Integer[] x = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 99, 100};
        ArrayList<Integer> nums = new ArrayList<>(Arrays.asList(x));
        System.out.println(UniqueDigits(nums));
    }

    public static boolean hasEvenDigit(int num) {
        String str = Integer.toString(num);
        for (int i = 0; i < str.length(); i++) {
            int digit = Integer.parseInt(Character.toString(str.charAt(i)));
            if (digit % 2 == 0) {
                return true;
            }
        }
        return false;
    }

    public static ArrayList<Integer> UniqueDigits(ArrayList<Integer> x) {
        ArrayList<Integer> nums = new ArrayList<>();
        for (int num : x) {
            if (!hasEvenDigit(num)) {
                nums.add(num);
            }
        }
        Collections.sort(nums);
        return nums;
    }
}
```

In Java, you'll have to begin by defining a class (here called `Main`). I've also included an example usage in a `main` method, which you can adapt as needed. 

The function `UniqueDigits` was slightly adapted, because Java doesn't handle arrays in quite the same way as Go. It's been adjusted to take in an `ArrayList<Integer>` instead, which functions similarly to a Go slice. 

Lastly, for the `hasEvenDigit` function, we use `Integer.toString` to convert the integer to a string and `Integer.parseInt` to convert the string back to an integer. In the `UniqueDigits` function, `ArrayList<Integer>` is used to create a dynamic array (like Go's slice) and `Collections.sort(nums)` is used for sorting the ArrayList.
