Formulate a JavaScript code snippet that generates a random whole number within the bounded arithmetic spectrum from 0 to 100.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here is a simple JavaScript code snippet that generates a random whole number between 0 and 100:

```javascript
var randomNum = Math.floor(Math.random() * 101);
console.log(randomNum);
```

In this code, Math.random() method will return a random decimal number between 0(inclusive) to 1(exclusive). We then multiply this number by 101 to shift this decimal range to 0-100.99. We use Math.floor() to round down this decimal, thus ensuring the result is a whole number from 0 to 100. 

Note: The Math.random() method will never actually return exactly 1, so the maximum random number produced by this code will be 100.
<|end|>


