I want to be able to capture the exception that is thrown when a user requests a non-existent controller and re-direct it to a 404 page. How can I do this?

For example, the user requests `http://www.nosite.com/paeges/1` ( `/pages/`). How do I make it so they get re-directed to the 404 rather than the exception screen?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
This functionality can be built into any project using the .NET MVC framework through the use of the customErrors and httpErrors settings in the web.config file.

In older versions of MVC, you can catch the Http 404 error in your web.config file and redirect it to a custom "Page Not Found" page. Following is the code snippet:

```xml
<customErrors mode="On" defaultRedirect="~/Error">
   <error statusCode="404" redirect="~/Error/NotFound" />
</customErrors>
```

In `~/Error/NotFound` the "Error" is the controller and "NotFound" is the action. You should have this controller and action in your project to handle the 404 error. 

For newer versions (IIS 7 and above), the httpErrors element would be used (and would be more accurate). 

```xml
<system.webServer>
   <httpErrors errorMode="Custom" existingResponse="Replace">
      <remove statusCode="404"/>
      <error statusCode="404" path="/Error/NotFound" responseMode="ExecuteURL"/>
   </httpErrors>
</system.webServer>
```

You should also configure your application to redirect any unhandled exceptions to a custom error page. This can be done in the `Application_Error` method in the `Global.asax.cs` file.

```csharp
protected void Application_Error(object sender, EventArgs e)
{
    Exception exception = Server.GetLastError();
    // Log the exception.

    Server.ClearError();

    Response.Redirect("/Error");
}
```

This will catch any unhandled exceptions and redirect the user to a custom error page. Again, make sure you have this "Error" controller and corresponding action in your project.
  
Remember to remove the `httpErrors` or `customErrors` settings from `system.web` if you are using `system.webServer`, as they can override each other.
<|end|>


