Write a SQL query to get the details of all Customers from the database, also include a calculated field that shows how many days since their first purchase. If no purchase has been made, return -1. Make sure to handle null values appropriately.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Assuming we have a table Customers with the fields: CustomerID, FirstName, LastName, and FirstPurchaseDate.

Also, note that syntax may vary a little between different SQL database systems.

``` SQL
SELECT 
    CustomerID, 
    FirstName, 
    LastName, 
    FirstPurchaseDate,
    CASE
        WHEN FirstPurchaseDate IS NULL THEN -1
        ELSE DATEDIFF(DAY, FirstPurchaseDate, GETDATE())
    END AS DaysSinceFirstPurchase
FROM Customers
```

In this SQL query, we're selecting all data from the Customers table and adding a new field `DaysSinceFirstPurchase`. If `FirstPurchaseDate` is NULL, i.e. the customer hasn't made a purchase yet, we'll return `-1`. Otherwise, we calculate the difference between the current date (`GETDATE()`) and `FirstPurchaseDate` in days.

Please adjust according to your database schema and SQL dialect as necessary. In MySQL, you would use `CURDATE()` instead of `GETDATE()` and `DATEDIFF(current_date, FirstPurchaseDate)` as MySQL's DATEDIFF function only requires two arguments.
<|end|>


