Construct an HTML page which outputs the phrase "Hello World!" on the screen, simultaneously utilizing a typographical rendering of 8px for exhibiting examples. Apply a two-step operation: first, integrate the textual contents, and subsequently, adjust the font size for the examples.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here is how you can achieve this using HTML and CSS:

Step 1: Constructing the HTML structure with textual contents.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>Hello World Page</title>
</head>
<body>
    <p id="example">Hello World!</p>
</body>
</html>
```

Step 2: Adjusting the font size for the examples.

We can do this by adding internal CSS in the head section of our webpage:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>Hello World Page</title>
    <style>
        #example {
            font-size: 8px;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <p id="example">Hello World!</p>
</body>
</html>
```

Explanation:

In the first snippet, we establish a simple HTML document structure. There is a `p` element in the `body` which contains the text "Hello World!".

In the second snippet, I added a `style` element to the `head` section of the HTML. This style block contains CSS that applies to the element with the ID "example".  The CSS instructs the browser to render the text in that element at a font size of 8px.
