Develop a function to identify all the prime numbers in a given range.
Start: 5
End: 20
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Sure, here is a Python function that can do that.

```python
def find_prime_numbers(start, end):
    prime_numbers = []

    for num in range(start, end+1):
        if num > 1:
            for i in range(2, num):
                if (num % i) == 0:
                    break
            else:
                prime_numbers.append(num)

    return prime_numbers

print(find_prime_numbers(5, 20))
```

When you run this code, it will give you a list of prime numbers between 5 to 20. In this case, it will return [5, 7, 11, 13, 17, 19] as these all are the prime numbers between 5 and 20.
