Enhance the current advanced web coding script by adding a supplementary HTML5 input mechanism. Specifically, integrate a selection box that dynamically loads options from a provided JSON file via AJAX call. In addition, format the selection box with CSS to incorporate a cohesive and custom user interface design. 

The structure of the JSON file is as follows:
```
{
    "options": [
        {
            "text": "Option 1",
            "value": "1"
        },
        {
            "text": "Option 2",
            "value": "2"
        },
        // This list can be extended   
    ]
}
```

Your solution should not only include the scripts for the dynamic loading of selection box options, but should also manage potential load failure.

The HTML template is provided below, implement AJAX, CSS, and error management:
```html
<html>
<head>
    <title>Personalized Form</title>
</head>
<body>
    <form>
        <label for="Individual's Name">Name</label>
        <input type="text" id="Individual's Name">
        <!-- Your dynamic selection box should appear here ->   
    </form>
</body>
</html>
```
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here is a simple solution that uses XMLHTTPRequest to load the JSON file and populate the select box. It also includes some basic CSS for formatting and error handling in case the JSON fails to load:

```html
<html>
<head>
    <title>Personalized Form</title>
    <style>
        select {
            width: 200px;
            height: 30px;
            background-color: #fff;
            border-radius: 5px;
            border: 1px solid #ccc;
            padding: 5px;
            font-size: 14px;
        }
        .error {
            color: red;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <form>
        <label for="name">Name</label>
        <input type="text" id="name">
        <label for="dynamicSelect">Select Option</label>
        <select id="dynamicSelect"></select>
        <div id="error" class="error"></div>
    </form>
    <script>
        var xhr = new XMLHttpRequest();
        xhr.onreadystatechange = function() {
            if (this.readyState == 4 && this.status == 200) {
                var json = JSON.parse(this.responseText);
                var select = document.getElementById("dynamicSelect");
                for (var i = 0; i < json.options.length; i++) {
                    var option = document.createElement("option");
                    option.text = json.options[i].text;
                    option.value = json.options[i].value;
                    select.appendChild(option);
                }
            } else if (this.readyState == 4) {
                document.getElementById("error").innerHTML = "Failed to load options.";
            }
        };
        xhr.open("GET", "/path_to_your_json_file.json", true);
        xhr.send();
    </script>
</body>
</html>
```

Replace `/path_to_your_json_file.json` with the actual path to your JSON file. The CSS rule formats the select element to make it more visually appealing, and the JavaScript script loads the JSON file and populates the select box with the options from the file.
In the case where the JSON file fails to load, an error message will be displayed on the page. Please ensure that errors are handled more robustly in a production setting.
