Formulate a function using Java programming language that carries out a perpendicular clockwise rotation on a two-dimensional square matrix of dimension N x N. The function should not only conduct the rotation but also create a rotated copy of the original matrix without altering the initial one.

In addition, provide an erroneous piece of code and perform debugging on it. Address the identified bugs and explain why those errors might have arisen and how your corrections resolve those problems.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here is the Java function for the clockwise rotation of a square matrix:

```Java
public class MatrixRotation {
    public static int[][] rotateClockwise(int[][] matrix) {
        int n = matrix.length;
        int[][] rotatedMatrix = new int[n][n];

        for(int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            for(int j = 0; j < n; j++) {
                rotatedMatrix[j][n-i-1] = matrix[i][j];
            }
        }

        return rotatedMatrix;
    }
}
```

This function works by iterating over each element in the input matrix and placing it in the appropriate position in the rotated matrix.

Now, let's consider a piece of code with some bugs:

```Java
public class MatrixRotation {
    public static int[][] rotateClockwise(int[][] matrix) {
        int n = matrix.length;
        int[][] rotatedMatrix = new int[n][n];

        for(int i = 0; i <= n; i++) {
            for(int j = 0; j < n; j++) {
                rotatedMatrix[i][n-j-1] = matrix[i][j];
            }
        }

        return rotatedMatrix;
    }
}
```
This code will throw `ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException` due to two bugs:

1. The outer loop is iterating from 0 to n inclusive (`i <= n`), while it should iterate from 0 to n-1 inclusive. Array indexes in Java start from 0, so the maximum valid index for an array of length n is n-1.

2. In the inner loop, we are trying to assign a value to `rotatedMatrix[i][n-j-1]`, but it should be `rotatedMatrix[j][n-i-1]` according to the formula for clockwise rotation.

Here's the corrected code:

```Java
public class MatrixRotation {
    public static int[][] rotateClockwise(int[][] matrix) {
        int n = matrix.length;
        int[][] rotatedMatrix = new int[n][n];

        for(int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            for(int j = 0; j < n; j++) {
                rotatedMatrix[j][n-i-1] = matrix[i][j];
            }
        }

        return rotatedMatrix;
    }
}
```

In this corrected version, we ensure that the iteration is well within array bounds, and the formula used to access elements in the rotated matrix is the appropriate one for a clockwise rotation.
<|end|>


