An additional challenge is to work with the following piece of Swift code that is believed to cause certain issues while parsing the feed:

```
  if let url = URL(string: "https://www.nytimes.com/svc/collections/v1/publish/https://www.nytimes.com/section/world/rss.xml") {
    URLSession.shared.dataTask(with: url) { data, response, error in
        if let data = data {
            do {
                let rssItems = try NSXMLParser(data: data)
                // Display content
            } catch {
                print("Error: \(error.localizedDescription)")
            }
        }
    }.resume()
  }
```

Can you fix the problem in the above mentioned code and also demo your solution in a live environment? Do take into consideration scalability, efficient resource management and best coding principles.
