When you will run this code with string = "Hello World", start_index = 2, end_index = 5, the output will be "llo". 

This is because in python indexing starts from 0, so the character at position 2 is 'l' and the substring ends just before the end_index, so it will not include the character at the end_index which is a 'space in this string'.
