```java
import java.util.*;
import java.lang.*;

class Solution {
    /**
    Compare whether two discrete strings contain the same set of characters.
    >>> sameChars("eabcdzzzz", "dddzzzzzzzddeddabc")
    true
    >>> sameChars("abcd", "dddddddabc")
    true
    >>> sameChars("dddddddabc", "abcd")
    true
    >>> sameChars("eabcd", "dddddddabc")
    false
    >>> sameChars("abcd", "dddddddabce")
    false
    >>> sameChars("eabcdzzzz", "dddzzzzzzzddddabc")
    false
     */
    public boolean sameChars(String s0, String s1) { 
```
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here's the Java solution:

```java
    import java.util.*;
    import java.lang.*;

    class Solution {
        public boolean sameChars(String s0, String s1) {
            Set<Character> set0 = new HashSet<>();
            Set<Character> set1 = new HashSet<>();
            
            for(int i = 0; i < s0.length(); i++){
                set0.add(s0.charAt(i));
            }
            
            for(int i = 0; i < s1.length(); i++){
                set1.add(s1.charAt(i));
            }
            
            return set0.equals(set1);
        }

        public static void main(String[] args) {
            Solution solution = new Solution();
            System.out.println(solution.sameChars("eabcdzzzz", "dddzzzzzzzddeddabc")); //expected true
            System.out.println(solution.sameChars("abcd", "dddddddabc")); //expected true
            System.out.println(solution.sameChars("dddddddabc", "abcd")); //expected true
            System.out.println(solution.sameChars("eabcd", "dddddddabc")); //expected false
            System.out.println(solution.sameChars("abcd", "dddddddabce")); //expected false
            System.out.println(solution.sameChars("eabcdzzzz", "dddzzzzzzzddddabc")); //expected false
        }
    }
```

This solution works by creating a Set of characters for s0 and s1. A Set is a data structure that only contains distinct elements. When we add all chars from s0 and s1 to their respective Sets, no duplicate characters are added to each Set. Thus, the Set only contains the distinct characters from each string. By comparing if the two Sets are identical (i.e., contain the same characters), we can determine if s0 and s1 contain the same set of characters.
<|end|>


