<|asst|>
No, Visual Studio's built-in ASP.NET Development Server does not support HTTPS. 

If you need to test and develop with HTTPS, you may want to consider using IIS Express or the full version of IIS, as they both provide support for HTTPS. You might also need to configure an SSL certificate for your local development environment.

Alternatively, for Visual Studio 2019 or later, the built-in development environment uses Kestrel which supports HTTPS by default. You just need to ensure that the launchSettings.json in your .NET Core project is configured correctly.
<|end|>


