Below is an example of an HTML document with a Javascript script that fulfills your requirements.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>Click Counter</title>
    <script type="text/javascript">
        var clickCount = 0;
       
        function handleClick() {
            clickCount++;
            document.getElementById('clickCountDisplay').innerHTML = 'Click Count: ' + clickCount;

            if (clickCount >= 5) {
                document.getElementById('myButton').disabled = true;
            }
        }

        function resetClickCount() {
            clickCount = 0;
            document.getElementById('clickCountDisplay').innerHTML = 'Click Count: ' + clickCount;
            document.getElementById('myButton').disabled = false;
        }
    </script>
</head>
<body>
    <button id="myButton" onclick="handleClick()">Visit Google</button>
    <br/>
    <span id="clickCountDisplay">Click Count: 0</span>
    <br/>
    <button onclick="resetClickCount()">Reset Click Counter</button>
</body>
</html>
```

However, please note the following:

1. This script is purely frontend, meaning that a user can simply refresh the page to reset the click count. For more secure tracking of user clicks, you would need to implement server-side logic.

