<|user|>
Generate a function in PHP which will calculate the Median of an array of numbers.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Sure, here is a PHP function that calculates the median of an array of numbers:

```php
function median($array) {
    $count = count($array);
    sort($array);

    if ($count % 2 == 0) {
        $lower = $array[$count / 2 - 1];
        $higher = $array[$count / 2];
        $median = (($lower + $higher) / 2);
    } else {
        $median = $array[floor($count / 2)];
    }

    return $median;
}
```

This function works by first sorting the array. If the array's length is even, the median is the average of the two middle numbers, in which case it adds them up and divide by 2. If the length is odd, it simply returns the value at the middle index.
<|end|>


