<|asst|>
You can get and display the title using WooCommerce's built-in functions and hooks. 

Here is a simple PHP code snippet that gets the title of the product in the cart and displays it:

```php
add_action( 'woocommerce_before_checkout_form', 'show_product_title_in_cart', 10 );
function show_product_title_in_cart() {
    foreach( WC()->cart->get_cart() as $cart_item ) {
        $product = $cart_item['data'];
        if( $product ) {
            echo '<div class="product-title">' . $product->get_name() . '</div>';
        }
    }
}
```

You can add this code to your theme's `functions.php` file. If you are not sure on how to do that, consult with a professional.

This code calls the 'woocommerce_before_checkout_form' action hook, runs a loop for all the products in the cart, gets the product data, and, if the product exists, it echoes the product name.

For the positioning of the title, you may need to adjust the hook or the CSS. 

NOTE: Make sure to backup your site before implementing this code to prevent issues. Also making changes to theme files could be overwritten in a theme update, so consider creating a child theme if you have not done so already.
