Construct a Java-based code architecture to transpose the sequence of alphabets within individual lexemes. The particular string for consideration is: "Hello world of artificial intelligence".
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here's a basic Java approach to solve this problem:

This program will take individual words (lexemes) in the given sentence and then it will reverse/transpose the sequence of alphabets within each word. For transposed alphabet, it simply inverts/ reverses the word as a whole.

```java
class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        // Insert your sentence here
        String str = "Hello world of artificial intelligence";

        // Split the sentence into words
        String[] words = str.split(" ");

        // transpose each word
        for (int i = 0; i < words.length; i++) {
            words[i] = transposeWord(words[i]);
        }

        // Combine them back into a sentence
        str = String.join(" ", words);

        // Print the sentence
        System.out.println(str);
    }

    // Method to transpose a word
    public static String transposeWord(String word) {
        char[] chars = word.toCharArray();
        for(int i = 0; i < chars.length / 2; i++) {
            char temp = chars[i];
            chars[i] = chars[chars.length - i - 1];
            chars[chars.length - i - 1] = temp;
        }
        return new String(chars);
    }
}
```

When you run this code, the output will be:

```
olleH dlrow fo laicifitra ecnegilletni
```

Each word from the initial input string "Hello world of artificial intelligence" has been transposed.
<|end|>


