Given a long string of words separated by spaces and commas, write a program using JavaScript. Your program should convert this string into a 2-dimensional array. Each sub-array should contain words grouped together by their first character. Words that start with the same letter must be in the same sub array, in the same order as they were originally.

Make sure to use the JS split() function as an integral part of your solution.

For example, the string "apples, arc, bananas, berries, cherries, grapes, kiwi, oranges, strawberry" should get converted into:

[
["apples","arc"],
["bananas","berries"],
["cherries"],
["grapes"],
["kiwi"],
["oranges"],
["strawberry"]
]
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here is a JavaScript solution to the given problem. This solution first separates the long string into an array of words, then groups these words into a 2-dimensional array based on their first character using the `reduce()` function.

```javascript
function groupWords(str) {
  var words = str.split(/, /); //split string into array based on commas and spaces

  var groupedWords = words.reduce(function (acc, word) {
    var char = word[0]; //get first character of each word
    if (!acc[char]) acc[char] = []; //if there's no array for this character yet, create one
    acc[char].push(word); //push the word to the array of its first character
    return acc;
  }, {});
  
  //Convert object into array
  var result = Object.values(groupedWords); 
  
  return result;
}

var str = "apples, arc, bananas, berries, cherries, grapes, kiwi, oranges, strawberry";
console.log(groupWords(str));
```

The `reduce()` function is used to transform the array of words into an object where the keys are the first characters, and the values are arrays of words that start with that character. Then, `Object.values()` is used to transform this object into an array of arrays.
<|end|>


