Formulate an SQL query to extract the 5 least frequently purchased items from the 'sales history table' within the last year.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Assuming your 'sales history' table have columns 'item_id', 'purchase_date', and 'quantity', and the 'items' table have columns 'item_id' and 'item_name'.

```SQL
SELECT items.item_name, COUNT(sales_history.item_id) as sales_count 
FROM sales_history 
JOIN items 
ON sales_history.item_id = items.item_id 
WHERE purchase_date >= DATE_SUB(CURRENT_DATE, INTERVAL 1 YEAR) 
GROUP BY sales_history.item_id 
ORDER BY sales_count 
LIMIT 5;
```

This query will return the 5 least frequently purchased items within the last year, along with the number of times they were purchased. Please replace the column and table names based on your actual database schema if they are named differently.

Please bear in mind that SQL might differ slightly based on the type of SQL you are using (for example, MS SQL Server, MySQL, PostgreSQL etc.). The above SQL is written in MySQL format.
<|end|>


