Write a JavaScript function to check if two numbers are in a given range.
Range 1: 2-5
Range 2: 20-25
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here is one way to define a function to check if two given numbers are in the mentioned ranges:

```javascript
function checkRange(num1, num2) {
    var inRange1 = num1 >= 2 && num1 <= 5;
    var inRange2 = num2 >= 2 && num2 <= 5;
    var inRange3 = num1 >= 20 && num1 <= 25;
    var inRange4 = num2 >= 20 && num2 <= 25;

    if ((inRange1 || inRange2) && (inRange3 || inRange4)) {
        return true;
    }
    return false;
}
```

You can call this function with two numbers to check if they are in the appropriate ranges:


```javascript
console.log(checkRange(3, 22)); // prints: true
```
<|end|>


