Suppose we have tables structured as follows:

- papers(id, title, publication_year)
- co_authors(paper_id, author_name)

Here is the SQL query:

```sql
SELECT papers.id, papers.title, papers.publication_year
FROM papers
JOIN co_authors
ON papers.id = co_authors.paper_id
WHERE papers.publication_year BETWEEN 1980 AND 1990 
AND co_authors.author_name = 'Jane Smith';
```

Assuming that the 'papers' table has fields 'id', 'title', 'publication_year', and that the 'co_authors' table has fields 'paper_id' and 'author_name'. The query retrieves all papers where the year of publication is between 1980 and 1990 and where Jane Smith is listed as a co-author. The JOIN operation combines rows from 'papers' and 'co_authors'.
