The given programming test question:

Construct a JavaScript function that implements a fibonacci sequence.

A slightly more difficult version:

Construct a JavaScript function that implements a fibonacci sequence, but with memoization to optimize it. The function must handle input values of up to 1000 efficiently.

Here, we not only ask the candidate to implement the fibonacci sequence, but also to optimize it using memoization, which would improve the time complexity of the algorithm significantly, requiring more understanding of the algorithm and its optimization.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
```javascript
// Simple version (less efficient)
function fibonacci(n) {
  if (n <= 1) {
    return n;
  }
  return fibonacci(n - 1) + fibonacci(n - 2);
}

// More efficient version with memoization
function fibonacciMemoized(n, memo = {}) {
  if (n <= 1) {
    return n;
  }
  if (!memo[n]) {
    memo[n] = fibonacciMemoized(n - 1, memo) + fibonacciMemoized(n - 2, memo);
  }
  return memo[n];
}

console.log(fibonacci(10)); // 55
console.log(fibonacciMemoized(1000)); // 4.346655768693743e+208
```
<|end|>


