You can accomplish this by using the `dup` method offered by ActiveRecord, which creates a new object with the same attributes. Then you can change the single field you want and save it as a new record. Here is an example:

```
old_record = Record.find(:id)

new_record = old_record.dup
new_record.some_field = 'new value'
new_record.save
```

Unfortunately, there's not a one-line method to specifically do what you're asking, but this is a fairly clean and understandable way of copying a record with a new value for a particular field. 

Please note that the `dup` method does not copy associated records or the ID. If you want to replicate associations, you will need to explicitly do so. Also remember to validate your new record before saving it to make sure that your changes have not caused any validation errors.
<|end|>


