I'm able to connect to and read an excel file no problem.  But when importing data such as zipcodes that have leading zeros, how do you prevent excel from guessing the datatype and in the process stripping out leading zeros?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
When importing data into Excel, you can force it to interpret a column as text (preserving leading zeros) by using the following steps:

1. Open Excel, click on "File" at the top left side and then click on "Open".
2. Navigate to and select the file you want to import, but do not click the "Open" button yet. Instead, click on the dropdown arrow next to the "Open" button, select "Open and Repair", then "Extract Data".
3. When the Text Import Wizard opens, choose "Delimited" and click "Next".
4. Check the box(es) for the appropriate delimiters for your file (comma, tab, etc.) and click "Next".
5. In the "Data preview" window, click the column containing the zip codes. In the "Column data format" section, select "Text". Repeat this step for each column that you want to import as text (preserving leading zeros).
6. Click "Finish".

This will import the file into Excel, treating the selected columns as text and preserving any leading zeros.
