<|asst|>
You can solve this using various programming languages. Here are solutions in Python, JavaScript, Java and C++.

Python:
```python
array = [i for i in range(0, 46) if i % 3 == 0]
print(array)
```

JavaScript:
```javascript
let array = [];
for (let i = 0; i <= 45; i++) {
  if (i % 3 === 0) {
    array.push(i);
  }
}
console.log(array);
```

Java:
```java
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.List;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        List<Integer> array = new ArrayList<>();
        for (int i = 0; i <= 45; i++) {
            if (i % 3 == 0) {
                array.add(i);
            }
        }
        System.out.println(array);
    }
}
```

C++
```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <vector>
using namespace std;

int main() {
    vector<int> array;
    for (int i = 0; i <= 45; i++) {
        if (i % 3 == 0) {
            array.push_back(i);
        }
    }

    for (int i = 0; i < array.size(); i++) {
        cout << array.at(i) << " ";
    }

    return 0;
}
```

All of these scripts will create an array that contains (in ascending order) every number between 0 and 45 inclusive that is divisible by 3. The output of each will be:[0, 3, 6, 9, 12, 15, 18, 21, 24, 27, 30, 33, 36, 39, 42, 45]
