Write a JavaScript program to generate a table and insert three rows of data into it.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here is a simple JavaScript program to generate a table and insert three rows of data into it.

HTML Code:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<title>Create a table using JavaScript</title>
</head>
<body>

<button onclick="createTable()">Create Table</button>

<div id="tbl">
<!-- Table will be inserted here -->
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

JavaScript Code:

```javascript
function createTable()
{
  // Create a new table element
  var table = document.createElement('table');

  // Create table Header
  var tr = table.insertRow(-1);
  var th1 = document.createElement('th');  
  var th2 = document.createElement('th'); 

  th1.innerHTML = "Header 1";
  tr.appendChild(th1);
  th2.innerHTML = "Header 2";
  tr.appendChild(th2);

  /* Insert 3 rows into the table
     using a loop for convenience */
  for (i = 0; i < 3; i++) {
    // Create a new row
    var row = table.insertRow(-1);

    for (j = 0; j < 2; j++) {
      // Create a new column
      var cell = row.insertCell(-1);

      // Insert data into the cell
      cell.innerHTML = "Row-" + i + " Column-" + j;
    }
  }

  // Add the created table to the div
  document.getElementById('tbl').appendChild(table);
}
```

The button calls 'createTable' function when clicked. This function creates a table element, then creates and inserts header, rows and data cells into the table. The table is then inserted into a div with id 'tbl'. Every time you click the button, a new table is created and appended to the div.
<|end|>


