Is there a method of accessing an Exchange server that does not have `IMAP` or `POP3` enabled without Outlook?

It does not appear that Outlook Express supports Exchange (only `IMAP and POP3`).
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Yes, there are alternatives. You can use Exchange Web Services (EWS), Outlook Web App (OWA), or even ActiveSync for mobile devices. 

Exchange Web Services (EWS) is a programmatic interface to Microsoft Exchange Server that's used by Outlook, Outlook for Mac, and third-party apps. EWS provides access to much of the same data that's available through Microsoft Office Outlook.

Outlook Web App (OWA) also known as "Outlook Web Access", is a webmail service of Microsoft Exchange Server. The web interface of OWA resembles the interface in Microsoft Outlook.

Both of these options allow email communication without needing the POP3 or IMAP protocols enabled. 

ActiveSync is also an option for mobile device access. 

All these alternatives are dependent on the configuration of the Exchange server. If the server administrator has disabled these interfaces then you may not be able to use them.
<|end|>


