Create an algorithm in C++ to sort an array of integers using insertion ssort.
[3,1,7,8,2,6,4]
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Insertion sort is a simple sorting algorithm that works similarly to the way you sort playing cards in your hands. The array is virtually split into a sorted and an unsorted region. Values from the unsorted region are picked and placed at the correct position in the sorted region.

Here is a clean implementation of insertion sort in C++

```c++
#include<iostream>
using namespace std;

void insertionSort(int arr[], int n) {
   int key, j;
   for(int i = 1; i<n; i++) {
      key = arr[i]; //take value
      j = i;
      while(j > 0 && arr[j-1]>key) {
         arr[j] = arr[j-1]; //shift number to one position ahead
         j--;
      }
      arr[j] = key; //insert in correct place
   }
}

void printArray(int arr[], int n) {
   for(int i = 0; i<n; i++)
      cout<< arr[i] <<" ";
   cout << endl;
}

int main() {
   int n;
   cout << "Enter the number of elements: ";
   cin >> n;
   int arr[n];   //create an array with given number of elements
   cout << "Enter elements:" << endl;
   
   for(int i = 0; i<n; i++) {
      cin >> arr[i];
   }
   
   cout << "Array before Sorting: ";
   printArray(arr, n);
   insertionSort(arr, n);
   cout << "Array after Sorting: ";
   printArray(arr, n);
}
```

This is a C++ program implementing the insertion sort algorithm. This program takes the number of elements in array and the array elements as input from the user, applies the insertion sort algorithm to sort the entered elements, and finally prints out the sorted array elements.
<|end|>


