How to add password lock to a zip file or any file in flutter?
I am using ZipFileEncoder for creating a zip file, but this does not allow to add password lock to it. How can I lock this file with password protection?
Is there any other way instead of using native platform specific code?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
As of now, Flutter does not have an inbuilt library to create a password-protected ZIP file. The Flutter community relies on platform-specific APIs for these features and uses Platform Channels to call those APIs from Flutter Dart code.

For the Android part, you can use "zip4j" which is capable to crate password-protected zip files:  
https://github.com/srikanth-lingala/zip4j

For iOS, "SSZipArchive" is capable to create password protected zip and it is written in Objective C: 
https://github.com/ZipArchive/ZipArchive

As the two libraries are platform-specific and written in different languages, you will have to do some work to connect them to your Dart/Flutter code but that's the only method available as of this moment because there is no existing Flutter package for creating password-protected zip files.

Essentially, you need to add these libraries to the iOS and Android part of your flutter project and then write platform-specific channel code. Here's a link to the Flutter example on how to call platform-specific APIs:
https://flutter.dev/docs/development/platform-integration/platform-channels

Currently, this is the only way to achieve password protection for ZIP files using Flutter.
I recommend to follow the official Flutter guide on how to call platform-specific APIs from Dart/Flutter code. It includes everything that you need to know.
You should also consider the pros and cons here. Flutter is designed to provide "native performance". Therefore, calling non-Dart code (like Java/Kotlin or ObjC) inevitably has a certain performance impact. That's something to keep in mind.
Hopefully, there will be a dedicated Flutter package to perform this in the future.
<|end|>


