lst = ["A", "B", "C", "1", "2", "3"]
<|end|>
<|asst|>
In hexadecimal, A = 10, B = 11, C = 12.

So, the transformation of the array to decimal numbers is: [10, 11, 12, 1, 2, 3]

Then, compute their cumulative product (each element is multiplied by the product of all previous elements):

10 -> 10 * 11 = 110 -> 110 * 12 = 1320 -> 1320 * 1 = 1320 -> 1320 * 2 = 2640 -> 2640 * 3 = 7920

So, the result of the cumulative product is: 7920
