How to pass on my own kubernetes audit policy yaml to the GKE master node?
For self-managed kubernetes, we can ssh into master node and pass the policy yaml into `/etc/kubernetes/manifests/kube-apiserver.yaml`. How could we achieve the same in GKE?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
In GKE, you do not have direct access to the master nodes to customize the configuration like you would in a self-managed Kubernetes cluster, due to the managed nature of the service. Google manages the master node for you, including the version, configuration, availability, and updates.

For audit logging in GKE, there are some controls available. GKE uses Cloud Audit Logs to log actions that affect your cluster. These logs include administrative actions performed through the user interface, command-line tools, and APIs, along with any actions performed by GKE itself. 

However, Kubernetes level audit logging which can be controlled by modifying the audit policy yaml file on the master node, is not currently supported on GKE. If you want detailed Kubernetes native audit logs you are currently required to host your own Kubernetes cluster. 

It's highly recommended that the requirements are consulted with the official GKE documentation for the most accurate information. Also, Google continues to update and add features, so what isn't supported now may be supported in the future. You might want to frequently check for updates if this is a feature that is critical to your needs.
<|end|>


