Often time I need to add a control to a dialog after the dialog has been generated via dialog template and CreateDialogIndirect.  In these cases the tab order is set by the dialog template and there is no obvious way to change the tab order by including a newly created control.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Yes, it is possible to dynamically add a control to a dialog and adjust its position (tab order) in the tab navigation sequence. 

In order to make it happen, you need to manage the Z-order of the controls in the dialog. The tab order is determined by the Z-order, with the "top" control (the one at the end of the Z-order list) having the first tab position, the one after it the second position and so on. 

Here's a rough example:

```cpp
// Assumed HWND hDlg is the handle to your dialog, ID_FIRSTCONTROL is the ID of existing control that 
// you want the new control to be tabbed to after

HWND hwndFirstCtrl = GetDlgItem(hDlg, ID_FIRSTCONTROL);
HWND hwndNewCtrl = CreateWindow(...); //Create your new control

// Now we set the new control to follow the existing control in the Z order, thus making it follow in the tab order.
SetWindowPos(hwndNewCtrl, hwndFirstCtrl, 0, 0, 0, 0, SWP_NOMOVE | SWP_NOSIZE);
```

Remember, tab order also considers WS_TABSTOP style. Therefore, your new control must have the WS_TABSTOP style flag set, as all controls participating in the tab sequence must have this style. Otherwise, it will be simply skipped when moving through the dialog with the Tab key.

```cpp
SetWindowLongPtr(hwndNewCtrl, GWL_STYLE, GetWindowLongPtr(hwndNewCtrl, GWL_STYLE) | WS_TABSTOP);
```

Please replace "CreateWindow(...)" and the IDs with your own respective code/function calls and IDs. And do remember that changing the Z-order of a window can affect drawing sequence, so if tweaking with Z-order creates visual artifacts, it might not be suitable for your case.
<|end|>


