Work out how many sum of pairs of numbers in a set of integers can be divisible by 3.
[2, 5, 10, 15, 20]
<|end|>
<|asst|>
First, determine the remainders when each number in the set is divided by 3. 2 has a remainder of 2, 5 has a remainder of 2, 10 has a remainder of 1, 15 has a remainder of 0, and 20 has a remainder of 2. 

A sum is divisible by 3 if the sum of the numbers' remainders is divisible by 3. This means pairs can either both have a remainder of 0, or one number can have a remainder of 1 and the other can have a remainder of 2. 

Only one number has a remainder of 0, so there are 0 pairs where both numbers have a remainder of 0.

There is one number with a remainder of 1 and three numbers with a remainder of 2. So there are 1 * 3 = 3 pairs where one number has a remainder of 1 and the other has a remainder of 2.

Therefore, there are 3 pairs of numbers in the set that can be added together to result in a multiple of 3: (2, 10), (5, 10), and (20, 10).
<|end|>


