If a user is already signed into Teams and they visit a Task Module React app, is it possible for the app to obtain an OAuth token without requiring the user to sign in again? I'm able to obtain a token using the `@microsoft/teams-js` node package, however this opens the browser and asks the user to sign in again which is bad user experience. Is there any way to avoid this? or will the app always require a user to sign in again
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Yes, Microsoft Teams provides Single Sign-On (SSO) functionality to avoid making the user sign in repeatedly. Teams will take care of user logins through token handling within the application. SSO in Teams is supported through tabs as well as with bots. To streamline the process, you should use the Teams JavaScript client SDK. 

You can use getAuthToken method from @microsoft/teams-js library which allows you to fetch tokens for your app silently using teams SSO.

First, ensure to update your app manifest to include "webApplicationInfo". Follow the Azure AD App registration process outlined in the Microsoft documentation for Single Sign-On (SSO).

Below is a sample of how to implement it:

```javascript
microsoftTeams.initialize();
microsoftTeams.authentication.getAuthToken({
    successCallback: (result) => {
      // You have an OAuth token here
      let authToken = result;
    },
    failureCallback: (error) => {
      console.log('Failure callback: ', error);
    }
});
```

