Can you provide an optimized solution to FizzBuzz in JavaScript using generators and iterators? Your function should be able to take any range of numbers, not just 1-100.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here is a solution using generators and iterators:

```JavaScript
function* fizzbuzz(start, end) {
    for (let i = start; i <= end; i++) {
        if (i % 3 === 0 && i % 5 === 0) {
            yield 'FizzBuzz';
        } else if (i % 3 === 0) {
            yield 'Fizz';
        } else if (i % 5 === 0) {
            yield 'Buzz';
        } else {
            yield i;
        }
    }
}

const fizzBuzz = fizzbuzz(1, 100);
for (let num of fizzBuzz) {
    console.log(num);
}
```

The `fizzbuzz` function is a generator function. This function generates the desired output for the numbers within the provided range. This code utilizes a `for... of` loop which iterates over the `fizzBuzz` generator object to consume its values. The generator doesn't compute all the values upfront, it generates each value when it’s requested. This makes this solution memory efficient and applicable to large ranges of numbers.
<|end|>


