<|asst|>
Creating a completely hand-drawn effect in SVG requires a bit of advanced coding. The "sketchy" or "hand-drawn" appearance is typically achieved using a technique where the path of your SVG is broken down to multiple small lines or curves which are then slightly randomized to create the 'imperfect' look.

Here's a step-by-step guide on how you can achieve a sketchy, hand-drawn effect:

1. Convert SVG to Line Segments

Since SVG paths are usually too perfect to imitate hand-drawn lines, you need to convert your paths to multiple small line segments. In SVG, when you define a `<path>` element, you can use the "lineto" command (L or l) to create these segments. Breaking down your path into smaller segments would allow you to manipulate each segment individually, which is crucial for the hand-drawn effect.

The conversion of complex curves to line segments is a bit of an advanced topic and might involve knowledge of Bezier curves and De Casteljau's algorithm.

   Example:
    Replace `<path d="M10 10 H 90 V 90 H 10 Z" />` with `<path d="M10 10 L90 10 L90 90 L10 90 Z" />`

2. Randomize Line Segments

To mimic the imperfection of a hand drawing, we will want to add a bit of jitter to each end of our line segments. This can be achieved by adding a small random value to each x and y coordinate of them. The resulting lines won't be straight anymore, but they will look more like hand-drawn lines.

   Example:
   Instead of `<path d="M10 10 L90 10 L90 90 L10 90 Z" />` you'll have something like `<path d="M10 11 L89 12 L91 90 L9 89 Z" />` where the values are slightly offset.

3. Apply the Effect to Your SVG

Finally, after converting to line segments and offsetting them, replace your original SVG paths with the new sketchy ones. Repeat this for all paths in your SVGs to achieve the hand-drawn effect.

Now bear in mind that manually handling this task can be quite cumbersome if your SVG image is complex. A workaround would be to use Javascript libraries that perform these tasks; rough.js is an example of one such library.

Note that the hand-drawn effect is meant to make your vector graphics look less perfect. The lines will look jittery, uneven, and a little chaotic – this is all a part of the 'hand-drawn' aesthetic.
<|end|>


