I use the Redemption library and I encountered a problem I can not solve by myself.
In my project, I use a local XML file to login to the Exchange server (Autodiscover service is disabled on the server and can not be enabled). For this purpose, I create an Outlook Autodiscover "PreferLocalXml" registry key value and a domain name value defining the path to the local XML file. Redemption works correctly, but for some reason it does not use SSL when sending requests to the server.
Is it possible to force SSL usage in this case? However, using Autodiscover (without local XML file) works fine (SSL is used). Thank you in advance for your help.
I tried setting RDOSession.ConnectEncryptData to true, but it did not work.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Redemption uses the default Outlook settings when it communicates with the servers as it fundamentally uses the underlying MAPI subsystem provided by Outlook. 

Now, to force SSL usage for the Exchange connection, you should set this in the Outlook Exchange account's settings: File -> Info -> Account Settings -> Change Account -> More Settings -> Security tab -> Encrypt data between Microsoft Outlook and Microsoft Exchange. 

Once you have set this in Outlook, Redemption should respect the same settings. It would also generally apply to all other applications that use MAPI.

Also, note that `ConnectEncryptData` property is only for the connection to a standalone Exchange server using the RPC protocol. It does not have any effect on the initial Autodiscover process.

Remember to restart the Outlook and your application to make sure the new settings take effect.

If you can't force SSL on the client side, you could try to force it on the server side to reject connections not using SSL. This you would need to discuss with your IT department if you have no control over the server yourself.
<|end|>


