Iam training tello drone to detecting the cars, so I use this code here: [https://github.com/Shreyas-dotcom/Tello_Obj_Recognition](https://github.com/Shreyas-dotcom/Tello_Obj_Recognition),  but the code contain others objects names such as bike. So my question is: How can I remove others objects from the trained model.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
You cannot directly remove other objects from an already trained model. An object detection model predicts and identifies the types of objects it has been trained on. If you want the model to only detect cars, you have to retrain the model with data that includes only cars. 

However, if you do not have the resources to retrain the model, can adjust the code to ignore detections that are not cars. The code you linked uses OpenCV's dnn module and utilizes the coco names file for object classification. Here's a quick way to adjust that code:

The fourth step of the `main` function is labeled 'Load Yolo'. After the line `layer_names = net.getLayerNames()`, you could add this to ignore all objects except cars:

```python
car_only = ['car']
layer_names = [layer_names[i[0] - 1] for i in net.getUnconnectedOutLayers()]
layer_names = [i for i in layer_names if i in car_only]
```
Be aware that this modification will only work if cars are a class in the model being used. Higher level edits will depend on the specifics of your code, but the basic principle is to filter out any object that is not a car.
<|end|>


