<path d="M17.0288 17.7321C17.6215 17.3877 18.02 16.746 18.02 16.0112C18.02 14.9128 17.1296 14.0223 16.0312 14.0223C14.9328 14.0223 14.0424 14.9128 14.0424 16.0112C14.0424 16.3601 14.1322 16.688 14.29 16.973L12.1504 20.679C11.8743 21.1572 12.0381 21.7688 12.5164 22.045C12.9947 22.3211 13.6063 22.1572 13.8824 21.679L15.0288 19.6934V24.0066C15.0288 24.5589 15.4765 25.0066 16.0288 25.0066C16.5811 25.0066 17.0288 24.5589 17.0288 24.0066V17.7321Z" fill="#212121"/>
<path d="M30 16C30 23.732 23.732 30 16 30C8.26801 30 2 23.732 2 16C2 8.26801 8.26801 2 16 2C23.732 2 30 8.26801 30 16ZM27 16C27 9.92487 22.0751 5 16 5C9.92487 5 5 9.92487 5 16C5 22.0751 9.92487 27 16 27C22.0751 27 27 22.0751 27 16Z" fill="#212121"/>
</svg>

<|end|>
<|asst|>
Creating a parallax effect usually involves separate layers of content moving at different speeds when you scroll the webpage. Typically this effect is achieved with a multiple-step process involving complex CSS settings.

However, since you're asking for a single SVG, I will provide a simple solution using HTML and CSS to create a basic parallax effect. Note that if you want more complex effects or multiple layers, you'll need to use a more complex setup, and possibly JavaScript or a library like `ScrollMagic.js`.

The following example will create a basic parallax effect where the SVG moves slower than the rest of the content when scrolling.

HTML:
```html
<div class="parallax">
  <svg style="background-size: cover;">
    <!-- Your SVG code here -->
  </svg>
<div>
var text = '';
for (var i = 0; i < 100; i++)
   text += '<p>Scroll down...</p>';
document.write(text);
```

CSS:
```css
.parallax {
  /* The image used */
  background-image: url("your_SVG_path_here");

  /* Set a specific height */
  min-height: 500px; 

  /* Create the parallax scrolling effect */
  background-attachment: fixed;
  background-position: center;
  background-repeat: no-repeat;
  background-size: cover;
}
```
Remember to replace `"your_SVG_path_here"` with the path or URL of your SVG file.

This will create a parallax scrolling effect where the SVG is the background and scrolls at a different speed than the paragraph text 'Scroll down...'
<|end|>


