Is there a way to take a model object trained in base XGBoost and load it as a SparkXGBoost model? The docs aren't super clear on this split. I've tried:

from xgboost.spark import SparkXGBClassifierModel
model2 = SparkXGBClassifierModel.load("xgboost-model")


Im getting the following error:

Input path does not exist: /xgboost-model/metadata


Assuming this means there is a format difference if the model had originally been trained as a SparkXGBoost model.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Your assumption is right. The SparkXGBoost model and the base XGBoost model follow different formats. The Spark version follows the MLlib persistence format, which includes additional metadata.

Trying to load a base XGBoost model as a SparkXGBoost model directly will lead to an error as the required metadata will not be available.

Unfortunately there is no direct conversion provided by XGBoost to convert from a base model to a spark model, and vice versa. You will need to retrain your SparkXGBoost model if you need to use it in Spark, given Spark's MLLib provides additional supporting infrastructure around the model (like metadata) which are not provided in the base XGBoost implementation. 

Here is an example of how to fit a XGBoost model in Spark:

```python
from pyspark.sql import SparkSession
from pyspark.ml.feature import VectorAssembler
from sparkxgb import XGBoostEstimator

spark = SparkSession.builder.getOrCreate()

# assuming df is your dataframe and features are your feature column names
vectorAssembler = VectorAssembler(inputCols=features, outputCol="Features_vector")
df_t = vectorAssembler.transform(df)

xgboost = XGBoostEstimator(
    featuresCol="Features_vector", 
    labelCol="label", 
    predictionCol="prediction"
)

model = xgboost.fit(df_t)
```

After fitting the model, you can save it and load it as shown below:

```python
model.save("/path/to/save/model")
loaded_model = XGBoostClassificationModel.load("/path/to/save/model")
```
<|end|>


