<|asst|>
Here are a few alternatives you might consider:

1. [Valgrind](http://valgrind.org/): An open source software testing tool that can automatically detect many memory management and threading bugs.

2. [DynamoRIO](https://github.com/DynamoRIO/dynamorio): A dynamic binary instrumentation framework for the development of comprehensive tools for application performance and correctness checking.

3. [Dr. Memory](https://drmemory.org/): A memory monitoring tool capable of identifying memory leaks and overflows in C and C++ programs.

4. [AddressSanitizer](https://github.com/google/sanitizers/wiki/AddressSanitizer): A fast memory error analyzer developed by Google, capable of detecting out-of-bounds, use-after-free and other memory-related bugs.

5. [MemoryScape](https://www.roguewave.com/solutions/static-code-analysis): A memory debugger that allows you to investigate memory usage and leaks in C++ applications.

6. [Parasoft C/C++test](https://www.parasoft.com/product/cpptest/): A comprehensive commercial testing solution for C and C++ code, offering static and dynamic analysis, unit testing, code coverage, and runtime error detection.

7. [Incredibuild](https://www.incredibuild.com/): Besides accelerating compilation, it also provides a comprehensive suite for code analysis, including memory error and leaks detection.

Remember to carefully evaluate the compatibility and suitability of these tools against your particular needs before deciding on any.
<|end|>


