This reduces to a non-terminating computation where you are trying to apply a function to itself infinitely, so it does not reduce to a simple term like (f g). So your result for part b- is incorrect.

Please note: lambda calculus is a powerful system for computation but some expressions do not terminate. This is such an example which leads to infinite recursion similar to what happens in functional programming languages like Haskell or JavaScript when a function calls itself without any termination condition.
