console.log("Age:",parsed_json.age);
```

In both scripts, 'json.loads()' (Python) or 'JSON.parse()' (JavaScript) is used to parse the JSON string. Then, we're printing out the entire parsed JSON and individual elements of the JSON.
Remember that JSON objects become dictionaries in Python and objects in JavaScript after parsing.
