Construct a PostgreSQL table encapsulating five unique columns, specifically: "id" (integer) as primary key, "firstName" (varchar) as first name, "lastName" (varchar) for last name, "dob" (DATE) representing date of birth, and "email" (varchar) as email address. Ensure each has the correct data type and constraints where necessary.
