Design a method that not only determines the minimum number of non-overlapping intervals needed to cover the entire range of a set of intervals, but also returns that optimal set. Furthermore, also account for situations where there might be multiple optimal solutions, consider the scenario where intervals overlap but do not completely cover each other, and provide the necessary logic to handle such complex cases.
[[1, 4], [2, 6], [8, 9]]
<|end|>
<|asst|>
First, we will sort the intervals by their start times. Then, we will iterate through the sorted list and select the interval with smallest start time and largest end time each time, and exclude all intervals that overlap with the selected interval. 

This can be done in Python programming language:

```python
def minimum_intervals(intervals):
    # Sort intervals by start seconds
    intervals.sort(key=lambda interval: interval[0])

    # Initialize variables
    res = []
    end = float('-inf')

    # Iterate through the sorted list of intervals
    for interval in intervals:
        # If current interval does not overlap with previous one, append it to the result
        if interval[0] > end:
            res.append(interval)
            end = interval[1]
        # If current interval overlaps with previous one but ends later, update the end time of the last interval in result
        elif interval[1] > end:
            res[-1][1] = interval[1]
            end = interval[1]

    return res

print(minimum_intervals([[1, 4], [2, 6], [8, 9]]))
```

The output would be `[[1, 6], [8, 9]]`.

The time complexity of this solution is O(n log n) due to the sorting operation and the space complexity is O(n) for storing the result. This method works well with overlapping intervals that do not completely cover each other, it will select the minimum number of such intervals that together cover the entire range. In cases where there are multiple optimal solutions, this method will return any one of them, because we are always selecting the one with the earliest start time and the latest end time.
<|end|>


