Here's the corrected JavaScript and additional CSS and HTML. This javascript function checks the age to be over 18 and also tests the email format:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <title>Form</title>
<style>
body {
  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
}

form {
  width: 60%;
  margin: 0 auto;
  padding: 20px;
  border: 1px solid #ddd;
  border-radius: 10px;
}

input {
  width: 100%;
  padding: 10px;
  margin: 15px 0;
}

button {
  padding: 10px;
  margin-top: 15px;
  background-color: blue;
  color: white;
  border: none;
  cursor: pointer;
}

button:hover {
  background-color: darkblue;
}
</style>
<script>
  function validateForm() {
    var age = document.forms["userInfo"]["age"].value;
    if (age < 18) {
      alert("You must be at least 18.");
      return false;
    }

    var email = document.forms["userInfo"]["email"].value;
    var atpos = email.indexOf("@");
    var dotpos = email.lastIndexOf(".");
    if (atpos<1 || dotpos<atpos+2 || dotpos+2>=email.length) {
      alert("Enter a valid e-mail address");
      return false;
    }
  }
</script>
</head>
<body>

  <form name="userInfo" action="/submit"  onsubmit="return validateForm()" method="post">
    <label for="fname">Full Name:</label><br>
    <input type="text" id="fname" name="fname" value="" required><br>

    <label for="email">Email:</label><br>
    <input type="email" id="email" name="email" value="" required><br>

    <label for="age">Age:</label><br>
    <input type="number" id="age" name="age" value="" required><br>

    <label for="address">Address:</label><br>
    <input type="text" id="address" name="address" value="" required><br>

    <button type="submit">Submit</button>
  </form>

</body>
</html>
```
The CSS makes the form more visually appealing and easier to use. The JavaScript function ‘validateForm’ is now designed to validate the fields for age and email. The age should be over 18 and email should be in correct format. Also, the HTML5 `required` attribute has been added for form data validation and to ensure each input field receives a value before the form data can be successfully submitted. The 'email' input type automatically checks for valid email format using built-in browser functionality.
