Generate a correct SQL query to select the three highest-priced products in a product table, also return the average price of all products and the average price of the top three.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here is the SQL query to get the desired result:

```sql
SELECT 
  product_name, 
  product_price 
FROM 
  (
    SELECT 
      product_name, 
      product_price, 
      ROW_NUMBER() OVER (
        ORDER BY 
          product_price DESC
      ) row_num 
    FROM 
      products
  ) t 
WHERE 
  t.row_num <= 3;
```

This SQL query will return the three highest-priced products from 'products' table. However, the task also demands the average price of all products and the average price of the top three products. SQL queries to get these averages are discussed below:

This is the SQL query to get average price of all products:

```sql
SELECT 
  AVG(product_price) AS average_price 
FROM 
  products;
```

And this is the SQL query to get average price of top three highest-priced products:

```sql
SELECT 
  AVG(product_price) AS average_top_three 
FROM 
  (
    SELECT 
      product_price 
    FROM 
      products 
    ORDER BY 
      product_price DESC 
    LIMIT 
      3
  ) AS sub_query;
```

Please remember to replace 'product_name' and 'product_price' with your actual column names. Also, 'products' should be replaced with your actual table name.
<|end|>


