I have written a thumbnail provider following the interfaces specified on MSDN.  However, I have been unable to figure out how to register it in a way that Vista actually calls into it.  Has anyone gotten a thumbnail provider working for Vista?  Sample code or links would be especially helpful.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here are the steps you need to register your thumbnail provider in a way that Windows Vista will call into it:

1. Locate the object and file type for which you want to provide thumbnails. The object specifies an item in the file system presented either as a file or a folder. The file type specifies the extension used to identify the type of a file.

2. In the registry, to the object or file type, add a new key called ‘{E357FCCD-A995-4576-B01F-234630154E96}’ under the ‘shellex’ key.

3. Set the default value of the ‘{E357FCCD-A995-4576-B01F-234630154E96}’ key to the CLSID of your thumbnail provider.

For example:

```
HKEY_CLASSES_ROOT
   .txt
      shellex
         {E357FCCD-A995-4576-B01F-234630154E96}
            (Default) = {Your Thumbnail Provider CLSID}

```
4. If you created your thumbnail provider as a COM object, you need to register the COM class.

5. You may need to log off and log back on, or reboot your computer to see the changes.

Remember that making modifications to the registry can potentially harm your system if done incorrectly, so be cautious when making these changes.

And here's an example how it can be done programmatically:

```csharp
using (RegistryKey root = Registry.ClassesRoot.CreateSubKey(".txt\\shellex\\{E357FCCD-A995-4576-B01F-234630154E96}"))
{
    if (root != null)
    {
        const string clsid = "{83D96563-DB11-42DF-92F9-32CE3396D766}";  // Your Thumbnail Provider CLSID
        root.SetValue(string.Empty, clsid);  
    }
}
```

Note that your shell extension DLL should be either in the system32 directory, or in any directory listed in the PATH system variable, otherwise the system won't find it.

For more detailed reference and sample code you can take a look at the Windows classic samples repo on GitHub, specifically the ThumbnailProvider sample: https://github.com/microsoft/Windows-classic-samples/tree/main/Samples/Win7Samples/winui/shell/appplatform/thumbnailprovider
<|end|>


