We have recently moved back to InstallShield 2008 from rolling our own install. So, I am still trying to get up the learning curve on it. 

We are using Firebird and a usb driver, that we couldn't find good msi install solutions. So, we have a cmd line to install firebird silently and the usb driver mostly silently.

We have put this code into the event handler DefaultFeatureInstalled. This works really well on the first time install. But, when I do an uninstall it trys to launch the firebird installer again, so it must be sending the DefaultFeatureInstalled event again.

Is their another event to use, or is there a way to detect whether its an install or uninstall in the DefaultFeatureInstalled event?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
The InstallShield 2008 event `DefaultFeatureInstalled` is indeed called during install and uninstall. It corresponds to the "OnFirstUIAfter" event in the InstallScript function `OnMaintUIBefore`, which is called when the first user interface dialog is displayed after a user begins an installation or chooses to maintain an already installed application.

One way to handle your issue is to check the installation state of your application in the InstallScript and decide whether to start the Firebird installation based on this.

Below is an example of how you can check the installation state in InstallScript:

```
if (MAINTENANCE) then
   // Maintenance mode
   if (REMOVEALLMODE) then
      // Uninstallation
   elseif (MODIFYMODE) then
      // Modify
   else // if (ADDMODE)
      // Repair
   endif;
else 
   // Install mode
endif;
```

So in `DefaultFeatureInstalled` function you can use such conditionals to determine if it's install mode or uninstall mode then perform the necessary steps accordingly. 

Please note that such conditionals should be set in the `OnMaintUIBefore` or `OnFirstUIBefore` function where the installation mode is determined based on user's selections, and before the `DefaultFeatureInstalled` event fires.

Here is the pseudo code to do this:

``` 
function DefaultFeatureInstalled()
begin 
   ...
   if (ADDLOCALMODE) then 
      // Here we are in installation mode
      // call Firebird installation
   else if (REMOVEALLMODE) then
      // Here we are in uninstallation mode
      // Do not call Firebird installation
   endif;
   ...
end;
```
Remember to replace pseudo conditionals by actual InstallShield conditions.

This will allow you to differentiate between an install and an uninstall, and based on the installation mode, you can make decisions for better handling install/uninstall scenarios.
<|end|>


