Craft a while loop in C++ programming language, specifically to output a sequence, displaying every third integer, limited within the range of 1 to 10, inclusively.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here is the solution using a while loop:

```c++
#include <iostream>

int main() {
    int i = 1;
    while(i <= 10) {
        if(i % 3 == 0) {
            std::cout << i << "\n";
        }
        i++;
    }
    return 0;
}
```

This program initializes a counter (i) to 1. The loop continues as long as i is less than or equal to 10. If the counter is exactly divisible by 3 (i.e., i % 3 == 0), then it outputs the current value. Regardless the divisibility, the counter is then incremented by 1 for next iteration.

Please note that as per the condition being "every third integer", the code should behave differently. "Every third integer" suggests the numbers 3, 6 and 9. However, if by "every third integer" you mean starting from 1 and then every third number (which are: 1, 4, 7, 10), then following would be your C++ code:

```c++
#include <iostream>

int main() {
    int i = 1;
    while(i <= 10) {
        std::cout << i << "\n";
        i += 3;
    }
    return 0;
}
```

This script starts from 1 and increments the counter by 3 after each print operation, displaying every third number within the range.
