Write a SQL query that returns the most expensive products in each product category.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Assuming you have a table named `Products` with columns `ProductName`, `CategoryID`, `Price`, you can group data by `CategoryID` and then select the most expensive product in each group. 

Here is a SQL query that can do this:

```sql
SELECT p.ProductName, p.CategoryID, p.Price
FROM Products p
INNER JOIN (
    SELECT CategoryID, MAX(Price) AS MaxPrice
    FROM Products
    GROUP BY CategoryID
) groupP
ON p.CategoryID = groupP.CategoryID AND p.Price = groupP.MaxPrice
```

The subquery calculates the maximum price for each category. Then, the main query uses an inner join to retrieve the products associated with these maximum prices.

Please replace `Products`, `ProductName`, `CategoryID`, `Price` with actual table and column names in your database.

Please note that if there are multiple products in the same category with equally highest price, all of these products will be selected.

If you want to select only one product per category when there are multiple with the same highest price, you might use ordered analytics functions like `ROW_NUMBER`, `RANK` or `DENSE_RANK` and filter for the first row in each partition. But this approach will have arbitrary selection among the products with the same highest price. The actual solution depends on the specific requirements and DBMS specifics.
<|end|>


