I have a meta user of type object on my custom post type.
Now I would like to query all custom-posts which have this meta value. I have not found a way how to query meta values of type object. Is there a way actually ?

$args = array(
  'post_type' => 'custom-posts',
  'post_status' => 'publish',
  'posts_per_page' => -1,
  'order' => 'ASC',
  'meta_query' => array(
    array(
      'key' => 'user.id',
      'value' => $this->user_id,
    ),
  )
);


Thanks in advance.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
In WordPress, meta values are typically stored as serialized strings, not objects. When you add an object as a meta value, it is converted to a serialized string for storage.

However, you can't directly search these serialized strings using meta queries. The 'value' in the meta query only supports actual values that are stored in the database. So, in your case, you cannot directly query the object property (`'user.id'`) in the meta query.

You could instead fetch all the posts of your custom posts type and then filter them based on the meta value object property but that wouldn't be an efficient method especially if you have a huge amount of posts.

An alternative better approach would be to store the 'user.id' not as an object but as a separate meta field, then you will be able to query it directly. For example:

```php
add_post_meta($post_id, 'user_id', 'value');
```

Then you can easily use this piece of code in the meta query:

```php
$args = array(
  'post_type' => 'custom-posts',
  'post_status' => 'publish',
  'posts_per_page' => -1,
  'order'=> 'ASC',
  'meta_query' => array(
    array(
          'key' => 'user_id',
          'value' => $this->user_id,
    )
  )
);
```

Consider structuring your data in a way that allows efficient querying. If you know you need to query based on some aspect of the data, consider storing that data in a separate meta value.
<|end|>


