Here's how you can set up an LMM with just one independent variable and both monthly and yearly variation using lmer:

```
summary(lmer(Y ~ X * month + (1 + X|year), data = dataset,REML="TRUE"))
```

Here, X is multiplied with month to create interaction terms which gives a different slope for each month. The random effect term `(1 + X|year)` permits the intercept to vary with the year.

Do note that this assumes `month` and `year` are factors that represent each month and each year respectively.

In your case, introducing every month as a different dataset is not advisable. The interaction term handles the influence of months and maintaining all the data in one dataset facilitates the model in comprehending the global patterns.

Remember that the variables must make sense in the context of your data and research question. Make sure that your data is appropriately coded and organized, and that the interaction between month and your predictor is meaningful.
