/*
Consider an immeasurably large, infinite river, with n boats traveling downstream and a different set of n boats navigating upstream. Both sets of boats take off from far apart from each other, yet have identical speeds. A meeting is constituted when a boat going downstream encounters a boat going upstream. Despite these meetings, the boats are sturdy enough to stick to their original course.

This function aims to calculate the number of such meetings.
