I have an automated action that send me an email warning me when a subscription will be renew in 30 days.
I have a domain that's suppose to stop subscription that are already closed from sending me an email but I sometimes have those in my email box and I don't understand why.
I have:
- - - - 
I try to see if I made a typo or if I forgot something but no there is nothing
What have I done wrong?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Without having a specific look at your actual code or automation setup, it's quite challenging to give you an accurate solution. However, here are some potential reasons and suggestions:

1. There might be a timing/buffer issue: Sometimes, automated systems may have already picked up the subscription renewal alert before it was closed. In such case, you'll still receive the email.

2. The system may not update the status in realtime: If the system doesn't update statuses in real time, it might still consider the subscription as open and if this happens right before a renewal warning, you might get the email.

3. There might be exceptions that are not handled properly: For instance, even if a subscription is marked as closed, but if there was an unpaid bill or a pending issue, it may still trigger the warning email.

4. Overlapping of processes: If the cancellation and renewal email processes are running simultaneously, some cancellations might not be taken into account before the renewal emails are processed.

Suggestions:

Review your automation rules to ensure they are working effectively and considering all possible cases as mentioned above. It's also good having some kind of buffer time between when a subscription is closed and when the system checks to make emails.

A technical audit could be beneficial, getting a second pair of eyes on your system may help to spot any errors or oversights. 

Lastly, if you continue to face challenges and don’t have the necessary technical expertise, it might be best to get in touch with a developer or technical expert to dive deep into your system and solve the problem.
<|end|>


