<|asst|>
There could be several reasons why you are experiencing this issue. Here are few things you can try:

1. Mail server configuration: It's possible that your mail server is configured in a certain way that prevents you from getting the body of those messages. Check with your server administrator if there are any special rules or configuration for bounced emails.

2. Missing MIME parts: Most emails contain MIME parts for both HTML and plain text. Some mail clients and servers handle this differently than others. Maybe the bounce message does not contain a text/plain MIME part. This would explain why `<a:htmldescription />` and `<a:textdescription />` are empty. Try to check if there's anything in the other MIME parts.

3. Message encoding/Bounce format: Bounce messages can be in different formats and encoding based on the mail server that generates them. If your code does not handle all the types, it could be why you're unable to read the body of these messages.

A workaround could be to route these bounce message to an account where you can manually or programmatically process them. 

Lastly, EWS Managed API or Graph API is more modern and robust interface when working with Exchange Online as compared to WebDAV. You might want to consider those if you haven't already, although it might require to upgrade your code from C# 2.0.
