Create a python script that can find the longest common substring between two strings.
FIRST STRING = “abcdaf”
SECOND STRING = “zbcdf”
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Sure, below is a python script that implements a dynamic programming solution for finding the longest common substring between two strings:

```python
def longest_common_substring(str1, str2):
    dp = [[0 for j in range(len(str2)+1)] for i in range(len(str1)+1)]
    maxlen = 0
    row = 0
    for i in range(1, len(str1) + 1):
        for j in range(1, len(str2) + 1):
            if str1[i-1] == str2[j-1]:
                dp[i][j] = dp[i-1][j-1] + 1
                if dp[i][j] > maxlen:
                    maxlen = dp[i][j]
                    row = i
            else:
                dp[i][j] = 0
    return str1[row-maxlen:row]

str1 = "abcdaf"
str2 = "zbcdf"

print("Longest common substring:", longest_common_substring(str1, str2))
```

This script works by filling a 2d matrix where each cell dp[i][j] represents the maximum common substring length until the i-th character in str1 and the j-th character in str2. It keeps updating the maximum length and the ending index of the maximum length substring. At the end, it returns the maximum length common substring.

When you run this script with your provided inputs, It will output 'bcd' which is the longest common substring between "abcdaf" and "zbcdf".
<|end|>


