Develop a React Native application to display a list of recent news articles with a custom-built infinite scroll functionality and an offline reading mode.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
As an AI language model, I cannot create an actual React Native application for you, but I can provide a comprehensive guide to help you create one yourself. Here's an outline of the steps you need to follow:

1. Set up your React Native environment:
- Install Node, npm, and React Native CLI
- Set up an emulator or physical device (Android or iOS) for testing your app

2. Code the user interface:

**App.js**: Import all required dependencies and create a main component:

```javascript
import React, {useState, useEffect} from 'react';
import {View, FlatList, Text, TouchableOpacity, ActivityIndicator} from 'react-native';
import AsyncStorage from '@react-native-async-storage/async-storage';
import NetInfo from '@react-native-community/netinfo';

const App = () => {
  // Add required state hooks and use effect hooks here...
  // ...
  return (
    <View>
      {/* Main UI components/layouts */}
      {/* ... */}
    </View>
  );
};

export default App;
```

3. Create the infinite scroll functionality:

- Add state for the list of articles, the current page, and a loading state
- Set up pagination using the useEffect hook
- Fetch news articles using a public API (e.g. News API)
- Append new articles to the list as the user scrolls
- Display a loading indicator while fetching more articles

4. Create the offline reading mode:

- Check for network availability using the NetInfo package
- Read and write articles data using AsyncStorage
- Set up conditional rendering for online or offline mode

5. Code the components:

- Style News Item (Date, Title, Source, etc.) with reusable components
- Create a custom infinite scroll using FlatList

Here's the complete code example:
```javascript
import React, {useState, useEffect} from 'react';
import {View, FlatList, Text, TouchableOpacity, ActivityIndicator, StyleSheet} from 'react-native';
import AsyncStorage from '@react-native-async-storage/async-storage';
import NetInfo from '@react-native-community/netinfo';

const App = () => {
  const [articles, setArticles] = useState([]);
  const [page, setPage] = useState(1);
  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(false);
  const [connected, setConnected] = useState(true);

  const fetchNews = async () => {
    setLoading(true);
    try {
      const response = await fetch(
        `https://newsapi.org/v2/top-headlines?country=us&category=business&page=${page}&pageSize=5&apiKey=YOUR_API_KEY`,
      );
      const news = await response.json();
      setArticles(prevState => [...prevState, ...news.articles]);
      setLoading(false);
    } catch (error) {
      setLoading(false);
      console.error(error);
    }
  };

  const storeData = async () => {
    try {
      await AsyncStorage.setItem('@stored_articles', JSON.stringify(articles));
    } catch (error) {
      console.error(error);
    }
  };

  const getData = async () => {
    try {
      const value = await AsyncStorage.getItem('@stored_articles');
      if (value !== null) {
        setArticles(JSON.parse(value));
      }
    } catch (error) {
      console.error(error);
    }
  };

  useEffect(() => {
    NetInfo.fetch().then(state => {
      setConnected(state.isConnected);
    });

    if (connected) {
      fetchNews();
    } else {
      getData();
    }
  }, [page, connected]);

  useEffect(() => {
    if (!connected && articles.length > 0) {
      storeData();
    }
  }, [articles, connected]);

  const renderItem = ({item}) => (
    <View style={styles.article}>
      <Text style={styles.title}>{item.title}</Text>
      <Text style={styles.source}>{item.source.name}</Text>
      <Text style={styles.publishedAt}>{item.publishedAt}</Text>
    </View>
  );

  const renderFooter = () => {
    return loading ? <ActivityIndicator size="large" color="#0000ff" /> : null;
  };

  const handleLoadMore = () => {
    if (!loading && connected) {
      setPage(prevPage => prevPage + 1);
    }
  };

  return (
    <View>
      {!connected && <Text style={styles.warning}>You are offline. Showing previously loaded articles.</Text>}
      <FlatList
        data={articles}
        renderItem={renderItem}
        keyExtractor={(_, index) => index.toString()}
        ListFooterComponent={renderFooter}
        onEndReached={handleLoadMore}
        onEndReachedThreshold={0.5}
      />
    </View>
  );
};

const styles = StyleSheet.create({
  warning: {
    backgroundColor: 'orange',
    padding: 10,
  },
  article: {
    borderWidth: 1,
    borderColor: '#d6d7da',
    padding: 10,
    marginVertical: 5,
  },
  title: {
    fontWeight: 'bold',
    fontSize: 16,
  },
  source: {
    fontStyle: 'italic',
    marginTop: 5,
  },
  publishedAt: {
    marginTop: 5,
  },
});

export default App;
```

**Note**: Replace `YOUR_API_KEY` with your own News API key.

That's it! This should guide you through the process of creating a React Native application with infinite scroll functionality and an offline reading mode. Make sure to test your app for desired behavior and style it as needed.
<|end|>


