Create a Python program that sorts an array of integers using the insertion sort algorithm. Additionally, implement a timer to determine the time complexity of the algorithm for the given input array (e.g. [4, 2, 6, 8, 1]).
<|end|>
<|asst|>
You can use the time module to implement a timer for your insertion sort algorithm. Here's the Python program to achieve it:

```python
import time

def insertion_sort(arr):
    for i in range(1, len(arr)):
        key = arr[i]
        j = i - 1
        while j >= 0 and key < arr[j]:
            arr[j + 1] = arr[j]
            j -= 1
        arr[j + 1] = key
    return arr

if __name__ == "__main__":
    arr = [4, 2, 6, 8, 1]
    print("Initial Array: ", arr)
    
    start_time = time.time()
    sorted_arr = insertion_sort(arr)
    end_time = time.time()
    
    print("Sorted Array: ", sorted_arr)
    print("Time taken to run algorithm:", end_time - start_time)
```

Running this code will display the sorted array, and the time taken to run the insertion sort algorithm, like below:

```text
Initial Array:  [4, 2, 6, 8, 1]
Sorted Array:  [1, 2, 4, 6, 8]
Time taken to run algorithm: 0.00003910000000000203
```

The "time taken to run algorithm" will show the execution time of the insertion sort algorithm.
<|end|>


