In order to wrap the SVG around a circular path, you would need to make use of SVG’s path functionality in conjunction with `<textPath>`. However, the SVG you have provided seems to be a complex shape and unfortunately, it's not possible to wrap this kind of SVG around a circular path.

Wrapping text or simple shapes (like straight line) around a circular path can be done using `<textPath>` inside the `<text>` in SVG which provides the ability to arrange text along a path.

Here is a simple example how we wrap text around a circular path:

```html
<svg viewBox="0 0 500 500" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
  <path id="circlePath" d="M 250, 250 m -200, 0 a 200,200 0 1,1 400,0 a 200,200 0 1,1 -400,0" fill="none"/>
  <text>
    <textPath xlink:href="#circlePath">This text is wrapped around a circular path</textPath>
  </text>
</svg>
```

Explanation: In this code, we first defined a circle path with `<path>` and gave it an id (`circlePath`). Then we used `<text>` and `<textPath>` tags to define the text that would following the path specified by `xlink:href="#circlePath"`. The text will then be wrapped in circular path.

Unfortunately, this kind of wrapping is limited to text content or simple paths and can’t be applied for complex shape like in your SVG. For complex SVG's you'd need to manually create the desired shape or use an image editing tool like Adobe Illustrator or Inkscape to "bend" or "wrap" your paths.
<|end|>


