You can achieve this through the use of JavaScript classes, where the class defines a blueprint of an object and its methods. Here's how you can create such a class:

```javascript
class Person {
  constructor(name, age) {
    this.name = name;
    this.age = age;
  }

  sayHello() {
    console.log("Hello, " + this.name);
  }

  addOneToAge() {
    this.age++;
  }
}
