In this code, `constructor`, `sayHello`, and `addOneToAge` are three methods in the class person. When a new object is created from the class (like `let john = new Person("John", 22);`), these methods become available for that object. The `constructor` method is called automatically when the object is created and assigns the initial values for `name` and `age`. The other two methods (`sayHello` and `addOneToAge`) can be called on-demand. For example, `john.sayHello()` would console.log "Hello, John", and `john.addOneToAge()` would increment the age by one.
