<|asst|>
'''
grid = GridSearchCV(svm.SVC(), param_grid, refit=True, verbose=3)

# fit the model
grid.fit(X_train, y_train)

grid.best_params_  # This gives the best parameters from the grid search

# make predictions
predictions = grid.predict(X_test)

# generate classification report
print(classification_report(y_test, predictions))
'''
This script trains the SVM classifier with the given parameters using grid search, predicts the results on the test set and then outputs a classification report which includes precision, recall, f1-score, and support for each class. The classification report is a comprehensive summary of the performance of your SVM model.
<|end|>


