We have a SharePoint list setup with history enabled so the Comments field keeps all the past values. When it displays, the Comments field is void of all line breaks. However, when SharePoint e-mails the change to us, the line breaks are in there. The Description field also shows the line breaks. 

So, something must be stripping out the line breaks in the read-only view of the Comments field. 

Any idea on how to customize that so it retains the formatting in the detail view of the SharePoint list item?


---



Update: the stock pages with this behavior are 

- -
<|end|>
<|asst|>
DispForm.aspx (displays item details when you click on an item in list view)
- ViewForm.aspx (displays item details when you select "View Item" in dropdown menu in list view)
- EditForm.aspx (displays item details when you select "Edit Item" in dropdown menu in list view). 

The issue is likely related to the display template of the Comments field being set to print as plain text rather than as rich text or HTML. Here's how you can customize it:

1. Navigate to the SharePoint list and click on Settings gear icon.
2. Click on List settings.
3. Under Columns, find and click the Comments field.
4. Change the type of text to Rich text or Enhanced rich text.
5. Click OK to save changes.

For the stock pages you mentioned, you might need to customize them using SharePoint Designer:

1. Open your SharePoint site in SharePoint Designer.
2. In the Navigation pane, click All Files.
3. Click on "Lists" and find your specific list.
4. Right click on the forms (DispForm.aspx / EditForm.aspx / ViewForm.aspx) that you want to edit and select "Edit File in Advanced Mode".
5. Find the field "Comments" in the code. It should be something like: "<SharePoint:FormField runat="server" id="ff4{$Pos}" ControlMode="Display" FieldName="Comments" />". 
6. Modify `ControlMode="Display"` to `ControlMode="Edit"`.
7. Save and close the file.

Please note that modifying SharePoint default forms using designer may influence normal behavior of your list item and should be done carefully. Always have a backup and test before applying the changes to your production environment. Also, this method will not work for Modern Experience, as it can't be customized using SharePoint Designer.
<|end|>


