Develop a C language program to perform the following tasks:

1. Calculate the summation of every pair of adjacent elements within an integer array;

2. Modify the original array with the resulting sums at their respective positions, shifting the remaining numbers to the right. In case of an array with even numbers, drop the last number; in case of an odd numbered array, keep the last number as is without shifting it;

3. Also, write functions to calculate the average and median of the new array and display these values;

4. Ensure your solution handles edge cases, such as empty arrays and arrays with just one element.

The concept is shown with an example: if initial array is [2, 3, 4, 5, 6], the new array after operation will be [5, 7, 9, 6]. Ensure your program works for positive, negative and zero integer values.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here is a C program which accomplishes the given tasks:

```c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>

// Function to calculate average
double calculate_average(int *arr, int length) {
    double sum = 0.0;
    for (int i = 0; i < length; i++) {
        sum += arr[i];
    }
    return sum / length;
}

// Function to calculate median
double calculate_median(int *arr, int length) {
    if (length % 2 == 0) {
        return (arr[length / 2 - 1] + arr[length / 2]) / 2.0;
    } else {
        return arr[length / 2];
    }
}

int main() {
    int arr[] = { 2, 3, 4, 5, 6 };
    int length = sizeof(arr) / sizeof(arr[0]);

    // Edge cases
    if (length == 0) {
    	printf("Array is empty");
    	return 0;
    }

    if (length == 1) {
    	printf("Average and Median: %d", arr[0]);
    	return 0;
    }

    // Calculate the sums of adjacent elements
    int new_length = length % 2 == 0 ? length / 2 : length / 2 + 1;
    int *new_arr = malloc(new_length * sizeof(int));
    for (int i = 0; i < length - 1; i += 2) {
        new_arr[i / 2] = arr[i] + arr[i + 1];
    }
    if (length % 2 != 0) {
        new_arr[new_length - 1] = arr[length - 1];
    }

    // Calculate the average and median of the new array
    double average = calculate_average(new_arr, new_length);
    double median = calculate_median(new_arr, new_length);
    printf("Average: %.2f\n", average);
    printf("Median: %.2f", median);

    // Free allocated memory
    free(new_arr);

    return 0;
}
```

This program creates a new array where each element is the sum of adjacent elements in the original array. The program then calculates and displays the average and median of the new array. It also handles empty arrays and arrays with just one element.

Remember to compile and run the program on your machine to see the execution.
