How do I find the start of the week (both Sunday and Monday) knowing just the current time in C#?

Something like:


DateTime.Now.StartWeek(Monday);
<|end|>
<|asst|>
You can use the DateTime class and its properties / methods in C# .NET framework in order to determine the start of a week. Here is how you can do it:

1. If Monday is the start of the week:

```csharp
DateTime now = DateTime.Now;  
int offsetDays = now.DayOfWeek - DayOfWeek.Monday;  

if(immediateWeek && offsetDays < 0)
    offsetDays += 7;

DateTime lastMonday = now.AddDays(-offsetDays);

```
LastMonday variable now holds the DateTime value which represents the start (Monday) of the current week.

2. If Sunday is the start of the week:

```csharp
DateTime now = DateTime.Now;  
int offsetDays = now.DayOfWeek == DayOfWeek.Sunday ? 0 : (7 - (int)now.DayOfWeek);

if(immediateWeek && offsetDays < 0)
    offsetDays += 7;

DateTime lastSunday = now.AddDays(-offsetDays);
```

LastSunday variable now holds the DateTime value which represents the start (Sunday) of the current week.

In both of these examples, it assumes that the start of the week is at 00:00 hours (i.e., midnight at the beginning) of the specified day.
<|end|>


