Write an HTML form to collect a user's name, email address, password, and date of birth. Also, include JavaScript which validates if the user is above 18 years old prior to form submission.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here's a simple HTML form with JavaScript validation:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<script>
  function validate() {
    const dateOfBirth = document.getElementById('dob').value;
    const dob = new Date(dateOfBirth);
    const today = new Date();
    const age = today.getFullYear() - dob.getFullYear();

    if(age < 18) {
      alert('Sorry, you must be at least 18 years old.');
      return false;
    }

    return true;
  }
</script>
</head>
<body>
<form onsubmit="return validate()">
  <label for="name">Name:</label><br>
  <input type="text" id="name" name="name"><br>
  <label for="email">Email:</label><br>
  <input type="email" id="email" name="email"><br>
  <label for="password">Password:</label><br>
  <input type="password" id="password" name="password"><br>
  <label for="dob">Date of Birth:</label><br>
  <input type="date" id="dob" name="dob"><br>
  <input type="submit" value="Submit">
</form> 
</body>
</html>
```
This form won't actually submit the data anywhere (you'll need a server-side script like PHP or Node.js to handle that). However, it does include a snippet of JavaScript that validates the user's age when the form is submitted. The validation function obtains the value of the 'dob' (date of birth) input field, computes the age of the person, checks if it is below 18, and shows an alert if it is. If the user is under 18, it will prevent the form from being submitted. 

Please adapt the code to fit the requirements of your application, for instance, you may want better handling of invalid date inputs, and a more sophisticated method of showing the validation error, etc.
