Define an interface in Java for a simple banking application. This interface should have methods for depositing money, withdrawing money, transferring funds, checking balance and computing interest. After that, create a class "SavingsAccount" that implements this interface. Furthermore, include exception handling to manage cases such as insufficient funds for withdrawals or transfers.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Below is the code.

First, we define the interface 'Banking':
```java
public interface Banking {
    void deposit(double amount);
    void withdraw(double amount) throws InsufficientFundsException;
    void transfer(double amount, SavingsAccount otherAccount) throws InsufficientFundsException;
    double checkBalance();
    double computeInterest();
}
```
Next, create the custom exception class 'InsufficientFundsException':
```java
public class InsufficientFundsException extends Exception {
    public InsufficientFundsException(String message){
        super(message);
    }
}
```
Then, we create the class 'SavingsAccount' that implements the 'Banking' interface:
```java
public class SavingsAccount implements Banking {
    private double balance;
    private double interestRate;
    public SavingsAccount(double balance, double interestRate){
        this.balance = balance;
        this.interestRate = interestRate;
    }

    @Override
    public void deposit(double amount) {
        balance+= amount;
    }

    @Override
    public void withdraw(double amount) throws InsufficientFundsException {
        if (amount > balance) {
            throw new InsufficientFundsException("Not enough balance for the withdrawal!");
        } else {
            balance -= amount;
        }
    }

    @Override
    public void transfer(double amount, SavingsAccount otherAccount) throws InsufficientFundsException {
        if (amount > balance) {
            throw new InsufficientFundsException("Not enough balance for the transfer!");
        } else {
            withdraw(amount);
            otherAccount.deposit(amount);
        }
    }

    @Override
    public double checkBalance() {
        return balance;
    }

    @Override
    public double computeInterest() {
        return balance * interestRate;
    }
}
```
This program defines a banking interface with methods for deposit, withdraw, transfer, check balance, and compute interest. The SavingsAccount class implements this interface. The withdraw and transfer methods feature exception handling to inform the user when there are insufficient funds for the transaction. The balance and the interest rate are kept as instance variables of each SavingsAccount object.

Note: This is a simplified model and does not cover all the aspects of a real banking application, such as user authentication, concurrent account access, different types of accounts, regulatory rules, etc.
