The `decode_json` function basically takes JSON data as input. If the data is a list, it iterates through each element of the list and calls itself. Similarly, if the input data is a dict, it iterates through each key-value pair and calls itself to decode the value. If the data is neither a list nor a dict (meaning it's a base case), it just prints the data.

