Here is an example of how you could read emails using POP3 in C# using OpenPop.NET library. OpenPop.NET supports various encodings including Unicode, UTF-7, UTF-8, and others. Note that OpenPop.NET is a .NET 2.0 library, so it should suit your needs.

Here is a sample code snippet to read emails:

```csharp
using System;
using System.Text;
using OpenPop.Pop3;
using OpenPop.Mime;

class Program
{
    static void Main(string[] args)
    {
        // Create an object to connect to the pop server
        Pop3Client pop3Client = new Pop3Client();
        pop3Client.Connect("pop3.server.com", 110, false);
        pop3Client.Authenticate("username", "password");

        // Get the number of emails on the POP3 server
        int emailCount = pop3Client.GetMessageCount();

        // Retrieve all Messages
        for (int i = emailCount; i >= 1; i--)
        {
            Message message = pop3Client.GetMessage(i);
            string subject = message.Headers.Subject; // Get the subject
            string body = message.FindFirstPlainTextVersion().GetBodyAsText(); // Get the body
            
            Console.WriteLine("Subject: {0}", subject);
            Console.WriteLine("Body: {0}", body);
        }
        pop3Client.Disconnect();
    }
}
```

In the above code, you'll need to replace the placeholders "pop3.server.com", "username", and "password" with your actual POP3 server address, username, and password accordingly.

