Your code looks mostly correct except there is an issue with the condition in the if statements (indent.length should be compared to the length of the string without spaces) and the regexp in the second if-statement (it should be the same as the first one).

You can use the replace function to add space after every 2 characters for the first 2 and then after every 3 characters for the rest. Here is the example:

```javascript
$("#form-field-indentification_number").keyup(function() {
    var indent = $(this).val().replace(/ /g, "");
    indent = indent.replace(/^(.{2})(.{0,3})/, "$1 $2");
    indent = indent.replace(/.+\s(.+)/, function (_, g1) { return indent.split(" ")[0] + " " + g1.replace(/(\d{3})/g, "$1 "); });
    $(this).val(indent.trim());
});
```

In the example above we first remove all spaces, then we create a masked string with space after every 2 characters for the first 2 and then after every 3 characters for the rest using replace function with regexp as parameters. After we split and join parts of this masked string to add spaces after every 3 characters for the rest. The trim function is used to remove additional space at the end. 

