Construct an HTML page that turns the provided quotation into a scrolling marquee. Also include a drop-down menu with speed options to control how fast the quote scrolls. The speed options should be slow, medium, and fast.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here is a simply coded HTML page which uses JavaScript to change the speed of the marquee. The quotation in the marquee can be replaced with any text which needs to be displayed as a scrolling marquee.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<body>

<header>
    <h1>Select Scroll Speed</h1>
</header>

<select onchange="changeSpeed(this)">
    <option value="slow">Slow</option>
    <option value="medium">Medium</option>
    <option value="fast">Fast</option>
</select>

<marquee id="quoteMarquee" behavior="scroll">
    "The only way to do a great job is to love what you do." - Steve Jobs
</marquee>

<script>
const quoteMarquee = document.getElementById('quoteMarquee');

function changeSpeed(selectObject) {
    let value = selectObject.value;
    if (value === 'slow') {
        quoteMarquee.setAttribute('scrollamount', '1');
    } else if (value === 'medium') {
        quoteMarquee.setAttribute('scrollamount', '3');
    } else if (value === 'fast') {
        quoteMarquee.setAttribute('scrollamount', '5');
    } 
}

// Initialize the marquee speed to slow
changeSpeed({ value: 'slow' });
</script>

</body>
</html>
```

The `changeSpeed` function gets the value of the selected option and adjusts the speed of the marquee accordingly using the `scrollamount` attribute. Note that the marquee tag is not supported in HTML5 and is obsolete. For modern web pages, this effect would typically be achieved using a mix of CSS and JavaScript.
<|end|>


