The decision to employ one or a combination of these constructs largely depends on the nature of the problem at hand, resource availability, and desired outcomes; no one approach is universally superior. However, these novel constructs and methods have the potential to disrupt existing paradigms and completely redefine what is computationally feasible. As these technologies advance, so will our ability to solve increasingly complex problems in real-time.
