Help me translate it to C++
It would be helpful if you could annotate the C++ code.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here is the C++ version of the Python function with comments on each block of code.

```c++
#include <string>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cctype>

std::string complex_transform_string(const std::string& s) {
    std::string new_s;
    
    // Iterate through all the characters in string s
    for (auto character : s) {
        // check if current character is a digit
        if (std::isdigit(character)) {
            // convert the char digit to int, then check if it's even or odd
            if ((character - '0') % 2 != 0) {
                // Create a string with two characters by adding 1 to the original digit
                std::string twice(std::to_string(character - '0' + 1));
                twice += twice[0];
                new_s += twice;
            }
            else {
                // Appending the character twice to the new string
                new_s += std::string(2, character);
            }
        }
        else if (std::islower(character)) { // check if current character is a lower case letter
            // Converting the character to upper case and appending it twice to the new string
            new_s += std::string(2, std::toupper(character));
        }
        else if (std::isupper(character)) { // check if current character is an upper case letter
            // Converting the character to lower case and appending it twice to the new string
            new_s += std::string(2, std::tolower(character));
        }
        else {
            // Appending the character twice to the new string
            new_s += std::string(2, character);
        }
    }
    
    // Reverse the new string and return it
    std::reverse(new_s.begin(), new_s.end());
    return new_s;
}
```

This function works by iterating over each character in the string `s`. It checks the type of each character - whether it's a digit, lowercase letter, uppercase letter, or another type of character - and applies different transformations depending on the type of the character. After the transformations, it appends the new characters to the new string `new_s`. Finally, it reverses the string `new_s` and returns it. The C++ string function `reverse(begin, end)` is used to reverse the string `new_s`.
<|end|>


