6   GG      K1        -2.4     -1.9      2.1     ......
This is merely a representation of the data frame, which could potentially have an indefinite number of columns like (Value_A, Value_B, Value_C, ........... Value_N). My objective is to filter all rows where the absolute value of all columns (Value_A, Value_B, Value_C, ....) is less than 1. For a limited number of columns, one can filter the data by simply applying 'and' condition on columns in the dataframe, but I am at a loss as to how to proceed in this scenario. I am unaware of the exact number of such columns, but I do know that such columns would be prefixed with 'Value'. The expected output in this case would be:
    A_Name  B_Detail  Value_B  Value_C   Value_D ......
1   BB      Y1        0.76     -0.7      0.8     ......
3   DD      L1        0.9      -0.5      0.4     ......
