<|user|>
Given that February of 2011 has 28 days and March has 31 days, if we know that February started on a Tuesday, could you calculate on what day of the week will first-day of April fall?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Yes, the day of the week on which the first day of April 2011 falls can be calculated using simple math. There are 28 days in February and 31 days in March. We add these two numbers together to get a total of 59 days. Since a week is seven days long, we take 59 mod 7 which equals 3. This means that the first day of April, which is 59 days after February 1st, falls 3 days after the day of the week on which February 1st falls. Given that February of 2011 started on a Tuesday, we can just add 3 days to Tuesday to get to the day of the week on which April 1st falls. The result is Friday. So, April 1, 2011 is a Friday.

This operation could be done with Python code such as the following:

```python
# Define the days of the week
days = [
    "Monday",
    "Tuesday",
    "Wednesday",
    "Thursday",
    "Friday",
    "Saturday",
    "Sunday"
]

# Define the starting day (February 1st, 2011)
start_day = "Tuesday"

# Define the number of days between February 1st and April 1st
total_days = 59

# Calculate the index of the day of the week on which April 1st falls
index = (days.index(start_day) + total_days) % 7

# Print the result
print(days[index])
```
When you run this code, it prints out: `Friday`.
<|end|>


