The purpose of this snippet of code is to sort the array in ascending order. It uses a bubble sort algorithm which is very inefficient, especially for larger arrays. A more efficient solution would be to use a pre-implemented Python function, like `sorted()`, that likely uses a more efficient sorting algorithm, like Timsort.

Here is how to do the same thing as the provided code much faster:

```
arr = sorted(arr)
```

Alternatively, if you want to use an in-place sorting algorithm:

```
arr.sort()
```

If you want to implement a more efficient sorting algorithm by yourself: Here is an example with Quick Sort.

```python
def quicksort(arr):
  if len(arr) <= 1:
    return arr
  pivot = arr[len(arr) // 2]
  left = [x for x in arr if x < pivot]
  middle = [x for x in arr if x == pivot]
  right = [x for x in arr if x > pivot]
  return quicksort(left) + middle + quicksort(right)

arr = quicksort(arr)
```
Doing this will considerably increase the speed of your sorting operation, especially for larger arrays.
