Construct a JavaScript function that obtains a string of text as input and returns an array that includes only those words which are palindromes and have more than seven characters.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
You can use regular expressions and higher order JavaScript functions like `split()`, `filter()`, `reverse()`, and `join()` to solve this problem. Here is a JavaScript function you can try:

```javascript
function getLongPalindromes(text) {
  // Split the text into words
  var words = text.split(' ');

  // Filter out those words that are not palindromes or have less than 8 characters
  var longPalindromes = words.filter(word => {
    // Check if the word is a palindrome and has more than 7 characters
    var isPalindrome = (word === word.split('').reverse().join(''));
    return (isPalindrome && word.length > 7);
  });

  return longPalindromes;
}
```

This function initially splits the input text into individual words and then filters out words that are not palindromes or have seven characters or less. We check each word if it is a palindrome by reversing it and comparing it with the original word. We also check the word's length.

This function would return an array of the words in the input text that are palindromes and have more than seven characters. If no such words exist in the input text, it would return an empty array.
