function validateHex() {
  var x = document.getElementById("hex").value;
  var regex = /^#?([a-f0-9]{6}|[a-f0-9]{3})$/i; // Regular expression for hexadecimal
  if (regex.test(x)) {
    document.getElementById("message").innerHTML = "Hexadecimal value accepted: " + x;
    localStorage.setItem('hexValue', x);  // Save the hexadecimal value to localStorage
  } else {
    document.getElementById("message").innerHTML = "Invalid hexadecimal value";
  }
}
```
This solution checks for hexadecimal values like 'a3b2c1' or '#a3b2c1' of length 3 or 6. It is designed to perform less computation during validation by making use of regular expressions. Regular expressions are built specifically for pattern matching in strings.

Running `validateHex()` checks whether the value of the input field is of correct format for a hexadecimal color code. If it satisfies the condition, the value is saved in localStorage. If it does not match, an error message is displayed.
