I have implemented the WMD control that Stack Overflow uses into a project of mine, it  works like a charm, but when I save the changes to the database it is saving the HTML version and not the Markdown version.

So where I have this in my text box:


**boldtext**



It is really saving this:


<b>boldtext</b>



How do I make it save the Markdown version?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
WMD editor on Stack Overflow converts Markdown to HTML client-side in the browser when user previews post or submits the form.

When the form is submitted, both versions (HTML and Markdown) are sent in the post request to the server. The Markdown version is embedded in a hidden input field named `post-text`. You can capture and save this value on the server-side code to store the Markdown version in addition to or instead the HTML version. Here's a sample code snippet.

```html
<!-- The WMD input box. -->
<textarea id="wmd-input" class="wmd-input"></textarea>
```

```javascript
// Attach event handler on form submit.
$('form').submit(function() {
  // Get Markdown version.
  var markdown = $('#wmd-input').val();

  // Add it to form data.
  $(this).append($('<input>').attr('type', 'hidden').attr('name', 'post-text').val(markdown));

  // Now, 'post-text' parameter will be available on the server-side with Markdown version.
});
```

Now in your server-side code, you can retrieve the `post-text` field from the form data to get the Markdown version. How you do this would depend on your server-side language and framework.

But, remember that the text from the hidden field `post-text` should also be sanitized on the server side before storing it in your database to prevent any sort of script injection or similar attacks.
<|end|>


