We have a SharePoint WSS site and some of our users on on the Mac OSX platform.  Are there any tips or tricks to get a similar experience to Windows with document shares and calendars on the Mac?

Edit: Browsing a SharePoint WSS site on a Mac, whether using Firefox or Safari, has a very similar look and feel as it does on Windows IE.  The similar experience I am looking for has to do with integrating the calendars, document shares, etc. into the desktop.

For example, with IE you can go to a calendar and select "Actions -> Connect to Outlook" and it will make the calendar visible and manageable from within Outlook.

Is there any way to get the Mac to work similarly?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Yes, it's possible to get a similar experience on a Mac to that of Windows regarding SharePoint integration. Here are some options:

1. Office 365 and Office for Mac 2016

In many cases, the integration you're looking for comes from Office 365 and the 2016 version of Office for Mac. These versions provide a similar integration experience to the Windows version. Many features will automatically synchronize including calendars, contacts, tasks, and notebooks. 

2. Outlook for Mac

You can use Microsoft's own Outlook for Mac email and calendar client, which, like its Windows counterpart, allows you to connect to SharePoint calendars. This will allow you to view and edit SharePoint calendar events within the Outlook client.

3. OneDrive

For document shares, you can use Microsoft's OneDrive application for Mac to synchronize SharePoint libraries to your Macintosh desktop. Once set up, you'll be able to manage and edit these files as if they were local, and all changes will be saved back to SharePoint. 

4. Browsers

If you just want to access SharePoint documents and calendars using a web browser, then both Safari and Firefox will work just fine. You won't get the full 'desktop integration' experience, but for many users this is sufficient.

Although Mac users may not get the same level of integration as their Windows counterparts, these options should provide a satisfactory SharePoint experience for most Mac users.

Please note that individual software configurations and versions may affect the level of support and integration between products, and it is suggested to consult with your IT department or a SharePoint specialist for best results.
<|end|>


