Develop a Java class structure that encapsulates the definition and behaviors of interstellar spacecraft entities.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here's a basic representation of what the class structure might look like for an interstellar spacecraft entity in Java:

```java
//import necessary libraries
import java.util.ArrayList;

// create the abstract class Spacecraft
public abstract class Spacecraft {
    private String name;
    private double mass;
    private double speed;

    public Spacecraft(String name, double mass, double speed) {
        this.name = name;
        this.mass = mass;
        this.speed = speed;
    }

    public abstract void launch();
}

// child class InterstellarSpacecraft
public class InterstellarSpacecraft extends Spacecraft {
    private ArrayList<String> cargo;

    public InterstellarSpacecraft(String name, double mass, double speed) {
        super(name, mass, speed);
        this.cargo = new ArrayList<>();
    }

    public void addCargo(String item) {
        cargo.add(item);
    }

    @Override
    public void launch() {
        if(this.cargo.isEmpty()){
            System.out.println("Cannot launch, cargo hold is empty.");
        }
        else{
            System.out.println("Launching spacecraft: " + super.getName() + "!");
        }
    }
}
```
This class structure includes an abstract Spacecraft class that provides the basic identifications (name), physical properties (mass), and operations (launch). It also includes a more specific InterstellarSpacecraft subclass that extends the functionalities from Spacecraft, adding an ArrayList to hold the spacecraft's cargo.

The InterstellarSpacecraft class also includes a method to add cargo to the cargo ArrayList and overrides the abstract launch method from Spacecraft to include a condition that checks whether the spacecraft's cargo hold is empty before it can launch.
