I want to handle events on failure in flink elasticserach connector to send events another place.
I saw relevant [docs](https://nightlies.apache.org/flink/flink-docs-release-1.14/docs/connectors/datastream/elasticsearch/#handling-failing-elasticsearch-requests) on version 1.14 but that custom failure handler is removed since version 1.15 in [docs](https://nightlies.apache.org/flink/flink-docs-release-1.15/docs/connectors/datastream/elasticsearch/#handling-failing-elasticsearch-requests).
And I'm using flink 1.15. Can I handle failure in flink elasticsearch connector 1.15 using custom failure handler?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
No, starting with Flink 1.15, you can't create custom failure handlers in Elasticsearch connector anymore. The official documentation notes that the capability to create a custom `ActionRequestFailureHandler` has been removed. Instead, Flink 1.15 introduces two built-in failure handling behaviours:

1. `RetryRejectedExecutionFailureHandler`: This handler will retry on `EsRejectedExecutionException` (meaning that the Elasticsearch cluster is overloaded) and let other exceptions fail the sink. This is the default handler.

2. `NoOpFailureHandler`: This handler suppresses all exceptions and drops the failed requests.

If you need to handle the failure in another way, you may need to fork and modify the Elasticsearch connector code yourself. But be aware that this might not be recommended due to the complexity of error recovery in a distributed stream processing system like Apache Flink. 

Instead, you could design a robust data ingestion pipeline with properly configured Elasticsearch clusters to minimize data ingestion failures. You could also use a Dead Letter Queue (DLQ) pattern for handling failures, where a message that cannot be processed correctly is placed on another queue so that it can be reprocessed or analyzed separately.
<|end|>


