String a1; // This can be a long text
String a2; // ej. above text with spelling corrections
String a3; // ej. above text with spelling corrections and an additional sentence

Diff diff = new Diff();
String differences_a1_a2 = Diff.getDifferences(a,changed_a);
String differences_a2_a3 = Diff.getDifferences(a,changed_a);    
String[] diffs = new String[]{a,differences_a1_a2,differences_a2_a3};
String new_a3 = Diff.build(diffs);
a3.equals(new_a3); // this is true
<|end|>
<|asst|>
The approach should involve the usage of a library that can diff string and apply patches. There are several Java libraries for determining diffs between two strings including:

1. Google's Diff-Match-Patch: It can create diff, match and patch text easily.
2. DiffUtils: Apache licensed library for creating and applying diffs.

Here is a sample to get the diffs using Google's Diff-Match-Patch library and rebuild the string using the original strings and differenced versions:

```java
import name.fraser.neil.plaintext.diff_match_patch;
import name.fraser.neil.plaintext.diff_match_patch.Patch;

import java.util.LinkedList;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        diff_match_patch dmp = new diff_match_patch();

        String a1 = "This can be a long text";
        String a2 = "This can be a long, corrected text";
        String a3 = "This can be a long, corrected text with an additional sentence.";

        LinkedList<diff_match_patch.Patch> patches_a1_a2 = dmp.patch_make(a1, a2);
        LinkedList<diff_match_patch.Patch> patches_a2_a3 = dmp.patch_make(a2, a3);

        String restored_a2 = (String) dmp.patch_apply(patches_a1_a2, a1)[0]; // Apply patches to a1 to get a2
        String restored_a3 = (String) dmp.patch_apply(patches_a2_a3, a2)[0]; // Apply patches to a2 to get a3

        System.out.println(a2.equals(restored_a2)); // true
        System.out.println(a3.equals(restored_a3)); // true
    }
}
```

You can get Google's Diff-Match-Patch library from here: https://github.com/google/diff-match-patch

Important: Don't forget to add library in classpath or in dependency management system like maven, gradle etc..
