              unzip CloudWatchMonitoringScripts-1.2.2.zip
              rm CloudWatchMonitoringScripts-1.2.2.zip
              (cd aws-scripts-mon && ./mon-put-instance-data.pl --mem-util --verify --verbose)
              EOF
}

```

This script creates an auto scaling group on AWS and start instances based on its configuration. It installs CloudWatch monitoring scripts to enable monitoring of the instances.

Remember to replace `ACCESS_KEY_HERE` and `SECRET_KEY_HERE` with your actual AWS access key and secret key, and `ami-0c94855ba95c574c8` with an actual AMI ID. The scripts aren't set to handle load-balancing, auto-scaling and don't take care of launching the webservers on the specified ports, but it should provide a good starting point for anyone interested to develop this into a working solution.
