<|asst|>
To add a pulsing effect to your SVG you can animate it using CSS. Here is an example for a glow effect:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<style>
@-webkit-keyframes glow {
  0% { stroke: white; fill:white }
  50% { stroke: #F9C23C; fill:#F9C23C }
  100% { stroke: white; fill:white }
}

@keyframes glow {
  0% { stroke: white; fill:white }
  50% { stroke: #F9C23C; fill:#F9C23C }
  100% { stroke: white; fill:white }
}

svg {
  -webkit-filter: drop-shadow( 0px 0px 10px #F9C23C );
  filter: drop-shadow( 0px 0px 10px #F9C23C );
}

svg:hover path {
  -webkit-animation: glow 2s ease-in-out infinite alternate;
  animation: glow 2s ease-in-out infinite alternate;
}
</style>
</head>
