I am using [flutter file view](https://pub.dev/packages/flutter_file_view) package to view document files but for the first it shows engine initialization failed and after restart app it work fine can someone help plzdart

FileView(controller: widget.controller),


widdget.controller is the path of file
<|end|>
<|asst|>
The "engine initialization failed" error usually occurs due to unavailability of the required resource at the time of initialization. There may be a number of reasons for this problem but mostly it happened due to Flutter Engine not getting fully initialized. 

Here are few things you can try:

- Make sure your widget.controller has a valid file path and the file actually exists there at the time of initialization.
- Try to delay the initialization of this widget until your Flutter Engine has been fully initialized.
- Also try wrapping your FileView inside FutureBuilder Widget and load your file inside this FutureBuilder and only return FileView when your file is fully loaded.
- Always make sure you have given enough permissions in your app to access and read files.

Here is how you can use FutureBuilder:

```dart
FutureBuilder<File>(
  future: getFile(), // function where you get your file
  builder: (BuildContext context, AsyncSnapshot<File> snapshot) {
    switch (snapshot.connectionState) {
      case ConnectionState.none:
        return Text('Press button to start.');
      case ConnectionState.active:
      case ConnectionState.waiting:
        return CircularProgressIndicator();
      case ConnectionState.done:
        if (snapshot.hasError)
          return Text('Error: ${snapshot.error}');
        return FileView(controller: snapshot.data.path); // Return your Widget Here when file is loaded
    }
  },
)
```

Make sure you replace getFile() with your own function to return file. And give the correct path to the FileView controller. Remember to handle the error cases as well.

If the problem persists, you might have to use flutter_downloader to manually download the file to a location and then view it using flutter_file_view.
<|end|>


