Construct a SQL data retrieval script to isolate and identify customer accounts that have accumulated orders with a collective financial value exceeding the benchmark of $100.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Assuming you have two tables "customers" and "orders". The "customers" table has columns "id" and "name". The "orders" table has columns "id", "customer_id", "amount". You can adjust according to your table structure.

Here is your SQL script:

```sql
SELECT c.id, c.name, SUM(o.amount) AS total_amount
FROM customers c
JOIN orders o ON c.id = o.customer_id
GROUP BY c.id, c.name
HAVING total_amount > 100
```
This script joins the "customers" and "orders" tables based on the customer's id, then groups the results by customer. The `HAVING` clause then filters out any customers whose total order amount does not exceed $100.
