<|asst|>
Sure, below is a simple C program that can multiply two matrices. Note that the program uses fixed 3x3 matrices, if you want to use matrices of different sizes, you'll need to adjust the code accordingly.

```c
#include<stdio.h>

int main(){
    int a[3][3]={{1,2,3},{4,5,6},{7,8,9}},b[3][3]={{10,11,12},{13,14,15},{16,17,18}},mul[3][3],r,c,i,j,k;
    
    printf("Output Matrix:\n");
    for(r=0;r<3;r++){
        for(c=0;c<3;c++){
            mul[r][c]=0;
            for(k=0;k<3;k++){
                mul[r][c]+=a[r][k]*b[k][c];
            }
        }
    }
    //printing resultant matrix
    for(r=0;r<3;r++){
