The provided code isn't really optimal and doesn't consider edge cases such as the case sensitivity of the term or the term occurring within a word (like 'program' within 'programmer'). Also, printing i won't help in finding the multiple occurrences of the term within the word list and would not be efficient if the list is large.

The function needs to return a list of indices where the term occurs or -1 if it is not found. The word list should probably be sorted first before implementing the binary search for efficient searching. However, binary search is not suitable for our problem because binary search is used in sorted array and it isn't guaranteed that indexes of occurrences are consecutive like elements in sorted array. Implementing binary search might cause loss of some occurrences.

