How would you write a function to find the median along with the frequency of this median in an array of unevenly distributed floating point numbers considering various edge cases? Also, write the function such that it performs efficiently in case of large arrays of data.

nums = [2.1, 3.4, 3.4, 4.7, 5.0, 5.5, 6.6, 7.2, 8.9]
<|end|>
<|asst|>
The task can be solved by a JavaScript function which uses the built-in `sort()` function to sort the array in ascending order first. Then, the median is calculated by finding the middle element if the length of the array is odd, or the average of the two middle elements if it is even.

The function also counts the number of times that the median occurs in the array, then both the median and the frequency are returned.

The complexity of this solution is O(n log n) due to the use of the sorting function, where n is the length of the array. This ensures decent performance even for larger arrays.

```Javascript
function findMedianFrequency(nums) {
  nums.sort(function(a, b) {
    return a - b;
  });
  
  let median;
  const numsLen = nums.length;
  
  // check if length of array is even or odd
  if (numsLen % 2 === 0) {
    // if even, calculate average of two middle elements
    median = (nums[numsLen / 2 - 1] + nums[numsLen / 2]) / 2;
  } else {
    // if odd, middle element is the median
    median = nums[(numsLen - 1) / 2];
  }
  
  // count occurrences of the median
  let frequency = 0;
  nums.forEach(num => {
    if (num === median) {
      frequency++;
    }
  });
  
  return [median, frequency];
}

let nums = [2.1, 3.4, 3.4, 4.7, 5.0, 5.5, 6.6, 7.2, 8.9];
console.log(findMedianFrequency(nums));  // Outputs: [ 5, 1 ]
``` 

This function will return the median and its frequency in the format: [median, frequency]. In this case, for the given input array, it will return [5, 1]. It means that the median is 5 and it appeared 1 time in the array. 

Note: This implementation assumes that the array of input numbers is not empty. Empty array and non-array inputs are edge cases that need to be handled separately according to requirements.
