Corrected Code:

```python
def parse_to_dict(string):
    result_dict = {}
    pairs = string.split(", ")
    for pair in pairs:
        if "=" in pair:
            parts = pair.split("=")
            key = parts[0].strip()
            value = parts[1].strip()
            result_dict[key] = value
    return result_dict

print(parse_to_dict("name=John, age=45, gender=m"))
```

This code will now ignore any parts of the string that don't have an "=" in them to form a key-value pair, and it correctly separates keys and values, removing any leading or trailing spaces, to ensure the correct input into the dictionary.

