```
This will print "True" if everything is correct, and print the error message otherwise.
  
The pattern "[a-zA-Z0-9._-]+@[a-zA-Z0-9.-]+\.[a-zA-Z]+" in the function now correctly considers:
- One or more occurrences of alphanumeric characters, '.', '_', or '-' before '@' in an email.
- One or more occurrences of alphanumeric characters, '.' or '-' after '@' but before '.' in an email.
- One or more occurrences of alphabetical characters after last '.' in an email.
