* Paging results for GET requests
* Linking related entities (e.g. linking Orders to a Customer, linking OrderItems to a Product)
* Error handling and logging
* Rate limiting to prevent abuse
* Caching for performance

Remember to correctly use status codes to indicate the success or failure of the request. For example, returning a 201 Created after successfully creating a new resource, or returning a 404 Not Found if the resource is not found.
