How to write a jQuery code to dynamically hide or show multiple HTML elements based on user interactions and efficiently apply additional styling changes?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
To dynamically hide or show multiple HTML elements based on user interaction and to apply styling changes with jQuery, you need to have a JavaScript event handler that triggers a jQuery action based on that event.

The basic syntax of jQuery is is `$(selector).action()`. Here, `$` accesses jQuery, `selector` finds HTML elements, and `action()` is the jQuery action performed on the elements.

Here is an example:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<script src="https://ajax.googleapis.com/ajax/libs/jquery/3.5.1/jquery.min.js"></script>
<script>
$(document).ready(function(){
  $("button").click(function(){
    $("p").toggle(); // This will hide or show all the <p> elements when the button is clicked
    $(". changeStyle").css( {"color":"red", "background-color":"yellow"}); // Adding additional style
  });
});
</script>
</head>
<body>
<button>Toggle between hide() and show()</button>
<p class="changeStyle">If you click on the "Hide" button, I will disappear.</p>
<p class="changeStyle">If you click on the "Show" button, I will appear.</p>
</body>
</html>
```
In this example:
- `$("button").click(function(){...});` specifies a click event on the HTML button. 

- Inside the click event, `$("p").toggle();` toggles the visibility state of all `<p>` elements (it hides currently visible elements, and shows hidden ones). 

- `$(". changeStyle").css( {"color":"red", "background-color":"yellow"});` changes the color of the text to red and the background color to yellow in elements with class "changeStyle". 

Make sure to replace the `selector` with the appropriate identifier for the HTML elements that you want to manipulate.

Note: In order for the jQuery code to work, you need to include the jQuery library in your project. You can do this by adding `<script src="https://ajax.googleapis.com/ajax/libs/jquery/3.5.1/jquery.min.js"></script>` in the header of your HTML file.
<|end|>


