Devise a Java code application capable of determining and quantifying the frequency of each individual word in a supplied sentence, handling potential duplications. The sentence for analysis is as follows: "apple banana apple orange banana grape".
<|end|>
<|asst|>
You can solve this problem by using a HashMap in Java. The HashMap data structure is part of the Java Collections Framework and it stores the data in pairs i.e., in the form of key and value. Below is a possible solution in Java, using a HashMap to keep track of frequencies:

```java
import java.util.HashMap;
import java.util.Map;

public class WordCounter {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String sentence = "apple banana apple orange banana grape";
        String[] words = sentence.split(" ");  // Splitting the sentence into words

        Map<String, Integer> wordCount = new HashMap<>();

        // Loop over each word
        for(String word : words) {
            if(wordCount.containsKey(word)) {
                // If word is already present in map, increment its count
                wordCount.put(word, wordCount.get(word) + 1);
            } else {
                // Otherwise, add the word to the map with count 1
                wordCount.put(word, 1);
            }
        }

        // Printing the word counts
        for(Map.Entry<String, Integer> entry : wordCount.entrySet()) {
            System.out.println(entry.getKey() + " : " + entry.getValue());
        }
    }
}
```

This program will output:
```
apple : 2
banana : 2
grape : 1
orange : 1
```
This indicates that "apple" and "banana" are present 2 times each in the sentence and "grape" and "orange" are present 1 time each in the sentence.
<|end|>


