<|asst|>
Here is a Python solution for the problem:

```python
def find_last_occurrence(S, p):
    # find the last occurrence of p in S
    last_occurrence = S.rfind(p)
    if last_occurrence == -1:
        print(f'Pattern "{p}" not found in string "{S}"')
    else:
        print(f'The last occurrence of pattern "{p}" in string "{S}" is at index {last_occurrence}')

# Test the function
S = "Accommodation"
p = "o"
find_last_occurrence(S, p)
```
In the code above, we utilize Python's built-in string method rfind(). The rfind() method finds the last occurrence of the specified value. It returns -1 if the value is not found. The function find_last_occurrence() takes a large string S and a pattern p, then it prints the last occurrence of pattern p in S if p is found in S. If p is not found in S, it informs that the pattern is not found in the string.

When run with S="Accommodation" and p="o", the function will output:

"The last occurrence of pattern "o" in string "Accommodation" is at index 6"
