I have a web application that generates a medium sized XML dataset to be consumed by a third party.
I thought it would be a good idea to provide some form of schema document for the XML that I generate so I pasted the XML into Visual Studio and got it to generate an XSD.
The annoying thing is that my XML doesn't validate to the XSD that was generated!

Is it better to roll your own XSD?
What about different schema docs like DTDs, Relax NG, or Schematron?  

The key is that I would like to be able to validate my document using C#. 

What are your XML validation strategies?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
You can roll your own XSD, that would be perfectly fine and many large applications do this. It's likely not validating because Visual Studio's auto-generated XSD may be too strict or imperfect, your XML might have slight discrepancies, or a combination of both.

From the choices you mentioned, I would recommend going with XSD. It is widely used, powerful, and has support in many different programming languages including C#.

In comparison, DTD is less expressive and offers less power. It is an old standard that is being phased out. Relax NG and Schematron also lacks the wide range of tool support that XSD has.

Here's a basic strategy you might find useful for validating XML with XSD in C#:

1. Design your XSD. Be precise and mindful of potential edge cases in your XML data (eg. optional elements/attributes)

2. Run XML data through an XML Validator to check if it conforms to your XSD. This can be part of your production code, or as a unit test.

Here's a basic example of validating an XML document against an XSD schema in C#:

```csharp
public void ValidateXmlWithSchema()
{
    var xmlDocument = new XmlDocument();
    xmlDocument.LoadXml(myXmlString); // Load your XML as a string into the document.

    xmlDocument.Schemas.Add("", XmlReader.Create(new StringReader(myXSDString))); // Load your XSD as a string.

    var eventHandler = new ValidationEventHandler(ValidationEventHandler);

    // the following call to Validate succeeds.
    xmlDocument.Validate(eventHandler);
}

// Display any validation errors.
private static void ValidationEventHandler(object sender, ValidationEventArgs e)
{
    switch (e.Severity)
    {
        case XmlSeverityType.Error: Console.WriteLine($"Error: {e.Message}"); break;
        case XmlSeverityType.Warning: Console.WriteLine($"Warning {e.Message}"); break;
    }
}
```

This code will validate the loaded XML with the provided XSD and cause an error/warning depending on the severity of the discrepency. Any errors or warnings are handled by the `ValidationEventHandler` which simply prints the error/warning message.
<|end|>


