Create a for loop in Java that iterates over the given array and prints the values. In addition, your program should also print the cumulative sum of the array values.
Array: int[] arr = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5};
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here is a Java code snippet that does exactly what you asked for. This code not only prints each value within the array but also prints the cumulative sum after each iteration.

```java
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[] arr = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5};
        int sum = 0;
        for(int i=0; i < arr.length; i++) {
            System.out.println("Value: " + arr[i]);
            sum += arr[i];
            System.out.println("Cumulative Sum: " + sum);
        }
    }
}
```
The output of this program would be:

```
Value: 1
Cumulative Sum: 1
Value: 2
Cumulative Sum: 3
Value: 3
Cumulative Sum: 6
Value: 4
Cumulative Sum: 10
Value: 5
Cumulative Sum: 15
```

This way, we iterate over each element in the array, print its value, add it to the running sum, and then print the new sum.
<|end|>


