Craft a JavaScript function that not only scrutinizes the robustness of a password established by a user but also furnishes instructive feedback. This function should be conveniently incorporated within the framework of an HTML webpage, bearing in mind considerations for efficiency and seamless user experience.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here is a simple password strength checker implemented in JavaScript, which can give feedback to the user.

The script checks for a variety of conditions: length (at least 8 characters), must include at least one digit, uppercase letter, and lowercase letter, and a special character. When the password meets each requirement, the corresponding feedback is displayed.

```javascript
function checkPasswordStrength() {
    var password = document.getElementById('password').value;
    var result = document.getElementById('result');

    // Check password length
    if (password.length < 8) {
        result.innerText = "Password should be at least 8 characters";
        return;
    }

    // Check for digit
    var digit = /\d/;
    if (!digit.test(password)) {
        result.innerText = "Password should include at least one digit";
        return;
    }

    // Check for uppercase letter
    var upperCase = /[A-Z]/;
    if (!upperCase.test(password)) {
        result.innerText = "Password should include at least one uppercase letter";
        return;
    }

    // Check for lowercase letter
    var lowerCase = /[a-z]/;
    if (!lowerCase.test(password)) {
        result.innerText = "Password should include at least one lowercase letter";
        return;
    }

    // Check for special characters
    var specialChars = /[\W]/;
    if (!specialChars.test(password)) {
        result.innerText = "Password should include at least one special character";
        return;
    }

    // If password passed all check, provide success feedback
    result.innerText = "Password is strong!";
}
```

In the HTML, ensure to link the JavaScript function to the password field as follows:

```html
<input type="password" id="password" oninput="checkPasswordStrength()"/>
<p id="result"></p>
```

Whenever the user types into the password field, the `checkPasswordStrength` function will be called to verify the strength of the password. The feedback is displayed in the `p` tag with id `result`.

Remember to integrate the JavaScript function into your HTML file. Either place the JavaScript function in between `<script></script>` tags in your HTML file, or link it from an external .js file using the `<script src="yourfile.js"></script>` tag.
<|end|>


