Write HTML code that creates a responsive table using Flexbox or Grid layout. The table should have a header with filter functionality that allows users to find a specific row based on content within that row.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
This problem involves both HTML structure, CSS for styling with Flexbox, and JavaScript for filter functionality. Below is an example of how it might be done:

HTML:
```
<input type="text" id="searchInput" onkeyup="filterTable()" placeholder="Search for info..">

<div id="flexTable" class="flex-table">
  <div class="flex-row header">
    <div class="flex-cell">Column 1</div>
    <div class="flex-cell">Column 2</div>
    <div class="flex-cell">Column 3</div>
  </div>
  <div class="flex-row">
    <div class="flex-cell">Cell 1</div>
    <div class="flex-cell">Cell 2</div>
    <div class="flex-cell">Cell 3</div>
  </div>
  .
  .
  .
</div>
```

CSS:
```
.flex-table {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
}

.flex-row {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: row;
}

.header {
  font-weight: bold;
}

.flex-cell {
  flex: 1;
  padding: 5px;
  border: 1px solid #ddd;
}
```

JavaScript:
```
function filterTable() {
  var input, filter, table, rows, cells, match;
  input = document.getElementById('searchInput');
  filter = input.value.toUpperCase();
  table = document.getElementById('flexTable');
  rows = table.getElementsByClassName('flex-row');

  for(var i = 1; i < rows.length; i++) {
    cells = rows[i].getElementsByClassName('flex-cell');
    match = false;
    for(var j = 0; j < cells.length; j++) {
      if(cells[j].innerHTML.toUpperCase().indexOf(filter) > -1) {
        match = true;
        break;
      }
    }
    if(match) {
      rows[i].style.display = '';
    } else {
      rows[i].style.display = 'none';
    }
  }
}
```

Note: This code may need additional error checking and modification depending upon specific requirements. This code is simply an example and may not be completely ready for production use.
<|end|>


