Develop a Python function that calculates the aggregate of all subarrays with an odd length. For more context, refer to this link: https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/sum-of-all-odd-length-subarrays/. Additionally, ensure that the function is efficient in terms of time complexity and space complexity.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
You can solve this problem in an efficient way with linear time complexity O(N) using a neat trick, instead of calculating the subarrays directly which will have higher complexity O(N^2). The trick is to realize that each element occurs in different odd-length subarrays, the count of which can be calculated by (i+1)*(n-i) (where i is the current index and n is the length of the array). 

Then since half of them will be even length subarrays, so we integer divide it by 2 to get the count of odd length subarrays for this element. If the count itself is odd, it means there's more odd length subarray, so we add 1. 

After getting the count, we multiply it with the element value to get the total sum from this element, then add it to the result. 

Here's the Python function:

```python
def sum_odd_length_subarrays(arr):
    res = 0
    n = len(arr)
    for i in range(n):
        res += ((i+1)*(n-i)+1)//2*arr[i]
    return res
```

In this function, we use a for loop to iterate through each element in the array. For each element, we calculate how many odd length subarrays it'll be in using the trick, then add the total sum from it to the result.

This function will handle any array with length from 0 to 10^5, and elements from 1 to 100, due to the constraints of the problem.
<|end|>


