Remember this 'transposition' won't yield a matrix that is the transpose in the traditional sense, because transposition (switching of columns and rows) is a concept defined for 2D matrices. The exact behavior on 3D matrices would depend on what specific transpose-like operation you want. The provided solution simply reverses the elements in each dimension. 

