Develop a recursive function that not only identifies the nth number in the Lucas sequence but also verifies if a given number is within the first nth numbers of the Lucas sequence. Additionally, the function should be able to handle exceptions such as the input being negative or not an integer. You should also provide a piece of code that may not be completely correct for reference purposes. This would challenge the candidate's ability to critically analyze, debug, and improve pre-existing code.
