I need to script the creation of app pools and websites on IIS 6.0. I have been able to create these using adsutil.vbs and iisweb.vbs, but don't know how to set the version of ASP.NET for the sites I have just created to 2.0.50727.0.

Ideally I would like to adsutil.vbs to update the metabase. How do I do this?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
To set a website to use a specific version of ASP.NET, you will have to use the aspnet_regiis.exe command. Following is an example of using the aspnet_regiis.exe command to set the ASP.NET version for a particular application:

```bash
C:\WINDOWS\Microsoft.NET\Framework\v2.0.50727\aspnet_regiis.exe -s W3SVC/1/ROOT/ApplicationName
```

In this command, `W3SVC/1/ROOT/ApplicationName` is the metabase path for the application. Replace `ApplicationName` with the name of your application.

Unfortunately, adsutil.vbs does not expose a method to update the ASP.NET version but you could wrap the aspnet_regiis.exe command within a .vbs or .cmd script to achieve your desired automation. You would still need to know the MetabasePath for the application, which you can get from adsutil.vbs. 

Here is an example vb script that can leverage aspnet_regiis.exe to update ASP.NET version for a specific application:

```vbscript
set WshShell = WScript.CreateObject("WScript.Shell")
appPath = "W3SVC/1/ROOT/ApplicationName"
aspnet = "C: & cd WINDOWS\Microsoft.NET\Framework\v2.0.50727 & aspnet_regiis.exe -s " & appPath
Return = WshShell.Run(aspnet, 0, true)
```

If you replace `ApplicationName` with your actual application name in above script, and save it as a .vbs file, running this script would change the ASP.NET version for that application to 2.0.50727.0.

Please note that aspnet_regiis.exe command needs to be run by a user who is a member of the Administrators group on the local computer. Also, the .NET version you are trying to apply must be installed on the computer. In above examples, it is applying .NET version 2.0.50727.0.
<|end|>


