</head>
<body>
    <form class="myForm">
        <label for="name">Name:</label><br>
        <input type="text" id="name" name="name"><br>
        <label for="email">Email:</label><br>
        <input type="text" id="email" name="email"><br>
        <label for="password">Password:</label><br>
        <input type="password" id="password" name="password"><br>
        <label for="birthday">Birthday:</label><br>
        <input type="date" id="birthday" name="birthday"><br>
        <input type="submit" value="Submit">
    </form>
</body>
</html>
```
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Below is an updated code that checks for validation using JavaScript. We verify if the form has any input in the required fields before submission, we also use regex to validate the email. Regarding the CAPTCHA check, this simply checks if a certain predefined answer (in this case '12345') is entered.

```html
<html>
<head>
    <style>
        .myForm {
            color: red;
            margin: 0 auto;
            width: 300px;
        }
        .myForm input[type="submit"] {
            background-color: blue;
            color: white;
        }
        .error {
            color: red;
        }
    </style>
    <script>
        function validateForm() {
            var name = document.forms["myForm"]["name"].value;
            var email = document.forms["myForm"]["email"].value;
            var password = document.forms["myForm"]["password"].value;
            var birthday = document.forms["myForm"]["birthday"].value;
            var captcha = document.forms["myForm"]["captcha"].value;

            var emailRegex = /\S+@\S+\.\S+/;

            if (name == "" || email == "" || password == "" || birthday == "" || captcha == "" || captcha != "12345" || !emailRegex.test(email)) {
                document.getElementById("error").innerHTML = "Please ensure all fields are filled correctly";
                return false;
            }
        }
    </script>
</head>
<body>
    <form class="myForm" name="myForm" onsubmit="return validateForm()">
        <div id="error" class="error"></div>
        <label for="name">Name:</label><br>
        <input type="text" id="name" name="name" required><br>
        <label for="email">Email:</label><br>
        <input type="email" id="email" name="email" required><br>
        <label for="password">Password:</label><br>
        <input type="password" id="password" name="password" required><br>
        <label for="birthday">Birthday:</label><br>
        <input type="date" id="birthday" name="birthday" required><br>
        <label for="captcha">Enter the code 12345:</label><br>
        <input type="text" id="captcha" name="captcha" required><br>
        <input type="submit" value="Submit">
    </form>
</body>
</html>
``` 

Please note that the CAPTCHA is as simple as inputting the hardcoded '12345'. If you need a more sophisticated CAPTCHA, you will need a server-side code or use a third-party service like Google reCAPTCHA.
<|end|>


