I need a function made using pure JS for accessing specific line of text file. I was looking for same questions and answers similar to this one but I couldn't find anything that matches my problem perfectly. I'm a beginner dev so I can't modify even the most similar programs (for example some which are returning whole file) so that's why I'm asking.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Do note that, JavaScript on its own cannot be used to read files due to browser security considerations. However, with Node.js, which is JavaScript library, we can perform file I/O operations.

Here is an example of a function in Node.js that reads a file and prints out a specific line.

You need to install 'readline' and 'fs' modules from npm.

```javascript
const fs = require('fs');
const readline = require('readline');

function readLineFromFile(filepath, lineNo) {
    const stream = readline.createInterface({
        input: fs.createReadStream(filepath),
        output: process.stdout,
        terminal: false
    });
    
    let currentLine = 0;
    
    stream.on('line', function(line) {
        if (currentLine === lineNo - 1) {
            console.log(line);
            stream.close();
        }
        currentLine++;
    });
}

readLineFromFile('yourfile.txt', 5); //replace 'yourfile.txt' with your file and 5 with the line number
```

In the above function, `readLineFromFile`, we create a readable stream with the `'readline'` package to read through the file line by line. When the target line number is reached, the line content will be logged to console and stop reading more line. Make sure you replace 'yourfile.txt' with your file path, and 5 with the line number you are looking for.

Again note that Node.js is server side JS and it won't work in a browser. This means that you can't use this approach if you're coding a website but it's okay for a stand alone running app.
<|end|>


