In MySQL, you cannot use "+" operator for string concatenation. You should use CONCAT or CONCAT_WS function instead.

Here is a revision of your function:

```sql
CREATE DEFINER=`root`@`localhost` FUNCTION `getDate`(getData date) RETURNS varchar(40) CHARSET utf8mb4
DETERMINISTIC
BEGIN
RETURN CONCAT(
    DAYNAME(getData), ' ', 
    DAY(getData), 
    CASE
        WHEN DAY(getData)  IN (1,21,31) THEN 'st'
        WHEN DAY(getData) IN (2,22) THEN 'nd'
        WHEN DAY(getData) IN (3,23) THEN 'rd'
        ELSE 'th'
    END, 
    ' ',
    MONTHNAME(getData), ' ',
    YEAR(getData)
 );
END;
```

This will return the date in the format that you specified: weekday day month year, for example: Monday 1st January 2022.
