```sql
CREATE TABLE customers (
    id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,
    name TEXT NOT NULL,
    email VARCHAR(255) UNIQUE NOT NULL
);

CREATE TRIGGER trg_customers_insert
BEFORE INSERT ON customers
FOR EACH ROW
BEGIN
    SELECT CASE
        WHEN NEW.email NOT LIKE '%_@__%.__%' THEN
        RAISE(ABORT, 'Invalid Email')
    END;
END;
```

In the modified SQL code above, a new table named 'customers' is created with 'id', 'name' and 'email' columns. The trigger, 'trg_customers_insert', will abort any INSERT operation trying to add an invalid email address into the 'email' column. The email validation is done by checking if the email follows the general pattern of emails, rather than using REGEXP function, as REGEXP function is not supported in SQLite by default and would require loading of external library. Please adjust according to your database engine if it supports REGEXP.
