You can design a Python class to represent an article in a tech-focused blog similar to the following example. This class named "BlogPost" has various attributes such as title, author, publication_date, content and tags to provide structure and functionality to the blog posts.

```python
class BlogPost:
    def __init__(self, title, author, publication_date, content, tags):
        self.title = title
        self.author = author
        self.publication_date = publication_date
        self.content = content
        self.tags = tags

    def get_summary(self):
        return self.content[:100]  # Get first 100 characters as summary

    def has_tag(self, tag):
        return tag in self.tags

    def __str__(self):
        return f'"{self.title}" by {self.author}, published on {self.publication_date}'
```

With this class, you can perform operations such as:

```python
# Create a new blog post
post = BlogPost('My tech article', 'Author Name', '2022-01-01', 'This is an interesting tech blog about...', ['python', 'tech'])

# Get a summary of the post
print(post.get_summary())

# Check if the post has a certain tag
print(post.has_tag('tech'))

# Print the post details
print(post)
```

