Given the piece of erroneous code below, correct and enhance it to create a cascading style sheet (CSS) directive. Your solution must globally apply a typographical vertical rhythm of 1.5 line height and a horizontal inter-character interval of 2 pixels. Your solution should ensure these styles are applied throughout the entirety of a web document's elements, including nested elements. The use of shorthand properties and CSS variables are encouraged for code efficiency. 

Erroneous Code Snippet:
```CSS
body {
   vertical rhythm: 1.5;
   horizontal space: 2px;
}
```
<|end|>
<|asst|>
CSS does not have properties like "vertical rhythm" and "horizontal space". Instead, you can use "line-height" for vertical spacing and "letter-spacing" for horizontal spacing. Here is the corrected and enhanced code snippet:

Corrected Code Snippet:
```CSS
:root {
   --spacing-vertical: 1.5;
   --spacing-horizontal: 2px;
}

* {
   line-height: var(--spacing-vertical);
   letter-spacing: var(--spacing-horizontal);
}
```
This CSS applies the line-height and letter-spacing to all HTML elements (represented by the "*" selector). The :root pseudo-class selector matches the root element of a tree representing the document. In HTML, :root represents the html element and is identical to the selector html, except that its specificity is higher. It's useful for declaring global CSS variables.
<|end|>


