<|asst|>
To change the URL, you need to update the Jenkins system configuration.

Here are the steps:

1. Open your Jenkins dashboard. Usually, it's accessible via "http://jenkins.abc.co:8080"

2. Click on "Manage Jenkins" in the left-sidebar.

3. From the configuration page opened, choose "Configure System".

4. In the "Jenkins Location" section, you will find two fields - "Jenkins URL" and "System Admin e-mail address".

5. Change the "Jenkins URL" from "http://jenkins.abc.co:8080" to "http://localhost:8080".

6. After you've made changes, Click on the "Save" button at the bottom of the page.

Please note, changing the URL to localhost might not always work, especially if you're trying to access Jenkins from a machine other than where it is installed. Localhost refers to the machine where the call originates, so if you try to access Jenkins via 'localhost' URL from a different machine than where Jenkins is installed, it will not find it.
<|end|>


