I've seen it mentioned in many blogs around the net, but I believe it shoud be discussed here.
What can we do when we have an MVC framework (I am interested in ZEND) in PHP but our host does not provide mod_rewrite?
Are there any "short-cuts"? Can we transfer control in any way (so that a mapping may occur between pages)? Any ideas?
Thank you :-)
<|end|>
<|asst|>
If your host doesn't support mod_rewrite or any other URL rewriting modules, in theory you can still have clean URLs by using the routing system provided by your framework.

Most modern PHP frameworks like Zend, Laravel, Symfony and others support routing functionality out of the box, and URLs are typically mapped to specific controller actions.

Here's a general example of what you could do. In your .htaccess, you can capture all requests and direct them to a single PHP file (usually index.php):

```
DirectoryIndex index.php
FallbackResource /index.php
```

And in your PHP script (index.php), you can manually parse the requested URL and run the appropriate controller and action:

```
<?php
// get the URL path
$path = parse_url($_SERVER['REQUEST_URI'], PHP_URL_PATH);

// then use the path to determine the controller and action
// assuming the URL is something like /controller/action
list(, $controller, $action) = explode('/', $path);

// sanitize controller and action names
$controller = preg_replace('/[^-a-zA-Z0-9_]/', '', $controller);
$action = preg_replace('/[^-a-zA-Z0-9_]/', '', $action);

// now load and run the controller and action
// the actual code here will depend on how your framework handles this
// but this should give you a basic idea
require_once "controllers/$controller.php";
$obj = new $controller();
$obj->$action();

```

And in Zend, the specific routing configuration to set up your routes manually would look something like this:

```php
$router = $ctrl->getRouter(); // returns a rewrite router by default
$router->addRoute(
    'user',
    new Zend_Controller_Router_Route('user/:username',
                                     array('controller' => 'user',
                                           'action' => 'info'))
);
```

This is very general and will need to be adjusted for your particular needs and constraints.

That said, the lack of URL rewrite can be a sign of a cheap host. If you want to use pretty URLs (which is usually a best practice), you might want to consider getting a better host.
<|end|>


