Fabricate a while loop utilizing the syntax and constructs of the Python programming language to exhibit all numerical entities, encompassing both integers and floating-point numbers, between 0 and 10 with increments of 0.1. 

Error Handling: Accommodate to addresses issues of precision allocation when working with floating-point numbers. Additionally, debug the following erroneous piece of code provided and incorporate it into your own solution.

```python
i = 0.0
while i <= 10:
    print(i)
i += 0.1
```
<|end|>
<|asst|>
The original provided code contains an error. The increment statement i += 0.1 is incorrectly located outside the while loop, causing an infinite loop. It must be contained inside the while loop.

Below is a corrected version of the code, incrementing with steps of 0.1 and correcting the precision problem by using Python's built-in round function:

```python
i = 0.0
while i <= 10.0:
    print(round(i, 2))  # to address precision issues
    i += 0.1
```

This will print out all numbers from 0 to 10, incremented by 0.1. Note that due to the way floating-point numbers are represented in computing systems, the printed results may not be perfectly accurate. Hence, rounding off to 2 decimal places ensures we're avoiding small discrepancies due to floating-point precision limitations. However, this solution will still show rounding errors for some numbers.

To avoid these errors altogether, a more accurate method would be using the decimal module in Python, which provides support for fast correctly rounded decimal floating point arithmetic.

```python
from decimal import Decimal

i = Decimal('0.0')
# some error can still occur due to representation of decimal numbers, so use a slightly larger end value
while i <= Decimal('10.0'):
    print(float(i))
    i += Decimal('0.1')
```

The above code will output floating-point numbers from 0 to 10 with increments of 0.1 without any rounding errors. However, note that the conversion of Decimal back to float for printing will still show the standard decimal representation of these float values.
<|end|>


