We will use Django, a high-level Python Web framework that encourages rapid development and clean, pragmatic design, for the main website and content management. Django comes with an admin panel that can be used as a content management dashboard. For the viewer count visualizer, we will use Django's built-in models and views along with Chart.js, an open-source JavaScript library, to display the data. We will also use Bootstrap for the front-end to ensure a clean and intuitive interface. The website will be hosted on Heroku, a cloud platform that supports Python. 

