I want to convert this to PHP, can you help?
def assemble(letters: str, string_connector: str) -> str:
    if string_connector.isdigit():
        return letters
    else:
        return string_connector.join(list(letters))
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Certainly, here is the equivalent PHP code for your Python function:

```php
function assemble($letters, $string_connector) {
    if (ctype_digit($string_connector)) {
        return $letters;
    } else {
        return implode($string_connector, str_split($letters));
    }
}
```

This PHP function does the same thing as your Python function. We use `ctype_digit()` in PHP equivalent to the `isdigit()` in Python to check if all the characters in the string are numeric. And then we use the `implode()` function as equivalent to `join()` and `str_split()` as equivalent to `list()`. Please note that `str_split()` function convert string to an array.
