Harness the principles of object-oriented programming to architect a sophisticated Java entity reception to depict distinct parameters like atmospheric warmth, moisture-ratio, and airstream speed, obtained and processed over a series of steps from a detailed weather forecast data.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
In this problem, we are asked to design a Java program using object-oriented principles to process weather data involving parameters like atmospheric warmth, moisture-ratio, and airstream speed. Here is an example how you can approach this problem:

```java
public class WeatherData {
    private double atmosphericWarmth;
    private double moistureRatio;
    private double airstreamSpeed;
    
    public WeatherData(double atmosphericWarmth, double moistureRatio, double airstreamSpeed){
        this.atmosphericWarmth = atmosphericWarmth;
        this.moistureRatio = moistureRatio;
        this.airstreamSpeed = airstreamSpeed;
    }
    
    // Getters
    public double getAtmosphericWarmth() {
        return this.atmosphericWarmth;
    }
    
    public double getMoistureRatio() {
        return this.moistureRatio;
    }
    
    public double getAirstreamSpeed() {
        return this.airstreamSpeed;
    }
    
    // Setters
    public void setAtmosphericWarmth(double newAtmosphericWarmth) {
        this.atmosphericWarmth = newAtmosphericWarmth;
    }

    public void setMoistureRatio(double newMoistureRatio) {
        this.moistureRatio = newMoistureRatio;
    }

    public void setAirstreamSpeed(double newAirstreamSpeed) {
        this.airstreamSpeed = newAirstreamSpeed;
    }
    
    @Override
    public String toString(){
        return "Atmospheric warmth: "+this.atmosphericWarmth+" Moisture ratio: "+this.moistureRatio+" Airstream speed: "+this.airstreamSpeed;
    }
}
```
In this code, we have defined a WeatherData class to encapsulate weather data that include atmospheric warmth, moisture ratio, and airstream speed. 

