Debug and improve a given piece of CSS that aims to style an HTML element with the characteristics of a block-level element. The CSS code provided below is wrongly affecting the positioning and layout of the HTML elements. Identify the errors and implement necessary corrections while explaining your logic.

#Given Code#:

```css
.block-style {
  float: left;
  position: relative;
  display: inline;
  margin: 10px;
  padding: 20px;
  border: 1px solid black;
}
```
Be sure to address how each CSS property should properly be used to style the block-level element. As part of your solution, include an HTML file that creates a demonstration of the corrected CSS.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
The given CSS contains a contradiction in properties. The 'display: inline;' is trying to make the element inline, but 'float: left;' and 'position: relative;' properties in the style are often used with block-level elements.

The 'display: inline;' property should be changed to 'display: block;'

Hence, the corrected CSS would look like:

```css
.block-style {
  float: left;
  position: relative;
  display: block;
  margin: 10px;
  padding: 20px;
  border: 1px solid black;
}
```
Explanation:

- 'float: left;' is used to wrap the text or other elements around the block to the right side.
- 'position: relative;' is used to position the block related to its normal position
- 'display: block;' is used to make this element behave like block level element.
- 'margin: 10px;' is used to keep space outside of the block from all sides.
- 'padding: 20px;' is used to keep space inside of the block from all sides.
- 'border: 1px solid black;' is used to draw a solid border of 1px around the block.

Below is the demonstration with an HTML file:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<style>
.block-style {
  float: left;
  position: relative;
  display: block;
  margin: 10px;
  padding: 20px;
  border: 1px solid black;
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="block-style">This is a block-level element styled with the corrected CSS</div>

</body>
</html>
```

This HTML file creates a div element with the class 'block-style'. This div is then styled using the corrected CSS. This block-level element will float to the left, it's positioned relative and has a margin of 10px around it, a padding of 20px, and a 1px black border around it.
<|end|>


