Write a Java program to create a class for a Circle, including the parameters for radius and color. Include a method for calculating the area, perimeter and the sector area of the circle. 

Ensure the circle color parameter is optional, and if not provided defaults to "white". The sector area method should take an angle as parameter and calculate the area of the sector that the angle creates. 

For added complexity, include error-checking code to ensure that an error is thrown if the sector angle given is greater than 360 degrees.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here is a Java program to solve the task: 

```java
public class Circle {

    private double radius;
    private String color;

    public Circle(double radius) {
        this.radius = radius;
        this.color = "white";
    }

    public Circle(double radius, String color) {
        this.radius = radius;
        this.color = color;
    }

    public double calculateArea() {
        return Math.PI * Math.pow(radius, 2);
    }

    public double calculatePerimeter() {
        return 2 * Math.PI * radius;
    }

    public double calculateSectorArea(double angle) {
        if (angle > 360) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Angle is larger than 360 degrees");
        }
        double area = (angle / 360) * Math.PI * Math.pow(radius, 2);
        return area;
    }

    public String getColor() {
        return color;
    }

    public void setColor(String color) {
        this.color = color;
    }

    public double getRadius() {
        return radius;
    }

    public void setRadius(double radius) {
        this.radius = radius;
    }
}

//Test the Circle class
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Circle circle = new Circle(5, "Red");
        System.out.println("Area: " + circle.calculateArea());
        System.out.println("Perimeter: " + circle.calculatePerimeter());
        System.out.println("Sector Area: " + circle.calculateSectorArea(60));

        Circle circle2 = new Circle(10);
        System.out.println("\nArea: " + circle2.calculateArea());
        System.out.println("Perimeter: " + circle2.calculatePerimeter());
        try {
            System.out.println("Sector Area: " + circle2.calculateSectorArea(400));
        } catch (IllegalArgumentException e) {
            System.out.println(e.getMessage());
        }
    }
}
```

This program creates a class for a Circle, including the parameters for the radius and color. It includes methods for calculating the area, perimeter and sector area of the circle. If no color is stated, it defaults to "white". The sector area method takes an angle as parameter and calculates the area of the sector the angle creates. 

If an angle greater than 360 is provided, the program throws an IllegalArgumentException.
<|end|>


