<|asst|>
Here is the solution in JavaScript:

```javascript
function calculateResult(a, b, c) {
  let result;
  switch (a) {
    case 0:
      result = b * c;
      break;
    case 1:
      result = b + c;
      break;
    default:
      result = b - c;
  }
  return result;
}
```

The above switch-case structure works similarly to the if-else clause and based on the value of 'a', it performs different operations on 'b' and 'c'.

Please adapt this example to the programming language you are using if it's not JavaScript, most modern languages support switch-case structure.
