Create a Java program for compressing a given String. The compression should return a count of repeated characters consecutively and the character.
"aaabbccccc"
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here's a simple Java program that compresses a string by counting repeated characters:

```java
public class StringCompressor {
    public static String compress(String input) {
        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();
        int count = 1;
        for (int i = 1; i < input.length(); i++) {
            if (input.charAt(i) == input.charAt(i - 1) && i < input.length() - 1) {
                count++;
            } else if (i == input.length() - 1 && input.charAt(i) == input.charAt(i - 1)) {
                count++;
                sb.append(input.charAt(i));
                sb.append(count);
            } else if (i == input.length() - 1 && input.charAt(i) != input.charAt(i - 1)) {
                sb.append(input.charAt(i-1));
                sb.append(count);
                sb.append(input.charAt(i));
                sb.append(1);
            } else {
                sb.append(input.charAt(i - 1));
                sb.append(count);
                count = 1;
            }
        }
        return sb.toString();
    }

    // Driver code
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String str = "aaabbccccc";
        System.out.println(compress(str));
    }
}
```
When you run this program with the input string "aaabbccccc", it returns "a3b2c5". This signifies that 'a' is repeated 3 times, 'b' is repeated 2 times and 'c' is repeated 5 times consecutively in the string.
<|end|>


