Craft a function in JavaScript that displays a detailed notification or alert. Additionally, the function should contain error-checking elements. It should handle exceptions if the input values are incorrect or if a delay in notifications happens due to network issues. Lastly, the function should also be able to format the notification message based on selected user preferences (e.g., bold, italic, underline etc).
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here's a basic example of how you could implement this in JavaScript:

```javascript
function notifyUser(message, preference = {}, delay = 0) {

    if(!message || typeof message !== 'string') {
        throw new Error("Invalid message input. Input must be a string.");
    }

    if(!preference || typeof preference !== 'object') {
        throw new Error("Invalid preference input. Input must be an object.");
    }

    if(!Number.isInteger(delay)) {
        throw new Error("Invalid delay input. Input must be an integer.");
    }

    setTimeout(function() {
        let formattedMessage = message;

        if (preference.bold) {
            formattedMessage = `<b>${formattedMessage}</b>`;
        }

        if (preference.italic) {
            formattedMessage = `<i>${formattedMessage}</i>`;
        }

        if (preference.underline) {
            formattedMessage = `<u>${formattedMessage}</u>`;
        }

        if('Notification' in window) {
            if(Notification.permission === 'granted') {
                new Notification(formattedMessage);
            } else if (Notification.permission !== 'denied') {
                Notification.requestPermission()
                    .then(permission => {
                        if(permission === 'granted') {
                            new Notification(formattedMessage);
                        }
                    })
                    .catch(err => console.error(err));
            }
        } else {
            console.log(formattedMessage);
        }
            
    }, delay * 1000);
}

// Example usage:

notifyUser("Hello, World!", {bold: true, underline: true}, 3);
```

This function first checks for exceptions (invalid input types). Then, it applies a delay (if specified), and formats the message according to the user's preferences. 

The formatted message is then displayed either as a browser notification (if the client supports it) or as a console log. For browser notifications, the function first confirms that the user has granted permission to display notifications. If not, it requests this permission.

Please note that for security reasons, browser notifications may not work directly from local files in some browsers (such as Chrome). Run this code on an actual server, or use a browser that allows local file access (like Firefox). Also, newer versions of Chrome require notifications to be generated in response to a user action (like a button click), so please logic your accordingly into your actual code.
<|end|>


