Here is a simple example of a React component accessing the Reddit API to fetch and display the top 10 highest-voted posts from the "Programming" subreddit. 

```jsx
import React, { useEffect, useState } from 'react';

const ProgrammingPosts = () => {
  const [posts, setPosts] = useState([]);

  useEffect(() => {
    fetch('https://www.reddit.com/r/programming/top.json?limit=10')
      .then(response => response.json())
      .then(data => setPosts(data.data.children.map(c => c.data)));
    }, []);
  
  return (
    <div>
      <h2>Top 10 Posts in Programming Subreddit</h2>
      <ul>
        {posts.map(post => (
          <li key={post.id}>
            <a href={post.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
              <h3>{post.title}</h3>
            </a>
            <p>Upvotes: {post.ups}</p>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </div>
  );
};

export default ProgrammingPosts;
```

This component first initiates an empty array state for 'posts' and then, upon component mount, it performs a fetch request to the Reddit API with the specified subreddit ('Programming') and the set constraint for posts (limit=10) to only take the top 10 posts.

When the fetch request resolves successfully, it injects the received array to 'setPosts' through mapping to extract the necessary data from 'children' and injects it into the 'posts' state. The 'useEffect' then re-renders the component to reflect the updated state.

Finally, the component performs a map function on 'posts' creating a list of linked post titles and their corresponding upvote count. These links when clicked open to a new tab.

Remember to handle errors properly in real-world applications. This is a basic example of how you can use Reddit's API to display the top 10 highest-voted posts from a subreddit.
<|end|>


