The Root Mean Square Error (RMSE) is a measure of how well a model can predict a single instance. Lower values of RMSE indicate better fit to a dataset. The fact that RMSE is similar for both training and testing indicates that your model generalizes well to unseen data.

However, you should also note that even though these metrics are good, it does not completely rule out the possibility of overfitting. You also need to ensure the model is reasonable and makes sense based on your understanding of the problem domain. It is also always a good practice to explore multiple different models and/or predictors before settling with one.
