Provided a sequence of positive integers and a specific target value, develop a Java algorithm that not only determines if the sequence contains a pair of numbers that add up to the proposed target sum, but also return all possible pairs that can make the sum. Moreover, augment your solution to return the pairs in ascending order with the smallest pair first. 

For instance, given arr = [2, 4, 6, 8, 10], target = 8, the algorithm should return: [[2,6], [4,4]]. If there are no such pairs, return an empty list. Now, optimize your solution to obtain an efficient algorithm.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here is the Java code that solves the problem:

```java
import java.util.Arrays;
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.HashMap;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[] arr = {2, 4, 6, 8, 10};
        int target = 8;
        ArrayList<int[]> result = findAllPairs(arr, target);
        for (int[] pair : result) {
            System.out.println(Arrays.toString(pair));
        }
    }
    
    public static ArrayList<int[]> findAllPairs(int[] arr, int target) {
        HashMap<Integer, Integer> map = new HashMap<>();
        ArrayList<int[]> result = new ArrayList<>();
        for (int i : arr) {
            if(map.containsKey(target - i)) {
                int[] pair = {i, target - i};
                Arrays.sort(pair);
                result.add(pair);
            } else {
                map.put(i, i);
            }
        }
        result.sort((pair1, pair2) -> {
            if(pair1[0] == pair2[0]) {
                return pair1[1] - pair2[1];
            } else {
                return pair1[0] - pair2[0];
            }
        });
        return result;
    }
}
```

In this solution, we use a HashMap to store the differences between target and the current number at each iteration. If a number exists in the map that equals the current difference, we found a pair of numbers that sums up to the target sum. And since we need to retain pairs in ascending order, we use `Arrays.sort()` function to sort each pair and `Collections.sort()` to sort the result list. The time complexity of this solution is O(n log n) because of the sorting.
<|end|>


