<|asst|>
There are some packages available in the Flutter ecosystem that may help you achieve this:

1. excel: A flutter package to create and read Microsoft Excel files. With this package, you can create a new Excel file and write data into it. You can read your existing Excel file too. Here is the link for the package: https://pub.dev/packages/excel

2. pdf: A flutter package for PDF creation, you can customize your page as per your need. This package can generate a PDF directly from your app. Here is the link for the package: https://pub.dev/packages/pdf

So, for accomplishing your task, you might need to use these two packages together. First, you need to use the excel package to fill in the data and then use the pdf package to convert it into a PDF.

Coding can be something like this:

```dart
// first add dependencies in pubspec.yaml
// dependencies:
//   excel: ^1.1.5
//   pdf: ^1.3.24

import 'package:excel/excel.dart';
import 'package:pdf/pdf.dart';
import 'package:pdf/widgets.dart' as pw;

void main() {
  var excel = Excel.createExcel(); // Create a new Excel file
  
  // Insert data into Excel file
  Sheet sheetObject = excel['SheetName'];
  sheetObject.cell(CellIndex.indexByString("A1")).value = 'Hello';
  sheetObject.cell(CellIndex.indexByString("B1")).value = 'World';

  // Save Excel file
  excel.encode().then((onValue) {
    File r"Path_to_destination/excel_file.xlsx")
      ..createSync(recursive: true)
      ..writeAsBytesSync(onValue);
  });  
  
  final pdf = pw.Document(); // Create a new pdf file
  
  // Insert data into pdf file
  pdf.addPage(pw.Page(
      build: (pw.Context context) => pw.Center(
        child: pw.Text('Hello World'),
      )));

  // Save pdf file
  final output = await getTemporaryDirectory();
  final file = File("${output.path}/example.pdf");
  await file.writeAsBytes(await pdf.save());
}```
The above script will create an excel file, fill it with 'Hello' and 'World' and save it. Then it will create a PDF file with 'Hello World', save it, and prepare it for printing. Modify it according to your needs and make sure to handle possible exceptions.

