Then, we have a function `add_variables` that uses `check_variables` to ensure both of its parameters `x` and `y` are in integer format before it attempts to add them. If one or both of them cannot be converted to integers, this function will raise an exception when `check_variables` is called.

Finally, we have a try-except block that attempts to calculate and print the sum of `x` and `y`. If an exception was raised when `add_variables` was called, it catches the exception and prints an error message instead of crashing the program.
