Design a doubly-linked list deletion function that effectively removes elements while preserving the intrinsic order and data structure.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
I'll provide a Python solution for creating and managing a doubly-linked list, including a function for deleting nodes:

```python
class Node:
    def __init__(self, data=None):
        self.data = data
        self.next = None
        self.prev = None

class DoublyLinkedList:
    def __init__(self):
        self.head = None

    # Adding data elements
    def add_node_end(self, data):
        if not self.head:
            self.head = Node(data)
        else:
            cur = self.head
            while cur.next:
                cur = cur.next
            new_node = Node(data)
            cur.next = new_node
            new_node.prev = cur

    # Deleting data elements
    def delete_node(self, data):
        cur = self.head
        while cur:
            # Node to delete is found
            if cur.data == data:
                # Node to delete is the head
                if cur.prev is None and cur.next is not None:
                    self.head = cur.next
                    self.head.prev = None
                # Node to delete is the last
                elif cur.next is None and cur.prev is not None:
                    cur.prev.next = None
                # Node to delete is in between
                elif cur.prev is not None and cur.next is not None:
                    cur.prev.next = cur.next
                    cur.next.prev = cur.prev
                # Node to delete is the only node
                elif cur.prev is None and cur.next is None:
                    self.head = None
                return True
            cur = cur.next
        return False   # Couldn't find the data in our list 

    # Printing elements of Doubly linked list
    def print_list(self):
        cur = self.head
        while cur:
            print(cur.data)
            cur = cur.next

# Driver program to test above
dll = DoublyLinkedList()
dll.add_node_end("Red")
dll.add_node_end("Green")
dll.add_node_end("Blue")
dll.print_list()
print("Deleting Red...")
dll.delete_node("Red")
dll.print_list()
print("Deleting Blue...")
dll.delete_node("Blue")
dll.print_list()
```
This program creates a Node class for creating individual nodes and a DoublyLinkedList class for managing those nodes. 

In the DoublyLinkedList class, we have methods for adding nodes to the end of the list, deleting nodes by data content, and printing the entire list. 

Deleting a node requires one full traversal of the list. In worst-case scenario, time complexity is O(n) where n is the number of elements in the list. The best-case scenario (deleting the head node) has a time complexity of O(1).
<|end|>


