I am trying to create calender event which has Google meet link. As of now i am able to create the event from ui but i have to do this from back-end and when i try to create service account json, i am not seeing calender api for access in the drop-down. 
I tried to search for documentation but i am ended up using oAuth type to access the api.
I am using node js so if there is any document to help me please assist.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
To access the Calendar API in backend and create an event with a Google Meet link, you will need to Authenticate with a service account that has access to Calendar API. Unfortunately, as of Sep 2021, creating a Google Hangout or Google Meet link through the Calendar API is not supported for service accounts. Even though it is possible to create a calendar event using the API, the conference data field (which includes the meet or hangout link) is read-only for service accounts and can only be used to read the link of the event that has already been created.

You can refer the information from the Google Workspace Developer documentation:
https://developers.google.com/google-apps/calendar/concepts/events-calendars

However, you can use OAuth 2.0 to authorize this. A customer with an authenticated request and write access can take advantage of automatic conference data creation for user-organised events. Here are the steps for setting this up:

1. Go to Google Cloud Console: https://console.cloud.google.com/

2. Create a new project if you don't have one.

3. In the sidebar, Click `APIs & Services -> Credentials`.

4. Click `Create Credentials`.

5. Select `OAuth client ID`.

6. In the `Create OAuth client ID` screen, for Application type, choose `Web application`.

7. In the `Authorized JavaScript origins` field, add your app domain.

8. In the `Authorized Redirect URIs` field, add your redirect uri.

9. Click `Save`.

Here is the sample code to create an event using OAuth in Node.js:

```
const {google} = require('googleapis');
const {OAuth2} = google.auth;
const calendar = google.calendar('v3');

const oauth2Client = new OAuth2(
  'YOUR_CLIENT_ID',
  'YOUR_CLIENT_SECRET',
  'REDIRECT_URI'
);

// get access_token using the authorization code
oauth2Client.getToken('AUTHORIZATION_CODE', (err, token) => {
  if (err) return console.error('Error retrieving access token', err);
  oauth2Client.setCredentials(token);

  const event = { // Your event data
    'summary': 'Meeting',
    'location': 'Virtual',
    'description': 'Discuss about the project',
    'start': {
      'dateTime': '2022-01-14T09:00:00-07:00',
      'timeZone': 'America/Los_Angeles',
    },
    'end': {
      'dateTime': '2022-01-14T17:00:00-07:00',
      'timeZone': 'America/Los_Angeles',
    },
    'conferenceData': {
      'createRequest': {
        'requestId': '7qxalsvy0e'
       }
     }
  };

  calendar.events.insert({
    auth: oauth2Client,
    calendarId: 'primary',
    resource: event,
    conferenceDataVersion: 1,
  }, (err, event) => {
    if (err) {
      console.log('Error: ' + err);
      return;
    }
    console.log('Event created: %s', event.htmlLink);
  });
})
```

In the above code do remember to replace AUTHORIZATION_CODE, YOUR_CLIENT_ID, YOUR_CLIENT_SECRET and REDIRECT_URI with your actual values.

Please note that automatic conference data creation (which generates the meet link) is still a Beta feature according to the documentation at the time of writing.

Keep in mind that you will have to exchange the authorization code that the client (frontend) provides for an access token+refresh token. The client can get this code from the Google OAuth flow, and will have to send it to your server for you to exchange and store for future use. 

Refer to following Google API client library for OAuth 2.0: 
https://developers.google.com/api-client-library/javascript/start/start-js#get-access-tokens-from-the-googleauth-object

If you have any more questions, leave them in the comment, happy to help.
<|end|>


