Create an SQL command that will append new data into a distinct table also keeping in mind the constraint that the 'email' field must be unique (i.e., no two users can have the same email). If a user with similar email already exists, the command should update the user's name, without changing the 'id'. 

Table Designation: users
Column Parameters: id, name, email
Specific Data to Insert: 1, John Doe, john@example.com
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Assuming you are using MySQL, you would use the `INSERT INTO ... ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE` command. This command checks for duplicate entries based on PRIMARY KEY or a UNIQUE index.

For it to work, your 'email' field should be set as UNIQUE. Please note that if the 'email' field isn't set as UNIQUE in your database, you should alter your table to enforce this uniqueness constraint:

```sql
ALTER TABLE users
ADD UNIQUE (email);
```
Now for the insertion/updation of data, use the following SQL command:

```sql
INSERT INTO users (id, name, email) 
VALUES (1,'John Doe','john@example.com')
ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE name = 'John Doe';
```
This command will insert a new row with the given values if an entry with a similar email doesn't already exist. If it does exist, it will update the 'name' field of that row without changing the 'id'. Please note that this is a MySQL solution, other databases may require a different solution.
