I need to know about Epoll On linux System.

Could you recommend manual or guides about epoll library?

need more detailed guides. it's better to have some examples.

help me. and Thank you for reading.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Epoll is a Linux kernel system call for input/output operations. It's a scalable I/O event notification mechanism, primarily used in asynchronous I/O and is considered to be more efficient than traditional polling.

Online Guides:

1. The blog post "Epoll – An efficient I/O event notification facility for Unix and Linux" (https://devarea.com/epoll-efficient-io-event-notification-facility-for-unix-and-linux/#.YdIeJujPzIV) provides a detailed walkthrough of how to work with epoll. The author includes example codes for a simple HTTP server and client.

2. The blog post "Linux System Programming: Using epoll instead of select()" (https://jvns.ca/blog/2017/06/03/async-io-on-linux--select--poll--and-epoll/) explains asynchronous IO, select(), poll(), and epoll(). This post features example codes and vivid diagrams.

3. The epoll(7) - Linux man page (http://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man7/epoll.7.html) provides a brief overview of the epoll interface and its usage. 

4. IBM Developer blog has a post titled "Building scalable I/O on Linux: Part 2: An introduction to the epoll API" (https://developer.ibm.com/articles/l-epoll/) that offers a thorough introduction to the epoll API and includes a basic example of epoll usage.

5. "Linux Mastery: Master the Linux Command Line in 11.5 Hours" by Ziyad Yehia (Udemy course). It’s not exclusively about epoll but it covers Linux programming comprehensively with lot of examples.

Books:

1. "The Linux Programming Interface" by Michael Kerrisk. It's a detailed reference to Linux and UNIX system programming which has a dedicated chapter on epoll.

2. "Linux System Programming: Talking Directly to the Kernel and C Library" by Robert Love. Again, epoll isn't the central theme but the book delves into the subject to some length.

Remember that epoll is a relatively advanced topic in Linux programming; Understanding network programming and the basics of Unix/Linux system call is beneficial before studying epoll.
<|end|>


