Create a JavaScript code snippet that transforms every string element within a specific array and every second level string in a nested array into upper case characters. Additionally, ensure the code ignores any non-string elements.
arr: ["this", "is", ["an", "example"], 2, "array"]
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here is a JavaScript solution using recursion to handle arrays nested at any depth:

```javascript
function transformStringsToUpper(arr) {
  // Iterate over the array.
  for(let i = 0; i < arr.length; i++){
    // Check if the current element is a string.
    if(typeof arr[i] === 'string'){
      // If it is, transform to upper case.
      arr[i] = arr[i].toUpperCase();
    }
    
    // If the current element is an array, use recursion.
    else if(Array.isArray(arr[i])){
      arr[i] = transformStringsToUpper(arr[i]);
    }
  }
  return arr;
}

let array = ["this", "is", ["an", "example"], 2, "array"];
console.log(transformStringsToUpper(array));
```

This script works by checking the type of each element in the passed array. If the element is a string, it's transformed to upper case. If the element is a nested array, the function calls itself with that array as an argument, effectively applying the transformations to any strings found in nested arrays, regardless of their depth.
<|end|>


