If you're not on a Linux system or if your firewall is not iptables, the principle remains the same but the command used will be different. You will need to use the specific commands or API functions available to interface with your firewall. Always ensure to handle this with care as blocking certain IP addresses or ports can disrupt expected network traffic for your applications or system.

