I've got an MDI application written in Delphi 2006 which runs XP with the default theme. 

Is there a way of controlling the appearance of the MDI Children to avoid the large XP-style title bar on each window? 

I've tried setting the `BorderStyle` of the `MDIChildren` to `bsSizeToolWin` but they are still rendered as normal Forms.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
To avoid the large XP-Style title bar for each MDI children window, you will have to modify how the OS renders those bars. In other words, you have to use the Windows API to achieve this.

However, I would discourage trying this approach because it leads to bad user interface practices where your application does not respect the user's OS settings. 
It's generally a negative user experience to intentionally deviate from what users have come to expect from their usual operating system behavior.

The recommended modern approach to MDI is to drop it altogether and switch to a different form/application architecture. You could use a Tabbed interface, Dockable windows or just open new instances of your forms. 

The big issue with MDI is that it often confuses users more than it helps. So, I would suggest moving away from that architecture if you are able to. If you must use MDI, then respect the OS settings for how MDI Children are rendered.

Here's an alternative approach you can use to pare down the appearance of the child windows:

1. Use TFrame
Instead of creating new forms for each window, you can use Frames. 

2. Place TFrame on a TPageControl
Each time you need a new "window", create a new TabSheet on a TPageControl and place your frame on it.

This gives you an interface similar to modern tabbed web browsers and IDEs and is far more understandable to users. It also conserves screen space.

Example of usage:

```delphi
var
  mFrame: TmFrame;
begin
  mFrame := TmFrame.Create(self);
  mFrame.Parent := PageControl1;
  mFrame.Align := alClient;
end;
```
In the above code, `TmFrame` is the custom frame which you have created and `PageControl1` is the `TPageControl` on your main form. Each time this code executes, a new instance of your frame will appear on a new tab in the `TPageControl`.
<|end|>


