I am working with a three dimensional numpy array and I am trying to understand how to use Boolean indexing. I have been using for-loop but I want to switch to Boolean indexing for efficiency. However, I am encountering an error: ValueError: boolean index array should have 1 dimension boolean index array should have 1 dimension.
Here is my attempt:
 arr_temp = arr.copy()
 mask = arry_temp &lt; n1
 mask2 = arry_temp &lt; n2
 mask3 = mask ^ mask3
 arr[mask] = 0
 arr[mask3] = arry[mask3] + 5
 arry[~mask2] = 30 
Specifically, I want values in arr that are lower than n1 to change into 0, values that are greater or equal to n2 to be 30 and others add 5. (n1, n2) might be different for different layers, but n1 &lt; n2 for sure.
The error occurs on mask3. I am new to this so I know the code above is not efficient trying to work out it.
