Create a MongoDB database with two collections for storing users and groups. The users collection should have fields for name, email, and group_id.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
MongoDB is a NoSQL database which mean it doesn't support conventional SQL syntax to create a database, tables(collections in MongoDB term), and insert data. Instead, you just have to use the database and it will be created on the fly when the data is inserted into collections.

You can use MongoDB shell or drivers for MongoDB in different languages to interact with the MongoDB server. Here, I will provide steps that you can execute in MongoDB shell. However, please note that the following steps are conceptual, structure defining and such structural definitions are not required in MongoDB as it is schema-less. The structure of the data can be defined on the application level:

```javascript
use MyDatabase;

db.createCollection('users');
db.createCollection('groups');

db.users.insert({
    name: 'John',
    email: 'john@example.com',
    group_id: ObjectId() //You can insert the specific ObjectID of the group.
});

db.groups.insert({
    _id : ObjectId(),
    groupName: 'Admin'
});
```

In `db.createCollection('users') and db.createCollection('groups');` command to create a new collections in MongoDB. The collection will store Users and groups detail. 

`db.users.insert() and db.groups.insert();` These commands add users and groups to collections respectively.

Please note that in MongoDB, each document stored in a collection requires a unique `_id`. You can let MongoDB auto-assign a unique `_id` (an ObjectId), or you can manually specify the `_id` to the document. 

In the example provided above, the `group_id` in the `users` collection is intended to link to a groups document in the `groups` collection. This is a concept of referencing, you store the `_id` of one document in another document as a reference to "link" them together.

Please also note that this demonstration assumes you have some specific ObjectID value to provide for `group_id`. In a real scenario, this value would be coming either from newly created Group document or from an existing one. It isn't usually a randomly set value.

Additionally, make sure to have MongoDB server running before executing these commands.
<|end|>


