<|asst|>
The problem lies in this line of your code: 

```c
printf("%s", *file);
```

You're dereferencing the pointer to the string with "*", which isn't needed in this case. `printf` with `%s` expects a `char*`, but `*file` is of type `char`. 

Instead, it should be:

```c
printf("%s", file);
```

So, your correct code will be:

```c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>

char *askFile()
{
    printf("Enter a file: ");
    char *file = malloc(512 * sizeof(char));
    scanf("%s", file);

    return file;
}

int main()
{
    char *file = askFile();
    printf("%s", file);

    free(file); // don't forget to free the memory

    return 0;
}
```
