Build a program that prints out the prime numbers between 1 and 100
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here is a simple Python program that prints out the prime numbers between 1 and 100:

```python
for num in range(1, 101):
    if num > 1:   # prime numbers are greater than 1
        for i in range(2, num):
            if (num % i) == 0:   # check for factors
                break
        else:   # no factors found, hence it is a prime number
            print(num)
```

This program works by iterating over all the numbers from 1 to 100 (in the outer "for" loop). Within that loop, for each number it then tries to divide it by all the numbers preceding it (in the inner "for" loop). If it finds any number that divides it without a remainder, it breaks out of the inner loop and moves on to the next number. If it doesn't find any such number, it means the current number is a prime number and it gets printed.
<|end|>


