AppTopbar is common layout of all pages.
when i click onchange AppTopbar.vue is only affectet AppTopbar page only.
but i want to if onchange AppTopbar.vue to triger Products.vue and all pages also
how to solve this?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
There are a few ways to share data or trigger methods on other components, here are some simple examples:

1. Using Vuex (Recommended approach when dealing with complex state):

First, you would need to setup Vuex in your project. Then, you can commit a mutation or dispatch an action from your `AppTopbar.vue` and use either getters or computed properties in your `Products.vue` to react to that change.

2. Emit an event from `AppTopbar.cue`:

From `AppTopbar.vue`:

```vue
this.$emit('shopChanged', event.value.value);
```

In your parent component (assuming `AppTopbar` and `Products` are siblings):

```vue
<AppTopbar @shopChanged="updateShop"/>
<Products :shopId="currentShopId"/>
```

And in your Vue instance:

```vue
data() {
  return {
    currentShopId: null
  }
},
methods: {
  updateShop(shopId) {
    this.currentShopId = shopId;
  }
}
```

3. Using an EventBus:

First, create an `EventBus`:

```javascript
import Vue from 'vue';
export const EventBus = new Vue();
```

Then, in `AppTopbar.vue`, emit the event:

```javascript
EventBus.$emit('shopChanged', event.value.value);
```

And, in `Products.vue`, listen to that event:

```javascript
created() {
  EventBus.$on('shopChanged', this.updateShop);
},
beforeDestroy() {
  EventBus.$off('shopChanged', this.updateShop);
},
methods: {
  updateShop(shopId) {
    // Do something with shopId
  }
}
```

Just remember to unsubscribe from the event when the component is destroyed to avoid memory leaks. This also helps avoid unexpected behavior when the `Products.vue` component is recreated, as would be the case with route navigation.
<|end|>


