def generate_float
  number = rand.round(2)
  if number >= 0 && number <=1
    return number
  else
    return 'Invalid value. Please generate another floating point number.'
  end
end
```

This method takes no arguments and returns a random floating-point number between 0 and 1, rounded to two decimal places. Because `rand` generates a random floating-point number between 0 and 1 by default, there is actually no need to check whether the number is within these boundaries because `rand` always guarantees that.
  
