<|asst|>
To mark a checkout as completed, you would typically need to process a payment. Shopify's API does not have a built-in mechanism that allows you to directly mark a checkout as complete.

But, if you want to make the checkout status to be "completed" without actual payment for test purposes, then you would need to create a test payment gateway or a bogus gateway. Be mindful though because this is usually for development purposes only and shouldn't be used on a live/production store.

As you have mentioned that "checkoutCompleteFree" is throwing a "Payment Pending" error, this suggest that there may have been a charge associated with your checkout. Please ensure that the checkout you are trying to complete is indeed free of any charges.

For the frontend, normally, when a user completes a checkout (by going through the entire payment process), Shopify automatically updates the checkout's status to "completed". 

The administrative functionality in the Shopify admin interface does not provide options to manually complete a checkout, they can only be archived or emailed.

Remember, the Shopify API treats Checkouts and Orders as separate objects. As per Shopify's flow, a Checkout object is used until the point where a customer completes the checkout. After that, it turns into an Order object which indicates a successful transaction.

For complex use cases, you might want to consider working with Shopify’s Storefront API or possibly some of the more advanced third-party applications that integrate with Shopify.

Lastly, it is always recommended to refer to the current API documentation specific to the API version that you are using and if in doubt, consult with a development professional or reach out to Shopify support.
