Give me a detail way to push a simple CRUD app to GCP APP engine
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here is a step-by-step guide to deploy a simple CRUD (Create, Read, Update, Delete) application on Google Cloud Platform (GCP) App Engine using Python. Please adjust any language preferences or code as per your preference.

Prerequisites: 

1. A Google Cloud Account.
2. A Project in GCP.
3. Google Cloud SDK installed on the local machine.
4. A simple CRUD app.

Steps to push:

Step 1: Test your application

Make sure your APP runs locally without any error since it needs to work perfectly before pushing it to App Engine.

Step 2: Create a Project in GCP

Log on to the Google Cloud Console. Create a new Project and enable billing for your project. Keep track of your project ID.

Step 3: Install GCP SDK

Install the Google Cloud SDK on your local machine as it will be required for communication between your machine and the GCP.

Step 4: Initialize App Engine

Use command prompt or terminal and navigate to your project folder. Then start App Engine by using this command:

```
gcloud app create
```

Follow the instructions as appeared and set the relevant region.

Step 5: Set the Project

Initialize your SDK to your project with:

```
gcloud config set project YOUR_PROJECT_ID
```

Replace YOUR_PROJECT_ID with your actual project ID.

Step 6: Prepare App Engine Configuration file

You need to create an app.yaml file in your CRUD app root folder. This is the configuration file for your App Engine.

Here's a simple example for a Python app:

```
runtime: python38
entrypoint: gunicorn -b :$PORT main:app
automatic_scaling:
  target_cpu_utilization: 65
  min_instances: 1
  max_instances: 10

env_variables:
  CLOUD_STORAGE_BUCKET: YOUR_PROJECT_ID
```

Replace "YOUR_PROJECT_ID" with your project's ID.

Step 7: Deploying the Application:

You are ready to deploy your application to App Engine:

```
gcloud app deploy
```

After a few minutes (or longer depending on the size of your app), your application will be live at YOUR_PROJECT_ID.appspot.com

This is a simple and detailed way to push a basic CRUD app to GCP App Engine. Further configurations might be needed depending on the complexity and needs of your app.

Remember to always safeguard sensitive data, such as ID, secrets, and keys, by not exposing them or using them directly in codes. Researchers should use Cloud Key Management Service or Environment variables where necessary.

The guide assumes a general understanding of GCP and Python. If some part seems confusing, it is recommended to refer to Google Cloud Platform's documentation or some Python tutorials, so you understand better what each code snippet is being used for.
<|end|>


