```csharp
Name:<br />
<%=Html.TextBox("txtName",null,new { @class="myCssClass"})%><br />
```

In the above example, the curly braces `{ @class="myCssClass"}` inside the Html.TextBox() helper method denote an anonymous object that contains the HTML attributes. The `@` before `class` is needed because `class` is a reserved word in C#. The helper will convert this to `class="myCssClass"` in the HTML output, which applies the CSS class to the text box.
