// The function requires a slice of integers and outputs a 2-element array of integers. The operation to be performed should yield the summation of cubed values and the resulting quantity of squared values multiplication for every entity in the slice. When the input list contains no elements, the cube sum defaults to 0 and the square product automatically becomes 1. See examples below:
// >>> In the scenario of CubeSumSquareProduct([]), the outcome will be (0, 1)
