Construct a C++ function that consumes a vector composed of decimal numerical values alongside its corresponding size as duo parameters, the function should calculate the median from the provided data set. In addition, the function should be able to handle outliers and ignore them in the calculation. Vector = {1.5, 3.0, 4.5, 2.5, 5000.0, 5.0}, length = 6.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
First, I want to clarify on how we define "outliers". There are many ways to define what outliers are. I will use the Interquartile Range (IQR) method to identify outliers. Here's a program that calculates the median ignoring the outliers.

```C++
#include <algorithm>
#include <vector>
#include <iostream>

double calculateMedian(std::vector<double> &numbers) {
    std::sort(numbers.begin(), numbers.end());
        
    double q1, q3, iqr;
    if (numbers.size() % 2 == 0) {
        //if size is even
        q1 = (numbers[numbers.size() / 4] + numbers[numbers.size() / 4 - 1]) / 2;
        q3 = (numbers[numbers.size() * 3 / 4] + numbers[numbers.size() * 3 / 4 - 1]) / 2;
    } else {
        //if size are odd numbers
        q1 = numbers[numbers.size() / 4];
        q3 = numbers[numbers.size() * 3 / 4];
    }

    iqr = q3 - q1;
    double lowerBound = q1 - 1.5 * iqr;
    double upperBound = q3 + 1.5 * iqr;
        
    // Remove numbers that fall below the lower bound and above the upper bound
    std::vector<double> cleanedNumbers;
    for (double num : numbers) {
        if (num < lowerBound || num > upperBound) continue;
        cleanedNumbers.push_back(num);
    }
        
    if (cleanedNumbers.size() % 2 == 0) {
        // if the length of cleaned numbers is even
        return (cleanedNumbers[cleanedNumbers.size() / 2 - 1] + cleanedNumbers[cleanedNumbers.size() / 2]) / 2;
    } else {
        // if the length of cleaned numbers is odd
        return cleanedNumbers[cleanedNumbers.size() / 2];
    }
}

int main() {
    std::vector<double> numbers = {1.5, 3.0, 4.5, 2.5, 5000.0, 5.0};
    std::cout << "Median: " << calculateMedian(numbers) << std::endl;
    return 0;
}
```

This code first sorts the vector in ascending order to find the quartiles. It calculates the IQR, and then finds the lower and upper bounds for outliers. It then filters out values that are outside these bounds, and finally calculates the median of the reamining numbers.
<|end|>


