Mongodb compass UI unresponsive when a collection size is more than 30MB, and average size of document could more than 5MB.
Is there any reason why it is slow, or is there any limitations on collection or document sizes.
Mongodb compass help
<|end|>
<|asst|>
MongoDB Compass is a graphical interface that lets you visualize your data, run queries, and more. However, it is known to become slow or unresponsive when dealing with large amounts of data. 

The reason for this is that MongoDB Compass was not optimized for large datasets. It tends to pull the entire dataset into memory, which can be a problem when dealing with large datasets or particularly large documents. This can cause your system to run out of memory, leading to the UI becoming slow or unresponsive.

In terms of document size, MongoDB does have a limitation of 16MB per document, as per BSON document size limit. If documents are larger than this, they may need to be split into multiple documents. 

If you need to work with large amounts of data often, you might want to consider a different tool. Alternatively, you can try increasing the available memory on your system, or work with smaller subsets of your data at a time. 

You can also minimize the fields to return in your query in MongoDB Compass to reduce the size of the result set and make the UI more responsive. 

Finally, always keep MongoDB and MongoDB Compass up to date, as new versions often incorporate performance enhancements optimizations.
<|end|>


