Output all items from an array in descending order in Java, but do so without using built-in sort functions. In addition, ensure that duplicate values within the array are only printed once.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
You could solve this problem using Java via implementing a simple 'Bubble Sort' algorithm, which sorts the array in descending order, and while printing out the result checking that the value isn't the same as the previous value.

Here's the code to solve this problem:

```java
import java.util.*;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int arr[] = {12, 34, 11, 9, 3, 2, 2, 34, 11};
        bubbleSort(arr);
        printArray(arr);
    }

    static void bubbleSort(int arr[]) {
        int n = arr.length;
        for (int i = 0; i < n - 1; i++)
            for (int j = 0; j < n - i - 1; j++)
                if (arr[j] < arr[j + 1]) {
                    int temp = arr[j];
                    arr[j] = arr[j + 1];
                    arr[j + 1] = temp;
                }
    }

    static void printArray(int arr[]) {
        int n = arr.length;
        int prev = arr[0];
        System.out.print(prev + " ");

        for (int i = 1; i < n; i++) {
            if (arr[i] != prev) {
                System.out.print(arr[i] + " ");
                prev = arr[i];
            }
        }
    }
}
```

The above program takes an array `arr[]` and implements the bubble sort algorithm on it. After sorting the array, it prints out the array, making sure to check for and ignore duplicates.
<|end|>


