Produce an arbitrary character sequence utilizing C# programming language.
Character sequence length: 8
<|end|>
<|asst|>
In the C# programming language, you can use the `System.Random` class to generate a random sequence of alphanumeric characters. Here is an example of how you can do it:

```csharp
using System;

class Program
{
    static void Main()
    {
        // Create a new instance of Random class
        Random rand = new Random();
        
        // Crare a constant string with all possible characters that you want in your string
        const string chars = "ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ0123456789";

        // Generate a random string
        string randomString = new string(Enumerable.Repeat(chars, 8).Select(s => s[rand.Next(s.Length)]).ToArray());

        // Print the random string
        Console.WriteLine(randomString);
    }
}
```

This program will output a random sequence of 8 characters, where each character can be any uppercase alphabet character or digit. The `Enumerable.Repeat(chars, 8).Select(s => s[rand.Next(s.Length)]).ToArray()` line creates an 8-length array of random characters from the `chars` string, and then the `new string(...)` code turns that array into a string.

You can change the possible characters and the length of the string by modifying the `chars` constant and the number of repetitions in the `Enumerable.Repeat(...)` call, respectively.

Note: don't forget to use `System.Linq` namespace to enable the `Enumerable.Repeat` function. Add `using System.Linq;` at the top of your code.

```csharp
using System;
using System.Linq;

class Program
{
    //... The rest of the code
}
```
