2. DART-Europe E-theses Portal: A partnership of research libraries and library consortia who are working together to improve global access to European research theses. 

3. EthOS (British Library): A British Library service that provides full text of a wide range of theses, although it requires payment for some theses.

4. Open Access Theses and Dissertations (OATD): An index of over 2.5 million theses and dissertations. Free to use. 

5. Networked Digital Library of Theses and Dissertations (NDLTD): An international organization dedicated to promoting the adoption, creation, use, dissemination, and preservation of electronic theses and dissertations (ETDs).

Remember to apply the filters or use the right keywords to find master's dissertations/theses in risk management & quantitative finance.
You can also approach universities directly and ask them about accessing their theses collections, or try contacting the authors of specific theses directly. Keep in mind that while not all universities provide open access theses, some of them do. Examples include University of Cambridge, Massachusetts Institute of Technology and North Carolina State University.
