can you make this snippet c#-ready?
def fibfib(n: int, dp={0: 0, 1: 0, 2: 1}):
    """
    Function to calculate FibFib(n).
    """
    if n in dp: # Directly return value if in dictionary to skip unnecessary calculations
        return dp[n]

    elif n > 2:  # Positive Case
        dp[n] = fibfib(n-1, dp) + fibfib(n-2, dp) + fibfib(n-3, dp)
        return dp[n]

    else: # Negative Case
        dp[n] = fibfib(n+3, dp) - fibfib(n+2, dp) - fibfib(n+1, dp)
        return dp[n]
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Sure, I can convert the given python function to C#. 

In this implementation, I'll use a Dictionary of type (int, long) as the C# counterpart to Python's dictionary - just note that I'm assuming the numbers will not exceed the limit of long. 

Here is the C# implementation:

```csharp
using System.Collections.Generic;

public static class FibFibCalculator
{
    private static Dictionary<int, long> Dp = new Dictionary<int, long> { { 0, 0 }, { 1, 0 }, { 2, 1 } };

    public static long FibFib(int n)
    {
        if (Dp.ContainsKey(n))
            return Dp[n];

        if (n > 2)
            Dp[n] = FibFib(n - 1) + FibFib(n - 2) + FibFib(n - 3);
        else
            Dp[n] = FibFib(n + 3) - FibFib(n + 2) - FibFib(n + 1);

        return Dp[n];
    }
}
```

Remember to call the `FibFib` function through the `FibFibCalculator` class as it is defined inside it as a static method.
<|end|>


