I have created an image that uses `zsh` as entrypoint and attached it to my Sagemaker Studio domain (I can use `zsh` just fine if I test the image locally using `docker run`), but when opening a terminal in the Studio with this custom image, I see it falls back to `bash`.
Is there a way to actually have the Studio terminal use the image I've provided?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Amazon SageMaker Studio uses a system shell which defaults to bash, irrespective of the entrypoint specified in custom images. The entrypoint of image in SageMaker determines only the runtime for Jupyter kernels.

If you want to use `zsh` in a terminal session within SageMaker Studio:

1. You have to ensure `zsh` is installed in your Studio's Image.
2. Open a new terminal in SageMaker Studio.
3. Run `zsh` command to switch to the `zsh` shell from the default bash shell for the current terminal session. 

Remember that SageMaker Studio can't change the default shell to `zsh`, and this needs to be done for every new Terminal session. As an alternative, you could add the `zsh` command to your bash profile so it's executed automatically each time a new terminal session is started. 

Note: Make sure your custom image has all the necessary permissions and isn't violating any security principles by changing default shells. 

For more information, you can refer to [Use Custom SageMaker Studio Images](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/studio-byoi.html).
<|end|>


