We have a table partitioned by key (binary(16))
Is there any option to calculate which partition record will go outside of MySQL?
What is the hash function (not linear one)?
The reason is to sort the CSV files outside MySQL and insert them in parallel in right partitions with LOAD DATA INFILE and then index in parallel too.
I can't find the function in MySQL docs
<|end|>
<|asst|>
MySQL uses internal algorithms to calculate partition keys, and this is not publicly disclosed. Hence, calculating where a record will go to a specific partition outside of MySQL server is not feasible.

However, you can still implement mass data ingestions using a parallel loader.
And while indexing, MySQL will automatically write data into appropriate partitions in parallel if the system resources allow it.

You can also design your partitioning keys in such a way so that you can predict which partition a row will go to, for example, range based on a timestamp or a user id. But it cannot be manually controlled.

Another option is to use external tools like Apache Nifi to preprocess and partition your data before loading it into MySQL based on your own custom function. But this would add another layer of complexity to your data processing pipeline.

Furthermore, note that MySQL itself manages partitions, So if you try to manually parallel load data using LOAD DATA INFILE into partitions, it could result in partition imbalance. 

Lastly, in terms of your requirement for the hash function, MySQL uses an internal hash function that isn't disclosed. MySQL supports two hash partitioning types: linear and non-linear (the exact function of which is not documented). The `KEY` partitioning type uses MySQL's internal hashing on the partitioning key value. The number of partitions must be a power of 2 if you use the `LINEAR KEY` partition type, however this restriction does not apply to the `KEY` partition type.
<|end|>


