A man has a fortune of $600k. He wants to divide it between his two children so that one gets 25% more than the other. In addition, he also wants to donate 5% of his total fortune to charity. How much does he allocate to each child and the charity respectively?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
The man wants to donate 5% of his $600k fortune to charity, which means that he'll donate $600k * 5/100 = $<<600*5/100=30>>30k to charity.

He will then be left with $600k - $30k = $<<600-30=570>>570k to distribute between his children.

Let's say that one child gets x dollars. The other child should then get 25/100 * x + x = 1.25x dollars.

So total the man will pay his children x + 1.25x = 2.25x = $570k.

This means that each x equals $570k / 2.25 = $<<570/2.25=253.33333333333334>>253.333k.

So one child will get $253.333k and the other one will get 25/100 * $253.333k + $253.333k = $316.666k.

The man will therefore give $253.333k, $316.666k and $30k  respectively to his first child, second child and the charity.
<|end|>


