Here's an example using Regex to eliminate undesirable alphanumeric symbols from a specified string input.

```csharp
using System;
using System.Text.RegularExpressions;

public class Program
{
    public static void Main()
    {
        string input = "12abc&%345def!!";
        string result = RemoveUndesirableSymbols(input);

        Console.WriteLine("Result: " + result);
    }

    public static string RemoveUndesirableSymbols(string input)
    {
        string pattern = "[^A-Za-z0-9]"; // This pattern will match any character that is NOT alphanumeric (A-Z, a-z, or 0-9)
        string replacement = "";

        // Use the Regex.Replace method to replace matched symbols with the replacement string
        string result = Regex.Replace(input, pattern, replacement);

        return result;
    }
}
```

The code defines a regular expression pattern that matches any non-alphanumeric characters and replaces them with an empty string, effectively removing them from the input string. You can update the pattern to match your specific requirements.

In this example, the RemoveUndesirableSymbols method removes all non-alphanumeric characters from the input string, "12abc&%345def!!", resulting in "12abc345def".
