In my parent component I am creating a ref and passing it to child -

<ChildComponent ref={submitRef}/>


In my ChildComponent, I have a form whose onSubmit should be triggered when I click a button in the parent.

<form onSumit={handleOnSubmit}>
    <Button type="submit" ref={submitRef}/>
</form>


Something seems wrong with this code as it's not working. What am I doing wrong here?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
The problem is that you are creating a `ref` in the parent component and trying to attach it to a DOM element in the child component. A `ref` does not provide a way to "trigger" an event—it only provides a way to access properties of the element.

In this scenario, you don't need a `ref` at all, you need to use callbacks to propagate the event from the child to the parent component. 

You need to control the states from the parent component. You basically need to "lift the state up". You can create a state in the parent component and pass it down to the child component as a prop together with a function that will set that state.

For instance,

in ParentComponent:

```
class ParentComponent extends React.Component {
    state = { clicked: false };

    handleClick = () => {
       this.setState({ clicked: true });
    }

    render() {
        return (
           <> 
           <button onClick={this.handleClick}>Submit</button>
           <ChildComponent clicked={this.state.clicked} />
           </>
        );
    }
}
```

In ChildComponent:

```
class ChildComponent extends React.Component {
     componentDidUpdate(prevProps) {
         // Typical usage (don't forget to compare props):
         if (this.props.clicked !== prevProps.clicked) {
             this.submitForm(); // Function which is causing form submission.
         }
     }

     submitForm = () => {
         // Code for form submission.
     }

     render() {
        // your input fields and other things
     }
}
```

In the above code, when your parent's button is clicked, it will change the state value to `true` and then child component will automatically detect the prop change and will call the function `submitForm()` which consists the logic of form submission.
<|end|>


