is it possible to log information about which user is trying to generate an oauth token? I would like to see user login or consumerKey. I know that the login can be seen in the audit.log file when the user generates the token via grant type password. Is this possible with grant type client_credentials?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Which specific technology or product you're using would influence how you could potentially log this information. However, regardless of the technology or framework, when a token is generated via the client_credentials grant type, typically it doesn't involve any specific end-user as it's meant for server-to-server authentication. 

However, usually, the clientID or consumerKey, which represents a specific application, is used in this flow and can give you information on which application is trying to generate a token. 

