Given an extensive IMDB dataset compendium encompassing diverse movie ratings, propose an appropriate graphical representation to decipher the dispersion of these ratings, taking into account the variable genres that categorize these films. The suggested visualization should facilitate a comprehensive understanding of the relationship between genres and rating distributions.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
One suitable graphical representation would be a multi-series box and whisker plot, also known as box plot.

For this instance, each "box" would represent a different genre of movies present in the dataset. The box plot would be created using the different ratings for each movie within that genre. This would allow the viewer to quickly see the dispersion of ratings within each genre - the minimum, first quartile, median, third quartile, and maximum values. 

The 'whiskers' extending from the box would represent the variability outside the upper and lower quartiles, thereby providing a sense of distribution asymmetry and extreme outliers. This would help to visualize the spread and skewness of movie ratings pertaining to different genres. 

Moreover, if you have data regarding the individual movies which are extreme outliers, they could be represented as distinct points overlaying the boxplot, thereby enhancing the granularity of the visualization. 

With all genres aligned beside each other in this multi-series box plot, comparisons would be easy, facilitating conclusions about the genre's influence on ratings. For improved readability, the plot could be arranged in descending order of median ratings.

Complementing the box plot with a genre-wise histogram or density plot (shows the distribution of a continuous variable) for movie ratings could provide supplementary insights into the genre-rating relationships. This could especially help in visualizing the modes in a genre’s rating distribution. 

Lastly, ensure appropriate titling and clear labelling of all axes, boxes, whiskers, and outlier points for maximum clarity and ease of comprehension for anyone viewing the graph.
<|end|>


