I Have a request for the TOTAL's and subtotals column to be moved to the top/left of columns it represents, and by default SSRS does it on the bottom or right hand side of the columns being totaled.  Is there a way to this?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Yes, you can manually change the default settings and place TOTAL's and subtotals at the top or left side of the columns in SQL Server Reporting Services (SSRS). Here's how you can do it:

1. Open your SSRS report in Report Builder or SQL Server Data Tools (SSDT).

2. Click on a cell in the matrix where you want the subtotal.

3. Under Row Groups, right click on the group for which you want to position the subtotal (usually at the 'Details' level).

4. Click on "Add Total", then choose "Before".

This will add a new row to your matrix for the subtotal above or to the left of your details (depending on whether it's a row or column group). Then you can customize the subtotal by clicking on cells in the subtotal row/column and changing the formula in the Properties box or the formula bar at the top.

Please note this method moves only sub totals, if you want to move grand total to top/left then you need to manually calculate and place them, as SSRS automatically places the grand total at the bottom or right.
<|end|>


