When I launch the "mvn install" command, maven sometimes tries to download dependencies that it has already downloaded. That's expected for SNAPSHOT but why does maven do that for other JARs?

I know I can avoid that behavior by "-o" flag but I just wonder what the cause is.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Maven tries to check if there are any updates or changes with the dependencies by default. Even though it has already downloaded dependencies before, if there are any recent updates on the same version of the dependencies on the repository, Maven will re-download the updates.

This is important for cases where a dependency might have been re-published or changed even if it is not a SNAPSHOT version. You can control this behavior by configuring the <updatePolicy> in the repositories section of your pom.xml or settings.xml.

And as you mentioned, for offline mode ("--offline" or "-o"), Maven will not attempt to check or download updated dependencies from remote repositories. It will use only the dependencies that are available in the local repository.
<|end|>


