print("Alphabet sequence: ", alpha_sequence)
print("Numeric sequence: ", numeric_sequence)
```
In this code, the function `alphanumeric_sequences` takes an input string and iterates over each character. If a character is an alphabet it is added to the `alpha` string, else if it is a number it is added to the `numeric` string. After iteration, the function returns two strings: `alpha` and `numeric`.

The function is then called with "Hello World!" and its return values are stored in `alpha_sequence` and `numeric_sequence`.  These sequences are then printed.

However, please note that the string "Hello World!" does not have any numeric characters. Therefore, in this specific case, `alpha_sequence` will output "HelloWorld" and `numeric_sequence` will output an empty string.
