print("The solution is ", solution)
```

When you will run the above code it will give you the values of x, y, and z that satisfy all the three equations.

Note: numpy.linalg.solve uses LU decomposition to solve the linear equations, and you should also be aware of whether your system of equations have a unique solution, if not, this may lead to errors or inaccurate results.
