I possess a DataFrame with the following structure:

+----------+---------+-------+
| username | post_id | views |
+----------+---------+-------+
| tom | 10 | 3 |
| tom | 9 | 23 |
| tom | 8 | 44 |
| tom | 7 | 82 |
| jack | 6 | 5 |
| jack | 5 | 25 |
| jack | 4 | 46 |
| jack | 3 | 56 |
+----------+---------+-------+
My objective is to manipulate it to enumerate views that are associated with specific bins as shown below:

views     (1, 10]  (10, 25]  (25, 50]  (50, 100]
username
jack            1         1         1          1
tom             1         1         1          1

I attempted the following:

bins = [1, 10, 25, 50, 100]
groups = df.groupby(pd.cut(df.views, bins))
groups.username.count()
However, it only provides aggregate counts and not counts per user. What method should I employ to obtain bin counts per user?

The aggregate counts (utilizing my actual data) appear as follows:

impressions
(2500, 5000] 2332
(5000, 10000] 1118
(10000, 50000] 570
(50000, 10000000] 14
Name: username, dtype: int64

A:
&lt;code&gt;
import pandas as pd

df = pd.DataFrame({&#39;username&#39;: [&#39;tom&#39;, &#39;tom&#39;, &#39;tom&#39;, &#39;tom&#39;, &#39;jack&#39;, &#39;jack&#39;, &#39;jack&#39;, &#39;jack&#39;],
