Delta compression using up to 8 threads
Compressing objects: 100% (266/266), done.
Writing objects: 100% (279/279), 3.63 MiB | 777.00 KiB/s, done.
Total 279 (delta 31), reused 0 (delta 0), pack-reused 0


And process stuck at this point. There are no errors or something. I'm tried to pushing with create a new repository but process stuck at the same and nothing pushed to repository.
Why does this problem occur?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
This kind of issue may occur due to several reasons. Here are some possible solutions you may want to consider:

1. Unstable internet connection: Check your internet connection. If it is unstable, that might be the cause. 

2. Large files: Your repository might have some large files or many small files that take more time to push. In this case, try to wait a bit more, maybe it's still processing. You can set git to track your progress during push, by executing: `git push --progress`.

3. Proxy/firewall settings: Make sure the proxy/firewall settings aren't interfering with your connection to the repository.

4. SSH/TLS issues: If you're using SSH to communicate with GitHub, try switching to HTTPS, or vice versa.

5. GitHub down: Sometimes, it could be GitHub that is experiencing issues. You can check GitHub's status on https://www.githubstatus.com/ 

6. Repository size: If your repository is too big, it might fail some internal checks for GitHub. Consider using GitHub LFS if you're dealing with larger files.

Make sure to distinguish if the process is being slow (due to large files or slow internet) or if it's truly freezing (could be other reasons stated above). If none of these solutions work, consider contacting GitHub support, providing them with as much detailed information as possible.
<|end|>


