Generate a function in JavaScript that takes a string as an input and capitalizes all the words.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here is a simple JavaScript function that capitalizes each word of a submitted string. This function splits the input string into an array of words, then transforms the first character of each word to uppercase with the remaining characters to lowercase. It then joins the resulting words back together into a complete string.

```javascript
function capitalizeWords(str) {
    return str.split(' ').map(function(word) {
        return word.charAt(0).toUpperCase() + word.slice(1).toLowerCase();
    }).join(' ');
}
```

You can use this function like this:

```javascript
console.log(capitalizeWords('hello there')); // Outputs: 'Hello There'
```
