Compose a Java program that performs an inversion operation on a string, where each individual character is substituted with its case counterpart (transforming lowercase letters to uppercase ones and the reverse).
Input string: HelloWorld
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here is a Java program for performing the inversion operation on a string. This program transforms each character of the given string to its case counterpart.

```java
public class Main
{
    public static void main(String[] args)
    {
        // Define the input string
        String input = "HelloWorld";
        // Create a char array from the string
        char[] array = input.toCharArray();        
        // Loop through each char in the array
        for (int i = 0; i < array.length; i++) {
            // Check if the current char is upper case
            if (Character.isUpperCase(array[i])) {
                // If it's upper case, convert it to lower case
                array[i] = Character.toLowerCase(array[i]);
            } else if (Character.isLowerCase(array[i])) {
                // If it's lower case, convert it to upper case
                array[i] = Character.toUpperCase(array[i]);
            }
        }
        // Create a new string from the updated char array
        String output = new String(array);
        // Print the output string
        System.out.println(output);
    }
}
```

This program will take the string "HelloWorld", invert the case of each character, and print the result: "hELLOwORLD".
