<|asst|>
Here is a Python function that counts the number of punctuation marks in the given paragraph, and also provides their distribution:

```python
import string

def punctuation_distribution(text):
    punctuation_dict = dict.fromkeys(string.punctuation, 0)
    for char in text:
        if char in punctuation_dict:
            punctuation_dict[char] += 1
    punctuation_dict = {k: v for k, v in punctuation_dict.items() if v != 0} # remove unused punctuation
    return punctuation_dict
```

The test string for the function would be the first paragraph of the 'Great Gatsby':

```python
gatsby_text = "In my younger and more vulnerable years my father gave me some advice that I’ve been turning over in my mind ever since. “Whenever you feel like criticizing any one,” he told me, “just remember that all the people in this world haven’t had the advantages that you’ve had.”

print(punctuation_distribution(gatsby_text))
```

