<|asst|>
Okay, here's a very basic example of how you could create a Flask website to do this. This example uses Flask and BeautifulSoup to scrape content from the BBC News website and render it in a simple HTML format. 

```python
from flask import Flask, render_template
import requests
from bs4 import BeautifulSoup

app = Flask(__name__)

@app.route('/')
def home():
    url = "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/"
    res = requests.get(url)
    bs = BeautifulSoup(res.text, 'html.parser')
    headlines = bs.find_all(class_='gs-c-promo-heading__title')

    news_headlines = [headline.text for headline in headlines]

    return render_template('index.html', news_headlines=news_headlines)

if __name__ == '__main__':
    app.run(debug=True)
```

This is some example code for index.html, which you need to put in the templates folder. 

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>Latest News</title>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>Latest News</h1>
    <ul>
        {% for news in news_headlines %}
            <li>{{ news }}</li>
        {% endfor %}
    </ul>
</body>
</html>
```

This is a simple Flask server that scrapes the BBC News site every time the home page route is accessed and puts the headlines it finds into a Python list. This list is then passed to the `render_template` function, which uses it to render the headlines inside a HTML template.

Please note that you should be aware of legal issue. Some website might disallow such activity by addressing in their Terms of Service. Always get permissions or use proper APIs for gathering information from websites.

For real world application, instead of scraping news websites, you can use News API like GNews, NewsAPI etc. which provides JSON data and makes it easier to get the information.

Moreover, this is a very simple example and you would probably want to use a database to store your data if you were actually building a real-world application. You should also consider adding functionality to automatically update the news at regularly intervals or whenever a new article is posted. Consider learning more about Flask and web development principles for better designs. 

