Develop a software module using OOP principles that evaluates and calculates the outcomes of a series of complex mathematical expressions. The mathematical expressions include, but are not limited to, expressions such as (x-1)^2 + y^3 + |z-x| and (3x^2)-4y+|z-2x|. The software should be able to handle different types and prioritization of mathematical operations in the same expression. Also, note that the software should account for both positive and negative values of x, y, and z. Be careful to handle edge cases related to arithmetic operations such as division by zero.
