In this example, the `attributeName` attribute specifies the attribute to animate (`fill`), the `from` and `to` specify the beginning and ending color value, `dur` attribute decides the duration of animation (2s here), and `repeatCount="indefinite"` allows the animation to loop continuously.

Before implementing animation, I'd recommend checking whether the browsers your users are using support SVG animation, because it's not supported by some older browser versions. Also, note that complex animations may be CPU-intensive, impacting performance on machines with lower capabilities.
