Write a generic class in C# which includes methods to calculate the area, circumference and diameter of a circle from its radius. Additionally, create functionality enabling the class to be used with other shapes, like squares and rectangles, through the implementation of an interface or abstract class. The class should also contain a method which validates the given radius, side or height-width pair to ensure they are not less than zero. If the value provided is less than zero, an appropriate exception should be thrown. The class should handle floating point numbers. Ensure your code is properly documented with relevant comments.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here is an example of how this could be done in C#. 

```csharp
using System;

// An interface that all shapes must implement
public interface IShape
{
    double CalculateArea();
    double CalculateCircumference();
    void Validate();
}

// Circle class
public class Circle : IShape
{
    private double radius;

    public Circle(double radius)
    {
        this.radius = radius;
        Validate();
    }

    public double CalculateArea()
    {
        return Math.PI * Math.Pow(radius, 2);
    }

    public double CalculateCircumference()
    {
        return 2 * Math.PI * radius;
    }

    public void Validate()
    {
        if (radius < 0)
        {
            throw new ArgumentException("Radius must be non-negative");
        }
    }
}

// Rectangle class
public class Rectangle : IShape
{
    private double width;
    private double height;

    public Rectangle(double width, double height)
    {
        this.width = width;
        this.height = height;
        Validate();
    }

    public double CalculateArea()
    {
        return width * height;
    }

    public double CalculateCircumference()
    {
        return 2 * (width + height);
    }

    public void Validate()
    {
        if (width < 0 || height < 0)
        {
            throw new ArgumentException("Width and height must be non-negative");
        }
    }
}

// Square class
public class Square : IShape
{
    private double side;

    public Square(double side)
    {
        this.side = side;
        Validate();
    }

    public double CalculateArea()
    {
        return Math.Pow(side, 2);
    }

    public double CalculateCircumference()
    {
        return 4 * side;
    }

    public void Validate()
    {
        if (side < 0)
        {
            throw new ArgumentException("Side should be non-negative");
        }
    }
}
```
This code first defines an interface `IShape` which includes the methods that all shapes must implement. Then, classes `Circle`, `Rectangle`, and `Square` are defined, each implementing the `IShape` interface. The `Validate` method in each class checks that the dimensions of the shapes are not negative. If a negative dimension is found, an `ArgumentException` is thrown. The `CalculateArea` and `CalculateCircumference` methods return the area or circumference of the shapes.
<|end|>


