<|asst|>
Here is how you can alter the code snippet to include the method of counting vowels:

```C#
using System;

class Program
{
    static void Main()
    {
        string str = "This is a sample string.";
        Console.WriteLine("Number of Vowels: " + CountVowels(str));
    }

    static int CountVowels(string str)
    {
        int vowelCount = 0;
        string vowels = "aeiouAEIOU";
        
        for (int i = 0; i < str.Length; i++)
        {
            if (vowels.IndexOf(str[i]) >= 0)
            {
                vowelCount ++;
            }
        }
        return vowelCount;
    }
}
```

This program defines a function, `CountVowels`, which iterates over each character in the string. If the character is a vowel (as determined by the `IndexOf` method which returns -1 if the character is not found in the string of vowels), it increases the vowel count.

The Main method calls `CountVowels` on the string "This is a sample string." and prints the result. In this case, the output will be:

```
Number of Vowels: 6
```
