Here is an example of a GraphQL mutation to update a post:

```graphql
mutation UpdatePost($id: ID!, $title: String, $content: String) {
  updatePost(input: {id: $id, title: $title, content: $content}) {
    post {
      id
      title
      content
    }
  }
}
```

In this mutation, we are updating a post using the `updatePost` mutation. We are taking arguments `$id`, `$title`, and `$content` where `$id` is required and `$title` and `$content` are optional. The values that are returned after the mutation are the `id`, `title`, and `content` of the post after updating.

