I am trying to figure out why a folder I created underneath another folder is no longer in alphabetical order
Here is the layout that I want

Environment
  Overview
  A topic that starts with A
  A topic that starts with C
  A topic that starts with J
  My new folder which starts with K
     K doc 1
     K doc 2


What I get is the K folder right after the Overview. I read about the `_category_.json` file so I create one at the environment level

{
  "label": "Environment",
  "position": 1
}


In the K folder I created another `_category_.json`. I used the following:

"label": "Kibana",
  "position": 2
}


If I remove the position, Kibana goes go the bottom of the list. I have tried entering a position of 6 because of other files but it goes to the second position after the overview.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Files and folders displayed in a documentation website, such as Docusaurus or others, are generally sorted based on their 'position' attribute in `_category_.json`. However, this attribute refers to the position amongst the folders/files at the same level, and not a global position. If the 'position' attribute is not set, the folders/files might be sorted alphabetically.

If you want your folder 'Kibana' to appear after 'A topic that starts with J', you should give it a position which suits your need. For example, if you give 'Kibana' a position of 5 and no other folders at the same level have a 'position' attribute, or their position is less than 5, 'Kibana' will be fifth in order.

If the 'Kibana' folder still appears right after 'Overview', it might be due to caching issues, different sorting rules (some systems sort upper-case and lower-case letters differently), or other conflicting `_category_.json` settings. Try to recheck these configurations or clear the cache to see if it helps.

Note that 'position' at the same hierarchical level doesn't mean the 'position' in alphabetical order.
<|end|>


