In this program, we define a function `multiply_list()` which takes a list of tuples as an argument. Inside this function, we use a generator expression `(x*y for x, y in lst)` to calculate the product of each pair of numbers in the tuples. The `sum()` function is then used to add up all these products. 

This Python program has a time complexity of O(n) where n is the number of tuples in the list which makes it feasible to handle a large amount of tuples up to 1,000,000 as required. 

