Write a C# program for parsing XML documents and extracting information.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here is an example of a program that parses XML documents and extracts information using the XmlDocument and XmlTextReader classes in C#. This program will extract and display all the book titles and authors from the XML file. 

First, let's assume the following XML file structure:

```xml
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<bookstore>
    <book>
        <title>Book Title 1</title>
        <author>Author 1</author>
    </book>
    <book>
        <title>Book Title 2</title>
        <author>Author 2</author>
    </book>
    <!-- more books -->
</bookstore>
```

Then, the C# code for parsing this XML file and extracting book titles and authors would look like this:

```csharp
using System;
using System.Xml;

public class Program
{
    public static void Main()
    {
        XmlDocument doc = new XmlDocument();
        doc.Load("D:\\yourfilepath\\books.xml"); // Please replace yourfilepath with the real path of your xml file

        XmlNodeList bookList = doc.GetElementsByTagName("book");

        foreach (XmlNode node in bookList)
        {
            XmlNodeList bookInfo = node.ChildNodes;
            string title = "", author = "";

            foreach (XmlNode info in bookInfo)
            {
                // Extract the book title
                if (info.Name == "title")
                {
                    title = info.InnerText;
                }

                // Extract the author
                if (info.Name == "author")
                {
                    author = info.InnerText;
                }
            }

            Console.WriteLine("Title: " + title + ", Author: " + author);
        }
    }
}
```

In this program, the Load method is used to load the XML file. Then, it extracts book nodes using the GetElementsByTagName method. For each book node, it extracts and prints out the title and author.

Remember to replace "D:\\yourfilepath\\books.xml" with the actual path to your XML file.
<|end|>


