This is how you can create a C++ program to read a string, find & print ASCII value of each character and identify the type of character.

```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <cctype>
using namespace std;

void printCharacterType(int asciiVal)
{
    if(islower(asciiVal))
        cout << " is a Lowercase Letter.\n";
    else if(isupper(asciiVal))
        cout << " is an Uppercase Letter.\n";
    else if(isdigit(asciiVal)) 
        cout << " is a Digit.\n";
    else 
        cout << " is a Special Character.\n";
}


int main() 
{
    string str;
    cout << "Enter a word or a sentence: ";
    getline(cin, str); // reading entire line including spaces

    for(int i=0; str[i] != '\0'; i++)
    {
        int asciiValue = int(str[i]);
        cout << "The ASCII value of '" << str[i] << "' is " << asciiValue;
        printCharacterType(asciiValue);
    }

    return 0;
}
```
In this program, `islower()`, `isupper()`, and `isdigit()` functions from `cctype` library are used to check if the character is a lowercase letter, an uppercase letter, and a digit respectively.

'for' loop is used to scan each character of the string. ASCII value of a character is obtained by type casting 'char' to 'int'. 'printCharacterType()' function is called to print type of the character.

You can run the program and input a string, and the program will print ASCII value of each character along with its type.
