Need to share product details with image URL to facebook wall post . I Have written the code using omg tag but it is taking only static image url how to send dynamic image URL using angular
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Angular is a front-end framework and does not have direct control over the meta tags needed by Facebook to display images in wall posts. Facebook scrapes these Open Graph meta tags to get the image url when shared. Thus these tags need to be modified on the server side each time a page is served with a new set of data.

That's said, if you're using Angular Universal or some form of Server Side Rendering (SSR), you could update the open graph tags dynamically with each request on the server.

On the other hand, you are sharing individual pages with unique URLs and there are few enough of them, you might also consider setting up a service server-side that updates the meta tags for each page as it is visited.

Here is a sample script to dynamically set Open Graph data:

```typescript
import { Meta } from '@angular/platform-browser';

constructor(private metaService: Meta) { }

setMetaTags(imgUrl: string) {
    this.metaService.addTags([
        { property: 'og:image', content: imgUrl },
        { property: 'og:image:secure_url', content: imgUrl }
    ]);
}
```

You just need to call `setMetaTags(imageUrl)` each time the product changes, passing in the new product's image URL.

Please note that Facebook might not immediately reflect changes due to caching the previously scraped information. You can use the Facebook Sharing Debugger to manually clear their cache on specific pages.
<|end|>


