In the realm of the C programming language, what would be deemed as the most optimal methodology to discern the highest value element present within a given array?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
The most optimal method in C to identify the highest value in an array is by running a single loop through the array and comparing each element to a variable storing the maximum value found so far. 

Here is a simple code snippet to find the maximum value in an array:

```c
#include <stdio.h>

int findMax(int arr[], int n) {
    int i;
    // Assume first element is maximum initially 
    int max = arr[0];  
    
    for (i=1; i<n; i++) {
        // If current array element is greater than max, update max
        if (arr[i] > max) {
            max = arr[i];
        }
    }
    return max;
}

int main() {
    int arr[] = {10, 20, 30, 45, 50, 66, 70, 80};
    int n = sizeof(arr)/sizeof(arr[0]);
    printf("Maximum value in the array is: %d", findMax(arr, n));
    return 0;
}
```

In this code, we iterate through the array only once, so the time complexity is O(n), where n is the length of the array. This is the most efficient method in terms of time complexity. Please note that you must ensure your array has at least one element, as the maximum is initialized to the first value in the array.
<|end|>


