Design a JavaScript function that not only removes all the diacritical marks from the input text string, but also transforms it into the obscure coded language known as Klingon.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
JavaScript by itself cannot transliterate text to a different language, say from English to German or Klingon. Transliteration is essentially replaceing each character in a string from one language/charset to its equivalent in another language/charset. It involves natural language understanding and context which is far more complex task and requires a library or NLP service that supports this kind of translation.

However, I can design a JavaScript function to remove all the diacritical marks from the input text string. The diacritical marks can be removed by using the normalize() function in combination with replace() function. normalize() is a string method that transforms a string into a Unicode normal form which means it will translate characters to a standard form and replace() function will then replace the normalized diacritical marked characters with the unaccented version.

Here's a simple function to remove diacritical marks:

```javascript
const removeDiacritics = (str) => {
    return str.normalize("NFD").replace(/[\u0300-\u036f]/g, "");
};

console.log(removeDiacritics("éèêëėęůúûüùūōòõöơñāäå"));
// Output: "eeeeeeuuuuuoooooonaaaa"
```

This function first normalizes the string to its Unicode normal form with `"NFD"` as a parameter which represents the Unicode Normalization Form D, then it's replacing all the characters with diacritical marks (from U+0300 to U+036f in UTF-16) with an empty string.

However, translating to Klingon or any other language would require a translation service, which is not feasible simply with JavaScript without accessing some translation API's or library of some sort. APIs that can translate English (or other languages) to Klingon include Bing's Microsoft Translator API. You would have to check the details of these for how you can use them for your JavaScript application. Here is a little example assuming you have written a function translateToKlingon which uses Microsoft's Text API:

```javascript
async function textToKlingon(text){
    text = removeDiacritics(text);
    text = await translateToKlingon(text); // assuming translateToKlingon is an async function making API call.
    return text;
}
```
