How would you find the frequency of each character in a string using JavaScript with case-insensitive comparisons? Also, ignore spaces and non-alphabetic characters. Assume the input, string = "Hello World 123"
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here is the JavaScript function to find the frequency of each character in a given string:

```javascript
function findFrequency(string) {
    // convert the string to lowercase
    var str = string.toLowerCase();

    // initialize an empty object
    var freq = {};

    // iterate over each character in the string
    for (var i = 0; i < str.length; i++) {
        // Ignore spaces and non-alphabetic characters
        if ('a' <= str[i] && str[i] <= 'z') {
            // If the character is already in the object, increment its count by 1
            // Else, add it to the object with count = 1
            freq[str[i]] = freq[str[i]] ? freq[str[i]] + 1 : 1;
        }
    }

    return freq;
}

console.log(findFrequency("Hello World 123"));
```

The output of this script will be:
```
{ h: 1, e: 1, l: 3, o: 2, w: 1, r: 1, d: 1 }
```

This code will iterate through each character in the string after converting it to lowercase. It then checks if the character is an alphabet character or not. If it is, it will add it to the `freq` object or increment its count by 1 if it's already in the object. The `freq` object will keep track of the count of each character in the input string. At the end, the `findFrequency` function will return this object.
