However, it's also possible that the feature didn't have an opportunity to show its importance in the data you're testing on, due to the way the tree was split during training. For instance, the feature could be important only in certain specific circumstances that were not present in your test data. 

Always approach feature elimination with caution and consider both the model insights as well as domain knowledge.
