I'd like my website to follow the content coming out of external source, which is loaded over time
I've tried to use
`chatContainer.scrollTop = chatContainer.scrollHeight;`
as my chatContainer is where the content is loaded, but it doesn't work as it should, could you give me some help with that? How to make a website follow the real-time rendered content with the view?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Your attempt was correct, you should set the scrollTop property of chatContainer to its scrollHeight. But you should do it immediately after new content is added to chatContainer.

However, in some cases (like when a user is reading previous messages), you may not want to interrupt their reading and instead stick to the end of the chat when it is already at the bottom and new message has arrived.

To achieve this, you can first check if the chatContainer's scroll position is at the bottom before a new message arrives, then determine whether to stay at the end or keep the current scroll position after the new message arrives. Here is an example:

```javascript
function addNewMessage() {
    // assume newContentNode is the new message element you received
    const wasScrolledToBottom = chatContainer.scrollTop + chatContainer.clientHeight === chatContainer.scrollHeight;
    
    // add new content
    chatContainer.appendChild(newContentNode);
    
    // scroll to the end if was at the end
    if (wasScrolledToBottom) {
        chatContainer.scrollTop = chatContainer.scrollHeight;
    }
    
}
```
Just make sure you call this function whenever new message is received and added to the chat container.

Also, there could be a style issue that causes this problem. Make sure your container (chatContainer) has a defined height and an overflow style property set to auto or scroll. Without these style settings the scrollTop and scrollHeight properties may not work as expected.

CSS:

```css
#chatContainer {
    height: 400px; /* Or any other value */
    overflow-y: auto;
}
```
HTML:

```html
<div id="chatContainer">
   <!-- Chat content here -->
</div>
```
<|end|>


