I'm working on an app that requires no user input, but I don't want the iPhone to enter the power saving mode.

Is it possible to disable power saving from an app?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Yes, it is possible. In iOS, you can prevent the device from auto-locking (and thus going into power saving mode) by setting the `isIdleTimerDisabled` property of the shared `UIApplication` instance to `true`. This means that as long as your app is running and is in the foreground, the device will not automatic lock.

Here is an example in Swift:

```swift
UIApplication.shared.isIdleTimerDisabled = true
```

Remember, it's necessary to reset this property to `false` when the app no longer needs to prevent auto-locking or when it's going to background. Continuously running on full power can drain the device's battery very quickly. 

Also, it's worth mentioning that this will only prevent the device from auto-locking while your app is in the foreground. This means it doesn't have control over power saving mode when you are in the background or when your app is not currently active. Only the user can disable power mode completely from the settings.
<|end|>


