Devise a SQL query to extract all entries from a table named "orders". From the extracted entries, select only those entries which have a total cost exceeding 15000 and total items purchased greater than 100, then sort the results by total cost in descending order and total items in ascending order. Additionally, provide a calculated field that provides the average cost of each item per order.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Please use the following SQL query to achieve the desired result:

```SQL
SELECT OrderID, CustomerID, TotalCost, TotalItems,
       (TotalCost / TotalItems) AS AverageCostPerItem
FROM orders
WHERE TotalCost > 15000 AND TotalItems > 100
ORDER BY TotalCost DESC, TotalItems ASC;
```

This query will return the OrderID, CustomerID, TotalCost, and TotalItems from the orders table where total cost exceeds 15000 and total items are more than 100. The items will be sorted by TotalCost (from highest to lowest) and then TotalItems (from lowest to highest). In addition, it also calculates the average cost per item by dividing the total cost by total items. This calculated value is returned as the column AverageCostPerItem. 

Remember to replace the placeholder column names (OrderID, CustomerID, TotalCost, TotalItems etc.) with the actual column names present in your 'orders' table.
<|end|>


