How can I draw trend lines or shapes on the chart using Pine Script?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Unfortunately, as of now, Pine Script does not support the functionality to directly draw trend lines or shapes on the chart. However, you may use built-in functions for drawing lines, labels, or shapes in specific points within the script.

Here are some example scripts to illustrate:

1) Line.new(x1 = bar_index[10], y1 = high[10], x2 = bar_index, y2 = high)

This code creates a new line from the high 10 bars ago to the current bar's high.

2) label.new(x = bar_index, y = close, text = "Label")

This code creates a new label at the close price of the current bar.

3) plotshape(series=close, title="Shape", location=location.belowbar, color=color.red, style=shape.triangleup, text="Tri")

This code plots a shape (triangle up) below the bar whenever the condition (series=close) is met.

Documentations for these functions can be found here:
- Line.new: https://www.tradingview.com/pine-script-docs/en/v4/annotations/drawings/Line.new.html
- label.new: https://www.tradingview.com/pine-script-docs/en/v4/annotations/drawings/Label.new.html
- plotshape: https://www.tradingview.com/pine-script-docs/en/v4/functions/Plots/plotshape.html

Use these functions to serve your purpose. However, note that dynamic updating of these objects (as a trend updated with each new bar) isn’t a supported or reliable operation. Remember that each new call of the drawing function creates a new object, it does not update existing ones.
<|end|>


