Develop a CSS style that changes the background color to light blue for a paragraph element only when the mouse pointer is hovering over it. Additionally, implement a smooth transition effect when the color changes.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
You can achieve this using CSS :hover pseudo-class and transition property together. Here's the sample CSS code:

```css
p {
  transition: background-color 0.5s ease; /* This line adds a smooth transition effect */
}

p:hover {
  background-color: lightblue; /* This line changes the background color to light blue on hover */
}
```
This CSS snippet means that all paragraph (`<p>`) elements will get a background color of light blue when a user hovers over it. When the user stops hovering over the paragraph, the background color will gradually return to its original color over a period of 0.5 seconds. 

The `transition` property is used to change an element from one state to another over a period of time, and is specified with the following values: `transition: property duration timing-function delay;`.

Replace `0.5s` with the length of time you'd like the color transition to take. The `ease` value means the transition will gradually change speed over its duration, being slower at the start/end and quicker in the middle. This gives a more gradual and realistic transition.

Here's a brief usage example:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<style>
p {
  transition: background-color 0.5s ease;
}

p:hover {
  background-color: lightblue;
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<p>Hover over this paragraph to see the effect.</p>

</body>
</html>
```
