The error in the provided SQL statement, is caused by the incorrect use of the `INSERT INTO` SQL keyword. The `INSERT INTO` statement in SQL is used to insert new records in a table, hence it cannot be used to alter the structure of an existing table. The correct SQL keyword to alter the structure of an existing table is `ALTER TABLE`.

Here is the corrected SQL statement:

```sql
ALTER TABLE Customers ADD COLUMN City VARCHAR(255);
```

This statement will add a new column named `City` of type `VARCHAR` with a maximum length of 255 characters to the `Customers` table.
