Build a multi-page form with navigations in React that will allow users to submit a message and details. The form should include a summary page that displays all user inputs before final submission for confirmation. 

In addition, debug the following piece of React code meant to execute these functions, explaining and solving any errors you find. Ensure to provide inline comments in your solution.

```react
import React from 'react';

class PageForm extends React.Component{
   constructor(){
      super();
      this.state = {
         name: '',
         email: '',
         message: '',
         currentPage: 0
      };
   }
   
   handleSubmitForm = event => {
      alert('Form has been submitted with the information: '
      + this.state.name + '\n'
      + this.state.email + '\n'
      + this.state.message);
      event.preventDefault();
   }

   render(){
      if(this.state.currentPage == 0){
         return (
            <div>
               <form onSubmit={this.handleSubmit}>
                  <input type='text' placeholder='Your Name' />
                  <input type='email' placeholder='Your Email' />
                  <button type='submit'>Next</button>
               </form>
            </div>
         );
      } else {
         return (
            <div>
               <form onSubmit={this.handleSubmit}>
                  <textarea placeholder='Your Message' />
                  <button type='submit'>Submit</button>
               </form>
            </div>
         );
      }
   }
}

export default PageForm;
```
<|end|>
<|asst|>
The main errors are:
1. No method to handle state changes when typing into the input fields. We need to add event handlers onNameChange, onEmailChange and onMessageChange, to update the state of our component whenever a user types into the input fields. Without this, our form will not function correctly.
2. In this render() function's returned forms, there is onSubmit method called handleSubmit which doesn't exist, this should be changed to handleSubmitForm.
3. No navigation function to move between pages. We need to add a method to handle moving to the next page without submitting the form. This can be achieved by adding the event.preventDefault() method to stop default form submission behavior, and then incrementing the currentPage state.
4. No summary page was found before the final submission.

Here's the revised version of the code:

```react
import React from 'react';

class PageForm extends React.Component{
   constructor(){
      super();
      this.state = {
         name: '',
         email: '',
         message: '',
         currentPage: 0
      };
   }

   handleNextPage = event => {
      event.preventDefault();
      this.setState({currentPage: this.state.currentPage + 1})
   }

   onNameChange = event => this.setState({name: event.target.value});

   onEmailChange = event => this.setState({email: event.target.value});

   onMessageChange = event => this.setState({message: event.target.value});

   handleSubmitForm = event => {
      alert('Form has been submitted with the information: '
      + this.state.name + '\n'
      + this.state.email + '\n'
      + this.state.message);
      event.preventDefault();
   }

   render(){
      if(this.state.currentPage == 0){
         return (
            <div>
               <form onSubmit={this.handleNextPage}>
                  <input type='text' placeholder='Your Name' onChange={this.onNameChange} />
                  <input type='email' placeholder='Your Email' onChange={this.onEmailChange} /> 
                  <button type='submit'>Next</button>
               </form>
            </div>
         );
      } else if(this.state.currentPage == 1){
        return (
           <div>
             <form onSubmit={this.handleNextPage}>
                 <textarea placeholder='Your Message' onChange={this.onMessageChange} />
                 <button type='submit'>Next</button>
             </form>
           </div>
        );
      } else {
        return (
           <div>
             <form onSubmit={this.handleSubmitForm}>
                <h3>Confirmation:</h3>
                <p>Name: {this.state.name}</p>
                <p>Email: {this.state.email}</p>
                <p>Message: {this.state.message}</p>
                <button type='submit'>Submit</button>
             </form>
           </div>
        );
      }
   }
}

export default PageForm;
```
This revised code fixes the issues present in original examples and provides added functionality as per the requirement. Now, the form navigates between name/email and message input with a final page that displays user input before final submission.
<|end|>


