Here is a simple HTML calculator layout using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>Simple Calculator</title>
    <style>
        .calculator {
            text-align: center;
            margin-top: 150px;
        }
        #result {
            margin-bottom: 20px;
            width: 200px;
            height: 30px;
        }
        button {
            width: 50px;
            height: 50px;
            margin: 2px;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="calculator">
        <input id="result" readonly>
        <br>
        <button onclick="addDigit('7')">7</button>
        <button onclick="addDigit('8')">8</button>
        <button onclick="addDigit('9')">9</button>
        <button onclick="performOperation('/')">/</button>
        <br>
        <button onclick="addDigit('4')">4</button>
        <button onclick="addDigit('5')">5</button>
        <button onclick="addDigit('6')">6</button>
        <button onclick="performOperation('*')">*</button>
        <br>
        <button onclick="addDigit('1')">1</button>
        <button onclick="addDigit('2')">2</button>
        <button onclick="addDigit('3')">3</button>
        <button onclick="performOperation('-')">-</button>
        <br>
        <button onclick="performOperation('+')">+</button>
        <button onclick="addDigit('0')">0</button>
        <button onclick="calculateResult()">=</button>
        <button onclick="clearResult()">C</button>
    </div>

    <script>
        var operation = '';
        var operand1 = 0;
        var operand2 = null;

        function addDigit(digit) {
            var resultElement = document.getElementById("result");
            resultElement.value = resultElement.value + digit;
        }

        function performOperation(op) {
            var resultElement = document.getElementById("result");
            operand1 = parseFloat(resultElement.value);
            operation = op;
            resultElement.value = '';
        }

        function calculateResult() {
            var resultElement = document.getElementById("result");
            operand2 = parseFloat(resultElement.value);
            switch (operation) {
                case '+':
                    resultElement.value = operand1 + operand2;
                    break;
                case '-':
                    resultElement.value = operand1 - operand2;
                    break;
                case '*':
                    resultElement.value = operand1 * operand2;
                    break;
                case '/':
                    resultElement.value = operand1 / operand2;
                    break;
            }
        }

        function clearResult() {
            var resultElement = document.getElementById("result");
            resultElement.value = '';
        }
    </script>
</body>
</html>
```

This webpage layout contains a basic calculator that performs arithmetic operations. The numeric and operator buttons, when clicked, call their respective function which implements the functionality. The result of the operations is displayed in an input field. The 'C' button is used to clear the input field.
<|end|>


