Write a PHP script that not only prints the current hour, minute, and second but also retrieves and prints the current timezone. The script should also include a function to convert the current time to any other given timezone. Test your script for at least two different timezones.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
<?php

// Function to convert the current time to any other given timezone
function convertTimezone($timezone){
    
    // Create a datetime object
    $date = new DateTime(null, new DateTimeZone(date_default_timezone_get()));
    
    // Assign the new timezone
    $date->setTimezone(new DateTimeZone($timezone));
    
    // Format and return the datetime string
    return $date->format('Y-m-d H:i:s');
}

// Print the current hour, minute, and second
echo 'Current Time: '.date('H:i:s').'<br>';

// Retrieve and print the current timezone
echo 'Current Timezone: '.date_default_timezone_get().'<br>';

// Test the script for two different timezones
$timezone1 = 'America/New_York';
$timezone2 = 'Australia/Sydney';

// Print the converted time for first timezone
echo 'Time in '.$timezone1.' is '.convertTimezone($timezone1).'<br>';

// Print the converted time for second timezone
echo 'Time in '.$timezone2.' is '.convertTimezone($timezone2).'<br>';

?>
This code, when executed, will first print the current time and timezone. It then converts the current time to the specified time zones i.e., "America/New_York" and "Australia/Sydney", and then prints the converted time for both.
The function convertTimezone() defined in the code takes a timezone as input, and returns the current time for that timezone. It creates a DateTime object initialized with the current time and timezone, sets the new timezone provided on this object and then formats and returns the date-time.
Please replace 'America/New_York' and 'Australia/Sydney' with the time zones you want to check the current time for.
