<|asst|>
Below is a simple Java program that creates a list of `Customer` objects and calculates the total purchases for each customer. Please note that the code would be more complicated if the data were to be retrieved from an actual database or a JSON file.

```java
import java.util.*;
import java.math.*;

public class Main {
    
    //Customer class
    public static class Customer {
        String firstName;
        String lastName;
        List<Integer> purchases;

        public Customer(String firstName, String lastName, List<Integer> purchases) {
            this.firstName = firstName;
            this.lastName = lastName;
            this.purchases = purchases;
        }
        
        public int totalPurchases() {
            return this.purchases.stream().mapToInt(Integer::intValue).sum();
        }
        
        @Override
        public String toString() {
            return this.firstName + " " + this.lastName + ": Total purchases = " + totalPurchases();
        }
    }
  
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        List<Customer> customers = new ArrayList<>();
        customers.add(new Customer("John", "Smith", Arrays.asList(20, 30, 70)));
        customers.add(new Customer("Mark", "Jones", Arrays.asList(90, 40, 50)));
        customers.add(new Customer("Patricia", "Williams", Arrays.asList(10, 20, 90)));
        
        for (Customer customer: customers) {
            System.out.println(customer.toString());
        }
    }
}
```

This program will output:

```
John Smith: Total purchases = 120
Mark Jones: Total purchases = 180
Patricia Williams: Total purchases = 120
```

This program makes use of a `Customer` internal class with `firstName`, `lastName`, and `purchases` as instance variables. There's a method `totalPurchases()` that returns the sum of all purchases made by a customer. The `toString()` method is overridden to return the full name of the customer and their total purchases.

The `main()` method creates a list of `Customer` as per your example and iterates over it to print each customer's full name and total purchases.
