# Context
[BOSS: Write HFT system based on statistic arbitrage, since performance is key I want to ensure performance is designed in the system, Product Manager: ## Original Requirements
The boss wants us to design a High-Frequency Trading (HFT) system based on statistical arbitrage. The key requirement is that the system must be designed with performance in mind.

## Product Goals
```python
[
    "Design a high-performance HFT system based on statistical arbitrage",
    "Ensure the system is reliable and robust to handle high volume trades",
    "The system should be user-friendly and intuitive to use"
]
```

## User Stories
```python
[
    "As a trader, I want the system to execute trades quickly so that I can take advantage of arbitrage opportunities",
    "As a trader, I want the system to be reliable so that I don't miss out on profitable trades",
    "As a system administrator, I want to be able to monitor the system's performance and make adjustments as necessary",
    "As a risk manager, I want the system to have safeguards in place to prevent catastrophic losses",
    "As a user, I want the system to be easy to use so that I can focus on trading strategies rather than navigating the system"
]
```

## Competitive Analysis
```python
[
    "Bloomberg Terminal: A comprehensive trading system with a wide range of features, but it may be overwhelming for new users",
    "E*TRADE: User-friendly interface but lacks the sophisticated features needed for HFT",
    "Interactive Brokers: Offers a robust trading platform with advanced features, but the user interface can be complex",
    "TradeStation: Known for its high-speed execution and customizable trading platform, but it has a steep learning curve",
    "MetaTrader 5: Offers advanced trading features and supports algorithmic trading, but its performance can be inconsistent",
    "NinjaTrader: Offers a powerful trading platform with advanced charting features, but it may be too complex for novice traders",
    "Thinkorswim: Offers a wide range of trading tools and educational resources, but its performance can be slow during peak trading hours"
]
```

## Competitive Quadrant Chart
```mermaid
quadrantChart
    title Performance and User-Friendliness of Trading Systems
    x-axis Low Performance --> High Performance
    y-axis Low User-Friendliness --> High User-Friendliness
    quadrant-1 High Performance, Low User-Friendliness
