By default each row of a Gridview maps to each row in a datatable or dataset attached to its datasource. But what if I want to display these rows in multiple columns. For example if it has 10 rows, 5 rows each should be displayed in 2 columns side by side. Also can I do this with the Infragistics grid. Is this possible?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
By default, GridView or Infragistics grid display the rows horizontally and you cannot display rows in multiple columns side by side. They are designed to present data in a tabular format.

However, you can achieve this by:
1. Manipulating your data to construct a new datatable with your desired format before binding it to GridView or infragistics grid. Essentially merging two rows into one with more columns.
2. Create a custom grid view. 

Here is a sample code in ASP.net for GridView to split rows into multiple columns:

```csharp
DataTable dt = new DataTable();
dt.Columns.Add("Column1");
dt.Columns.Add("Column2");
for (int i = 0; i < YourOriginalDataTable.Rows.Count; i += 2)
{
    DataRow dr = dt.NewRow();
    dr[0] = YourOriginalDataTable.Rows[i][0];
    if (i + 1 < YourOriginalDataTable.Rows.Count)
        dr[1] = YourOriginalDataTable.Rows[i + 1][0];
    dt.Rows.Add(dr);
}
YourGridView.DataSource = dt;
YourGridView.DataBind();
```
This code takes 2 rows at a time from your original datatable and creates 1 row with 2 columns in the new datatable. If you want more columns, you can adjust the loop step size and datatable row assignment accordingly.

You can do a similar process for Infragistics grid.

Remember, this is just merging two rows into one. The column cells in GridView and Infragistics are not designed to hold entire rows of data by default, and any such functionality would need to be custom built and go against their traditional use case.
<|end|>


