You are given a matrix where each row is a separate sequence but without any duplicate rows. The task is to rearrange the rows (if necessary) to ensure the columns of the matrix are strictly increasing. If such a rearrangement is possible, return the following dictionary:
{'row_index': r, 'rearrange_with': n, 'total_rearrangements': c}

where 'row_index' is the index of the row that needs rearranging,
'rearrange_with' is the index of the row with which you can swap to get the sorted columns,
'total_rearrangements' is the total number of rearrangements the algorithm performed. 

If no such row exists or if the matrix is already sorted by columns, return {'row_index': -1, 'rearrange_with': -1, 'total_rearrangements': 0}.

