```java
import java.util.Comparator;

class Person {
  String name;
  int age;

  // Constructor for Person class with input name and age
  public Person(String name, int age) {
    this.name = name;
    this.age = age;
  }

  // Custom comparator for sorting objects of class Person based on age
  public static Comparator<Person> ageComparator = new Comparator<Person>() {
    @Override
    public int compare(Person p1, Person p2) {
      return p1.age - p2.age;
    }
  };
}
```

This code defines a `Person` class with two instance variables `name` and `age`. It also provides a constructor for initializing the `name` and `age` values. Finally, a custom comparator `ageComparator` is implemented for sorting objects of class `Person` based on their age.
