Develop a JavaScript function that generates a random sequence composed of letters and numbers. The function should allow the user to specify the length of the sequence as an argument within a specified range (from 8 to 32 characters). The sequence should be balanced with equal (or as close as possible) numbers of uppercase Latin script letters, lowercase Latin script letters, numeric digits, and special characters from a defined set ("!@#$%^&*()"). Additionally, your function should not generate the same sequence twice.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Your task requires creating a JavaScript function to generate a random sequence. A key requirement is that the sequence should have an equal number of uppercase characters, lowercase characters, digits, and special characters. However, considering that the character length could be any number not necessarily divisible by 4 (number of character types), perfect equal distribution of different types of characters is not possible in all scenarios. Furthermore, ensuring the sequence is not repeated ever is a complex task and would typically require storing all previously generated sequences for comparison, which is not feasible for very large number of sequences. That being said, here's a solution that randomly generates sequences of the given length ensuring a roughly equal distribution of character types:

```javascript
const specialCharacters = "!@#$%^&*()";
let previouslyGeneratedSequences = new Set();

function generateSequence(length) {
    if (length < 8 || length > 32) {
        throw new Error("Length must be between 8 and 32.");
    }

    let sequence = '';
    const characters = [
        'ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ',
        'abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz',
        '0123456789',
        specialCharacters
    ];

    for (let i = 0; i < length; i++) {
        let characterSet = characters[i % characters.length];
        sequence += characterSet[Math.floor(Math.random() * characterSet.length)];
    }

    sequence = shuffle(sequence);

    // Check if sequence has been previously generated
    while (previouslyGeneratedSequences.has(sequence)) {
        sequence = shuffle(sequence);
    }

    // Store generated sequence
    previouslyGeneratedSequences.add(sequence);

    return sequence;
}

// Helper function to shuffle characters in a string
function shuffle(input) {
    let a = input.split("");
    let n = a.length;

    for(let i = n - 1; i > 0; i--) {
        let j = Math.floor(Math.random() * (i + 1));
        let tmp = a[i];
        a[i] = a[j];
        a[j] = tmp;
    }
    
    return a.join("");
}
```
This function attempts to ensure an even distribution of different character types and tries to maintain uniqueness among generated sequences by storing them in a set and checking each new one against it. Use the function `generateSequence(n)` with `n` being the length you want for the sequence. Please note that, due to randomness and distribution of types, uniqueness among generated sequences can't be guaranteed in all possible scenarios, especially when the length of the sequence is short and the set of previously generated sequences is large.
<|end|>


