Write a query in SQL that retrieves the minimum value and the maximum value for each distinct subcategory and the average cost for each subcategory in the last quarter. A subcategory should be considered only if it contains more than 3 distinct products.
TABLE products
product_id INT PK
subcategory VARCHAR
cost INT
entry_date DATE
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Assuming the last quarter to be 3 months before the current date, you can use the SQL query below. This query filters to consider only subcategories with more than 3 distinct products by using GROUP BY HAVING. It also considers only the products added in the last quarter by using WHERE entry_date.

```SQL
SELECT 
    subcategory,
    MIN(cost) AS Min_Cost,
    MAX(cost) AS Max_Cost,
    AVG(cost) AS Average_Cost
FROM 
    products
WHERE
    entry_date >= DATEADD(MONTH, -3, GETDATE())
GROUP BY 
    subcategory
HAVING 
    COUNT(DISTINCT product_id) > 3
```

Remember, replace GETDATE() with NOW() if you are using MySQL or CURDATE() in Oracle. DATEADD is also MSSQL specific, in MySQL the equivalent is DATE_SUB(NOW(), INTERVAL 3 MONTH), in ORACLE it's ADD_MONTHS(SYSDATE, -3).

Please replace these functions as per your DBMS.

And as it's a good practice to handle NULL or missing values, consider the case when cost can be NULL. If yes, then do handle those cases in your SQL query. 

Also please ensure to use the proper DATE function as per your date column's format.
<|end|>


