<|asst|>
Sure, the regular expression (regex) pattern for detecting numerical values specifically starting with the integer 8 would look like this in Python:

```python
import re

pattern = r'^8\d*$'

# Test the pattern
text = '823'
match = re.search(pattern, text)
if match:
  print("'{}' starts with 8".format(text))
else:
  print("'{}' does not start with 8".format(text))
```

In the regex pattern `'^8\d*$'`, `^` asserts the start of a line. `8` is the digit to start with. `\d*` matches any number of digits (including zero), and `$` asserts the end of the line. Hence, the entire pattern matches any string (i.e. number) that starts with 8.
<|end|>


