<|asst|>
The surface area A of a circular shape is given by the formula A = πr². If the radius r of the circle is 7 cm, we will substitute 7cm into the formula to get the surface area.

So, A = π(7 cm)² = π(49 cm²) = 153.94 cm² approximately.
