Design a class 'Sportsman' in Java that keeps a sportsman's name, sport, country of origin, age, and the number of medals won. Additionally, implement sorting functionality to order athletes by medals won. Also handle potential exceptions for invalid age entries.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here's a simple implementation of a 'Sportsman' class in Java.

```java
import java.util.*;

class Sportsman implements Comparable<Sportsman>{
    private String name;
    private String sport;
    private String country;
    private int age;
    private int medalsWon;

    // Constructor
    public Sportsman(String name, String sport, String country, int age, int medalsWon){
        this.name = name;
        this.sport = sport;
        this.country = country;
        setAge(age);
        this.medalsWon = medalsWon;
    }

    // Getters
    public String getName() { return this.name; }
    public String getSport() { return this.sport; }
    public String getCountry() { return this.country; }
    public int getAge() { return this.age; }
    public int getMedalsWon() { return this.medalsWon; }

    // Setters
    public void setName(String name) { this.name = name; }
    public void setSport(String sport) { this.sport = sport; }
    public void setCountry(String country) { this.country = country; }

    // Set age with exception handling
    public void setAge(int age) { 
        if(age <= 0){
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Invalid age entry");
        }
        this.age = age; 
    }
    
    public void setMedalsWon(int medalsWon) { this.medalsWon = medalsWon; }

    // Method to compare objects for sorting
    @Override
    public int compareTo(Sportsman other) {
        return other.getMedalsWon() - this.getMedalsWon();
    }

    @Override
    public String toString() {
        return "Name: " + this.name + ", Sport: " + this.sport + ", Country: " + this.country + ", Age: " + this.age + ", Medals won: " + this.medalsWon;
    }
}
```

Now we can create a list of Sportsman objects, sort them, and print the sorted list:

```java
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args){
        ArrayList<Sportsman> sportsmen = new ArrayList<>();
        sportsmen.add(new Sportsman("Tom", "Football", "USA", 30, 5));
        sportsmen.add(new Sportsman("Jerry", "Basketball", "USA", 26, 8));
        sportsmen.add(new Sportsman("Spike", "Baseball", "USA", 28, 6));
        
        Collections.sort(sportsmen);
        
        for(Sportsman sportsman : sportsmen){
            System.out.println(sportsman);
        }
    }
}
```

This will print the sportsmen sorted by the number of medals won in descending order. In case of a tie, it orders them based on the order in which they were added to the list.
