Construct a function in Python programming language that normalizes a designated string but with added restrictions: Apart from eradicating blank spaces, converting all characters to lower case, and transforming non-alphanumeric characters to underscore symbols, it should also replace consecutive underscores with a single underscore and remove trailing underscores.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here is the Python function to fulfill your requirement:

```python
import re 

def normalize_string(input_string):
    # Converting all characters to lower case
    input_string = input_string.lower()

    # Transforming non-alphanumeric characters (excluding whitespaces) to underscore symbols
    input_string = re.sub(r'\W', '_', input_string)

    # Eradicating blank spaces
    input_string = re.sub(r'\s', '', input_string)

    # Replace consecutive underscores with a single underscore
    input_string = re.sub(r'_+', '_', input_string)

    # Remove trailing underscores 
    input_string = re.sub(r'_+$', '', input_string)
    input_string = re.sub(r'^_+', '', input_string)
    
    return(input_string)

print(normalize_string("Hello, Wor_ld! This is a test string  "))
```
This function will take a string as input and return the normalized string that fits all of provided criteria. We are using regular expressions to perform string manipulations. The `re.sub(pattern, repl, string)` function in the `re` module can replace the matches of `pattern` in `string` with `repl`.

This function will convert the string to lower case, replace all non-alphanumeric characters with underscores, remove all spaces, replace consecutive underscores with a single underscore, and remove any underscores at the start or end of the string.
<|end|>


