Design a function in JavaScript which is capable of accepting an array filled with numerical values and, upon execution, proceeds to ascertain and return the numerical value signifying the median from the given array.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here is a JavaScript function that calculates and returns the median of an array. It first sorts the array, then calculates the middle index. If the array has an odd length, it just returns the middle number. If the array has an even length, it returns the average of the two middle numbers:

```javascript
function calculateMedian(arr) {
    // Sort the array in ascending order
    arr.sort((a, b) => a - b);

    // Calculate the middle index
    var midIndex = Math.floor(arr.length / 2);

    // If the array length is even, return the average of the two middle numbers
    if (arr.length % 2 === 0) {
       return (arr[midIndex - 1] + arr[midIndex]) / 2.0;
    }
    // If the array length is odd, return the middle number
    else {
       return arr[midIndex];
    }
}
```
You can call this function with an array, like so:

```javascript
var arr = [5, 2, 9, 1, 5, 6, 7, 3, 4, 2, 1];
console.log(calculateMedian(arr)); // Will output median of the input array
```
Keep in mind this function will mutate (sort) the original array, so if you don't want that you'll need to copy the array inside the function before sorting it.
<|end|>


