Is there a way to read a module's configuration ini file? 

For example I installed php-eaccelerator ([http://eaccelerator.net](http://eaccelerator.net)) and it put a `eaccelerator.ini` file in `/etc/php.d`. My PHP installation wont read this `.ini` file because the `--with-config-file-scan-dir` option wasn't used when compiling PHP. Is there a way to manually specify a path to the ini file somewhere so PHP can read the module's settings?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Yes, you can specify an additional .ini file for PHP to read using the PHP_INI_SCAN_DIR environment variable.

If you want PHP to scan /etc/php.d folder, you could set the environment variable like this:

```
export PHP_INI_SCAN_DIR=/etc/php.d/
```

You could add this line to your shell profile (.bashrc, .bash_profile, etc) so that it gets set every time you open your terminal.

Or, you could set it only for the current script execution:

```
PHP_INI_SCAN_DIR=/etc/php.d/ php your_script.php
```

Note that PHP will still use its regular php.ini file, the PHP_INI_SCAN_DIR just specifies additional directories to scan for .ini files. If you want to only use /etc/php.d/eaccelerator.ini, you should set PHP_INI_SCAN_DIR to /etc/ and run PHP like `php -c /etc/php.d/eaccelerator.ini your_script.php`. This will make PHP only use the eaccelerator.ini file and not any other .ini files.

Remember to restart your web server or PHP-FPM (if you're using FPM) after making these changes. If you're running PHP from the command line, no restart is necessary.
<|end|>


