Formulate a segment of HTML structure that incorporates an interactive interface, specifically a form, in a manner that authorizes a user to input their contact number in a universally recognized international format.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
To create this task in HTML, you would require an input form where the user can type in their phone number. Here is a simple way to achieve this using a HTML form and input field:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>Contact Form</title>
</head>
<body>
    <form>
        <label for="phone-number">Contact Number (in international format: +1234567890):</label>
        <input type="tel" id="phone-number" name="phone-number" pattern="\+[0-9]{1,3}[0-9]{3,14}$" required>
        <small>Format: +1234567890</small>
        <br>
        <input type="submit" value="Submit">
    </form>
</body>
</html>
```

In the above code:

- The `<form>` element is used to create an HTML form for user input.
- The `<input>` element with `type="tel"` is used to create an input field for a telephone number. 
- The `pattern` attribute specifies a regular expression that the input field's value is checked against. The regular expression `"\+[0-9]{1,3}[0-9]{3,14}$"` checks for a leading "+" followed by 1-3 digits (the country code) and then a 3-14 digit number (the rest of the phone number).
- The `required` attribute is a boolean attribute. When present, it specifies that an input field must be filled out before submitting the form.
- The `<label>` tag defines a label for the input field.
