Develop a Java function that alternates array elements, swapping every 2nd item with its preceding item in an integer array.
[1, 2, 3, 4, 5]
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here is a simple Java method that swaps every second item with its preceding item in an array:

```java
public class Test {

    public static void alternateArrayElements(int[] array) {
        for (int i = 0; i < array.length-1; i += 2) {
            int temp = array[i];
            array[i] = array[i+1];
            array[i+1] = temp;
        }
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[] arr = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5};
        alternateArrayElements(arr);
        for (int num: arr){
            System.out.print(num + " ");
        }
    }
}
```
What this does is that it goes through the array 2 indexes at a time, and then swaps the current index 'i' with the next index 'i+1' in the array.

Please note that if the array has an odd length, then the last element will not be swapped since there is no subsequent element to swap it with.

In the main method, we call the function and print out the content of the array to see the output. For array {1, 2, 3, 4, 5}, the output will be: 2 1 4 3 5. As you can see, each pair of elements have been swapped.
<|end|>


