Develop a piece of programming code that executes the Bubble Sort algorithm, a comparison-based sorting method, on a provided array of integer values. This code should be able to handle any array size and should be efficient in terms of time complexity.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Sure, here's the Python implementation of the Bubble Sort algorithm:

```python
def bubbleSort(arr):
    n = len(arr)
    for i in range(n):
        for j in range(0, n-i-1):
            if arr[j] > arr[j+1] :
                arr[j], arr[j+1] = arr[j+1], arr[j]
    return arr
```

You can use this function on any integer list as follows:

```python
print(bubbleSort([64, 34, 25, 12, 22, 11, 90]))
```

This will print the sorted list: [11, 12, 22, 25, 34, 64, 90]

However, please note that Bubble Sort is not an efficient sorting algorithm for large data sets as its average and worst-case time complexity are both O(n^2), where n is the number of items. Alternative sorting algorithms with better time complexities include QuickSort, MergeSort, or HeapSort.
<|end|>


