*Assume that we conducted an ANOVA test, and we have a difference.
Now let's say we measured the difference between groups (countries in my case), and Python outputted the following table (it's a partial output)
[](https://i.stack.imgur.com/tjNdN.png)
Is that possible to know who are the groups that are different from each other?
