Write a Java program to calculate and display the factorial of the first 7 natural numbers.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Consider the following Java program that calculates and displays the factorial of the first 7 natural numbers.

```java
public class Factorial {
    // define the main function
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        // loop from 1 to 7
        for (int i=1; i<=7; i++) {
            System.out.println("The factorial of " + i + " is " + calculateFactorial(i));
        }
    }

    // function to calculate factorial
    public static long calculateFactorial(int n) {
        long factorial = 1;
        for (int i= 1; i<=n; i++) {
            factorial *= i;
        }
        return factorial;
    }
}
```

This program will output:

```
The factorial of 1 is 1
The factorial of 2 is 2
The factorial of 3 is 6
The factorial of 4 is 24
The factorial of 5 is 120
The factorial of 6 is 720
The factorial of 7 is 5040
```

The `calculateFactorial(int n)` function calculates the factorial of a number n and returns the result. This function is used in a loop in the `main` function to calculate and print the factorial of numbers 1 through 7.
