Design a JavaScript function that not only accepts integers but also fractions as inputs, each representing a complex number (real and imaginary part), and gives the result of performing multiplication on these complex values. In addition to multiplication, allow the function to perform subtraction on complex values.
num1_real = 2.5, num1_imaginary = 3.2, num2_real = 4.7, num2_imaginary = 5.8
<|end|>
<|asst|>
You can create a JavaScript function like this:

```javascript
function Complex(real, imaginary) {
  this.real = real;
  this.imaginary = imaginary;
}

Complex.prototype.multiply = function (other) {
  const real = this.real * other.real - this.imaginary * other.imaginary;
  const imaginary = this.real * other.imaginary + other.real * this.imaginary;
  return new Complex(real, imaginary);
};

Complex.prototype.subtract = function (other) {
  const real = this.real - other.real;
  const imaginary = this.imaginary - other.imaginary;
  return new Complex(real, imaginary);
};

//Input
let num1 = new Complex(2.5, 3.2);
let num2 = new Complex(4.7, 5.8);

// Perform multiplication
let multiplicationOutput = num1.multiply(num2);

// Perform subtraction
let subtractionOutput = num1.subtract(num2);

// Print the results
console.log(`Multiplication result: ${multiplicationOutput.real} + ${multiplicationOutput.imaginary}i`);
console.log(`Subtraction result: ${subtractionOutput.real} + ${subtractionOutput.imaginary}i`);
```

This code defines a class representing a complex number, with two prototype functions for performing multiplication and subtraction of complex numbers.

In the multiplication function, the formula of multiplication for complex numbers is applied (a+bi)(c+di) = ac-bd + (ad+bc)i.
In the subtraction function, the formula of subtraction for complex numbers is applied (a-bi) - (c+di) = a-c -(b-d)i.

Then we create two complex numbers num1 and num2 using the input values, perform the multiplication and subtraction, and print the results.
<|end|>


