<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here's the JavaScript code to solve the problem:

```javascript
const strongestExtension = (class_name, extensions) => {
    let strongestExt = extensions[0];
    let maxStrength = getStrength(extensions[0][0]);
    
    for (let i = 1; i < extensions.length; i++) {
        let strength = getStrength(extensions[i][0]);
        if(strength > maxStrength) {
            maxStrength = strength;
            strongestExt = extensions[i];
        }
    }
    
    return `${class_name}.${strongestExt[0]}.${strongestExt[1]}`;
};

const getStrength = (extension) => {
    let uppercaseCount = [...extension].filter(letter => letter === letter.toUpperCase()).length;
    let lowercaseCount = [...extension].filter(letter => letter === letter.toLowerCase()).length;
    return uppercaseCount - lowercaseCount;
};
```
In the code, `getStrength` function receives an extension name as a parameter and calculates the difference between the numbers of uppercase and lowercase letters in this name. This score presents the strength of the extension.
In function `strongestExtension`, I sequentially go through all the extensions, calculate their strength and check if the current extension is stronger than the current strongest. We initiate the strongest extension with the first one and update it if we find a stronger extension. Finally, we return the string containing class_name, strongest extension, and method_name.
