Design an advanced Java class that efficiently constructs a wide-ranging repository of literary works along with their corresponding authors and date of publication. This should be done with the ability to handle different types of literary styles (like poetry, prose, drama) and also manage different editions of the same literary work.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here is a simple implementation of this problem:

```java
import java.util.*;

class Author {
    private String name;

    Author(String name) {
        this.name = name;
    }

    String getName() {
        return name;
    }
}

class Edition {
    private String editionName;
    private Date publicationDate;

    Edition(String editionName, Date publicationDate) {
        this.editionName = editionName;
        this.publicationDate = publicationDate;
    }

    String getEditionName() {
        return this.editionName;
    }

    Date getPublicationDate() {
        return this.publicationDate;
    }
}

class Work {
    private String title;
    private String type; // type can be poetry, prose, drama
    private List<Edition> editions;
    private Author author;

    Work(String title, String type, Author author) {
        this.title = title;
        this.type = type;
        this.author = author;
        this.editions = new ArrayList<>();
    }

    void addEdition(String editionName, Date publicationDate) {
        this.editions.add(new Edition(editionName, publicationDate));
    }
  
    String getTitle() {
        return this.title;
    }

    String getType() {
        return this.type;
    }

    Author getAuthor() {
        return this.author;
    }

    List<Edition> getEditions() {
        return this.editions;
    }
}

class LiteraryWorksRepository {
    private List<Work> works;

    LiteraryWorksRepository() {
        this.works = new ArrayList<>();
    }

    void addWork(String title, String type, Author author) {
        works.add(new Work(title, type, author));
    }
  
    void addEditionToWork(String title, String editionName, Date publicationDate) {
        for (Work work : works) {
            if (work.getTitle().equals(title)) {
                work.addEdition(editionName, publicationDate);
                break;
            }
        }
    }

    List<Work> getAllWorks() {
        return this.works;
    }
}
```
In the above Java code, four classes have been defined: `Author`, `Edition`, `Work`, `LiteraryWorksRepository`. To handle different literary styles, we use a string variable "type" for the `Work` class. For managing different editions of the same literary work, we use a `List` of `Edition` objects in the `Work` class.
<|end|>


