Construct two distinct and individual CSS code segments: the premier segment should exemplify a nested dropdown navigation menu employing CSS, while the ensuing segment should portray an interactive gallery of images, harnessing the power of CSS Grid and Flexbox. The latter code segment must possess the ability to adapt to diverse screen resolutions and viewing angles.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
1. CSS nested dropdown navigation menu:

HTML:
```html
<nav class="navbar">
  <ul>
    <li><a href="#">Home</a></li>
    <li><a href="#">About Us</a></li>
    <li>
      <a href="#">Services</a>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="#">Graphics</a></li>
        <li><a href="#">Development</a></li>
        <li><a href="#">Marketing</a></li>
      </ul>
    </li>
  </ul>
</nav>
```
CSS:
```css
.navbar ul {
  list-style-type: none;
  padding: 0;
}

.navbar li {
  display: inline-block;
  position: relative;
}

.navbar li ul {
  display: none;
  position: absolute;
  top: 100%;
}

.navbar li:hover ul {
  display: block;
}
```

2. CSS Grid and Flexbox for a responsive image gallery:

HTML:
```html
<div class="gallery">
  <div class="image-box"><img src="img1.jpg"></div>
  <div class="image-box"><img src="img2.jpg"></div>
  <div class="image-box"><img src="img3.jpg"></div>
  <!-- add as many images as you want -->
</div>
```
CSS:
```css
/* Grid for larger screens */
.gallery {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(200px, 1fr));
  grid-gap: 10px;
}

.image-box {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: center;
  align-items: center;
}

.image-box img {
  max-width: 100%;
  height: auto;
}

/* Flexbox for smaller screens */
@media (max-width: 600px) {
  .gallery {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
  }
 
 .image-box {
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }
}
```
With the power of CSS Grid and Flexbox, the image gallery is now responsive and will adapt its layout depending on the viewer’s screen size.
<|end|>


