Generate a Java program that creates a random multi-dimensional array with 3 dimensions each of size 10, filled with random integers ranging from 0 to 99. Additionally, write a function to find the maximum value within this three-dimensional array.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here is a Java program that generates a 3D array filled with random integers and finds the maximum value in the array.

```java
import java.util.Random;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[][][] array = create3DArray(10, 10, 10);
        System.out.println(findMax(array));
    }

    // Function to generate a 3D array with random values
    public static int[][][] create3DArray(int dim1, int dim2, int dim3) {
        Random random = new Random();
        int[][][] array = new int[dim1][dim2][dim3];
        for(int i = 0; i < dim1; i++) {
            for(int j = 0; j < dim2; j++) {
                for(int k = 0; k < dim3; k++) {
                    array[i][j][k] = random.nextInt(100); // Random number between 0 and 99
                }
            }
        }
        return array;
    }

    // Function to find the maximum value in the 3D array
    public static int findMax(int[][][] array) {
        int max = Integer.MIN_VALUE;
        for(int[][] twoDArray : array) {
            for(int[] oneDArray : twoDArray) {
                for(int number : oneDArray) {
                    if(number > max) {
                        max = number;
                    }
                }
            }
        }
        return max;
    }
}
```

In the `create3DArray` function, we generate a 3D array and fill it with random integers from 0 to 99. We create a `Random` object and then loop through each dimension of the array, assigning a new random integer to each element.

The `findMax` function iterates over every element in the 3D array and keeps track of the maximum value seen so far. It assumes that all values in the array are non-negative. If this is not the case, you would start `maxValue` at `Integer.MIN_VALUE` before the loop.
<|end|>


