The provided code snippet seems to be using Apache Flink, a Java/Scala framework that is not readily translatable to JavaScript, especially because JavaScript doesn't inherently support streams in the same way. However, you should be able to consume messages from a Kafka topic in Node.js (which supports JavaScript) using the library `kafka-node`. Here is an equivalent JavaScript version:

```javascript
const kafka = require('kafka-node');
const client = new kafka.KafkaClient({kafkaHost: 'localhost:9092'}); // replace with your Kafka host

const clickstreamLogsConsumer = new kafka.Consumer(client, [{ topic: 'clickstream-topic' }], {encoding: 'utf8'});
clickstreamLogsConsumer.on('message', function (message) {
    let clickstreamLogs = message.value;
    // continue processing
});

const productDetailsConsumer = new kafka.Consumer(client, [{ topic: 'product-topic' }], {encoding: 'utf8'});
productDetailsConsumer.on('message', function (message) {
    let productDetails = message.value;
    // continue processing
});

const userDetailsConsumer = new kafka.Consumer(client, [{ topic: 'user-topic' }], {encoding: 'utf8'});
userDetailsConsumer.on('message', function (message) {
    let userDetails = message.value;
    // continue processing
});
```
I hope this help you. Please have configured and set your own `kafkaHost`.
