CSS code:

```css
/* This defines keyframes for the animation, specifying that 
   the animation should start with the original color, gradually 
   change to a lighter color, and then change back to the original color. */
@keyframes pulsate {
  0%, 100% {
    background-color: initial;
  }
  50% {
    background-color: #ff0; /* Change this to a lighter color of your initial color */
  }
}

/* This applies the animation effect to the button when it's not being hovered over.
   The animation-name property specifies the name of the animation ('pulsate'). 
   The animation-duration property specifies how long one cycle of the animation should take.
   The animation-iteration-count property specifies that the animation should repeat indefinitely.
   The animation-timing-function property specifies that the animation should progress smoothly. */
#submit:not(:hover) {
  animation: pulsate 2s infinite ease-in-out;
}

/* This applies the animation effect to the button when it's being hovered over, 
   overriding the previous animation-duration to make the animation run faster (1s instead of 2s). */
