<|user|>
Create an animation with HTML and CSS.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Creating a simple animation with HTML and CSS involves designing the HTML structure for the animated element and then applying CSS styles and animations to it. 

Here's a simple example of a rectangle which moves horizontally from left to right.

Part 1: The HTML
```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="styles.css">
</head>
<body>
  <div class="animated-box"></div>
</body>
</html>
```
In this HTML code, we're creating a div with the class `animated-box`. We'll be applying styles and animations to this div in our CSS.

Part 2: The CSS
```css
.animated-box {
  width: 100px;
  height: 100px;
  background-color: red;
  position: relative;
  animation-name: slide;
  animation-duration: 4s;
  animation-iteration-count: infinite;
}

@keyframes slide {
  from {left: 0px;}
  to {left: 300px;}
}
```

In this CSS code, we're defining both the styles for the `animated-box` div and the animation it should use. 

- The `width`, `height`, and `background-color` properties define the look of the box. 
- The `position: relative;` is necessary for us to be able to animate the movement of the box using the `left` property.
- The `animation-name` refers to a @keyframes at-rule, which defines what styles the animation will have at certain times. 
- The `animation-duration` specifies how long time an animation should take to complete. 
- If the `animation-iteration-count` property is set to `infinite`, the animation will be repeated forever.

In the `@keyframes` rule called "slide", we're defining that the box should start (`from`) at `0px` left position, and end up (`to`) at `300px` left position. This will create the effect of the box sliding horizontally from left to right.

Remember that for the CSS and HTML to be connected they need to be either in the same file or the CSS file needs to be linked to the HTML file. 

This is just a very simple example, and CSS animations can get a lot complex, allowing for many amazing effects.
<|end|>


