Character Sequence: hello world
Designated Quantity: 5
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here's how you can achieve that using JavaScript:

```javascript
function extractSymbols(string, quantity) {
    var result = ''; 
    var count = 0;
    for (var i = 0; i < string.length; i++) {
        if ((string[i].charCodeAt(0) >= 65 && string[i].charCodeAt(0) <= 90) || (string[i].charCodeAt(0) >= 97 && string[i].charCodeAt(0) <= 122) || (string[i].charCodeAt(0) >= 48 && string[i].charCodeAt(0) <= 57)) {
            result += string[i];
            count++;
        }
        
        if (count == quantity) {
            break;
        }
    }

    return result;
}

var sequence = "hello world";
var quantity = 5;
console.log(extractSymbols(sequence, quantity));
```
This function takes a string and a quantity as inputs. It goes through each character in the string and checks whether it is an uppercase letter, a lowercase letter, or a number (between '0' and '9') by using the ASCII values of the characters. If it is, it's added to the result. This continues until the quantity has been met.

Test this using your given parameters, and you'll receive "hello" as the output, which are the first 5 alphabet characters. Do note that this function considers spaces and special characters, if you want to ignore these characters and only consider alphanumeric characters you might have to modify the function accordingly.
