I used to use the following method to get the name of a text file shared via  to my app:

string GetIntentFilename(Android.Net.Uri uri)
{
    string filename;
    string temp;

    using (var c1 = ContentResolver.Query(uri, null, null, null, null))
    {
        c1.MoveToFirst();
        temp = c1.GetString(0);

        filename = temp.Substring(temp.LastIndexOf(":") + 1);
    }

    return filename.Trim();
}


If I shared a file , the above method would return 
Recently however it has been returning me a weird name, similar to the following: 
I've tried sharing the file with other apps and they successfully extract the  filename, so I'm sure the information exists somewhere in the intent, but I don't know how to get it.
Any ideas?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Since Android 10, due to privacy measures, Android introduced scoped storage concept & changed the way of sharing files using content providers, which started generating random names for files.

The code you have been using, relies on Uri's last path segment, which is not the real filename anymore.

Here's the method updated to handle this and extract the actual file name:

```
public string GetFileName(Android.Net.Uri uri)
{
    string filename = null;
    if (ContentResolver.SchemeContent.Equals(uri.Scheme))
    {
        ICursor cursor = ContentResolver.Query(uri, null, null, null, null);
        try
        {
            if (cursor != null && cursor.MoveToFirst())
            {
                filename = cursor.GetString(cursor.GetColumnIndex(OpenableColumns.DisplayName));
            }
        }
        finally
        {
            cursor?.Close();
        }
    }
    if (filename == null)
    {
        filename = uri.Path;
        int cut = filename.LastIndexOf('/');
        if (cut != -1)
        {
            filename = filename.Substring(cut + 1);
        }
    }
    return filename;
}
```

The updated method first tries to get file name from cursor using `OpenableColumns.DisplayName`. If it fails, it falls back to using the last path segment as before.
<|end|>


