Develop a valid C code to print the array elements in reverse order. You are provided with an erroneous code snippet below. Identify the error in this code and correct it to print out the array elements in reverse without using built-in functions.

```c
int arr[] = {1,2,3,4,5};
int length = sizeof(arr)/sizeof(arr[0]);
for(int i=0; i<length; i++){
    printf("%d ", arr[length-i]);
}
```

