I'm doing some automation for Reddit via Chrome extension, and ran into a problem that I can not get the name of the authorized user. I have access to cookies/session storage, but Reddit doesn't store the username there. I tried GET-request to `https://www.reddit.com/api/v1/me` but getting only some settings for authorized account. Is there any way to get authorized user name? Will be grateful to any help!
<|end|>
<|asst|>
You can get Reddit username using the Reddit API endpoint /api/v1/me. You need to supply the correct headers to this endpoint at the time of sending a request. This includes authorization and user agent details.

From the browser extension, you can do the request with Fetch API. Here's an example:

```javascript
fetch('https://oauth.reddit.com/api/v1/me', {
  headers: {
    'Authorization': `bearer YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN`,
    'User-Agent': 'YOUR_APP_NAME_AND_VERSION',
  },
})
.then(response => response.json())
.then(responseJson => console.log(responseJson['name']));
```

Replace `'YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN'` with the access token you receive when your extension initially authenticates with Reddit, and `'YOUR_APP_NAME_AND_VERSION'` with a string that indicates your app's name and version.

The `/api/v1/me` endpoint will then return a JSON object that contains lots of useful information about the authorized user, including their username, which you can access with: `responseJson['name']`.

However, keep in mind that receiving the access token requires a more involved OAuth process where the user needs to give your application the appropriate permissions to access their account details, and your app needs to provide Reddit with a `client_id` and `client_secret` which you get when you register your app with Reddit. Keep these values confidential to prevent unauthorized use. 

You can check out Reddit's API OAuth documentation for more details.
<|end|>


