<|asst|>
Sure, I can help with that. Here is the translation of the code to PHP:

```php
function count_upper_case_vowels($s) {
    // Define the array of vowels
    $vowels = array('A', 'E', 'I', 'O', 'U');
    $count = 0;

    // Split the input string into an array of characters
    $chars = str_split($s);

    // Loop through each character in the string
    foreach($chars as $i => $c) {
        // Check if the character is in the vowel array and the index is even
        if (in_array($c, $vowels) && $i % 2 == 0) {
            // If it's a vowel and its position is even, increase the count
            $count++;
        }
    }

    // Return the count of uppercase vowels on even indices
    return $count;
}
```

This PHP function does the same thing as the Python function. It counts the number of uppercase vowels in a string located at the even index. It does that by first defining a list of vowels, then it turns the input string into an array of characters. It then loops through this array and checks each character. If the character is in the list of vowels and its index is even (i.e. the character is at an even position in the string), it increments a counter. Finally, it returns this count.
