<|user|>
I recently started using the package `flutter_animate` and it was love at first sight. But how do I restart an animation when a widget gets rebuilt?
E.g., my widget below animates great

Text('Good\nJob!')
  .animate()
  .fadeOut(duration: 2000.ms).scaleXY(duration: 2000.ms, end: 2.0)


But when I `setState` and the widget rebuilds, the animation doesn't restart and the text remains faded out. Is there a way to trigger a restart on animations every time a widget rebuilds?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
As soon as your widget rebuilds, necessarily it builds a new instance of the widget tree and hence the `flutter_animate` package will not restart the animations automatically. To achieve this, whenever the widget rebuilds, you need to explicitly control the animation and reset it to its initial conditions.

You can achieve this by using the `AnimationController` provided by Flutter.

Below is an example of how to restart an animation when a widget rebuilds:

```dart
// Step 1: Initialize AnimationController and Animation
AnimationController animationController;
Animation animation;

// Step 2: Initialize Animation in initState
@override
void initState() {
  super.initState();
  animationController =
    AnimationController(duration: const Duration(milliseconds: 2000), vsync: this);

  animation = Tween<double>(begin: 1, end: 2).animate(animationController);
}

// Reset animation inside of the build method
Text('Good\nJob!')
  .animate(animationController)
  .fadeOut(duration: 2000.ms).scaleXY(duration: 2000.ms, end: 2.0)

  // Use a `setState` to reset the animation when any specific condition holds true
  setState(() {
    animationController.reset(); // reset the animationController
    animationController.forward(); // restart the animation
  });
```

Note: You need to clean-up the `AnimationController` when the widget is disposed using `animationController.dispose()` method to avoid memory leaks.

Please ensure to modify the code according to your needs.
<|end|>


