Here are some solutions using several popular programming languages:

Python:
```python
def headline(title):
    return title.title()

title = 'the quick brown fox'
print(headline(title))  # Outputs: The Quick Brown Fox
```

JavaScript:
```javascript
function headline(title) {
    return title.replace(/\w\S*/g, function(txt){return txt.charAt(0).toUpperCase() + txt.substr(1).toLowerCase();});
}

var title = 'the quick brown fox';
console.log(headline(title));  // Outputs: The Quick Brown Fox
```

Java:
```java
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String title = "the quick brown fox";
        System.out.println(toTitleCase(title));  // Outputs: The Quick Brown Fox
    }

    public static String toTitleCase(String input) {
        StringBuilder titleCase = new StringBuilder();
        boolean nextTitleCase = true;

        for (char c : input.toCharArray()) {
            if (Character.isSpaceChar(c)) {
                nextTitleCase = true;
            } else if (nextTitleCase) {
                c = Character.toTitleCase(c);
                nextTitleCase = false;
            }

            titleCase.append(c);
        }

        return titleCase.toString();
    }
}
```

Note: The Java solution is more verbose because the Java `String` class does not provide a built-in method for converting a string to title case. We therefore need to implement this functionality manually.

C#:
```csharp
using System;
using System.Globalization;

class MainClass {
    public static void Main(string[] args) {
        string title = "the quick brown fox";
        Console.WriteLine(ToTitleCase(title));  // Outputs: The Quick Brown Fox
    }

    public static string ToTitleCase(string title) {
        return CultureInfo.CurrentCulture.TextInfo.ToTitleCase(title);
    }
}
```

In each of these solutions, the function takes a string as input and returns a new string where the first letter of each word is capitalized and all other letters are in lowercase. This format is a common style for headlines.
<|end|>


