Swift currently does not support direct access to Google Sheets or TextBlob like Python. The conversion or reimplementation of the current text sentiment analysis algorithm might need a different approach due to the platform and language limitations.

You can create a web API using Python and Flask where you will wrap your current Python code that communicates with Google sheets and performs sentiment analysis. Then in your Swift code, you would make a request to this web API and get the response.

Here's an approximate Swift example of how you can make HTTP requests:

```swift
import Foundation

let url = URL(string: "http://localhost:5000/sentiment")!
let task = URLSession.shared.dataTask(with: url) {(data, response, error) in
    guard let data = data else { return }
    print(String(data: data, encoding: .utf8)!)
}

task.resume()
```
The Python script with Flask could look something like this:

```python
from flask import Flask, jsonify
import gspread
from oauth2client.service_account import ServiceAccountCredentials
from textblob import TextBlob
import nltk

nltk.download('punkt')
nltk.download('averaged_perceptron_tagger')

app = Flask(__name__)

@app.route('/sentiment', methods=['GET'])
def sentiment_analysis():
    scope = ['https://spreadsheets.google.com/feeds','https://www.googleapis.com/auth/spreadsheets',"https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive.file","https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive"]
    creds = ServiceAccountCredentials.from_json_keyfile_name('creds.json', scope)
    client = gspread.authorize(creds)

    doc = client.open('Document name')
    sheet = doc.sheet1

    rows = sheet.get_all_records()

    all_reviews = []

    for row in rows:
        text = row['Review']
        blob = TextBlob(text)
        all_reviews.append({"row": row, "sentiment": str(blob.sentiment)})

    return jsonify(all_reviews)

if __name__ == "__main__":
    app.run(debug=True)
```

You could develop a native Swift application using Google's iOS SDK for accessing Google Sheets and a language processing library for sentiment analysis but it would need significantly more code and programming experience in Swift and iOS development.
