<|asst|>
Sure, Here's how you can achieve this in Python:

```python
def alternate_case(s):
    """Switch cases in a string."""
    return ''.join(c.upper() if i % 2 == 0 else c.lower() for i, c in enumerate(s))

# Test the function
print(alternate_case("Hello World!"))
```

Here, we have created a simple python function named `alternate_case`, which takes a string input and for every character in the string, it changes the case to uppercase if the current index is even, otherwise it changes the case to lowercase. This gives us the alternating pattern of upper and lowercase letters. We then join the transformed characters back into a string using `join()`. 

When you run this script with the input of "Hello World!", the output will be: "HeLlO WoRlD!".
