<|asst|>
Here is a solution to make the `input` elements use the available horizontal space in a flex container:

```html
<main>
    <section class="sectionClass">
        <span>Name:</span>
        <input type="text" bind:value={...} class="inputClass" />
        <span>Age:</span>
        <input type="text" bind:value={...} class="inputClass" />
    </section>
</main>

<style>
    .sectionClass {
        display: flex;
        gap: 1rem;

        /* Add this to handle overflowing elements */
        flex-wrap: wrap;
    }

    .inputClass {
        flex: 1 0 auto; /* Try using this instead */
        min-width: 0; /* Add this to prevent problems with text input width on smaller screens */
    }
</style>
```

There're several problems you're likely running into:

1. Text inputs want to be wider, and the `flex: 1;` rule isn't strong enough to make them shrink. `flex: 1 0 auto;` and `min-width: 0;` fix this. It makes element to take its share of the remaining space in the container.
2. If elements overflowed container, you could set `flex-wrap: wrap;` to move items that can't fit onto a new line.
<|end|>


