Alter the following sequence of lowercase English alphabets into their equivalent respective symbols in uppercase typographical representation: hello world
<|end|>
<|asst|>
This problem can be solved using programming languages such as Python, Java, C++, JavaScript, etc. Below are the solutions in some of these languages.

Python:
```python
# Python solution
text = "hello world"
uppercase_text = text.upper()
print(uppercase_text)
```

If you run this Python code, it will output `HELLO WORLD`.

Java:
```java
// Java solution
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String text = "hello world";
        String uppercaseText = text.toUpperCase();
        System.out.println(uppercaseText);
    }
}
```

When you run this Java code, it will print `HELLO WORLD`.

JavaScript:
```javascript
// JavaScript solution
var text = "hello world";
var uppercaseText = text.toUpperCase();
console.log(uppercaseText);
```

Above JavaScript code displays `HELLO WORLD` in console.

C++:
```cpp
// C++ solution
#include <algorithm>
#include <iostream>
#include <string>

int main() {
    std::string text = "hello world";
    std::transform(text.begin(), text.end(),text.begin(), ::toupper);
    std::cout << text << std::endl;
    return 0;
}
```

If you run this C++ code, it will output `HELLO WORLD`.
<|end|>


