I just migrated my old MAMP version on Windows. I uninstalled properly MAMP 4.2.0 and installed MAMP 5.0.5. I went into the MAMP preferences / PHP tab and changed from PHP version 8.0.1 to version 8.1.0.
After starting the servers, I tried to open the WebStart page and I got a blank screen with lot of errors in php_errors.log file like : "PHP Startup: Unable to load dynamic library *.dll". The DLL are all in the specified directory.
If I change to PHP 8.0.1, everything works fine.
I looked at all the log files and tried PHP 8.0.1 which works fine. Trying again with PHP 8.1.0 leads to the same errors.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
This seems like an issue with your PHP configuration, specifically regarding the dynamic libraries. There are a couple of things you can try to solve this:
 
1. Ensure that the path to your PHP's "ext" folder is correctly specified in your php.ini file. You should see a line in your php.ini file that looks something like this: `extension_dir = "PATH_TO_YOUR_PHP/ext"`. Replace "PATH_TO_YOUR_PHP" with the actual path to your PHP folder. The "ext" folder should contain all the .dll files your PHP installation needs.

2. It might also be possible that some necessary DLL files are either missing or doesn't compatible with PHP 8.1.0. In this case, you may want to consider downloading and installing those DLLs specifically.

3. One more thing you can try is to disable some of the extensions you don't need in your php.ini file, then restart MAMP and see if that resolves the issue.

4. If all else fails, consider contacting MAMP support or forums for more help or possible revert to executing your projects under PHP 8.0.1 until there is a clear path on migration to 8.1.0.

Any change in the php.ini file requires a restart of the servers for the changes to take effect.

Remember to always save a backup of your php.ini file before making any changes. This way, you can revert back to the original configuration if anything goes wrong.
<|end|>


