how to wait request to be done before clicking on btn in puppeteer-sharp ?
what I am trying to do is:
1.click on btn ( to make ajax request on website ) 
2.wait request to be done 
3.click on submit btn
what I am doing now is:
1.click on btn ( to make ajax request on website  ) `await page.ClickAsync("#id")` 
2.wait for some time ( `await page.WaitForTimeoutAsync(2000);` ) 
3.click on submit btn
<|end|>
<|asst|>
To monitor if a request is finished, you could listen into the `RequestFinished` event provided by PuppeteerSharp:


Here is a code representation:

```csharp
// First we have to subscribe to the event
page.RequestFinished += async (sender, e) => {
    // Check if it's the request you are looking.
    if (e.Request.Url.Contains("the_url_or_part_of_the_url_you_are_waiting")) {
        // You can also check the response status.
        if (e.Response.Status == HttpStatusCode.OK) {
            // Then you can click the submit btn
            await page.ClickAsync("#submit-button-id");
        }
    }
};

// Then you click on the button to make the AJAX Call
await page.ClickAsync("#button-id");
```

The code above is looking for requests that ends with a specific URL, and if the request ends correctly, we click on the "submit" button.

Remember to unsubscribe the event once it's no longer needed.

Please note that this is just an example, make sure to modify the URL and conditions based on your requirements.
  
The `RequestFinished` event gets emitted when a request finishes successfully after the response is received and all data chunks are delivered.

This technique is safer than a `page.WaitForTimeoutAsync(2000)` because the latter simply adds a delay which can result in race conditions if the request is delayed for some unforeseen reason.

Moreover, the website might block you if you are sending requests in a very short span of time because it could be detected as a bot activity. So, it's advised to add some delay when you are clicking or navigating in Puppeteer browser programmatically.
<|end|>


