Write a Java program to convert a recursively given array of characters to a string and find the longest palindrome substring within the converted string. You must implement your own recursive function to perform the string conversion, not using Java's built-in functions. Also, ensure that the solution has an optimal time complexity.

Input: ['a', 'b', 'c', 'a', 'b', 'b', 'c']
Output: "abbcabb" - Longest palindrome substring: "abba"
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here is a java program that solves the problem using recursion, dynamic programming and has an optimal time complexity of O(n^2). The program first converts the array of characters to string using a recursive function and then finds the longest palindrome substring.

```java
public class Main {
    public static String convertToString(char[] arr, int start) {
        if (start >= arr.length) {
            return "";
        }
        return arr[start] + convertToString(arr, start + 1);
    }
    
    public static String longestPalindrome(String str) {
        int n = str.length();   
        boolean table[][] = new boolean[n][n]; 
        int maxLength = 1;
        
        for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i)
            table[i][i] = true;
        
        int start = 0;
        for (int i = 0; i < n - 1; ++i) {
            if (str.charAt(i) == str.charAt(i + 1)) {
                table[i][i + 1] = true;
                start = i;
                maxLength = 2;
            }
        }
        
        for (int length = 3; length <= n; ++length) {
            for (int i = 0; i < n - length + 1; ++i) {
                int j = i + length - 1;
                
                if (table[i + 1][j - 1] && str.charAt(i) == str.charAt(j)) {
                    table[i][j] = true;
                    start = i;
                    maxLength = length;
                }
            }
        }
        return str.substring(start, start + maxLength);    
    }
    
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        char[] arr = { 'a', 'b', 'c', 'a', 'b', 'b', 'c' };
        String str = convertToString(arr, 0);
        System.out.println("Converted string: " + str);
        System.out.println("Longest palindrome substring: " + longestPalindrome(str));
    }
}
```

Explanation:

The 'convertToString' function converts the array of characters to string using recursion. It adds the current character to the result of the conversion of the rest of the array.

The 'longestPalindrome' function uses dynamic programming to find the longest palindrome substring. It creates a 2D boolean table where table[i][j] indicates whether the substring from index i to j is palindrome or not. It initializes the table for substrings of length 1 and 2, and then fills up the table for longer substrings using bottom up approach. The longest palindrome substring is the substring that has the maximum length and is palindrome according to the table.

The main function reads the character array, converts it to string using the 'convertToString' function, and then calls the 'longestPalindrome' function to find the longest palindrome substring.
<|end|>


