insert into fiche_qualites (poi_id, qualites_id) values (idPoi, 'Code error');


My error:

ERROR:  syntax error at or near "insert"


I'm in a loop doing mass inserts and I want to be able to keep track when I have a duplicate (detected by uniqueness).
<|end|>
<|asst|>
In Postgres, the `ON CONFLICT DO` clause can only be used with `DO NOTHING` or `DO UPDATE` commands. You can't directly insert into another table within this clause.

If you are dealing with duplicate situation, it's more like you need a separate `PL/pgSQL` function or stored procedure or consider other ways to handle insertion into the log table.

Example of a function would be like:

```
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION insert_fiche(content text)
RETURNS VOID AS
$$
DECLARE
id fiche.poi_id%type;
BEGIN
    INSERT INTO fiche (content)
    VALUES (content)
    ON CONFLICT (content)
    DO NOTHING
    RETURNING poi_id INTO id;

    IF id IS NULL THEN
        INSERT INTO fiche_qualites (poi_id, qualites_id)
        VALUES (id, 'Code error');
    END IF;
END;
$$
LANGUAGE plpgsql;
```

Then you can use this function in your insert statement:

```
SELECT insert_fiche('content value');
```

This function will insert a row into the `fiche` table, if the `content` value is duplicated (which will cause a conflict), then it will insert a log into the `fiche_qualites` table.

**Please adjust data types and the function according to your requirements. This is just a basic guidance of how you could potentially handle the situation.**
<|end|>


