I want to save the Rich Text Editor value automatically. Like during content updating, content should automatically be saved after 1 minute. I got this link [https://sitecoregadgets.blogspot.com/2011/11/rich-text-auto-save.html](https://sitecoregadgets.blogspot.com/2011/11/rich-text-auto-save.html). But solution files are not available at the given link. I also tried using javascript to hit the "Accept" button in the rich text editor, but the editor closed that case. 
Following code write down for testing:

setTimeout(function(){
         
                    
                     scSendRequest(event, 'editorpage:accept'); // This is call to RTE Accept button.
                     var test =document.getElementsByClassName("scRibbonToolbarLargeButton");
                     test[0].click(); // This is call to the ribbon save button

          },30000);


Auto save RTE value.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here's an example of how you can accomplish the auto-save functionality using JavaScript: 

1. First, you need to override the Rich Text Editor (RTE) page to include your own JavaScript file. To do so, duplicate the default rte page located at `/sitecore/shell/Controls/Rich Text Editor/Default.aspx` and include your custom JS file into it before the closing body tag.

```html
<script src="/path/to/yourjavascriptfile.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
```

2. In your Sitecore configuration include the patch to use the new RTE page:

```xml
<configuration xmlns:patch="http://www.sitecore.net/xmlconfig/">
<sitecore>
  <settings>
    <setting name="WebStylesheet">
      <patch:attribute name="value">/sitecore/shell/Controls/Rich Text Editor/YourRTEPage.aspx</patch:attribute>
    </setting>
  </settings>
</sitecore>
</configuration>
```

3. Create a JavaScript timer function that saves the content every minute. To save, we just fire the `scSave` event. If you look at `webedit.js`, you can see how Sitecore handles these sc events:

```javascript
var autoSaveFrequency = 60000; // 60000ms = 1 minute
var autoSaveTimer;

function autoSave() {
  try {
    //scSave is part of Sitecore's webedit.js and saves the current item
    scSave();
  } catch (err) {
    console.log(err);
  } finally {
    //reset our timer
    clearTimeout(autoSaveTimer);
    autoSaveTimer = setTimeout('autoSave()', autoSaveFrequency);
  }
}

//start our timer
autoSaveTimer = setTimeout('autoSave()', autoSaveFrequency);
```

The code above does not interfere with the Accept button or manually saving the item; it just programmatically fires the same event at a regular interval.

The auto-save frequency is set to 1 minute (60000 milliseconds), but you can adjust this to any value you want. The JavaScript `setTimeout` function is used to call the `scSave` function at the specified interval. The `scSave` function is part of Sitecore's `webedit.js` file and it saves the current item. 

After saving, the timer is reset to start the countdown to the next save. This will ensure that changes made in the RTE are saved every minute, even if the user forgets to manually save them. This is especially useful in case of a browser crash or session timeout where otherwise all changes would be lost.
<|end|>


