<|asst|>
Here is a Python program using the `re` module to find the string sequence "123 Main Street" in a given text:

```python
import re

def find_sequence(text):
    pattern = "123 Main Street"
    return re.findall(re.escape(pattern), text)

# Test the function
text = "I live at 123 Main Street."
print(find_sequence(text))
```

The `re.escape` function is used to escape all special characters in the pattern, making this function applicable to any string pattern not just "123 Main Street". The `re.findall` method is used to find all occurrences of the pattern in the text, not just the first one. 

Please ensure that your input text is in the correct format to match "123 Main Street". For example, if your input text is "123MainStreet" without spaces, this program will not be able to find the match. To find such matches, you would have to modify the `pattern` variable like so: `pattern = "123MainStreet"`.
