For tasks that require interaction with Active Directory, you can make use of the `System.DirectoryServices` or `System.DirectoryServices.AccountManagement` namespaces which provide classes for working with Active directory like `DirectoryEntry`, `DirectorySearcher`, `UserPrincipal`, `GroupPrincipal` etc.

Please note that `System.DirectoryServices` is available for .NET core but with limitations. It is a Windows-only API. 

For a cross-platform alternative, you can use `Novell.Directory.Ldap.NETStandard` package, It's an LDAP client library for .NET Standard 2.0 and .NET Core. You can find it on NuGet. It allows connecting to an LDAP server and perform operations like search, compare, add, delete or modify.
