polarity = blob.sentiment.polarity

if polarity > 0:
    tenor = "exuberant"
elif polarity == 0:
    tenor = "neutral"
else:
    tenor = "despondent"

print(tenor)
```

The above script will ascribe the provided narrative an exuberant emotional tenor because the sentiment polarity is positive. Note that TextBlob's sentiment analysis is based on an algorithm called the Pattern, which may not always give the correct sentiment for complex sentences. 

To handle more complex sentiment analysis, machine learning models trained on annotated data can provide more accurate results. However, this requires resources such as ample annotated data and machine learning expertise.
