<|asst|>
The issue you are experiencing is likely due to the fact that Azure Front Door is a global service, not a regional one. That means you can't specify a particular location when you're creating a Front Door resource. Instead, Azure will automatically provision it across its global network.

You may receive a `BadRequest` error with the message `Frontdoor location must be global` if you've specified a particular region in your code.

Typically, in Pulumi, you can set the location in `resource options` when you create a resource, like so:

```ts
...
}, { location: "westeurope" }); // Or other location string
```

If you currently have this in your code, to resolve this issue, simply remove the location option from your `FrontDoor` resource. Here's an example for the FrontDoor resource creation:

```ts
const frontDoor = new azurenative.network.FrontDoor('frontDoor', {
    frontDoorName: "NameOfYourFrontDoorService",
    resourceGroupName: resourceGroup.name,
    routingRules: [],
    frontendEndpoints: [],
    backendPools:[],
});
```

If this doesn't resolve your issue, it might be helpful if you shared the relevant parts of your Pulumi code.
<|end|>


