1. The navigation bar should be fixed at the top of the screen and span the full width of the screen, with a height of 60px and a background color of your choice.

2. The sidebar should appear on the left side of the screen with a fixed width of 200px and a padding of 10px. Its height should be equal to the height of the main content area.

3. The main content area should be displayed inline with the sidebar and occupy the remaining available width of the screen. It should also have a padding of 10px.

4. Use media queries to make the design responsive. When the screen width is 768px or less, the sidebar should be hidden, and the main content area should span the full width of the screen.

5. Use CSS Grid or Flexbox to achieve the layout wherever appropriate.
