Here is a CSS stylesheet that implements the above specifications. 

HTML markup:

```html
<body>
    <nav class="navbar">Navigation Bar</nav>
    <div class="container">
        <aside class="sidebar">Sidebar</aside>
        <div class="content">Main Content Area</div>
    </div>
</body>
```

CSS code:

```css
.navbar {
    position: fixed;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 60px;
    background-color: #f9f9f9; /* Change as per your liking */
}

.container {
    display: flex;
    margin-top: 60px; /* To account for the fixed navbar */
}

.sidebar {
    width: 200px;
    padding: 10px;
    background-color: #ddd; /* Change as per your liking */
    height: min-content; /* Adjusts height as per the content */
}

.content {
    padding: 10px;
    background-color: #ccc; /* Change as per your liking */
    width: calc(100% - 200px); /* Subtracted sidebar width. */
    height: min-content; /* Adjusts height as per the content */
}

@media screen and (max-width: 768px) {
    .sidebar {
        display: none;
    }

    .content {
        width: 100%; /* When sidebar is hidden, content should span full width */
    }
}
```

