Could you finalize this piece of code? We need a function that receives a string as an input and determines if the combined ASCII values of the characters within that string form a prime number. If so, return true. If the total ASCII value is not a prime number, return false. Here's examples for clarity: ("Hello") results in true, ("abcdcba") is true, ("programming") gives false, and ("orange") is true. So, the beginning of your coding task in C++ is as follows:
```C++
#include<stdio.h>
#include<string>
using namespace std;
bool prime_ascii_sum(string str){
```
Remember not to alter any sections of code found in the original request.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Sure, here is the completion of your C++ function:

```C++
#include<stdio.h>
#include<string>
using namespace std;

bool is_prime(int num) {
    if(num <= 1) return false;
    if(num == 2) return true;
    if(num % 2 == 0) return false;
    for(int i = 3; i * i <= num; i += 2) {
        if(num % i == 0) 
            return false;
    }
    return true;
}

bool prime_ascii_sum(string str) {
    int sum = 0;
    for(int i = 0; i < str.size(); i++) {
        sum += (int)str[i];
    }
    
    if(is_prime(sum)) 
        return true;
    else 
        return false;
}
```

In the solution, first, we compute the sum of ASCII values of all the characters in the input string. Then the sum is passed on to the helper function `is_prime` to check whether the sum is a prime number or not. 

The `is_prime` function checks whether the input number is divisible by any integer other than 1 and itself. If the number is only divisible by 1 and itself, then it is a prime number so function returns true, otherwise it's not a prime and function returns false. 

If the sum value is prime, `prime_ascii_sum` function will return true; otherwise, it will return false.
<|end|>


