how to use specific date formats in data validation in Google Sheets.
I set this date format in google sheet dd-mmm-yyyy (09-Jan-2023) but the user enters a different date format in the sheet so im want to use data validation for this the user must enter data in specific format dd-mmm-yyyy
i want that when user enter data in different format its auto rejects entry.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Unfortunately, Google Sheets data validation can't directly enforce a specific date format, but there are workarounds you can use to help ensure that users input dates correctly.

Here's a method using conditional formatting and data validation:

1. First ensure all cells are formatted to the date style that you want: select the cells, click on "Format" in the top menu, then "Number", and choose "More Formats", then select "More date and time formats". In the pop-up box, set the format you want e.g. `dd-mmm-yy` and click "Apply".
   
2. In the cell that will hold the date, set a data validation rule by right-clicking and choosing "Data validation". For "Criteria", choose "Date". You can choose whether invalid entries are rejected outright or a warning shown. Set the "Help text" to indicate that users must enter a date in the `dd-mmm-yy` format.

3. Use "Conditional formatting" to make visual alerts for when data is not in the right format. Right-click on the cell and choose "Conditional formatting". Under "Format cells if..." choose "Date is" and then "not valid date". Set cell background or text to an alert color, for example red. Click "Done".

Now, when a date is entered in the wrong format, it won't pass data validation (if set to reject input) and will also turn red via conditional formatting. Users get an alert and can correct their input.

Remember to set helpful error messages to guide them on the right format.

Again, this method does not directly enforce a specific date format (like `dd-mmm-yy`), but does ensure that users enter valid dates, and encourages them to use the correct formatting.
<|end|>


