```python
# Create a 4D array with dimensions 4x4x4x4
array_4d = [[[[j for i in range(4)] for j in range(4)] for x in range(4)] for y in range(4)]

# Modify elements of 4D array
for i in range(4):
    for j in range(4):
        for k in range(4):
            for l in range(4):
                array_4d[i][j][k][l] *= 2 # Doubles the value of each element

# Print elements of 4D array
for i in range(4):
    for j in range(4):
        for k in range(4):
            for l in range(4):
                print(array_4d[i][j][k][l])
```

This code initializes a 4D array with dimension sizes of 4 each. Each element in the array is then doubled. The script finally prints out each element in the 4D array.  

In the initial stage, each element is the same as its column number from innermost brackets. After the modification, these numbers are doubled. The printed result reflects all the elements of the modified 4D array.
