Are there any Common Lisp implementations for .Net?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
There is no active or well-maintained Common Lisp implementation specifically for .Net to the best of my knowledge as of early 2022. 

The project that was attempting to create one, called LispCLR, appears to have paused and not been updated since 2006. It can still be found on SourceForge, but with no recent activity or maintenance, it's hard to recommend for any modern use. 

If you need to use Lisp with .Net, your best bet might be to use a different Lisp dialect that has .Net support, like ClojureCLR, which is a variant of Clojure (a Lisp dialect) for the .NET runtime.
<|end|>


