<|user|>
Design an HTML page that accepts and dynamically displays a user's input text on the page utilizing JavaScript. In addition, apply CSS style changes to the input text based on user-defined style options, such as font color, font size, and background color.

Bonus points if you implement additional style properties or animations for the displayed text.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Sure, here is a simple implementation of your requirement in HTML, CSS and JavaScript:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <title>Interactive Text Styling</title>
  <style>
    #textDisplay {
      transition: all 1s;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <h1>Interactive Text Styling</h1>

  <label for="userInput">Enter your text:</label>
  <input type="text" id="userInput" name="userInput"><br><br>

  <label for="fontColor">Choose a font color:</label>
  <input type="color" id="fontColor" name="fontColor"><br><br>

  <label for="fontSize">Choose a font size:</label>
  <input type="number" id="fontSize" name="fontSize"><br><br>

  <label for="bgColor">Choose a background color:</label>
  <input type="color" id="bgColor" name="bgColor"><br><br>

  <button onclick="updateStyles()">Update Styles</button>

  <p id="textDisplay"></p>

  <script>
    function updateStyles() {
      // Get input values
      let text = document.getElementById("userInput").value;
      let fontColor = document.getElementById("fontColor").value;
      let fontSize = document.getElementById("fontSize").value;
      let bgColor = document.getElementById("bgColor").value;
      
      // Get display element
      let display = document.getElementById("textDisplay");

      // Update display text and styles
      display.innerHTML = text;
      display.style.color = fontColor;
      display.style.fontSize = fontSize + "px";
      display.style.backgroundColor = bgColor;
    }
  </script>
</body>
</html>
```

This page allows the user to input text and style options, updating the displayed text's style dynamically when the "Update Styles" button is clicked.

For the bonus, I've added a transition animation to the text's styles which gives a smooth change effect over 1 second.

When implementing in a production environment, you'll want to add error handling and validation of the user's input for security and usability.
<|end|>


