Construct a Java program that is tasked with reversing the order of individual characters within each separate word in the specified sentence: "Hello world of artificial intelligence". This task demands the effective utilization of concepts like string manipulation and character arrays in Java.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here is a Java program that uses string manipulation and character arrays to reverse the order of individual characters within each separate word in the specified sentence, "Hello world of artificial intelligence".

```java
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String sentence = "Hello world of artificial intelligence";
        String[] words = sentence.split(" ");
        StringBuilder result = new StringBuilder();

        for (String word : words) {
            result.append(new StringBuilder(word).reverse().toString()).append(" ");
        }
        
        System.out.println(result.toString().trim());
    }
}
```

This program splits the sentence into words using the `split` method of the `String` class. It then iterates over each word in the resulting array and appends a reversed version of the word to the `result` StringBuilder. The `reverse` method of the `StringBuilder` class is used to reverse the order of characters in each word. The `.append(" ")` part ensures that there is a space between each word.

Finally, the `toString` method of `StringBuilder` is used to convert the reversed words back into a string and `trim` is used to remove the extra white spaces at the end of the sentence.
