  width: 100%;
  margin: 10px 0;
}
```

In the above CSS:

1. The `.container` has been given `flex` display and center alignment for all child elements regardless of the screen size. The `padding-top` property is used instead of the `margin-top` to avoid the collapse of margins.
2. The `.registerForm` has also been given `flex` display and its content direction is set to `column` which stacks the child elements vertically. It has a maximum width of `600px` for a better viewing experience on large screens, and `margin: 25px auto` centers the form horizontally and provides space above and below the form.
3. The `.formItem` has a `width: 100%` which makes it completely responsive in varying screen width, and `margin: 10px 0` provides space above and below each form item. The `display: block` ensures that every form item takes up the entire row.
