While it's understandable you'd want your post to look as visually compelling as possible, Facebook doesn't currently provide an option to remove the link title and description entirely when sharing a URL link post. Instead, they automatically generate these details based on the metadata of the website you're linking to. 

However, there are ways to manipulate how your link information appears by changing your website's metadata or using a link preview editor such as 'Sharing Debugger' that Facebook provides.

Here are steps for using 'Sharing Debugger': 

1. Open Facebook's Sharing Debugger: https://developers.facebook.com/tools/debug/.
2. Enter the URL you want to share on Facebook.
3. Click on 'Debug.'
4. Change or remove the title and description metadata on the page you're linking to.
5. Then, click on 'Scrape Again' to refresh the link data.
6. Share your link on Facebook. It should now display without a title or description.

Bear in mind that the success of this method depends upon the website's metadata settings or the platform it uses.

As for the image size, Facebook recommends an image ratio of 1.91:1 for best display in most places.

In case manipulating metadata seems to be too technical, you can always consider using Facebook's Ad platform. The Facebook ads manager provides more control over how the link, title, description, and image appear on your post.
