Construct an SQL query to retrieve the top five customers who had the most purchases.
Table: customers
Columns: id, name, purchases
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Assuming the 'purchases' column represents the total number of purchases the customer has made, here is a simple SQL query:

```sql
SELECT id, name, purchases 
FROM customers 
ORDER BY purchases DESC 
LIMIT 5;
```
This query selects the id, name, and purchases from the customers table, then sorts the results by the number of purchases in descending order (i.e., from highest to lowest), finally, it limits the result to the top 5 customers.
