## Data structures and interface definitions
```mermaid
classDiagram
    class User{
        +str username
        +str email
        +str password
        +create_user(username: str, email: str, password: str)
        +authenticate(username: str, password: str)
    }
    class Product{
        +str title
        +str description
        +float starting_bid
        +datetime deadline
        +User owner
        +create_product(title: str, description: str, starting_bid: float, deadline: datetime, owner: User)
    }
    class Bid{
        +float amount
        +User bidder
        +Product product
        +create_bid(amount: float, bidder: User, product: Product)
        +is_highest_bid()
    }
    class Notification{
        +str message
        +User recipient
        +create_notification(message: str, recipient: User)
    }
    User "1" -- "*" Product: owns
    User "1" -- "*" Bid: places
    Product "1" -- "*" Bid: has
    User "1" -- "*" Notification: receives
```

## Program call flow
```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant U as User
    participant P as Product
    participant B as Bid
    participant N as Notification
    U->>P: create_product(title, description, starting_bid, deadline)
    U->>B: create_bid(amount, product)
    B->>P: is_highest_bid()
    P->>U: notify_highest_bid()
    U->>N: create_notification(message, recipient)
```

