What is the procedure to add a new element at a specific index of an array without changing the positions of existing elements in JavaScript?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
In JavaScript, you can use the array method splice() to add a new element at a specific index without changing the positions of existing elements. Following is the procedure:

```javascript
// Initialize an array
let arr = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5];

// Index where new element need to be added
let addAtIndex = 2;

// Element to be added
let newElement = 'New Element';

// Using splice() to add newElement at index 'addAtIndex'
// splice(index, deleteCount, item1)
// Here,
// index : addAtIndex
// deleteCount: 0 (because we are not deleting any elements)
// item1 : newElement (Element that needs to be added)
arr.splice(addAtIndex, 0, newElement);

// Output: [1, 2, 'New Element', 3, 4, 5]
console.log(arr);
```

Given an array, the splice() method changes the content of an array by removing or replacing existing elements and/or adding new elements in place. In this scenario, we're adding a new element in a specific position into an array without deleting others. Thus, deleteCount is 0, as we're not removing any elements.
<|end|>


