When I run the code below in oracle developer, I get error
> `ORA-00936: missing expression . CREATE TABLE table_prc4 ( name VARCHAR2(20) );`
this code :

CREATE OR REPLACE PROCEDURE addnewmembe (
    str IN VARCHAR2
) AS
BEGIN
    INSERT INTO table_prc4 VALUES (
        SELECT
            regexp_substr(str, '[^,]+', 1, level) AS parts 
        FROM
            dual
        CONNECT BY
            regexp_substr(str, '[^,]+', 1, level) IS NOT NULL 
    );
commit;
END ;

BEGIN
    addnewmembe('saeed,amir,hossein');
END;


I want to show in the result in the row sequence number and a name of the input string
<|end|>
<|asst|>
You have an incorrect syntax in your `INSERT INTO` statement with `SELECT` clause inside `VALUES` clause. This is not allowed in Oracle SQL. 

So, you need to use the `INSERT INTO SELECT FROM` syntax to correct this.

Here is the correct code:

```sql
CREATE OR REPLACE PROCEDURE addnewmembe (
str IN VARCHAR2
) AS
BEGIN
    INSERT INTO table_prc4
    SELECT regexp_substr(str, '[^,]+', 1, level) AS parts FROM 
    dual CONNECT BY regexp_substr(str, '[^,]+', 1, level) IS NOT NULL;
    commit;
END;
/

BEGIN
    addnewmembe('saeed,amir,hossein');
END;
/
```

Then you should be able to retrieve the inserted record by running:

```sql
SELECT * FROM table_prc4;
```

However, please take note that writing `COMMIT` inside a procedure is generally not a good practice. It is better to control your transactions (commit and rollback) from your application.
<|end|>


