Design a Java software utility that identifies all the distinct extensive palindromic subsequences concealed within an allotted text sequence and counts the total number of these unique subsequences. Also, the utility should have the functionality to ignore case differences and special characters while considering palindromes.

Input text sequence: "Able, was I saw elba!"
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here is a Java solution to the problem. It uses the concept of dynamic programming to find all the distinct palindromic subsequences.

```java
import java.util.Arrays;
import java.util.HashMap;
import java.util.Map;

public class PalindromeSubsequence {

    static void printPalindromicSubsequence(String str) {
        int n = str.length();
        int[][] dp = new int[n][n];
        boolean[][] palindrome = new boolean[n][n];

        for (int i= 0; i< n; i++)
            palindrome[i][i] = true;

        for (int i=0; i<n-1; i++) {
            if (str.charAt(i) == str.charAt(i+1)) {
                dp[i][i+1] = 1;
                palindrome[i][i+1] = true;
            }
        }

        for (int gap=2 ; gap<n; gap++) {
            for (int i=0; i<n-gap; i++) {
                int j = gap + i;
                if (str.charAt(i) == str.charAt(j) && palindrome[i+1][j-1] )
                    palindrome[i][j] = true;

                if (palindrome[i][j] == true)
                    dp[i][j] = dp[i][j-1] + dp[i+1][j] + 1 - dp[i+1][j-1];
                else
                    dp[i][j] = dp[i][j-1] + dp[i+1][j] - dp[i+1][j-1];
            }
        }

        System.out.println("Total palindromic subsequence are : " + dp[0][n-1]);
    }

    public static void main (String[] args) {
        String str = "Able, was I saw elba!";
        str = str.replaceAll("[^a-zA-Z]", "");
        str = str.toLowerCase();
        printPalindromicSubsequence(str);
    }
}
```

This Java program handles the case ignorance and inclusion of alphabets (both small and capital) only by changing the whole string to lowercase and removing all the non-alphabetical characters before processing it for finding the palindromic subsequences.

It uses a dynamic programming based approach where it utilizes a 2D table where an entry dp[i][j] represents the count of palindromic subsequences in str[i..j].

It will print the total count of unique palindromic subsequences. The time complexity of this solution is O(n^2).
<|end|>


