The aggregate exterior space of a non-regular polyhedron object, also known as the volume of irregular polyhedron, can be solved by the method below using Python and a third-party library called scipy. Here is a Python function:

```python
import numpy as np
from scipy.spatial import ConvexHull

def calculate_volume(coords):
    hull = ConvexHull(coords)
    volume = hull.volume
    return volume

# test it
vertices_coords = np.random.rand(30, 3)  # 30 random vertices in 3D
print(calculate_volume(vertices_coords))
```

Each row of the input numpy array is a 3D coordinate of a vertex of the polyhedron.

This program will calculate the volume of the convex hull of the given vertices, which means it is assuming the polyhedron is convex. If the polyhedron is non-convex or has holes, this method will not work out-of-the-box.                    

If you need to calculate the volume of non-convex polyhedra or polyhedra with holes, the problem is more complex and does not have a one-size-fits-all solution. You may need to divide the polyhedron into smaller convex polyhedra, calculate the volume of these smaller polyhedra separately, and then add them up.

Remember, this code should be run in a proper Python environment where numpy and scipy.spatial libraries have been installed. Run the command 'pip install numpy scipy' on your terminal to install them if they are not on your Python environment.
