Devise a structured query language (SQL) operation to extract the titles of films which were made public within the previous decade, also taking into account the exact month and day of their respective release dates.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
To solve this problem, we will suppose the name of the table is "films" and it has two columns: 'title' (which stores the names of the films) and 'release_date' (which stores the release dates, type: DATE). We can use the CURDATE() function to get the current date and INTERVAL 10 YEAR to subtract 10 years from that.

Here is the solution:

```sql
SELECT title 
FROM films 
WHERE release_date >= DATE_SUB(CURDATE(), INTERVAL 10 YEAR);
```
This SQL statement will return the titles of the films released in the last decade up to the same month and day as today's date.

Note: It's worth mentioning that the exact implementation might differ slightly based on the SQL variant used. For example, in SQL Server instead of the DATE_SUB and CURDATE functions, one would have to use GETDATE function and DATEADD function.
<|end|>


