At work we use [WiX](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/WiX) for building installation packages. We want that installation of product X would result in uninstall of the previous version of that product on that machine.

I've read on several places on the Internet about a major upgrade but couldn't get it to work.
Can anyone please specify the exact steps that I need to take to add uninstall previous version feature to WiX?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Yes, you can create a major upgrade to automatically uninstall the older version and install the new one. Here's how you can do it with WiX:

1. First of all, you should add `<MajorUpgrade/>` element to your WiX code. This will cause the WiX to automatically handle most of the standard actions associated with the major upgrade. 

    ```xml
    <Product ... UpgradeCode="PUT-GUID-HERE" ... > 
       .....
       <MajorUpgrade DowngradeErrorMessage="A newer version of [ProductName] is already installed." />
       .....
    </Product>
    ```

2. Change the `Product/@Id` attribute to `'*'` to generate a new GUID.

3. The `DowngradeErrorMessage` attribute is that error message that will be displayed when a newer version of your application is already installed. It is a common good practice to prevent downgrades.

4. Change the `Product/@Version` attribute to a higher version than the previous one.

5. Keep the same `UpgradeCode` attribute in newer versions. This `UpgradeCode` is used to find related versions of the product. 

6. If there're specific actions you want to perform based on the newer version found, you can leverage the `Upgrade/@Property` attribute.

Following these steps should give you the major upgrade behavior whereby the older version of the product is uninstalled before the new one is installed.

For more details, refer to the WiX documentation at:
http://wixtoolset.org/documentation/manual/v3/
<|end|>


