Is it possible to call a COM API from Java (specifically the HP/Mercury Quality Center OTA API)? If so, what's the best way?

Is something like JACOB appropriate?

Code fragments would be helpful for the basics :-)
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Yes, it is indeed possible to call a COM API from Java. To do so traditionally, you can use JNI (Java Native Interface) or JNA (Java Native Access) to call native codes.

But working with COM interface using Java JNI or JNA is quite difficult. Instead, you can use JACOB which is a JAVA-COM Bridge. JACOB works in a similar way to JNI but instead of calling C/C++ libraries, it calls COM libraries. It provides a way to call COM objects from Java using native interface.

Here is a simple code snippet on how you can use JACOB:

```
import com.jacob.activeX.ActiveXComponent;
import com.jacob.com.Dispatch;
import com.jacob.com.Variant;

public class JacobTest {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        ActiveXComponent activeXComponent = new ActiveXComponent("YourComObject.ProgID");

        Variant[] variants = new Variant[1];
        variants[0] = new Variant("Your parameter");

        Variant result = Dispatch.callN(activeXComponent, "Your COM Method", variants);
    }
}
```

The Dispatch objects you create using the ActiveXComponent class in JACOB represents COM objects. The Dispatch.callN method is used to call a COM method, where the method name and an array of parameters are passed as arguments. Note that all method calls to COM API should be done using Dispatch.callN method.

Please replace "YourComObject.ProgID", "Your parameter" and "Your COM Method" with your own details.

Before running the program, add jacob.jar to the classpath and then add jacob.dll (for 32 bit JVM), jacob-x64.dll (for 64 bit JVM) to the java library path or system32 folder, according to your JVM version. You can download JACOB from the official website:

http://sourceforge.net/projects/jacob-project/

For HP Quality Center, the program ID is "TDAPIOLELib.TDConnection" and you will need to refer to QC ALM OTA API Reference to find the methods and properties you can use.

Also do not forget about dealing with COM event handling, and releasing resources properly. Otherwise you may face memory leak and other issues.
<|end|>


