Design a NodeJS program to calculate the average age of a given array of objects.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
The following NodeJS program provides the implementation of the desired requirement for calculating the average age for a given array of objects. This program uses the "reduce" method available in JavaScript.

```javascript
const calculateAverageAge = (persons) => {
    if (!Array.isArray(persons)) {
        return 'Input should be an array';
    }

    if (persons.length === 0) {
        return 'Array cannot be empty';
    }

    let totalAge = persons.reduce((sum, person) => {
        if (typeof person.age !== 'number') {
            return sum;
        }
        
        return sum + person.age;
    }, 0);

    let averageAge = totalAge / persons.length;

    return averageAge;
};

const persons = [
    { name: 'Lucy', age: 20 },
    { name: 'John', age: 30 },
    { name: 'Doe', age: 45 },
    { name: 'Anna', age: 35 },
];

const averageAge = calculateAverageAge(persons);

console.log(`Average Age is: ${averageAge}`);
```

This program calculates the sum of ages of all persons in the array using the `reduce` method and then divides the sum by the total number of persons (array length) to find the average.

Please replace the persons array with the array that has the data of your interest and run the program. The average age will be printed on the console.
<|end|>


