I'm looking for a simple, easy to understand algorithm to alphabetically sort an array of characters in C.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here's a simple algorithm to sort an array of characters in C; it is based on the bubble sort algorithm, which is also one of the simplest sorting algorithms.

```c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <string.h>

void sort_array(char arr[], int n) {
    for(int i = 0; i < n-1; i++) {
        for(int j = i+1; j < n; j++) {
            if(arr[i] > arr[j]) {
                // Swap arr[i] and arr[j]
                char temp = arr[i];
                arr[i] = arr[j];
                arr[j] = temp;
            }
        }
    }
}

int main() {
    char arr[] = {'z', 'b', 'r', 'a', 'e', 'f', 'm', 'c'};
    int n = sizeof(arr)/sizeof(arr[0]); // Calculate length of array

    printf("Before sorting: ");
    for(int i=0; i<n; i++)
        printf("%c ", arr[i]);
    printf("\n");

    sort_array(arr, n); // Sort the array

    printf("After sorting: ");
    for(int i=0; i<n; i++)
        printf("%c ", arr[i]);
    printf("\n");

    return 0;
}
```
This algorithm compares each pair of adjacent items and swaps them if they are in the wrong order. This process is repeated until no swaps are needed, indicating that the array is sorted. Note that this sorting algorithm is case-sensitive: uppercase letters are considered "smaller" than lowercase letters. If you need case-insensitive sorting, you should convert all characters to the same case before sorting.
<|end|>


