Design a JavaScript function which accepts a text string as its input. This function will not only count the total words in the string but also identify and segregate the unique words along with their individual count.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here is the JavaScript function that will work for this problem:

```javascript
function wordCountAndUniqueWords(str) {
    const words = str.split(' ');
    const wordCount = words.length;
    const wordMap = {};

    words.forEach(word => {
        wordMap[word.toLowerCase()] = (wordMap[word.toLowerCase()] || 0) + 1;
    });

    return {
        totalWords: wordCount,
        uniqueWords: wordMap
    };
}

// Calling the function:
let text = "Welcome to the Programming world. Welcome again!";
console.log(wordCountAndUniqueWords(text));
```

In the above code, first we split the input string into an array of words using the split() method. Then we initialize a variable to keep track of the total word count and an empty object to store the unique words along with their count.

We then loop through each word in the array using the forEach() method and check if it exists in the wordMap object. If it does, we increment its value by 1, else we add the word to the object with a value of 1. All this is done case insensitively by converting each word to lowercase with the toLowerCase() method.

Finally, we return an object containing the total word count and the unique words along with their count.
<|end|>


