Design a JavaScript function that creates an SVG element representing a zigzag line with adjustable angles.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
You can make use of two libraries D3 and jsdom to carry out this task in JavaScript. D3 library can be used to generate SVG and jsdom library to implement window.document in Node.js environment. 

Below is the JavaScript code that generates an SVG of a zigzag line:

```javascript
const d3 = require("d3");
const { JSDOM } = require("jsdom");

// Create a new JSDOM instance.
const dom = new JSDOM(`<!DOCTYPE html><body></body>`);
// Get the document object.
const document = dom.window.document;
// Create SVG element.
let svg = d3.select(document.body).append('svg');

// Function to draw zigzag line
function drawZigzagLine(x, y, length, angle, numberOfZags, color) {
    let path = `M ${x} ${y} `;
    let directions = [1, -1];
    let idx = 0;

    for (let i = 0; i < numberOfZags; i++) {
        x += length * Math.cos(angle * Math.PI/180);
        y += length * Math.sin(angle * Math.PI/180) * directions[idx];
        path += `L ${x} ${y} `;
        idx = 1 - idx;  // Switch between 1 and 0 for zigzag direction.
    }

    svg.append('path')
       .attr('d', path)
       .attr('stroke', color)
       .attr('stroke-width', '2')
       .attr('fill', 'none');
}

// Draw zigzag line
drawZigzagLine(0, 0, 50, 60, 10, 'black');

const html = d3.select(document.body).html();
console.log(html);
```

This code will log the string representation of the SVG element in the console.

Note that you may need npm install d3 and jsdom if you haven't installed these in your node.js environment already.

This is a very basic zigzag line, and the function parameters can be adjusted for different results. DrawZigzagLine() function parameters x and y initializes starting position, length initializes the length of each zag, angle is in degrees (adjusts the angle of zigzag), numberOfZags sets the number of total zags in the line and color sets color of the line.
<|end|>


