In my rails app I use the validation helpers in my active record objects and they are great. When there is a problem I see the standard "3 errors prohibited this foobar from being saved" on my web page along with the individual problems. 

Is there any way I can override this default message with my own?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Yes, you can customize this message. 

If you look in config/locales/en.yml file (or the particular language file you are using), you can find that default error message. 

```xml
en:
  activerecord:
    errors:
      template:
        header:
          one: "1 error prohibited this %{model} from being saved"
          other: "%{count} errors prohibited this %{model} from being saved"
```

You can customize it here, but editing this file will affect all models in your application.

If you want to override only for a specific model, you can create a new file (for example, config/locales/models/foobar/en.yml) and specify the message like this:

```xml
en:
  activerecord:
    models:
      foobar:
        one: "1 error stopped your Foobar from being saved."
        other: "%{count} errors stopped your Foobar from being saved."
```

Then in your view, display the error messages like this:

```ruby
<%= @foobar.errors.full_messages.to_sentence %>
```

You can also include specific attributes' error messages like this:

```ruby
<% @foobar.errors.full_messages.each do |message| %>
  <%= message %>
<% end %>
```

This will give you greater control over how you want to present error messages.
<|end|>


