        color=color.blue, width = line.width_1)

if not na(yLevel)
    line.set_xy1(ln, bar_index[1], yLevel)
    line.set_xy2(ln, bar_index, yLevel)
```
This script will create a horizontal line on the height of `close + ta.atr(10)` when you hover a bar with your cursor. Line will adjust its length to match the current bar you covered with your cursor, and its level will be re-calculated every 10 bars only. You can adjust the parameters according to your requirements.
