I just got into developing using unity and I got the fps movement going, but I decided to test myself and tried to add a sprint toggle feature with my own code and it doesn't work, the issue is when I go into play mode and press left ctrl it doesn't change the value of speed, any suggestions would be appreciated.

if (speed == 5.0f && Input.GetButtonUp("LeftControl"))
    {
       speed += 2f;
    } 

    if (speed == 7.0f && Input.GetButtonUp("LeftControl"))
    {
        speed -= 2f;
    }
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here are a few suggestions.

1. Input.GetButtonUp("LeftControl") will only return true if the button was pressed and released during the last frame. Hence, you should use Input.GetKeyDown(KeyCode.LeftControl) to check if the left control key was pressed during this frame.

2. Be careful how you compare floats, because of the floating point precision issue, you can't do an exact comparison like if (speed == 5.0f). Most of the time, they won't equal because of a tiny fraction of difference. This might be the cause of your problem.

Here is the corrected code:

```
float tolerance = 0.1f;

if (Mathf.Abs(speed - 5.0f) < tolerance && Input.GetKeyDown(KeyCode.LeftControl))  
{
   speed += 2.0f;
} 

if (Mathf.Abs(speed - 7.0f) < tolerance && Input.GetKeyDown(KeyCode.LeftControl)) 
{
   speed -= 2.0f;
} 
```

This way, you're checking if left control key was indeed pressed and also checking if the speed is roughly around 5.0f or 7.0f with a bit of tolerance to account for floating point precision issue.

Also, if you are trying to implement toggle sprint, you'd be better off with single if condition statements something like this:

```
bool isSprinting = false;

if (Input.GetKeyDown(KeyCode.LeftControl)) 
{
   if (isSprinting) 
   {
      speed -= 2.0f;
      isSprinting = false;
   } 
   else 
   {
      speed += 2.0f;
      isSprinting = true;
   }
} 
```
This way you are checking if the sprint key was pressed and if you are currently sprinting. If you are sprinting, you stop sprinting, if not you start sprinting. It is a more clear and straight forward toggle implementation.
<|end|>


