print(check_consecutive_chars(['KeyboArd', 'Boa']))  # returns: True
```
This function works by converting both input strings to lower case, thus achieving case insensitivity, and then checking whether the second string is a substring of the first string. This effectively confirms if the characters from the second string appear consecutively and in the same sequence in the first string.
