Here is a simple JavaScript code snippet to solve your problem:

```javascript
var myUnicodeSeq = "abcdefgh"; //Predefined sequence

var uniArray = []; // Initialize an array to hold the unicode sequence
for (var i = 0; i < myUnicodeSeq.length; i++) { //Run through the sequence one by one
    var unicode = myUnicodeSeq.charCodeAt(i); // Get the Unicode number for the character
    var hexCode = unicode.toString(16); // Convert the Unicode to hexadecimal
    uniArray[i % 8] ? uniArray[i % 8].push([myUnicodeSeq[i], hexCode]) : uniArray[i % 8] = [[myUnicodeSeq[i], hexCode]]; // Push to the array, will overflow to beginning if past length
}
console.log(uniArray);
```
This will generate a nested array where every outer array element is a separate sub-array of length 8 or less with each element in the format [character, hexadecimal code]. Overflow is managed by starting back at the beginning of the outer array when the pre-defined length is exceeded.
