The function `countDistinctCharacters()` converts the given string to lower case using `strtolower()` function, then it iterates over each character of the string. If the character is an alphabet (checked using `ctype_alpha()` function), the function adds it to the `$distinctChars` array with the character itself being the key. Note that if the character already exists as a key in the array, it will just overwrite the existing value without creating a new key. This way, we ensure that we count each character only once even if it appears multiple times in the string. Finally, it returns the count of keys in the `$distinctChars` array which would be the count of distinct characters.
