Create a JavaScript function that sets the margin of all elements with a given class to a specified value, and implement event listeners to trigger the function on specific user actions.

Additionally, ensure that your code is optimized for scalability and maintainability.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here's a simple JavaScript function that will achieve what you need. It uses querySelectorAll to obtain all the elements with the given class and then applies a forEach loop to individually apply the required margin. For the event listeners, the function takes an object where the you specify the events for which the function should trigger.

```js
function setMarginByClassName(className, marginValue, eventObject) {
    // getting the node list of elements with the specified class   
    var elements = document.querySelectorAll(`.${className}`);
    
    // function to apply the margin
    function applyMargin() {
        elements.forEach(element => {
            element.style.margin = marginValue;
        });
    }

    // apply margin immediately
    applyMargin();

    // applying the event listeners
    for (const key in eventObject) {
        if (Object.hasOwnProperty.call(eventObject, key)) {
            const elementId = eventObject[key];
            const element = document.getElementById(elementId);
            if (element) {
                element.addEventListener(key, applyMargin);
            }
        }
    }
}
```

This function can be used like this:

```js
setMarginByClassName("test-class", "10px", {
    click: "clickElementId",
    mouseover: "mouseoverElementId"
});
```

This call would immediately set the margin of all elements with class `test-class` to 10px and also set event listeners on the elements with ids `clickElementId` and `mouseoverElementId` so that when those elements are clicked or moused over, the margins will again be applied. This setup is flexible, maintainable and could scale to include additional events or target elements as required.
<|end|>


