I'm working on an email solution in SQL Server ONLY that will use Database Mail to send out HTML formatted emails.  The catch is that the images in the HTML need to be embedded in the outgoing email. This wouldn't be a problem if I were using a .net app to generate & send the emails but, unfortunately, all I have is SQL Server.

Is it possible for SQL Server to embed images on its own?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
No, SQL Server itself does not have the capability to embed images in HTML emails. SQL Server Database Mail can send email in plain text, HTML or with file attachments, but it does not contain functionality to embed images in HTML code.

Usually, when sending HTML emails with embedded images, the images are not truly embedded within the HTML, but are referenced via a URL and the email client loads the images when displaying the email. The images are normally hosted on a web server and the HTML email contains an <img> tag referencing the URL of each image.

If you have to embed images in the emails using only SQL Server, you might need to find an alternative method, such as uploading the images to a web server and referencing the URL in your HTML as stated above, or include the images as attachments and reference them in the HTML body as CIDs. However, keep in mind the latter method will need the recipient email client to support viewing emails in this format.
<|end|>


