I am using Cypress `12.2.0`. How to increase the connection retry count when running `cypress run`?

We will try connecting to it 3 more times...
We will try connecting to it 2 more times...
We will try connecting to it 1 more time...
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Cypress does not have a built-in command to change the reconnection attempts. It tries to reconnect exactly 4 times (at 0, 5, 10, 15 seconds) before quiting.

However, you can use an indirect method to allow more retry attempts by increasing the command timeout. 

You can set this in your `cypress.json` configuration file:
```json
{
  "defaultCommandTimeout": 20000
}
```
This sets the default command timeout to 20000 milliseconds (20 seconds). Note, however, that this affects all default commands, not just the connection retry count.

If you believe you are experiencing connectivity issues, you may wish to look into your network settings or consider running tests at times when network load is less intense.
<|end|>


