Can you accurately arrange the following set of integers, which consists of positive and negative numbers: 6, -1, 8, -3, -4, in an ascending sequence from the smallest to the largest value?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Sure, sorting a list of numbers in ascending sequence means arranging them from the smallest value to the largest value. Negative numbers are always smaller than positive numbers, so they will come first. Within the negative numbers, more negative values are smaller. For the positive numbers, smaller positive values come first. Here is a way to solve this using Python:

```python
numbers = [6, -1, 8, -3, -4]
sorted_numbers = sorted(numbers)
print(sorted_numbers)
```

When you run this code, the output will be `[-4, -3, -1, 6, 8]`. This is the list of numbers arranged in an ascending sequence from the smallest to the largest value.
<|end|>


