<|user|>
Create a React component that not only shows a list of items with a delete button for each item, but also provides a drag-and-drop feature to reorder the list and an input field for adding new items.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
To implement this feature, you can use various libraries but in this example, I will use React, React-DnD(for drag and drop functionality), and uniqueid(for generating a unique id for each item). This implementation demonstrates the main functionality however you can always improve it according to your requirements.

```jsx
import React, { useState, useCallback } from 'react';
import { DndProvider, useDrag, useDrop } from 'react-dnd'
import { HTML5Backend } from 'react-dnd-html5-backend'
import uniqueId from 'uniqueid';

const ItemTypes = {
  ITEM: 'item',
}

const Item = ({ id, text, index, moveItem, deleteItem }) => {
  const [{ handlerId }, drop] = useDrop({
    accept: ItemTypes.ITEM,
    collect(monitor) {
      return {
        handlerId: monitor.getHandlerId(),
      };
    },
    hover(item, monitor) {
      if (!ref.current) {
        return
      }
      const dragIndex = item.index;
      const hoverIndex = index;
      if (dragIndex === hoverIndex) {
        return
      }
      moveItem(dragIndex, hoverIndex)
      item.index = hoverIndex
    },
  })

  const [{ isDragging }, drag, preview] = useDrag({
    type: ItemTypes.ITEM,
    item: () => {
      return { id, index };
    },
    collect: (monitor) => ({
      isDragging: monitor.isDragging(),
    }),
  })

  const opacity = isDragging ? 0 : 1;
  drop(preview)

  return (
    <div ref={preview} style={{ opacity }}>
      <div ref={drag}>
        {text} 
      </div>
      <button onClick={() => deleteItem(index)}>Delete</button>
    </div>
  )
}

const DragAndDropList = () => {
  const [items, setItems] = useState([]);
  const [newItemText, setNewItemText] = useState("");

  const moveItem = useCallback(
    (dragIndex, hoverIndex) => {
      const dragItem = items[dragIndex];
      setItems((items) => {
        const newItems = [...items];
        newItems.splice(dragIndex, 1);
        newItems.splice(hoverIndex, 0, dragItem);

        return newItems;
      });
    },
    [items]
  );

  const addItem = () => {
    setItems([...items, { id: uniqueId(), text: newItemText }]);
    setNewItemText("");
  };

  const deleteItem = (index) => {
    const newItems = [...items];
    newItems.splice(index, 1);
    setItems(newItems);
  };

  return (
    <DndProvider backend={HTML5Backend}>
      <div>
        <input value={newItemText} onChange={(e) => setNewItemText(e.target.value)} />
        <button onClick={addItem}>Add</button>
      </div>
      {items.map((item, index) => (
        <Item
          key={item.id}
          id={item.id}
          text={item.text}
          index={index}
          moveItem={moveItem}
          deleteItem={deleteItem}
        />
      ))}
    </DndProvider>
  );
};
export default DragAndDropList;
```
Please install the libraries using the command:
```bash
npm install --save react-dnd react-dnd-html5-backend uniqueid
```
Please note you need to global install npm if you haven't:
```bash
npm install npm -g
```

This DragAndDropList component has an input field and a button for adding new items to the list. Each item in the list is a Draggable Item component which you can drag and drop to reorder the list. Each item also returns back to its own position if you cancel the drag or drop outside the list. Also, a delete button is available for deleting the item from the list. Please adjust the functionality according to your requirements.
<|end|>


