<|asst|>
Using the range operator (`..`) with the `Take` method for paginating your data is not yet supported in EF Core. This is an inherent limitation of EF Core iteration of how it interprets LINQ expressions.

For now, you should stick with using the Skip/Take approach for pagination on your data. The `Skip` method is used to bypass a specified number of elements in a sequence and then return the remaining elements. The `Take` method returns a specified number of contiguous elements from the start of a sequence.

```csharp
var dataToSend = await data.Skip(x).Take(y - x).ToListAsync();
```

Always remember to keep on eye on the official EF Core updates. EF Core constantly adds new features to provide more convenience to developers. The range operator support may be added in the future.
