## Requirement Analysis
The product should be an online auction platform where users can post their products for auction, bid on products, and track the status of their bids. The platform should be user-friendly, secure, and reliable. It should also have a system for setting and tracking auction deadlines.

## Requirement Pool
```python
[
    ("User registration and login system", "P0"),
    ("Product posting with detailed description and images", "P0"),
    ("Real-time bidding system", "P0"),
    ("Auction deadline system", "P0"),
    ("Notification system for bid status", "P1")
]
```

## UI Design draft
The website should have a clean and intuitive design. The homepage should display featured auctions, categories of products, and a search bar. Each product page should display the product details, current highest bid, time remaining for the auction, and a place for users to enter their bid. There should also be user profile pages where users can track their posted products and bids.

## Anything UNCLEAR
There are no unclear points., Architect: ## Implementation approach
The ecommerce platform will be developed using Django, a high-level Python Web framework that encourages rapid development and clean, pragmatic design. Django is chosen for its robustness and its "batteries-included" philosophy which includes functionalities like authentication and messaging out of the box. 

For the real-time bidding system, Django Channels will be used. Django Channels extends Django to handle WebSockets, HTTP2, and other protocols. 

The auction deadline system will be implemented using Celery, an asynchronous task queue/job queue based on distributed message passing. 

The notification system will be implemented using Django's built-in messaging framework. 

The website will be secured using Django's built-in security features, which include protection against cross-site scripting (XSS), cross-site request forgery (CSRF), and SQL injection. 

