I want to set the name of the file that will upload by multer,from client in react app.
my multer storage is this :

const storage = multer.diskStorage({
  destination : (req , file , cb)=>{
    cb(null , './images')
  },
  filename : (req , file , cb)=>{
    cb(null, req.body.name)

  }
})


and my form handler function in react is this :

async function handle(e) {
    e.preventDefault()
    const data = new FormData()
    data.append('name' , 'something')
    data.append('avatar' , file )
   await axios.post('http://localhost:5000/api/upload' , data)
    .then(res => console.log(res.data))
  }


I want to set the file name from the client.
I set name "something" in here.
But when I log req.body in the storage cb it shows an embpty object.
how can I do this?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
The data appended in a `FormData` instance before the file, won't be visible in `multer` because `multer` stops when it encounters the file data in the stream.

Instead, try to change the order of your `FormData`.

```javascript
async function handle(e) {
    e.preventDefault()
    const data = new FormData()
    data.append('avatar' , file)
    data.append('name' , 'something')
    await axios.post('http://localhost:5000/api/upload' , data)
    .then(res => console.log(res.data))
}
```
When you send `FormData` with file through axios, it's not a simple POST request, it's `multipart/form-data`, so the file is an attachment which will be processed separately.

Also make sure to use a middleware in your server like below:

```javascript
app.use(express.urlencoded({ extended: true })); // To parse the incoming requests with urlencoded payloads
app.use(express.json()); // To parse the incoming requests with JSON payloads
```
Remember that form-data is sent in a different way than a typical post request with JSON data, so make sure you have the appropriate middleware in your server side to handle form-data.

In terms of extracting the name after the file has been processed, you can access it through `req.body.name`. 

If you can't do it directly in Multer's `filename` option, due to asynchronous issues, you'll have to handle it in the route handling after the file has been processed. For instance:

```javascript
app.post("/api/upload", upload.single('avatar'), (req, res) => {
    console.log(req.body.name); // Here 'name' is accessible 
    // Continue your logic here...
});
```
