2. Use App Annie: This is a platform that tracks apps' records on various app stores including Apple and Google. It's free to sign up and use the basic features of the platform.

3. 148apps.com: This website has a search engine that covers the Apple App Store and makes it easy to find an app you're looking for.

4. AppShopper.com: This is another website where you can search for apps in the Apple App Store.

5. Use Sensor Tower: This is another platform that's similar to App Annie. It also tracks app stores for trending apps, updates, and more.

Remember, even if an app name appears to be free, it's best to double-check as Apple has complicated policies around app names and it's possible for a name to be used by an unpublished app or reserved by a developer.
