Here's how you could write the C# version of the function, and a few unit test for it:

```csharp
using System;
using System.Linq;
using NUnit.Framework;

class Program
{
    public static bool EvenSumWithinBounds(int[] arr, int lowerLimit, int upperLimit)
    {
        if (arr.Length % 2 != 0 || arr.Length == 0) 
        {
            return false;
        }

        var evenSum = arr.Where((x, i) => i % 2 == 0).Sum();

        return lowerLimit <= evenSum && evenSum <= upperLimit;
    }
}

public class ProgramTests
{
    [TestFixture]
    public class Tests
    {
        [Test]
        public void EvenSumWithinBoundsTest()
        {
            int[] arr = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6};
            bool result = Program.EvenSumWithinBounds(arr, 10, 20);
            Assert.IsTrue(result);
        }

        [Test]
        public void EvenSumOutOfUpperBoundTest()
        {
            int[] arr = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6};
            bool result = Program.EvenSumWithinBounds(arr, 10, 12);
            Assert.IsFalse(result);
        }

        [Test]
        public void EvenSumOutOfLowerBoundTest()
        {
            int[] arr = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6};
            bool result = Program.EvenSumWithinBounds(arr, 15, 20);
            Assert.IsFalse(result);
        }

        [Test]
        public void OddArrayTest()
        {
            int[] arr = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5};
            bool result = Program.EvenSumWithinBounds(arr, 10, 20);
            Assert.IsFalse(result);
        }

        [Test]
        public void EmptyArrayTest()
        {
            int[] arr = {};
            bool result = Program.EvenSumWithinBounds(arr, 10, 20);
            Assert.IsFalse(result);
        }
    }
}
```

The function `EvenSumWithinBoundsTest` tests that an even array with a sum within the bounds returns `true`. 

The function `EvenSumOutOfUpperBoundTest` tests that an even array with a sum above the upper bound returns `false`.

The function `EvenSumOutOfLowerBoundTest` tests that an even array with a sum below the lower bound returns `false`.

The function `OddArrayTest` tests that an odd array returns `false`.

The function `EmptyArrayTest` tests that an empty array returns `false`.

Please note that in C#, the list data structure is analogous to the List<> or array[] data structures. So, for the conversion, I've used an array. Also, please replace `YOUR_NAMESPACE` with your actual namespace.
