Create a simple node program that runs a timer.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Sure, here is a simple Node.js timer program. This program will display the count every second starting from 0.

```node
// Import the builtin 'events' module
const EventEmitter = require('events');

// Create an instance of EventEmitter
const event = new EventEmitter();

let count = 0;

// Define a 'timer' event that increments the count and prints it every second
event.on('timer', () => {
    setInterval(() => {
        console.log(++count);
    }, 1000);
});

// Emit the 'timer' event to start the timer
event.emit('timer');
```
To run this program, save it to a file (e.g., `timer.js`), and then use Node.js to run that file, i.e., `node timer.js`.
<|end|>


