<|asst|>
You should probably set the DirectoryIndex directive to point to your WSGI script, like so:

```python
DirectoryIndex mod_wsgi-handler.wsgi
```
Place this line inside your VirtualHost directive.

Being able to see the directory index implies that apache is not configured to handle .wsgi files with mod_wsgi. You can either set this up, or alternatively simply use 

```html
WSGIScriptAlias / /path/to/mysite/apache/django.wsgi
``` 

instead of a DirectoryIndex in your VirtualHost. This will direct all requests to the WSGIScript in question, thus you don't have to bother configuring apache for .wsgi. See the Django mod_wsgi documentation for the second approach.
<|end|>


