<|asst|>
Here is the completed function as per your requirements:

```javascript
const anyInt = (x, y, z) => {

  // Check if all parameters are integers
  if (Number.isInteger(x) && Number.isInteger(y) && Number.isInteger(z)) {
    
    // Check if the sum of two parameters equals the remaining one
    if (x + y === z || x + z === y || y + z === x) {
      return true;
    }
  }

  // Return false if the conditions aren't met
  return false;
};

console.log(anyInt(5, 2, 7));  // true
console.log(anyInt(3, 2, 2));  // false
console.log(anyInt(3, -2, 1)); // true
console.log(anyInt(3.6, -2.2, 2)); // false
```

This function works by first checking if all the parameters 'x', 'y', and 'z' are integers. It then checks if the sum of any two integers equals the third one. If both these criteria are met, the function returns 'true'. Otherwise, it returns 'false'.
