To reverse the given string sequence, you need to use the `Reverse()` function provided by the `System.Linq` namespace. 

Here's how the code should look:
```csharp
using System;
using System.Linq; // Include the System.Linq namespace 

namespace StringInversion
{
    class Program
    {
        static void Main()
        { 
            string greeting = "Hello World";
            string reversed = new string(greeting.Reverse().ToArray()); // Use the Reverse method
            Console.WriteLine(reversed); 
        }
    }
}
```
In the added line, `greeting.Reverse().ToArray()` first reverses the string and then converts it into an array of characters. This array is then passed to `new string()` constructor to get a reversed string.

When you run this code, it will print `dlroW olleH` which is the reversed version of `Hello World`.
