Craft a programming code snippet that accomplishes the reversal of a string without employing any looping mechanisms. Utilize the following input: String = "Hello World!"
<|end|>
<|asst|>
You can easily reverse a string in Python without using loops by using slicing. Here is an example code:

```python
# Input string
input_string = "Hello World!"

# Reverse string using slicing
reversed_string = input_string[::-1]

# Print reversed string
print(reversed_string)
```

In this code snippet, `[::-1]` is a slicing trick in Python for reversing string. This slice statement means start at the end of the string and end the slice at the start of the string, stepping backwards by 1. In other words, the slice statement `[::-1]` generates a reversed copy of the string.
<|end|>


