Construct CSS style sheet to custom design a tabular data display.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Sure, below is an example of a CSS style sheet for tabular data display:

```css
/* Style the table */
table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
}

/* Even rows (nth-child(even)) */
tr:nth-child(even) {
    background-color: #f2f2f2;
}

/* Odd rows (nth-child(odd)) */
tr:nth-child(odd) {
    background-color: #ddd;
}

/* Table headers */
th {
    background-color: #4CAF50;
    color: white;
}

/* Table cells */
td {
    border: 1px solid #ddd;
    padding: 15px;
    text-align: left;
}

/* Hover effect on rows */
tr:hover {
    background-color: #yellow;
}

/* Add a bottom border to all table headers */
th {
    border-bottom: 3px solid #ddd;
}

/* Add a bold font to table headers */
th, td {
    font-weight: bold;
    font-size: 18px;
}

/* Make the first column of data bold and large */
td:first-child {
    font-weight: bold;
    font-size: 20px;
}
```
In the above CSS, properties such as background-color, border, padding, and text-align are used to enhance the presentation of your table.

Note: This is CSS for a simple table. Depending on the complexity of your table (such as if it uses colspans or rowspans), you may need more detailed CSS or even some JS to get things looking exactly how you would like. It also doesn't take into account responsiveness for different sized screens, you might want to add that depending on your needs.
<|end|>


