    NewMsg = message.Forward()
    NewMsg.Body = message.Body
    NewMsg.Subject = message.Subject
    NewMsg.To = "Remas@email.com"
    #NewMsg.Send()
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Before checking each message in messages, you're going to want to set up a restriction for your Items. In your case, we'll need to set a restriction for both the sender's email and the time the email was received.

However, before we get to that, let's make sure we have all the messages sorted by ReceivedTime. Out of the box, the win32com client will get the emails from the oldest to the newest. The code to sort them is:

```python
messages = messages.Sort("[ReceivedTime]", True)
```

Then, we need to set up a restriction for emails received today from a specific email address:

```python
# set up today's date at midnight
start_date = dt.datetime.now().replace(hour=0, minute=0, second=0)
# set up tomorrow's date at midnight
end_date = start_date + dt.timedelta(1)

# get email address
sender_email = "invoice@email.com"

# Restriction: formatted to utilize the Start & End Dates above
restriction = ("@SQL=" 
               "urn:schemas:httpmail:sendername = '{}' "
               "AND "
               "urn:schemas:httpmail:datereceived >= '{}'"
               "AND "
               "urn:schemas:httpmail:datereceived < '{}'"
               ).format(sender_email, start_date.strftime('%m/%d/%Y %H:%M %p'), end_date.strftime('%m/%d/%Y %H:%M %p'))

messages = messages.Restrict(restriction)
```  

This will give you all messages from the specific email address that were received today before the current time. I'm not sure from your question whether you only want to forward the message if it has an attachment, but if you do, you can put a check for this in your for loop:

```python
for message in messages:
    if message.Attachments.Count > 0:
        NewMsg = message.Forward()
```      

Here's how your final code would look like:

```python
import win32com.client
import time
import datetime as dt
from os import path

outlook = win32com.client.Dispatch("Outlook.Application").GetNamespace("MAPI")
inbox = outlook.GetDefaultFolder(6)

# sort emails from latest to oldest
messages = inbox.Items
messages = messages.Sort("[ReceivedTime]", True)

# Restriction
start_date = dt.datetime.now().replace(hour=0, minute=0, second=0)
end_date = start_date + dt.timedelta(1)
sender_email = "invoice@email.com"
restriction = ("@SQL=" 
               "urn:schemas:httpmail:sendername = '{}' "
               "AND "
               "urn:schemas:httpmail:datereceived >= '{}'"
               "AND "
               "urn:schemas:httpmail:datereceived < '{}'"
               ).format(sender_email, start_date.strftime('%m/%d/%Y %H:%M %p'), end_date.strftime('%m/%d/%Y %H:%M %p'))

messages = messages.Restrict(restriction)

# check for attachments and then forward
for message in messages:
    if message.Attachments.Count > 0:
        NewMsg = message.Forward()
        NewMsg.Body = message.Body
        NewMsg.Subject = message.Subject
        NewMsg.To = "Remas@email.com"
        #NewMsg.Send() #Uncomment this line when you want to send for real
```   

Lastly, please be sure to uncomment the "NewMsg.Send()" line when you are ready for your emails to actually be forwarded.
<|end|>


