Devise a multi-threaded Java-based HTTP web server, specifically configured to tackle and process a POST request method, also, it must verify client certificates and have a defense against SQL injections.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
The actual codes for the aforementioned situation will be vast, since it requires several details and specific implementations. However, I will provide a general idea in Java to perform these tasks. For simplicity and limitation of space, I've ignored many details.

```java
import javax.net.ssl.*;
import java.io.*;
import java.util.concurrent.*;
import java.net.*;
import java.sql.*;

public class SecureHttpServer {
    private int port;
    private int maxThreads;
    private SSLServerSocket serverSocket;

    public SecureHttpServer(int port, int maxThreads) {
        this.port = port;
        this.maxThreads = maxThreads;
    }

    public void startServer() throws IOException {
        SSLServerSocketFactory sslServerSocketFactory =
                    (SSLServerSocketFactory) SSLServerSocketFactory.getDefault();
        serverSocket = (SSLServerSocket) sslServerSocketFactory.createServerSocket(port);
        ExecutorService executor = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(maxThreads);
        while (true) {
            try {
                SSLSocket clientSocket = (SSLSocket) serverSocket.accept();
                executor.execute(new RequestHandler(clientSocket));
            } catch (IOException ex) {
                System.out.println("Error accepting client connection" + ex);
                break;
            }
        }
        executor.shutdown();
    }

    private class RequestHandler implements Runnable {
        private final SSLSocket socket;
        
        RequestHandler(SSLSocket socket) { this.socket = socket; }

        @Override
        public void run() {
            try {
                InputStream input = socket.getInputStream();
                BufferedReader reader = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(input));

                while (true) {
                    String line = reader.readLine();
