Sure, You can create a function like this.

```javascript
function getCountryByCity(data, city) {
    return data.countries.reduce((acc, country) => {
        if (country.cities.includes(city)) acc = country.name;
        return acc;
    }, 'City not found in any country');
}
```
This function reduces the countries array. On each iteration it checks if the cities array of the current country includes the city passed as argument. If it does it sets the accumulator (acc) to the name of this country. If the city isn't found in any country 'City not found in any country' is returned as a default value.
