My designer keeps throwing out the term "liquid" layout. What does this mean?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
A "liquid" layout, also known as a fluid or responsive layout, is a type of website design where the layout can adjust and adapt to the screen size on which it is viewed. This means all elements of the webpage - from images to text - will resize proportionally and seamlessly whether viewed on a mobile device, tablet, or desktop. It gives a better user experience as it optimizes the view for different devices.
