how do i save int argc, char* argv in to int someting.
i am trying to get the arguments from a test program and save it into int ****;

#include <iostream> 
#include <cstdlib>
using namespace std;

int main(int argc, char* argv[]) {
 int limit = argc;
 cout<< limit <<endl;
 for (int candidate = 2; candidate < limit; candidate++) {
    int total = 1;
    for (int factor = 2; factor * factor < candidate; factor++) {
        if (candidate % factor == 0)
            total += factor + candidate / factor;

    }
    if (total == candidate) {
        cout << candidate << ' ';
    }
}
return 0;
}


and the program is pre-set the arguments is 100, and it just can't save in to `int limit`
<|end|>
<|asst|>
The variable argc is an integer that represents the number of arguments that were entered on the command line when running your program. argv is an array of pointers to these values. These command line values are accessed as strings by your program.

The problem you're having is that you're trying to save the value of argc (which is a count of the number of arguments) to limit instead of the actual argument value. In addition, command line arguments are passed as strings, so you need to convert the string to integer if you want to use it for arithmetic calculations.

Here's how you can get the first command line argument as an integer:

```cpp
#include <iostream> 
#include <cstdlib>
using namespace std;

int main(int argc, char* argv[]) {
    if(argc < 2) {
        cout << "No command line argument provided" << endl;
        return 1;
    }

    int limit = stoi(argv[1]);  // Converts the first command line argument to an int
    cout << limit << endl;

    for (int candidate = 2; candidate < limit; candidate++) {
        int total = 1;
        for (int factor = 2; factor * factor < candidate; factor++) {
            if (candidate % factor == 0)
                total += factor + candidate / factor;
        }
        if (total == candidate) {
            cout << candidate << ' ';
        }
    }
    return 0;
}
```
In the above code, `stoi()` function is used to convert string value to an integer. Also, a check is added to make sure command line argument is provided. If no argument is provided, it will print an error message and exit the program.
<|end|>


