Design a live, blockchain-focused collaborative system proficient in flawlessly integrating various data forms, particularly social media feeds, into a Cassandra data warehouse. This system should prioritize user-friendly interaction and instant transparency of alterations. It should also consider the system's capacity for growth and performance improvement, while foreseeing upcoming technological advancements and the need for effective resource distribution. Moreover, the system should demonstrate outstanding competence in managing massive data and ensure data authenticity and protection. This task requires a multi-step reasoning process, considering not only the immediate requirements but also future-proofing the system.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
System Name: Social-CasseChain

Step 1: System Architecture Development

The foundational architecture of Social-CasseChain will be a hybrid peer-to-peer network with nodes that can both provide and consume resources. It will join together data streams from various sources (particularly social media feeds) and ensure a flawless integration into a Cassandra data warehouse.

Step 2: Blockchain Implementation

The system will use a blockchain to process and record all data alterations. Blockchain's inherent transparency and immutability properties are perfect for hosting this data. Every change made to data on the Social-CasseChain will be recorded on a block and added to the chain. 

Step 3: User-Friendly Interaction

The system will have a ready-to-use interface making it easy for users to interact with. It can be used to view the data, to verify authenticity, and to trace its origins. The system will also provide a dashboard to manage and monitor in real-time the data streams and detect data anomalies.

Step 4: Data Integration

System should make use of Apache Kafka for real-time integration of social media feeds into a Cassandra data warehouse. Kafka is built for streaming enormous amounts of data in real-time and can be integrated with Cassandra for storing streamed data. 

Step 5: Scalability and Performance

Social-CasseChain will be designed to handle growth and improve performance. Using Cassandra ensures scale-out architecture and the ability to add new resources as demand grows, without impacting system performance. The system will also employ sharding to distribute data across multiple machines and improve query performance.

Step 6: Provision for Future Technological Advancements

To future-proof the system, Social-CasseChain will adopt a flexible microservice architecture. Each module will be constructed to be standalone, making it more straightforward to add, modify, or remove components as needed.

Step 7: Data Security Measures

The solution will implement robust access control mechanisms to protect sensitive data. It will adopt encryption to ensure data privacy. 

By performing these steps, we can build the Social-CasseChain to be proficient in integrating varied data forms into the Cassandra warehouse and allowing transparent instant alterations. This system will demonstrate remarkable competence in managing massive data flow while providing user-friendly access and securing data authenticity.
