The Recent Projects panel on the Start Page of VS2008 Professional doesn't appear to work, and constantly remains empty.

I've noticed this on 3 of our developers VS2008 installations, in fact all the installations that weren't updated from 2005 but installed from scratch. I generally treat this as a bit of a curiosity, but now I have a new laptop and fresh install of VS2008, it's also happening to me, and I've upgraded the phenomena from a curio to an annoyance.

Anyone know if this is a bug or if there is a setting I'm missing somewhere.

Thanks

 Thanks, but Tools | Options | Environment | General | "items shown in recently used lists" was and is set to 6 by default
<|end|>
<|asst|>
This could be because the settings for keeping a list of recently opened projects are not being retained. When you close Visual Studio, it is supposed to save the list of opened projects in a particular registry key. If that process is being interrupted for any reason, the list would not be retained and the Recent Projects panel would then appear to be broken.

Try running Visual Studio as an administrator and see if the issue persists. This will allow it to read and write to the registry without any restrictions.

Also, check the registry key where this data is stored: HKEY_CURRENT_USER\Software\Microsoft\VisualStudio\9.0\ProjectMRUList. You should see the most recently used projects listed in there.

Finally, there may be an issue with your Visual Studio installation. You could try repairing or reinstalling the application to see if that resolves the issue.
