I would like to create a mechanism that extracts proper titles and possibly other metadata from Torrent names for TV shows and other types. As you may be aware, Torrent names contain various crap such as dots and other irrelevant strings.
Specifically, I have data of some ten thousand correctly converted torrent names to proper title and more. I should use this "training set" somehow.
What ML method should I employ? I know there are regex-type solutions to this problem, but I would like to find a Machine Learning solution.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
This kind of problem can be solved using a Named Entity Recognition (NER) model. NER is a subtask of information extraction that seeks to locate and classify named entities in text into predefined categories such as person names, organizations, locations, medical codes, time expressions, quantities, monetary values, percentages, etc.

You can use a deep learning technique for this problem, Recurrent Neural Networks (RNN), more specifically, bidirectional LSTM might also work for this task. LSTM (Long Short Term Memory) is a type of Recurrent Neural Network which has a memory state that helps in remembering the previous context/input.

RNN will help to tackle the sequence data effectively because the position of words in torrent names could be really important.

You could also look at Seq2Seq Models which are originally designed for translation problems but could be used for this use-case too. The idea is that you can 'translate' your torrent name into a clean title.

In terms of libraries, you might look into Tensorflow or Pytorch for deep learning models. For a more direct approach, the SpaCy library in Python has Named Entity Recognition built-in that could be trained on your data.

Lastly, as you mentioned you have 10k records of correct conversions, this would certainly help in training your models. Remember more the data better the model's performance.

These models would need to be trained in a supervised method, using your conversions as labeled data. After training is over, the model will be able to predict and convert unseen torrent names.

Here is an outline of what you need to do.

1. Preprocess the torrent names, such as removing common words, or making words all lower case, removing punctuations etc.
2. Convert your words to a list of numbers, or word embedding like word2vec or Glove.
3. Split your data into train and test sets
4. Create your model architecture
5. Train your model
6. Test the accuracy of your model on the test set
7. Iterate and refine your model if necessary. 

Please remember there might not be a one-size-fits-all solution. Depending on the data and your requirement, you might need to try different models to see which could work best for your case.
