Identify the type of data structure used in the following algorithm.
In this algorithm, a series of elements from a particular data structure called "stack" are processed:

while not stack.isEmpty():
    process(stack.pop())
<|end|>
<|asst|>
The type of data structure used in the following algorithm is a Stack. 

A Stack is a linear data structure that follows the LIFO (Last In First Out) principle. This means the last element inserted into the stack will be the first one to be removed. It allows two main operations push and pop. 

Push inserts an element onto the stack whereas pop removes the recently added element. Additionally, this algorithm uses an operation called isEmpty() which checks whether the stack is empty.

In the algorithm presented, elements from the stack are processed from the top (most recently added element) until the stack is empty. This is a common usage of the stack data structure.
<|end|>


