To make an SVG responsive, the width and height attributes of the SVG element are typically set in percentage values so that it scales relative to the dimensions of its containing element. However, your SVG uses a viewBox to define the aspect ratio, so it will maintain these proportions as its dimensions change. 

You can make the SVG responsive by removing the width and height values like so:

```html
<svg viewBox="0 0 32 32" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
