If you want to set a scaling factor manually (e.g to ensure the SVG does not exceed a certain size), you can use CSS to control the SVG's width or height. For example, you can use `max-width` or `max-height`.

Here's an example:

```css
svg {
  max-width: 100%;
  height: auto;
}
```

This will ensure that your SVG will not exceed the width of its parent container and will scale its height to maintain its aspect ratio.
