Design an elaborate JavaScript function that not only determines the total count of leap years, but also identifies each individual leap year within a provided range of years, ensuring precision and accuracy.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here is a JavaScript function that accomplishes this. This function determines whether a year is leap or not by checking the following criteria:
- The year is evenly divisible by 4;
- If the year can be evenly divided by 100, it is NOT a leap year, unless;
- The year is also evenly divisible by 400, then it is a leap year.

```javascript
function identifyLeapYears(startYear, endYear) {
    // An array to store the leap years
    var leapYears = [];
  
    for(let year = startYear; year <= endYear; year++) {
        if ((year % 4 === 0 && year % 100 !== 0) || (year % 400 === 0)) {
            leapYears.push(year);
        }
    }
  
    // Log out the total count and the individual leap years
    console.log('Total count of leap years: ', leapYears.length);
    console.log('Individual leap years: ', leapYears);
    
    return leapYears; // Return leap years
} 

identifyLeapYears(2000, 2020);
```

This code will log the count of leap years and individual leap years from 2000 to 2020 (both years inclusive).
<|end|>


