Problem:
I have a multi-index dataframe as follows:

                        a  b
name        number         
John        123   100  7
Jane        456   90  8
Jack        789    80  9
Where numbers are stored as str.

I want to parse number index using pd.to_numeric, and swap the two levels.
The final output should be:

                a  b
number  name            
123     John   100  7
456     Jane   90  8
789     Jack   80  9
Any help would be appreciated.

A:
&lt;code&gt;
import pandas as pd
def f(df):
    # return the solution in this function
    # df = f(df)
    ### BEGIN SOLUTION
<|end|>
<|asst|>
df.index = df.index.set_levels([df.index.levels[0], pd.to_numeric(df.index.levels[1])])
df = df.swaplevel(0,1)
return df
### END SOLUTION
<|end|>


