Create a web scraper using Python that collects the title and content from the homepage of a given website.
https://www.example.com as the target website.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Web scraping involves fetching data from a website and extracting the needed information. Ensure to check the website’s scraping policy before you start web scraping to avoid legal issues.

Below is a simple Python script using BeautifulSoup and requests libraries for web scraping. These libraries are not included in the basic Python packages, and you need to install them through pip.

```
from bs4 import BeautifulSoup
import requests

# Step 1: Send HTTP request to website
url = 'https://www.example.com'

response = requests.get(url)

# Step 2: Parse HTML content 
soup = BeautifulSoup(response.content, 'html.parser')

# Step 3: Extract Title
title = soup.title.string
print("Title: ", title)

# Step 4: Extract content on homepage
# here we will get all text inside the body tag
body = soup.find_all("body")
for content in body:
    print(content.get_text())
```

Notes:
1. We use 'https://www.example.com' as an example website, replace it with your target, also some websites block scraping bots, so make sure the website allows it.
2. This script simply fetches the page's title and all text present inside the body of the HTML. 
3. Real-world websites are usually more complex. To accurately grab specific data pieces or navigate through multiple pages, you’ll need to make your scraper more sophisticated.
4. Some websites have a robots.txt file (www.website.com/robots.txt), which tells web crawlers which pages or files the crawler can or can't request from your site. Make sure to check this file before starting to scrape a website.
5. Web scraping may violate the Terms of Service of some websites. Always check a website's policy before performing any scraping activities.
<|end|>


