I know you can just use CSS to hide the DIV or Silverlight Plugin, but is there a way to instantiate a Silverlight Component/App using JavaScript that doesn't show any UI element at all?

There is alot of great functionality in Silverlight, like MultiThreading and compiled code, that could be utilized by traditional Ajax apps without using the XAML/UI layer of Silverlight at all.

I would like to just use the standard HTML/CSS for my UI layer only, and use some compiled .NET/Silverlight code in the background.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Yes you can do this by setting height and width properties of div tag to be 0px where siliverlight plugin is configured. Here is an example.

```html
<div id="silverlightControlHost" style="height:0px; width:0px;">
    <object data="data:application/x-silverlight-2," type="application/x-silverlight-2" width="100%" height="100%" >
        <param name="source" value="ClientBin/YourSilverlightApp.xap"/>
    </object>
</div>
```

And you can interact with Silverlight app using Javascript.

Read more details here: https://msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/cc645085(v=vs.95).aspx

However, please be aware that Silverlight is being phased out. Microsoft announced that Silverlight development and support will be discontinued and it would be best to move to a more modern technology stack for new development work.
<|end|>


