In my Google Workspace account, I use [color label strings](https://support.google.com/calendar/answer/12377581) in Calendar to track time. I want to use these to automate timesheet reporting using the Calendar API. How do I access the label strings associated with each color ID?
The [Colors resource](https://developers.google.com/calendar/api/v3/reference/colors) (2022-12-19 version) only provides foreground and background color data, no label string. Also the [Settings resource](https://developers.google.com/calendar/api/v3/reference/settings) (2022-12-19 version) does not provide what I need. I have also tried the [CalDAV API](https://developers.google.com/calendar/caldav/v2/guide) (2022-12-19 version) but that does not seem to provide color or label information at all.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Unfortunately, as of now, Google Calendar API (v3) does not have official support for fetching color label strings. The Color resource in the API allows you to access color IDs and their corresponding RGB values, but it does not provide the labels(strings) associated with these color IDs.

As you mentioned, the Settings resource does not store this information either. The Calendar API primarily deals with the events on the Google Calendar, and while it allows tagging these events with color IDs for organizational purposes, the labels(strings) for these IDs are not exposed by the API.

As a workaround, you may consider maintaining your custom mapping of color IDs to labels within your application. You can manually map the color IDs to their corresponding labels as provided by Google Workspace according to your usage. This, however, requires manual maintenance and does not scale/reflect Google Workspace UI changes automatically.
<|end|>


