I want to consumer to consume messages in  batch based on the length/size of the message batch means batch of 1kb and max poll.record with 100. at max it polls 100 message or 1kb of message.

max.poll.records =100


How do I set 1kb of message at max in the batch ?
I have tried with `max.partition.fetch.bytes=1024` but I am getting 100 message even message batch  is larger than 1024 bytes. How to control this behaviour ?
How do I set at max 1kb of message with cap of 100 message per batch at max ?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Kafka consumer uses two main properties to control the amount of data the consumer fetches in a single request: 

- `max.poll.records` (which you've used to limit the number of records)

- `fetch.max.bytes` (which allows you to limit the total bytes in the fetched records)

If you want to restrict the consumer to fetch 1kb across all partitions, you can set `fetch.max.bytes` to 1024. However, please note that `fetch.max.bytes` limits the total amount of bytes the fetcher will accumulate before it stops fetching more records. It's not a strict limit on record batch size. 

Another property is `max.partition.fetch.bytes` that you tried. It designs to limit the total bytes from a single partition. If you have multiple partitions, your fetched data can be larger than this when data from other partitions are accumulated.

Unfortunately, Kafka Consumer does not provide a strict single setting to limit the number of bytes fetched per poll and stop fetching even it has not reached `max.poll.records`. A combination of `max.poll.records` and `fetch.max.bytes` should be used together to initialize a batch size. 

If you are fetching from multiple partitions, and you want to control the byte size strictly under 1kb, you might need to control this at the application level. That is to code a logic which calculates the total size of received messages, and if it exceeds 1Kb, then stop consuming more messages in the current poll. 

Remember that, in Kafka, records are fetched in batches by the consumer, and if a batch of records is larger than this amount, the first record batch will be returned to the consumer and the maximum size of the next fetch request to Kafka will be adjusted downwards.
<|end|>


