Problem:
I have a dataframe in Pandas that looks like this:
    name  x  y   z
0  Alice  2  4   6
1  Alice  2  5   8
2  Alice  2  5  11
3  Bob    3  5   0
4  Bob    2  5   2


I want to combine name and x and replace each of them with a unique ID so output looks like:
  ID  y   z
0    1  4   6
1    1  5   8
2    1  5  11
3    2  5   0
4    3  5   2


How can I achieve this?
Thanks!


A:
&lt;code&gt;
import pandas as pd


df = pd.DataFrame({&#39;name&#39;: [&#39;Alice&#39;, &#39;Alice&#39;, &#39;Alice&#39;, &#39;Bob&#39;, &#39;Bob&#39;, &#39;Charlie&#39;],
                   &#39;x&#39;: [2, 2, 2, 3, 2, 4],
                   &#39;y&#39;: [4, 5, 5, 5, 5, 2],
                   &#39;z&#39;: [6, 8, 11, 0, 2, 5]})
&lt;/code&gt;
result = ... # put solution in this variable
BEGIN SOLUTION
&lt;code&gt;
<|end|>
<|asst|>
df['ID'] = (df['name'] + df['x'].astype(str)).astype('category').cat.codes
df.drop(columns=['name', 'x'], inplace=True)
result = df
&lt;/code&gt;
END SOLUTION
<|end|>


