Refactor the following code:

/*
   Given an array of integers nums, find the product of the maximum and minimum numbers in each non-empty sub-array of nums. Then find the maximum product amongst all sub-arrays.
  
   Example
   maxSubarrayProduct([2, 3, -2, 4]) should return -4, as the sub-arrays are [2], [3], [-2], [4], [2,3], [2,3,-2], [2,3,-2,4], [3,-2], [3,-2,4], [-2, 4] and their products are 2, 3, -2, 4, 6, -12, -48, -6, -24, -8 respectively.
   
   maxSubarrayProduct([-1, -2, -3]) should return -1, as the sub-arrays are [-1], [-2], [-3], [-1,-2], [-1,-2,-3], [-2,-3] and their products are -1, -2, -3, 2, 6, 6 respectively.
*/
const maxSubarrayProduct = (nums) => {
<|end|>
<|asst|>
The given problem can be solved using dynamic programming. 

I would start by defining two arrays `maxProduct` and `minProduct` to keep track of the maximum and minimum product till the current element respectively. 

Then I would iterate through the given array and at each index, update the `maxProduct` and `minProduct`.

Finally, I would return the max value from the `maxProduct` array as it represents the maximum product amongst all sub-arrays.

Here is the refactored code:

```
const maxSubarrayProduct = (nums) => {
    let maxProduct = new Array(nums.length);
    let minProduct = new Array(nums.length);

    maxProduct[0] = nums[0];
    minProduct[0] = nums[0];

    for (let i = 1; i < nums.length; i++) {
        if (nums[i] > 0) {
            maxProduct[i] = Math.max(nums[i], maxProduct[i - 1] * nums[i]);
            minProduct[i] = Math.min(nums[i], minProduct[i - 1] * nums[i]);
        } else {
            maxProduct[i] = Math.max(nums[i], minProduct[i - 1] * nums[i]);
            minProduct[i] = Math.min(nums[i], maxProduct[i - 1] * nums[i]);
        }
    }

    return Math.max(...maxProduct);
}
```

This code works by keeping track of the maximum and minimum product upto each element in separate arrays. The maximum product can be obtained by multiplying the current element with the maximum product so far (if the current element is positive) or by multiplying with the minimum product so far (if the current element is negative). The minimum product is calculated in a similar fashion.

The time complexity of this code is O(n) as we are only iterating once through the given array and the space complexity is also O(n) as we are storing the maximum and minimum product upto each element in separate arrays.
<|end|>


