When developing a new web based application which version of html should you aim for?

EDIT:

cool I was just attempting to get a feel from others I tend to use XHTML 1.0 Strict in my own work and Transitional when others are involved in the content creation.

I marked the first XHTML 1.0 Transitional post as the 'correct answer' but believe strongly that all the answers given at that point where equally valid.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
As of 2021, you should aim for HTML5 when developing a new web-based application. HTML5 is the latest version of HTML and it is widely supported by all modern browsers. It also provides many new features and capabilities that were not available in previous versions of HTML, such as native support for video and audio elements, drawing capabilities with the canvas element, and the ability to create more interactive and dynamic web pages with the addition of new form controls and API's.
 In addition, HTML5 is designed to be backwards compatible, so older browsers that do not support all of the new features will still be able to render HTML5 pages correctly.
