Design a methodology in Java programming language to compute the factorial of a given integer input.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
The problem involves computing the factorial of a given number. In mathematics, the factorial of a non-negative integer n is the product of all positive integers less than or equal to n. It is denoted by n!.

A simple approach to designing the solution would involve using a loop that iteratively multiply each integer from 1 to the given number.

Below is a simple Java code snippet that computes the factorial of a number:

```java
import java.util.Scanner;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);
        System.out.print("Enter the number: ");
        int num = scanner.nextInt();

        long factorial = getFactorial(num);
    
        System.out.printf("Factorial of %d = %d", num, factorial);
    }

    private static long getFactorial(int num) {
        long factorial = 1;
        for(int i = 1; i <= num; i++) {
            factorial *= i;
        }
        return factorial;
    }
}
```
In this code, the `getFactorial` function computes the factorial of a number by iterating from 1 to the given number and multiplying the factorial variable.

Please note that the factorial of a large number can be a very large number, we use long rather than int for the factorial variable to avoid overflow.

This code works by reading the number from user input, then the 'getFactorial' function is called which calculates the factorial of the number and returns it. The result is then printed in the console.

Also, it is important to note that the calculation of the factorial is a standard example for demonstration the concept of recursion, although the provided implementation does not use this approach due to potential issues with stack overflow errors for large numbers if a recursive approach is taken.
<|end|>


