- The conditions of the ternary operator are inconsistent, it is first checking if score is greater than 80 and then again checking if it is less than 60. This would result in no output for scores between 60 and 80 (exclusive).

Here is the corrected function:
```javascript
function scoreFeedback() {
  var score = 95;
  return (score > 80) ? "Well done" : ((score >= 61) && (score <= 80)) ? "Satisfactory" : "Improvement needed";
}
```

Here, the function returns "Well done" if score is greater than 80, "Satisfactory" if score is between 61 and 80 (inclusive) else it returns "Improvement needed". Also note that the function now returns the feedback string as expected.
