Implement a Palindrome checker in Java that ignores special characters and whitespace. The program should also be case-insensitive.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here is a simple Java program to solve your problem:

```java
public class PalindromeChecker {
  
    // Method to check if string is palindrome
    public static boolean isPalindrome(String str) {
        // Removing special characters and converting string to lowercase
        String sanitizedStr = str.replaceAll("[^a-zA-Z0-9]", "").toLowerCase();

        // Reverse the cleaned string
        String reverseStr = new StringBuilder(sanitizedStr).reverse().toString();

        // Checking if reverse string is same as original string
        return sanitizedStr.equals(reverseStr);
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println(isPalindrome("A man, a plan, a canal: Panama")); // true
        System.out.println(isPalindrome("Not a palindrome")); // false
    }
}
```
This program works by first removing all the special characters from the input string and converting it to lower case, then reversing the cleaned string, and finally checking if the reversed string is the same as the original cleaned string. If yes, then the string is a palindrome, otherwise it's not.
<|end|>


