I'm trying to find a simple way to change the colour of the text and background in `listview` and `treeview` controls in WTL or plain Win32 code.

I really don't want to have to implement full owner drawing for these controls, simply change the colours used.

I want to make sure that the images are still drawn with proper transparency.

Any suggestions?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Sure, to change the text/ background color of a ListView or a TreeView control you don't need to fully ownerdraw it; you can respond to NM_CUSTOMDRAW notification which these controls send. 

Here is an example of how you can do it:

Step 1: Set up the window procedure for the control. 

```cpp
case WM_NOTIFY: {
    LPNMHDR lParam = reinterpret_cast<LPNMHDR>(lParam);
    if (lParam->idFrom == IDC_YOURCONTROLID && lParam->code == NM_CUSTOMDRAW) {
        SetWindowLong(hWnd, DWL_MSGRESULT, (LONG)ProcessCustomDraw(lParam));
        return TRUE;
    }
    break;
}
```

Step 2: Set up custom drawing procedure

```cpp
LRESULT ProcessCustomDraw (LPNMHDR nmhdr) {
    LPNMLVCUSTOMDRAW lplvcd = reinterpret_cast<LPNMLVCUSTOMDRAW>(nmhdr);

    switch(lplvcd->nmcd.dwDrawStage) {
        case CDDS_PREPAINT:
            return CDRF_NOTIFYITEMDRAW;
        case CDDS_ITEMPREPAINT:
            lplvcd->clrText = RGB(255, 255, 255); // Set the text color
            lplvcd->clrTextBk = RGB(0, 0, 255); // Set the background color
            return CDRF_DODEFAULT;
        }
    return CDRF_DODEFAULT;
}
```

And similarly for TreeView control. 

Remember to replace `RGB(255,255,255)` and `RGB(0,0,255)` with the colors you want to apply to text and backgrounds respectively.

The code above will set the ListView's text color to white and the background color to blue.

In the code above the colors are hardcoded, but you can replace `RGB(255,255,255)` and `RGB(0,0,255)` with variables which you could update when required. Remember to refresh the control to update the colors using `InvalidateRect()`.

In CDDS_ITEMPREPAINT case, the function `SetTextColor()` and `SetBkColor()` change the colors for each item as they are drawn.
