If the template only pertains to Windows, but is written in C#, then you can place the template in the Windows directory so it shows up correctly.

This is how you should do it:

1. Open the template .zip file.
2. Open the .vstemplate file in a text editor.
3. Modify the `<TemplateGroupID>` element to `WinApp`.

Like this:

```xml
<TemplateGroupID>WinApp</TemplateGroupID>
```

4. Save and close the .vstemplate file.
5. Copy the template .zip file to the relevant directory in the user templates folder, e.g. “...\Documents\Visual Studio 2008\Templates\ProjectTemplates\Visual C#\Windows”

The template should now appear under the relevant Windows category in the New Project dialog.

Note: If you can't find the template there, try restarting Visual Studio to ensure it detects the new template.
