Design a system for users that precisely tracks a particular thread within the Peer-to-Peer communication model, leveraging the application programming interface of Slack to dispatch an alert every time a new file is shared in the network.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
System Name: P2PFileTracker

1. User Authentication:
The system will initially authenticate users by using Slack's API for user authentication. This will ensure the secure and legitimate access to the system.

2. Thread Tracking:
The system will keep track of all activities happening throughout particular threads as specified by the user. This threading feature will be accomplished using the Slack Conversations API. Users can select the specific threads or all threads to monitor.

3. File Sharing Detection:
Once the tracking is activated, the system will monitor all activities for file sharing events. This functionality will be achieved with the help of Slack's Files API. The Files API enables the system to detect when any new files are uploaded or shared within the threads.

4. Alert Dispatch:
As soon as new file sharing activity is detected, the system will trigger an alert. This would be realized by utilizing Slack's Incoming WebHooks feature to post a message to the specified Slack channel or user. The alert message would contain details of the file, user and the thread.

5. Settings & Customization:
The system will also provide settings to customize the level of alert sensitivity such as frequency of alerts, kinds of files to alert for, specific threads to monitor, etc. 

6. Log & Report:
The system will maintain a log of all alerts and generate reports showing the statistics of file sharing activities in the chosen threads.

7. Slack App:
To facilitate usage, a Slack App will also be developed so users can set up and control the system directly from Slack.

Tech Stack:
The back-end logic of this system could be developed with Node.js using the Slack Node SDK. For data storage and management, MongoDB or any other NoSQL databases can be used due to its flexibility and scalability. The webhooks would be handled by Express.js framework.

In summary, P2PFileTracker will use various APIs provided by Slack to monitor threads in a Peer-to-Peer communication network and will alert users whenever a new file is shared in the monitored threads.
<|end|>


