I found one post that suggested I use

HostNetwork: true


in the spec: section on my bind9-deployment.yaml file but I'm not sure whether it goes in the spec: under

kind: Service


or

kind: Deployment


section of my file.
I am hoping eventually to make my on-prem bind9 service available to my local network.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
The `HostNetwork: true` field belongs in the `spec:` under the `kind: Pod` section, which you will typically find under the `spec: template:` section inside `kind: Deployment`.

If your bind9 deployment file is like most `kind: Deployment` configurations, it will look something like this:

```
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: my-deployment
spec:
  replicas: 3
  template:
    spec:
      containers:
      - name: bind9
        image: bind9:latest
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: my-app
```
You need to add `hostNetwork: true` under the `spec:` fields related to the `template:`. Like so:

```
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: my-deployment
spec:
  replicas: 3
  template:
    spec:
      hostNetwork: true
      containers:
      - name: bind9
        image: bind9:latest
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: my-app
```
