Develop an algorithmic solution that classifies a supplied sequence of dates, taking into account the nuances of consecutive weekly intervals, while supporting edge cases such as weeks that overflow into the next month or year.
Sequence of dates: ["2022-01-01", "2022-01-02", "2022-01-08", "2022-01-15", "2022-01-16", "2022-01-22", "2022-02-01"]
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here is a Python solution using the datetime module which can analyze your list of dates and classify them by week.

The script works by converting each date string into a datetime object. It then assigns each datetime object to a week number within its respective year. Finally, it sorts the dates into weeks taking in account dates that overflow into the next month or year.

```python
from datetime import datetime, timedelta

def classify_dates(date_list):
    week_dict = {}
    
    for date_str in date_list:
        date_obj = datetime.strptime(date_str, "%Y-%m-%d")
        
        start_week = date_obj - timedelta(days=date_obj.weekday())
        end_week = start_week + timedelta(days=6)
        
        if start_week.month != end_week.month or start_week.year != end_week.year:
            week_key = f"Week starting {start_week.strftime('%Y-%m-%d')} (Overflow Week)"
        else:
            week_key = f"Week starting {start_week.strftime('%Y-%m-%d')}"

        if week_key in week_dict:
            week_dict[week_key].append(date_str)
        else:
            week_dict[week_key] = [date_str]
            
    return week_dict

date_list = ["2022-01-01", "2022-01-02", "2022-01-08", "2022-01-15", "2022-01-16", 
             "2022-01-22", "2022-02-01"]

result = classify_dates(date_list)
for key in result:
    print(key, ':', result[key])
```

This script considers Monday as the first day of the week. If you consider Sunday as the first day of the week, we can modify the "date_obj.weekday()" to "(date_obj.weekday() + 6) % 7". 

This script assumes the input dates are in ascending order. If the dates come in some random order, a bit of preprocessing is needed to sort the dates.
