Create a Vue.js component with a button that calls an action when clicked.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Sure, here is an example of a Vue.js component with a button that calls an action when it is clicked:

```vue
<template>
  <button @click="performAction">Click Me</button>
</template>

<script>
export default {
  methods: {
    performAction() {
      alert("Button was clicked");
      // You can replace the alert with the action you want to perform
    },
  },
};
</script>
```

Here are some things to note about this code:

- The `<template>` section is where you put the HTML for your button.
- `@click` is Vue.js shorthand for the `v-on:click` directive - it tells Vue.js to perform the action (i.e., the method in the component's methods property) when the button is clicked.
- `performAction` is a function defined in the methods attribute of our Vue.js component. This is where you specify the action you want to execute when the button is clicked.
