      </div>
      <div class="column">
        <h2>Column 2</h2>
        <p>Pear</p>
        <p>Kiwi</p>
        <p>Mango</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
```

In the above code, HTML `<div>` elements are used to create two columns inside a row. CSS is used to give these elements their "column" behavior, by assigning 50% width and a little bit of padding. The style `.row::after` is used clear the floats and maintain the normal layout flow after the two columns. The `<h2>` tags are used to provide headers to the columns and the `<p>` tags are used to list the fruits in each column.
