If I have a 


<input id="uploadFile" type="file" />



tag, and a submit button, how do I determine, in IE6 (and above) if a file has been selected by the user.

In FF, I just do:


var selected = document.getElementById("uploadBox").files.length > 0;



But that doesn't work in IE.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
In Internet Explorer (including legacy versions like IE6), the File API, which includes the "files" property, is not fully supported. However, you can check the "value" property of the file input to see if a file is selected. The "value" property contains the full path of the file on the user's local system.

In JavaScript:

```javascript
var selected = document.getElementById("uploadFile").value;
if(selected.length > 0){
    //file was selected
}
```

Please remember that, due to security restrictions in modern browsers, the file path returned from the "value" property might be obfuscated or not a full path. It is generally best not to rely on the value for anything other than checking whether it is empty.
<|end|>


