<|user|>
Develop a JavaScript program that not only calculates the geometric mean of four provided numbers but also checks if the numbers are positive integers. If not, return a custom error message. Note: The four numbers could range from 1 to 10,000.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here's a simple function in JavaScript that performs those actions:

```javascript
function geometricMean(a, b, c, d){
    // Check if the values are positive integers
    if (!Number.isInteger(a) || a < 1 || !Number.isInteger(b) || b < 1 || !Number.isInteger(c) || c < 1 || !Number.isInteger(d) || d < 1){
        return "All parameters should be positive integers!";
    }

    // Check if the values are within the defined range
    if (a > 10000 || b > 10000 || c > 10000 || d > 10000) {
        return "The parameters should be in the range from 1 to 10,000!";
    }

    // Calculate the geometric mean
    var product = a * b * c * d;
    var mean = Math.pow(product, 0.25);
    
    return mean;
}
```

You can call the above function using 4 numbers. The function will check if all 4 numbers are positive integers within the defined range, and then return the geometric mean of those 4 numbers. If any number doesn't meet the criteria, the function will return an error message.
<|end|>


