Develop a C++ code to generate a sequence of Fibonacci series up to nth place and also count the number of even and odd numbers in the series. Your program must handle input errors. <n = 5>
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here is a simple C++ code to generate a sequence of the Fibonacci series up to nth place and also count the number of even and odd numbers in series. This code also checks for invalid inputs.

```C++
#include<iostream>
using namespace std;
int main()
{
    int n, a = 0, b = 1, nextTerm;
    int evenCount = 0, oddCount = 0;

    cout << "Enter a positive number: ";
    cin >> n;

    // check if the input is valid, if not prompt the user again
    while (cin.fail() || n <= 0)
    {
        cin.clear(); //clear the error flags
        cin.ignore(std::numeric_limits<std::streamsize>::max(), '\n'); //ignore the wrong input
        cout << "Invalid input. Please enter a positive number: ";
        cin >> n;
    }
    cout << "Fibonacci Series: ";
    for (int i = 1; i <= n; ++i)
    {
        cout << a << ", ";
        if (a % 2 == 0)
            evenCount++;
        else
            oddCount++;

        nextTerm = a + b;
        a = b;
        b = nextTerm;
    }
    cout << "\nNumber of even numbers: " << evenCount;
    cout << "\nNumber of odd numbers: " << oddCount;

    return 0;
}
```
This program prompts the user for a number n and generates the Fibonacci series up to the nth term. It also counts the number of even and odd numbers in the series. If the user enters an invalid input (like a negative number or a non-numeric value), the program will prompt the user to enter a correct number until a valid input is provided.
<|end|>


