As a text-based AI, I do not have the ability to manipulate SVG or any other type of visual element. However, I can guide you on how to make the SVG appear like it's breathing or pulsating.

Here's a simple way to do that using CSS:

1. Save the SVG in a file and include it into your HTML file via `img` tag:
```html
<img id="pulsatingSVG" src="image.svg" />
```

2. Add CSS animation to make the SVG 'breathe'
```css
@keyframes pulsate {
   0% { transform: scale(1); }
   50% { transform: scale(1.1); }
   100% { transform: scale(1); }
}

#pulsatingSVG {
   animation: pulsate 2s infinite;
}
```
This CSS animation will cause the SVG to scale up by 10% (to 1.1 times its original size) and then scale back down to its original size in a continuous loop, giving the effect of 'breathing' or 'pulsating'. 

Remember, transform and animation properties work in modern browsers. Always check the compatibility of CSS features.
<|end|>


