You would need to have information on what fields are contained within the two Tables. But assuming typical Retail Database structures, SQL codes to solve the above task might look something like this:

```SQL
SELECT Customers.customer_id, Customers.customer_name
FROM Customers
JOIN Purchases ON Customers.customer_id = Purchases.customer_id
WHERE Purchases.item_price > 20;
