Ensure your program handles edge cases such as non-numeric, negative, and unusually large inputs gracefully. The form should not allow non-numeric inputs and the program should not crash for other incorrect inputs. 

Furthermore, to increase the complexity, identified a piece of erroneous code given below and provide a brief explanation of why this program could not generate the Fibonacci series correctly:

```javascript
function fibonacci(n){
  var fib_array = [0, 1];

  for(var i = 2; i <= n; i++){
    fib_array[i] = fib_array[i-2];
  }

  return fib_array;
}
```

Note: Only consider the n number of sequence, there is no need to consider performance improvement for memory usage.
