```python
def count_char_pairs(text, pair):
    count = sum(1 for i in range(len(text)-1) if text[i:i+2] == pair)
    return count

text = "abracadabra"
pair = "ab"
occurrences = count_char_pairs(text, pair)

print('The pair "{}" occurs {} times in the string "{}".'.format(pair, occurrences, text))
```
When the algorithm is run with the input string "abracadabra" and the pair "ab", it counts how many times "ab" occurs in the given string. It achieves this by iterating over the string one character at a time, creating a substring from the current character and the next one, and comparing this substring to the provided pair. If they match, it increments the count. After going through all characters in the string, it outputs the total count.

Just replace "abracadabra" and "ab" with your desired string and pair to apply this solution on different inputs.
