Could you provide me with the guidance to extract the terminating element from this array of numbers, signified through the syntax of the Python list which is as follows?
list = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Yes, you can extract the terminating (last) element from an array/list in python using list indexing. In python, you can use negative indices to access elements from the end of the list. The index of -1 refers to the last item, -2 refers to the second last item and so on.

Here is how you can extract the terminating or last element:

Python code:
```python
my_list = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]
last_element = my_list[-1]
print(last_element)
```
When you run this program, it will print the last element of the list:
```python
5
```
In this code, `my_list[-1]` is used to get the last item from the list. `my_list` is the name of the list and `-1` is the index of the last element.
<|end|>


