I encountered an issue with Cassandra 2.0.6.
I want to create a new role in Cassandra via cqlsh as following create role command. However, it returns Bad Request error message.

cqlsh> CREATE ROLE abc WITH SUPERUSER=true AND LOGIN=true AND PASSWORD='mypass';
Bad Request: line 1:7 no viable alternative at input 'ROLE'


I run the same command on Cassandra 2.2.x, it was good.
If anyone can help me understand the reason of it? Does Cassandra 2.0.6 not support ROLE in cqlsh?
If so, what is the alternative option?
Thank you so much!
Jun
<|end|>
<|asst|>
The role-based access control (RBAC) features that include `ROLE` were introduced in Apache Cassandra 2.2. Prior to version 2.2, only the concept of `USER` was there. So, the `ROLE` command is not supported in your version Cassandra 2.0.6.

Instead, you can use the `CREATE USER` command:

```
cqlsh> CREATE USER abc WITH PASSWORD 'mypass' SUPERUSER;
```

Keep in mind that this only creates users, not roles, and the user will have superuser privileges. For more granular control over permissions in version 2.0.6, you might have to use the GRANT and REVOKE permissions commands on specific keyspaces and tables.

Remember, if you need features like roles, consider upgrading to a newer version of Cassandra. Before upgrading, make sure to check the compatibility and migration guides, as there can be breaking changes between major versions.
<|end|>


