AndroidStudio formats custom line breaks.
Version: Dolphin | 2021.3.1

I tried to disable this function like below:
AndroidStudio> Preferences> Editor> Code Style> Java> Wrapping and braces> Keep when reformatting > unchecked "Line breaks"
But the problem remained.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
This may be happening because the formatter is not considering your custom line breaks as valid according to the specified style. "Keep when reformatting > Line breaks" may not work as expected when the line breaks violate other rules or policies.

Here are some things you can try:

1. Re-check "Line breaks" option: Often, it might be a small bug with the IDE where the settings may not be applied correctly. Try rechecking "Line breaks", Apply the changes and then uncheck it again. Then, try formatting your code and see if the problem persists. 

2. Check policies for chained method calls: Check the settings for chained method calls in Android Studio because by default, they are set to 'Wrap if long'. If you change its policy to 'Do not wrap', possibly, Android Studio would stop formatting it.

3. Disable reformat and rearrange code: Go to Preferences > Editor > Code Style > Java > Wrapping and Braces. Check 'Do not wrap'. Also, scroll down to 'Keep when reformatting' section and check everything.

4. Use `// @formatter:off` and `// @formatter:on`: Your last resort is to surround your custom formatted code with these lines. They instruct the IDEA/Android Studio code formatter to skip the section between the comments. Please note that this will disable all code formatting within these comments, so use this sparingly.

   For example:
   ```Java
   // @formatter:off
    your_code_here
   // @formatter:on
   ```
   
5. Reset Code Style Settings: If none of these solutions works, there's a possibility that your Code Style settings were changed mistakenly. You can try resetting these settings back to default. 

   To reset these settings, follow this path: Android Studio > Preferences > Editor > Code Style > Java > Click on the gear icon next to 'Scheme' > Select 'Reset'.
   
Remember to save your settings and possibly restart the IDE after making these changes to ensure they're correctly applied.
<|end|>


