Can you make this code C#-compliant?
def char_count(s):
    vowels = ['a', 'e', 'i', 'o', 'u', 'y']
    consonants = ['b', 'c', 'd', 'f', 'g', 'h', 'j', 'k', 'l', 'm', 'n', 'p', 'q', 'r', 's', 't', 'v', 'w', 'x', 'z']
    counts = {'Vowels': 0, 'Consonants': 0, 'Special characters': 0}

    for char in s.lower():
        if char in vowels:
            counts['Vowels'] += 1
        elif char in consonants:
            counts['Consonants'] += 1
        else:
            counts['Special characters'] += 1

    return counts

print(char_count("abcde"))
print(char_count("ACEDY"))
print(char_count("éxamplë"))
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Sure, below is the C# version of the code you have provided:

```C#
using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;

public class Program
{
    public static void Main()
    {
        Console.WriteLine(CharCount("abcde"));
        Console.WriteLine(CharCount("ACEDY"));
        Console.WriteLine(CharCount("éxamplë"));
    }

    private static Dictionary<string, int> CharCount(string s)
    {
        char[] vowels = { 'a', 'e', 'i', 'o', 'u', 'y' };
        char[] consonants = { 'b', 'c', 'd', 'f', 'g', 'h', 'j', 'k', 'l', 'm', 'n', 'p', 'q', 'r', 's', 't', 'v', 'w', 'x', 'z' };
        Dictionary<string, int> counts = new Dictionary<string, int>()
        {
            { "Vowels", 0 },
            { "Consonants", 0 },
            { "Special characters", 0 }
        };

        foreach (char c in s.ToLower())
        {
            if (Array.IndexOf(vowels, c) > -1)
            {
                counts["Vowels"]++;
            }
            else if (Array.IndexOf(consonants, c) > -1)
            {
                counts["Consonants"]++;
            }
            else
            {
                counts["Special characters"]++;
            }
        }

        return counts;
    }
}
```
In this C# code, I use Dictionary to store the counts of vowels, consonants and special characters. The `IndexOf` method of `Array` is used to check if a character is in the vowels or consonants array.
