Write code in Java for a user input prompt that states "Please enter a number". Additionally, ensure the input is an odd integer greater than 10 and less than 100.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Sure, here is a simple Java program that uses the Scanner class for user input and checks if the input is an odd number greater than 10 and less than 100.

```java
import java.util.Scanner;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);
        int num = 0;

        while (true) {
            System.out.println("Please enter a number");

            // check if input is an integer
            if (scanner.hasNextInt()) {
                num = scanner.nextInt();

                // checking if number is greater than 10, less than 100 and is an odd number
                if (num > 10 && num < 100 && num % 2 != 0) {
                    System.out.println("You've entered correct number: " + num);
                    break;
                } else {
                    System.out.println("Invalid number. Please enter odd number between 10 and 100");
                }
            } else {
                System.out.println("That's not a number. Please enter a number");
                scanner.next(); // to ignore non integer input
            }
        }

        scanner.close();
    }
}
```
This program will keep asking the user for a valid number until they input an odd number between 10 and 100.
<|end|>


