Create a responsive HTML table with five columns consisting of ID, name, email address, phone number, and date of birth. The table must include the following features:

1. The table should have a header row that differentiates it from the data rows.
2. Alternate row colors should be used for better readability.
3. The date of birth column should be hidden on mobile devices to improve responsiveness.
4. Add sort functionality to each column so that users can sort the data in ascending or descending order.
5. Ensure proper HTML syntax and structure while keeping best practices for accessibility in mind.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Sure, you could create the table using plain HTML and CSS, but to add functionalities like sorting you would typically use a JavaScript library. In this example, I use jQuery and a plugin called DataTables. I'll walk you through the code.

Here's an example of the HTML content:

```html
<table id="myTable" class="display">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th>ID</th>
            <th>Name</th>
            <th>Email</th>
            <th>Phone Number</th>
            <th class="desktop">Date of Birth</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td>1</td>
            <td>John Doe</td>
            <td>john@example.com</td>
            <td>123-456-7890</td>
            <td class="desktop">1990-01-01</td>
        </tr>
        <!-- Add additional rows as needed -->
    </tbody>
</table>
```

For CSS, I will assign alternate colors to the rows and provide responsive styling:

```css
#myTable tr:nth-child(even) {background: #CCC}
#myTable tr:nth-child(odd) {background: #FFF}

@media only screen and (max-width: 600px) {
    .desktop { display: none;}
}
```

Finally, let's add jQuery and DataTables to enhance the table:

```html
<!-- Include jQuery -->
<script src="https://ajax.googleapis.com/ajax/libs/jquery/3.5.1/jquery.min.js"></script>

<!-- Include DataTables -->
<link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="https://cdn.datatables.net/v/dt/dt-1.10.25/datatables.min.css"/>
<script type="text/javascript" src="https://cdn.datatables.net/v/dt/dt-1.10.25/datatables.min.js"></script>

<!-- Enhance the table using DataTables -->
<script>
    $(document).ready(function() {
        $('#myTable').DataTable();
    } );
</script>
```

Please note, the `max-width` value in the `@media` query should be adjusted according to your needs. It's currently set to hide the date of birth column on screens that are 600px or less in width. The classes for responsiveness are part of DataTable, which includes "desktop", "tablet-l", "tablet-p", "mobile-l", and "mobile-p". Also, the DataTables plugin provides sort functionality by default, so no additional code is required for that.
<|end|>


