I have a requirement to be be able to embed scanned tiff images into some SSRS reports.

When I design a report in VS2005 and add an image control the tiff image displays perfectly however when I build it. I get the warning :

`Warning 2 [rsInvalidMIMEType] The value of the MIMEType property for the image ‘image1’ is “image/tiff”, which is not a valid MIMEType. c:\SSRSStuff\TestReport.rdl 0 0`

and instead of an image I get the little red x.

Has anybody overcome this issue?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
It seems that SQL Server Reporting Services (SSRS) doesn't natively support TIFF image format. Only standard formats like JPEG, GIF, PNG and BMP are supported.

As a workaround, you could convert the TIFF image into one of the supported formats (like JPEG or PNG) before embedding it into the SSRS report. There are many free online tools available that can convert TIFF images to other formats.

Alternatively, if you have the option to control how the images are scanned, you can choose to scan them into a format that is natively supported by SSRS.

If you need to use TIFF due to its lossless compression and you can't use another format, you'll probably have to develop a custom control that can render TIFF images. This would likely involve some COM Interop to utilize the Windows Imaging Component (WIC), GDI+ or a third-party library that can handle TIFF images. Be aware that this would certainly add a layer of complexity to your report.
<|end|>


