Construct a rudimentary web page utilizing React.js framework, integrating a pair of application components into it.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
You would first need to install Node.js and npm on your computer. Then you can initialize your React app using the following commands in your terminal:

```
npx create-react-app my-app
cd my-app
npm start
```

You will replace "my-app" with whatever you want to name your application. The final command opens the application in a development server at localhost:3000.

You then create two component files. For simplicity, we'll create functional components. These could be "Header.js" and "Footer.js" placed in 'src/components' directory.

`Header.js:`
```jsx
import React from 'react';

function Header() {
    return (
        <header>
            <h1>Welcome to our Website!</h1>
        </header>
    );
}

export default Header;
```

`Footer.js:`
```jsx
import React from 'react';

function Footer() {
    return (
        <footer>
            <p>Copyright 2022</p>
        </footer>
    );
}

export default Footer;
```

To integrate these components into your main app, you need to import them into the 'App.js' file:

```jsx
import React from 'react';
import Header from './components/Header';
import Footer from './components/Footer';

function App() {
  return (
    <div className="App">
      <Header />
      {/* Here you can add the main content of your page */}
      <Footer />
    </div>
  );
}

export default App;
```

Remember to run 'npm start' again after you've created your files.

These are the basics of creating a rudimentary page with React. Components are used to make the code more modular and manageable. You can create as many components as you need, depending on the complexity of your web page.
<|end|>


