Below is a simple method definition in order to get the first digit of a number in C# language. The logic behind the method depends on converting the int number to a string and then getting the first character and parsing it back to an integer:

```C#
using System;

class Program
{
    static void Main()
    {
        Console.WriteLine(GetFirstDigit(12345));
    }   
    
    static int GetFirstDigit(int number)
    {
        string numberString = number.ToString();
        return int.Parse(numberString[0].ToString());
    }
}
```

