Here we will use React hooks and File API to implement the system. Use NPM to install the required dependencies ('react', 'react-dom' and 'bootstrap').

```jsx
import React, { useState } from 'react';
import 'bootstrap/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css';

const PhotoUploader = () => {
  const [chosenImage, setChosenImage] = useState();
  const [previewSource, setPreviewSource] = useState();
  
  const handleFileInputChange = (e) => {
    const file = e.target.files[0];
    previewFile(file);
  };
  
  const previewFile = (file) => {
    const reader = new FileReader();
    reader.readAsDataURL(file);
    reader.onloadend = () => {
      setPreviewSource(reader.result);
    };
  };
  
  return(
    <div>
      <input type='file' name='image' onChange={handleFileInputChange} className='form-input' />
      {previewSource && (
        <img src={previewSource} alt='chosen' style={{ height: '300px', width: '300px' }} />
      )}
    </div>
  );
};

export default PhotoUploader;
```

Your project should contain the following components:
`Input`: Handles choosing the image file in the file dialog.
`handleFileInputChange`: Gets the file from the event object.
`FileReader`: JavaScript File API to convert the selected file into a Base64 URL.
`img`: HTML element to display the preview image source.

