As described in the question I want to query the cloud watch logs for the lambdas that are failed and succeeded after consequentive retry attempts to the same lambda, I couldn't figure this out , any approaches on how to achieve this ?
I tried and only got until querying lambda invoke failed logs in the cloud watch, pretty new to AWS
Edit: I have my lambdas in step function states
<|end|>
<|asst|>
In AWS, you can use the CloudWatch Log Insights feature to search and analyze your log data. 

CloudWatch publishes Lambda function logs and automatically captures logs from Lambda functions including logs to track progress, detailed error messages that help in debugging, and output from `print` statements like `console.log()` that you include in your function's code. Lambda retries failed executions of a function, so multiple logs might be written for a single request.

The retry logs and actual error from the code can be queried by using the AWS RequestId. Here's a simple example on how to do it.

For example your lambda failed with a specific `RequestId`:

```
{
    "errorType": "Error",
    "errorMessage": "Some Error Message",
    ...
    "awsRequestId": "6bc28136-xmpl-4365-b021-0ce6b2e64ab0",
    ...
}
```

Now, log events with the specific `requestId` can be queried, including retries:

```
fields @timestamp, @message
| filter @message like /6bc28136-xmpl-4365-b021-0ce6b2e64ab0/
| sort @timestamp desc
```

Edit: If your lambda is integrated with Step Function, you can leverage Step Function Execution History. It provides a complete history of every step in your state machine executions. With Step Functions, you can handle failures and retries without writing any operational logic in your Lambda function. The state machine defined in Step Functions would show the retries, failures and successful attempts.

You can monitor AWS Step Functions using CloudWatch metrics, do remember to enable detailed CloudWatch metrics for AWS Step Functions.
Detailed CloudTrail logging, including the input and output field of states and it’s AWS X-Ray for analysis of the executed function. This will allow you to have a clear trace of function executions, input/output result, time stamps, error paths and so on.

You can use the following AWS CLI command to describe a state machine execution history:

```
aws stepfunctions describe-execution \
    --execution-arn <execution-arn>
```

Also, check the Step Function Execution event history in AWS Management Console. It will show you the error, retry count, succeeded event and so on for each execution.

Reference: https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws/new-cloudwatch-logs-insights-fast-interactive-log-analytics/
<|end|>


