In this script, `\b` is a word boundary in regex. This means that `pattern` will only match 'cat' when it is a whole word - it won't match 'cat' when it is part of another word (like 'caterpillar' or 'concatenate'). The flag `re.IGNORECASE` is used to make the match case-insensitive. `re.sub` is used to replace 'cat' with 'bird' in the original text string. The flag `re.IGNORECASE` is also used in `re.sub` to ensure the replacement is case-insensitive.
