Not only identify and list the title attribute values, but also the alt attribute values from all the <img> tags present in the provided HTML document. If the alt attribute is missing for any image, raise an exception. 
The HTML document is as follows:

<html>
<body>
    <p>This is an image example</p>
    <img src="flower.jpg" alt="Flower" title="Carnation">
    <img src="tree.jpg" alt="Tree" title="Palm Tree">
    <img src="bird.jpg" title="Eagle">
    <p>This is the end of examples.</p>
</body>
</html>
<|end|>
<|asst|>
You can solve this problem using Python's `BeautifulSoup` library. BeautifulSoup is a Python library for parsing HTML and XML documents. 

Here is the Python script:

```python
from bs4 import BeautifulSoup

html_doc = """
<html>
<body>
    <p>This is an image example</p>
    <img src="flower.jpg" alt="Flower" title="Carnation">
    <img src="tree.jpg" alt="Tree" title="Palm Tree">
    <img src="bird.jpg" title="Eagle">
    <p>This is the end of examples.</p>
</body>
</html>
"""

soup = BeautifulSoup(html_doc, 'html.parser')

imgs = soup.find_all('img')

for img in imgs:
    try:
        print(f'Title: {img["title"]}')
        print(f'Alt: {img["alt"]}')
        print("")
    except KeyError:
        raise Exception("Alt attribute is missing for an image")
```

This script parses the provided HTML document and find all `<img>` tags. For each image, it prints out the title and alt attribute. If the alt attribute is missing, it raises an exception.

When you run this script for the provided HTML document, it will throw an exception because the alt attribute for the third image (with title Eagle) is missing.
<|end|>


