<|asst|>
Google Cloud BigQuery does not have an SDK or Client Libraries for C or C++. Client Libraries are provided for multiple languages like Java, .NET, Python, PHP, and Node.js, but not for C or C++.

The typical approach to interface with BigQuery from C or C++ code is to use the REST API provided by Google. Here is an example with a simple HTTP request using libcurl in C which can be adapted to work with Google's REST API:

```c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <curl/curl.h>

int main(void)
{
  CURL *curl;
  CURLcode res;

  curl_global_init(CURL_GLOBAL_DEFAULT);

  curl = curl_easy_init();
  if(curl) {
    curl_easy_setopt(curl, CURLOPT_URL, "https://www.google.com/");
    
    /* If you want to set extra headers or authentication */
    // struct curl_slist *headers = NULL;
    // headers = curl_slist_append(headers, "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_AUTH_TOKEN");
    // headers = curl_slist_append(headers, "Accept: application/json");
    // curl_easy_setopt(curl, CURLOPT_HTTPHEADER, headers);
    
    /* Perform the request, res will get the return code */ 
    res = curl_easy_perform(curl);
    /* Check for errors */ 
    if(res != CURLE_OK)
      fprintf(stderr, "curl_easy_perform() failed: %s\n", curl_easy_strerror(res));

    /* always cleanup */ 
    curl_easy_cleanup(curl);
  }

  curl_global_cleanup();

  return 0;
}
```

Remember to replace the URL and headers necessary for your BigQuery requests. 

Also note that, when using the REST API, parsing the JSON response will require some more effort, as you will have to do it manually or find a library to do so. You might consider using a high-level language with a BigQuery SDK or use a language which Google provide a client library.
