<|asst|>
Following the below quick guide on how to use the library.

Step 1: Add the dependencies

Make sure you have added the library dependencies to your app.gradle file as described in the library's GitHub page. Like this:

```gradle
dependencies {
    implementation 'com.github.mukeshsolanki:android-otpview-pinview:2.1.2'
}
```

And also make sure you have jitpack in your project level build.gradle file like this:

```gradle
allprojects {
    repositories {
        maven { url 'https://jitpack.io' }
    }
}
```

Step 2: Use the custom view in your layout.xml file:

You can add the custom view in your xml file using the full path to the class, like this:

 ```xml
<com.mukesh.OtpView
 android:layout_width="wrap_content"
 android:layout_height="wrap_content"/>
```

Step 3: Make sure you recompile your project

After adding the custom view in your layout file, recompile your project. If there isn't any error, the view should be displayed in your layout preview.

Step 4: In case it doesn't work

If you are sure that everything is done right and still it's not working, it's possible that there is an issue between the library and your Android Studio version. Sometimes an update in Android Studio can cause some conflicts with some libraries. In these cases the best approach is usually to report the bug to the library authors.

Note: You can also check the 'Infer Constraints' option in the design view in XML file. Android studio sometimes by default uses 'AutoConnect' which can give you a trouble. Switching it to 'Infer Constraints' might solve the problem.
