Can I display all the terms of a woocommerce product attribute in a specific page (even empty terms) and in front of each term the number of products linked with it?
Example:
Attribute A
Term 1 (2)
Term 2 (1)
Term 3 (0)
Term 4 (2)
Term 5 (1)
Term 6 (0)
Regards
I like to have a short code, a small php code or even a plugin
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Yes, by creating a custom shortcode, you can list WooCommerce product attribute, even with empty ones. Here's a sample code that could be added to your theme's functions.php file:

```php
add_shortcode( 'attributes_list', 'display_product_terms' );

function display_product_terms() {
    $taxonomy     = 'pa_your-attribute'; // Replace 'your-attribute' with your attribute name
    $orderby      = 'name';  
    $order        = 'asc';  

    $args = array(
         'taxonomy'     => $taxonomy,
         'orderby'      => $orderby,
         'order'        => $order,
         'hide_empty'   => false
    );

    $all_terms = get_terms( $args );

    if( !empty( $all_terms ) ) {
        $output = '<ul>';

        foreach($all_terms as $term) {
            $product_count = $term->count;
            $output .= '<li>' . $term->name . ' (' . $product_count . ') </li>';
        }

        $output .= '</ul>';

        return $output;
    } else {
        return 'No Attributes found';
    }
}
```
You can display it on a specific page using the `[attributes_list]` shortcode.

Regarding plugins, there is no specific WooCommerce plugin that provides a shortcode to display terms of an attribute, but you can customize some plugins like 'Shortcodes Ultimate' or similar to create custom shortcodes.

Remember to replace `'pa_your-attribute'` with your attribute name, such as 'pa_color' for color attribute etc.

Also, it's always recommended to use child themes when editing your PHP files so that you won't lose the changes when the theme updates. This function doesn't check if the attribute exists or not, so make sure you replace `'pa_your-attribute'` with your existing attribute slug.
<|end|>


