Craft a Node.js function that is able to inverse the sequence of characters in a given string without utilizing any of the built-in function methods of Node.js for this purpose.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here is a simple Node.js solution using a for loop to iterate through the string in reverse order.

```JavaScript
function inverseString(str){
    let result = "";
    for(let i = str.length - 1; i >= 0; i--){
        result += str[i];
    }
    return result;
}

console.log(inverseString("Hello"));  // Outputs "olleH"
```

This function uses standard JavaScript commands only; no modules required since Node.js allows JavaScript to run on servers.

Test the function by running the script file (let's say the filename is script.js): in a terminal command line, navigate to the directory in which script.js is saved, and type 'node script.js'.

Just a note, contrary to what the question implies, there are no built-in function methods in Node.js specifically for reversing a string. This functionality is typically achieved using standard JavaScript methods.
<|end|>


