I deleted a branch in TFS and just found out that I need the changes that were on it.

How do I recover the branch or the changes done on it?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
To recover a branch or changes you accidentally deleted in Team Foundation Server (TFS), you can typically use the following steps:

1. Open "Source Control Explorer" from Team Explorer in Visual Studio.
2. Right click on project collection and click on "Advanced -> Undelete".
3. In Undelete dialog box click on "Show Delete Items" checkbox. It shows up all deleted items.
4. Now select the items you want to undelete (restore) and click on "Undelete" button.
5. Lastly, remember to check in your undelete operation.

That will restore your branch or changes.

Note: You should have the proper permissions to see and perform undelete operations. Backup frequently to avoid disasters in the future, and use branch policies to avoid unwanted deletion.
<|end|>


