Suggest a method to render the text inside a paragraph element to the colour red, without using inline CSS.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
You can achieve this by using either external or internal CSS.

Method 1: Using External CSS
-------------------------------

Create a CSS file, let's name it 'styles.css'

In the styles.css file, add the following code:

```CSS
p {
    color: red;
}
```

Then in your HTML file, link the CSS file:

```HTML
<head>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css">
</head>
```

Method 2: Using Internal CSS
-------------------------------

You can also write the CSS code within the HTML file itself inside a `<style>` tag, which should be placed in the `<head>` section:

```HTML
<head>
    <style>
        p {
            color: red;
        }
    </style>
</head>
```

For both methods, every paragraph `<p>` element in the HTML file will have red text.

If you want to only target a specific paragraph, you can use a class or an id. For example:

External or Internal CSS
```
p.myParagraph {
    color: red;
}
```

HTML
```
<p class="myParagraph">This paragraph will have red text</p>
<p>This paragraph will not have red text</p>
```
<|end|>


