<|asst|>
You can calculate the sum of an array of integers in Java using a for-each loop. Here is a code snippet that would accomplish that:

```java
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[] numbers = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5};
        int sum = 0;

        for (int number : numbers) {
            sum += number;
        }

        System.out.println("The sum of the array elements is: " + sum);
    }
}
```

When you run the above code, it will output "The sum of the array elements is: 15", which is the sum of 1, 2, 3, 4, and 5.
