給定兩個字符串，分別找出和刪除其相同部分，然後結合剩下的兩部分。
string1 = "Programming is Fun!";
string2 = "Coding is Fun!"
<|end|>
<|asst|>
This problem can be solved in Python using set operations and join function. Here is a possible solution:

```python
string1 = "Programming is Fun!"
string2 = "Coding is Fun!"

# Change strings to set to eliminate identical characters
set1 = set(string1)
set2 = set(string2)

# Find the difference between the two sets
diff1 = set1 - set2
diff2 = set2 - set1

# Combine the differences and convert to list
combined_diff = list(diff1) + list(diff2)

# Combine the characters in the list to a string
result = ''.join(combined_diff)

print(result)
```

Please note that this solution will remove all identical characters from both the strings irrespective of their positions. Also, the output string will not have a meaningful order of characters. If you want to keep the order, you can use the built-in replace function in python:

```python
string1 = "Programming is Fun!"
string2 = "Coding is Fun!"

for char in string1:
    if char in string2:
        string1 = string1.replace(char, '')
        string2 = string2.replace(char, '')

result = string1 + string2
print(result)
```

This solution will keep the remaining characters of both strings in their original order.
<|end|>


