Here is a simple javascript function which can replace all web URLs present in a text with the word "URL".

```javascript
function replaceURLWithWord(text) {
    var urlRegex = /\b((http|https):\/\/?)[^\s()<>]+(?:\([\w\d]+\)|([^[:punct:]\s]|\/?))/g;
    return text.replace(urlRegex, 'URL');
}
```

This function looks for any pattern that starts with either "http://" or "https://" which usually initiates a URL and replaces it with 'URL'.

You can use the function like this:

```javascript
var text = 'Hello, visit https://www.google.com for searching information';
var result = replaceURLWithWord(text);
console.log(result); // 'Hello, visit URL for searching information'
```

In this example, `https://www.google.com` is replaced with `URL`.
