Assemble a function utilizing JavaScript programming language that ascertains the validity of a user's postal code input.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here is a JavaScript function that can be used to validate a user's postal code input. This function assumes the postal code is in the US format, i.e., a five digit number or a five digit number followed by a hyphen and four more digits. 

The function uses a regular expression to verify this pattern. If the input doesn't match the pattern, the function will return false, otherwise true. 

```javascript
function isValidPostalCode(postalCode) {
  // Regular Expression pattern to match a US postal code
  const postalCodePattern = /^(\d{5}(-\d{4})?)$/;

  // Test the input against the pattern
  let valid = postalCodePattern.test(postalCode);

  // Return the result
  return valid;
}
```

An example usage of the function:

```javascript
console.log(isValidPostalCode('94103')); // Returns true
console.log(isValidPostalCode('94103-1234')); // Returns true
