Here are a few comprehensive tutorials that can get you up and running with ASP.NET MVC:

1. [Microsoft ASP.NET MVC -  Official Tutorials](https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/aspnet/mvc/overview/getting-started/) - This set of tutorials by Microsoft, the developer of ASP.NET, is comprehensive and covers everything from getting started with MVC, to advanced topics like working with databases, authentication, and deployment. It can get you started and moving in less than a couple of hours.

2. [Tutorial: Get started with ASP.NET Core MVC](https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/aspnet/core/tutorials/first-mvc-app/start-mvc?view=aspnetcore-5.0) - Another guide from Microsoft, but this time focused on ASP.NET Core MVC. This is a newer version of ASP.NET, and this tutorial is aimed at beginners who are just starting out with MVC.

3. [MVC 5 with EF 6 in Visual Studio 2013](https://www.entityframeworktutorial.net/mvc/mvc5-with-ef6.aspx) - This tutorial is specifically designed for people who want to use MVC 5 with Entity Framework 6. While it's a bit specific, you can get started with MVC and learn more as you go, all the while using some of the latest technologies.

