I've seen there are some race condition analysis tools for C++, C and Java. Anyone know of any static analysis tools that do the same for .NET?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
There are several tools that provide static analysis for .NET languages such as C# for race condition detection:

1. Microsoft's Concurrency Visualizer in Visual Studio - A tool that can help you visualize and analyze the behavior of your multithreaded code and more specifically observe its critical areas and the synchronization primitives that protect them.

2. PVS-Studio - An analyzer that detects bugs in the source code of programs written in C, C++, and C#. It has some experimental rules to detect potential race conditions.

3. Code Contracts - This Microsoft tool provides static code analysis for .NET. It isn't specific to race conditions, but it could detect issues that might lead to a race condition.

4. Coverity - A static analysis tool that has thread safety and concurrency checkers.

5. Parasoft dotTEST - An integrated, full-life-cycle solution for .NET that helps prevent and eliminate potential concurrency issues.

6. NDepend - This tool has several concurrency-related rules.

7. ReSharper - This isn't specific to race conditions, but it can alert developers about certain threading-related issues.

Please note that static analysis tools may only be able to detect a subset of potential race conditions, and they can also produce false positives (identifying an issue when there isn't one) or false negatives (not identifying an issue when there is one). It is recommended to combine these tools with best coding practices, thorough testing, and dynamic analysis tools for concurrency issues.
<|end|>


