I'm seeking a method to ascertain the (row, column) index of the smallest value within a numpy array or matrix. For instance, if I have A = array([[1, 2], [3, 0]]), my desired output would be (1, 1). Could you provide a solution that would work for any arbitrary 2D numpy array? I appreciate your assistance!
A:
&lt;code&gt;
import numpy as np
a = np.array([[1, 2], [3, 0]])
&lt;/code&gt;
result = ... # insert the solution here
BEGIN SOLUTION
&lt;code&gt;
<|end|>
<|asst|>
result = np.unravel_index(a.argmin(), a.shape)
print(result)
&lt;/code&gt;
The result of the above code will be (1, 1), which is the index of the smallest value in array a. The function 'np.unravel_index()' translates the flat index returned by 'a.argmin()' into a coordinate in the shape of a.
<|end|>


