<|user|>
How to read a web server log file in Java. This file is getting updated all the time.  If I open a new FileInputStream, will it read the log real time?

Regards
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here is a simple way of reading a log file in Java using java.io.BufferedReader class:

```java
import java.io.*;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        
        File logFile = new File("/path/to/logFile.log");
        
        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new FileReader(logFile));
        
        String line;
        
        while((line = br.readLine()) != null) {
            System.out.println(line);
        }
        br.close();
    }
}
```

However, this will only read the file to the end and then close. It will not keep reading as the file updates. To do real-time monitoring of a file, you could use the Apache Commons IO library's `Tailer` class.

Add maven dependency for Apache Commons IO:

```xml
<dependency>
    <groupId>commons-io</groupId>
    <artifactId>commons-io</artifactId>
    <version>2.6</version>
</dependency>
```

Here's an example of how to use `Tailer`:

```java
import org.apache.commons.io.input.Tailer;
import org.apache.commons.io.input.TailerListenerAdapter;

import java.io.File;

public class LogFileTailer extends TailerListenerAdapter {
    @Override
    public void handle(String line) {
        System.out.println(line); // implementation of log line handling
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        File logFile = new File("/path/to/logFile.log");
        LogFileTailer tailerListener = new LogFileTailer();

        // Create and start the Tailer
        Tailer.tail(logFile, tailerListener, 1000);
    }
}
```
This tailer version will continually check the file, even as it's being changed, and output any changes to the system console. Remember to replace "/path/to/logFile.log" with the actual file path.
<|end|>


