Design an HTML form that requires the user to enter details: their name, email address, password, and date of birth. Enhance the form by adding JavaScript validation for the following conditions: 

1. The name should not contain any numbers or special characters. 
2. The email address should be in the correct format and shouldn't be left blank. 
3. The password should contain a minimum of eight characters, at least one uppercase letter, one lowercase letter, and one number.
4. The user must be at least 18 years old according to the date of birth entered.

Also, incorporate an AJAX call to simulate sending this data off to a server after validation. Include error handling to notify the user if there are any issues using clear and appropriately placed error messages.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Sure, here's a simple implementation using HTML, JavaScript, and AJAX:

HTML code:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>Form Validator</title>
    <script src="https://ajax.googleapis.com/ajax/libs/jquery/3.5.1/jquery.min.js"></script>
    <script src="form_validation.js"></script>
</head>
<body>
    <form id="userForm">
        Name: <input type="text" id="name"><br>
        <p id="nameError" style="color: red;"></p>

        Email: <input type="text" id="email"><br>
        <p id="emailError" style="color: red;"></p>

        Password: <input type="password" id="password"><br>
        <p id="passwordError" style="color: red;"></p>

        Date of Birth: <input type="date" id="dob"><br>
        <p id="dobError" style="color: red;"></p>

        <input type="submit" value="Submit">
    </form>
</body>
</html>
```

JavaScript code (separate "form_validation.js" file):

```javascript
$(document).ready(function () {
    $("#userForm").on("submit", function (event) {
        event.preventDefault();
        var isValid = true;

        // Name Validation
        var name = $("#name").val();
        if (!/^[a-zA-Z\s]+$/.test(name)) {
            $("#nameError").text("Name should not contain numbers or special characters.");
            isValid = false;
        } else {
            $("#nameError").text("");
        }

        // Email Validation
        var email = $("#email").val();
        if (!/^\S+@\S+\.\S+$/.test(email)) {
            $("#emailError").text("Please enter a valid email address.");
            isValid = false;
        } else {
            $("#emailError").text("");
        }

        // Password Validation
        var password = $("#password").val();
        if (!/(?=.*\d)(?=.*[a-z])(?=.*[A-Z]).{8,}/.test(password)) {
            $("#passwordError").text("Password should contain at least 8 characters, one upper case, one lower case, and one number.");
            isValid = false;
        } else {
            $("#passwordError").text("");
        }

        // DOB validation
        var dob = new Date($("#dob").val());
        var today = new Date();
        if ((today.getFullYear() - dob.getFullYear()) < 18) {
            $("#dobError").text("User must be at least 18 years old.");
            isValid = false;
        } else {
            $("#dobError").text("");
        }

        if (isValid) {
            $.ajax({
                url: 'your_server_url',
                type: 'POST',
                data: {
                    'name': name,
                    'email': email,
                    'password': password,
                    'dob': dob
                },
                success: function (data) {
                    alert('Form submitted successfully');
                },
                error: function (jqXHR, textStatus, errorThrown) {
                    alert('Error in form submission');
                }
            });
        }
    });
});
```

Please note you will need to replace 'your_server_url' with the actual URL, where you'll send the AJAX request. Also, as for the birth date, this script assumes that the user must be at least 18 years old from today's date. If you want to check if the user's age is 18 according to the 1st January of the current year, you might need to adjust the logic of the age check. 

Ensure that jQuery library is included in the HTML head section for AJAX and jQuery functions to work properly.
<|end|>


